{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do","id":1549710,"title":"What the Spheres Say They Can Do","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-01T09:30:38-07:00","id":1549710,"title":"What the Spheres Say They Can Do","content":"Time for a different pass through the Spheres. This time I\u2019m going to look at the Sphere write ups by rank and break down what abilities they say they give a mage. I\u2019ll analyze obvious interpretations, potential exploits, and unintuitive uses seen elsewhere in the book.<br /> <br /> In previous analyses I\u2019ve been quick to call out contradictions and say a passage is wrong. However, the real problem is I missed what the text was actually saying, so let\u2019s take a different approach here. When an apparent false statement arises, I want to search for a possible interpretation that would make the statement make sense.<br /> <br /> If M20 really does contradict itself, though, here is how I will weigh its statements:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> 1) A statement from a Sphere writeup about that Sphere takes precedence over a statement from anywhere else in the book, including one from a different Sphere writeup.<br /> <br /> 2) A statement from the base description of the sphere takes precedence over any Rank description.<br /> <br /> 3) A statement from a Sphere Rank about that Rank takes precedence over a statement from a different Rank. That is, if Matter 2 and Matter 3 disagree about the capabilities of Matter 2, Matter 2 has priority.<br /> <br /> 4) Statements from M20 take precedence over statements from other books and previous editions. So other texts can fill in missing information but they can\u2019t contradict a direct statement from M20.</div> <br /> I can\u2019t be as exhaustive as I\u2019d like, so I welcome any suggestions you have. Especially on different interpretations of powers and alternate uses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T09:37:49-07:00","id":1549711,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><b>Correspondence Base</b></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Purview: Correspondence governs both Space and Connections. Often one is described as an effect of the other, but either way it covers both.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></b><br /> <br /> <b>1 - There are specific rules about using connections to bypass normal distance restrictions.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2 - Correspondence can extend range, allowing mages to interact with distant things as if they were present. If this requires more than just physical contact, it may require additional spheres.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The most straightforward interpretation of this is: if they could do something without magic if they were present, they can do it with the appropriate rank in Correspondence without additional spheres. If they would need spheres in person, they still need those spheres from a distance.<br /> <br /> Note: This specifically gives Correspondence 2 the ability to grasp and manipulate items from a distance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>3 - When using Correspondence with other spheres, a mage\u2019s rank in Corr caps the rank in other spheres than can be used. This was probably intended for effects where Correspondence is altering the range of another spell, or something similar.</b><br /> <br /> On a strict reading this applies <i>any</i> time Corr is added to a spell, such as adding a Corr 1 sensory effect to an invisibility spell.<br /> <br /> I should point out that M20 does not include the higher rating of Correspondence when it gives Sphere requirements, though other texts do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>4 - Correspondence deals with whole patterns only. Moving a full pattern does not require additional spheres. Moving a partial pattern requires the appropriate spheres to split the pattern.</b><br /> <br /> I can think of a few cases where 2 and 4 seem to contradict, but I think this is easily resolved by viewing 2 as a rule about extending range and 4 as a rule about applying Correspondence directly to a target. So teleporting half a piece of paper requires Corr alone if the mage is manually reaching out, tearing it in half, and pulling one half back to himself, but it takes Corr and Matter to teleport half the sheet directly. Teleporting an elephant directly would take Corr alone, while opening a portal and pushing the elephant through would take Corr and a spell to do the pushing. (Though that pushing effect might itself be a Correspondence effect)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T09:48:12-07:00","id":1549713,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A note on M20s formatting. Each rank writeup starts with a list of abilities and/or rote names from previous editions and then goes into deeper descriptions of the rank. I\u2019ll try to give weight to both the list and the description, although this isn\u2019t always possible. Often the powers in the list are cute but uninformative. I\u2019m not going to complain too much about that; as will become clear, I\u2019m a fan of coming up with creative names for effects.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Immediate Spatial Perceptions / Landscape of the Mind </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Basic spatial understanding allows a mage to sense things in her immediate vicinity even if she can\u2019t perceive them with her normal senses. Using that perception, she can estimate the distances between objects; intuitively find a direction (North, South, East, West); notice hidden objects or characters; and spot spatial instabilities \u2013 warps, anomalies, wormholes, etc. \u2013 especially the ones caused by other Correspondence Effects.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is one of M20\u2019s poorly curated lists. The paragraph gives one power- sensing things in the immediate vicinity- and everything else is listed as an application of that one power. Except that finding a direction isn\u2019t an application of that power as it doesn\u2019t rely on sensing objects in range. Let\u2019s ignore the idea that they are related powers for now.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anyways, Corr 1 lets a mage:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Things in Vicinity (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Hidden Objects (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m pairing these up because they seem to be descriptions of the same thing. At a direct reading, this allows mages to have a sense of the area around them, without using their regular senses, and regardless of camouflage or concealment. This is potentially very powerful, but depends on what level of detail the ST allows. This is not clear. It also isn\u2019t clear how to adjudicate contests between this and attempts at concealment.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Based on use in other areas of the book, this should at the very least eliminate penalties for operating without sense. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unconventional use:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Detect Illusion</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power reasonably can tell the difference between things that take up space and things that do not (even if they visually appear to). Using this, a mage can see through various illusions, unless those illusions are specifically tailored to fool Correspondence senses.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know Directions (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As I said earlier, this power can\u2019t reasonably be an application of sensing objects in the local area. It has to be sensing direction/orientation directly. That gives this ability much more potential than it first appears. Cardinal directions are just one of many reference frames. This ability could potentially be used to know the direction \u201chome\u201d or to know the current longitude and latitude coordinates.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a reasonable extension because 1) There\u2019s no better sphere for a sensory effect to tell a mage where he is, and 2) knowing the current location was a rote in previous editions.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>You Are Here</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can know his location in a variety of reference systems. Esoteric reference frames and systems that provide more information may require more successes.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know Distance Between Objects (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Range</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the one power where it matters a lot whether this is an application of sensing objects or not. If it is, it is limited to objects within sensory distance, both because that\u2019s the listed range of that power and it\u2019s the listed range of magic in general. On the other hand, it could be sensing something more abstract, like knowing directions does. That\u2019s why it is so damaging when M20 uses these badly compiled lists, because we can\u2019t use positioning in the sentence to determine what is supposed to happen.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That said, since we are dealing with objects and since extending range via things like photos is distinctly a Corr 2 power, I would say the objects in question do need to be within sensory range. Given that, this power is quite situational. It becomes much more useful, though, once Corr 2 rolls around and it can be used from a distance. Consider how much use a detective, spy, sniper, or thief could get out of knowing exactly where someone or something is in relation to themselves or something else.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unconventional use:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Follow Your Nose </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When I think of sensory distance I usually think of line of sight, but it should also include other senses. This power could determine the distance to an unexpected sound or smell.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Detect Spatial Anomalies (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is explicitly said to be most useful in detecting the effects of other uses of Correspondence. This is not surprising, since there aren\u2019t many naturally occurring spatial anomalies in day to day life. The Old Ways that Verbena can detect with this Sphere rank might be one, or they might be ancient workings of magic.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Detect Strangeness</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Or are there? An oft overlooked aspect of Mage is that the world itself doesn\u2019t always behave the way we expect. Have you ever had the experience of driving to work and looking up to see you are further along than you reasonably should be. In real life that\u2019s probably just a perceptual trick, but in Mage that could be real. If so, this power would detect what was going on.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Elsewhere in M20:</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Know Perfect Spot (???)</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Thunder Punch it appears a mage can determine the ideal spot to strike. </span>\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Missing Powers:</b></span> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Detect Connection (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Considering how important connections between things are to the use of Correspondence, the Sphere clearly has the ability to determine how strongly two things are connected. This was explicit in previous editions.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know the Right Way (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t see this one elsewhere, but if a player wanted a spell to determine which of two (or more) paths led to a destination or was the shortest path to a destination, I\u2019d say that was Corr 1. This would only be in terms of directions, though. Knowing the safest or most reliable path would involve Entropy.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T09:50:24-07:00","id":1549714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549711#post1549711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of a few cases where 2 and 4 seem to contradict, but I think this is easily resolved by viewing 2 as a rule about extending range and 4 as a rule about applying Correspondence directly to a target. So teleporting half a piece of paper requires Corr alone if the mage is manually reaching out, tearing it in half, and pulling one half back to himself, but it takes Corr and Matter to teleport half the sheet directly. Teleporting an elephant directly would take Corr alone, while opening a portal and pushing the elephant through would take Corr and a spell to do the pushing. (Though that pushing effect might itself be a Correspondence effect)</div> </div> </div> </div>Would teleporting an elephant head only kill it? if so should we count that as part of the damage table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T09:57:35-07:00","id":1549716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549714#post1549714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would teleporting an elephant head only kill it? if so should we count that as part of the damage table?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would unless Correspondence 5 was involved, yes.<br /> <br /> I don't think I've seen anything about the difficulty of splitting a living pattern, but I would certainly set the successes to separate an elephant's head from its body based on how much damage that would take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T13:10:01-07:00","id":1549717,"title":"","content":"Great work, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> , I look forward for the analysis of the other spheres!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T15:27:20-07:00","id":1549720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do#post1549710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If M20 really does contradict itself, though, here is how I will weigh its statements:</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do the base rules for magic fall into this heuristic? There's lots of things that could explain some of the vagueness in Correspondence 1 if we're looking at how the base casting rules implement various concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549714#post1549714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would teleporting an elephant head only kill it? if so should we count that as part of the damage table?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. M20's write-up directly addresses this. Correspondence only deals in whole patterns. You can steal a knife from someone because the knife is a separate pattern from the person using it. You can't cut their hand off because the hand is part of the assailant's pattern instead of a pattern of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T16:42:56-07:00","id":1549721,"title":"","content":"Not if you add other spheres<br /> &quot;Despite its ability to warp space and distance,<br /> Correspondence deals only with whole Patterns, unless a target<br /> has been altered by another Pattern Sphere; Correspondence<br /> alone, for example, cannot teleport someone\u2019s head off \u2013 the<br /> mage would need to use Life magick to separate the head from<br /> its body. A gun, on the other hand, could be snatched away by<br /> Correspondence alone.&quot;<br /> - 513 M20 Core","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-02-2025, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T07:13:27-07:00","id":1549731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549720#post1549720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do the base rules for magic fall into this heuristic? There's lots of things that could explain some of the vagueness in Correspondence 1 if we're looking at how the base casting rules implement various concepts.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My first choice would be to make the rules themselves primary, but that's not exactly possible. The Sphere writeups often suspend basic rules, especially in the Base sections. Time has special Paradox rules, Mind and Spirit have special difficulty rules, Forces has special damage rules and area limitations, etc. Some of these are reiterated in the rules section but I don't think all of them are, so when the rules and sphere writeups don't match up we can't discount the possibility that is intentional. I would put the rules as more important than most of M20, but potentially overridden by the Sphere writeups (though only for the purposes of that Sphere). <br /> <br /> I am aware this heuristic isn't going to be infallible, it's just meant to be a framework for this thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T09:23:29-07:00","id":1549742,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 2</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Sense, Touch, Thicken &amp; Reach Through Space/ Correspondence Sensing </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That mage can now extend her senses across intervening space, sensing things in other locations. Such extensions, however, leave minor ripples in space\u2026 the kind noticed by Rank 1 Correspondence. Fortunately, she can also thicken space to cover her tracks; each success used in doing so deducts one success from the roll of a character who\u2019s trying to spy on her or notice her sensory Effects.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By adding Life or Matter to Rank 2 Correspondence, the mage can grasp small items or organisms (housecat-sized or smaller) and then pull them through tiny holes in space. This lets her snatch business cards, guns, rabbits, and such from another location, apparently pulling them out of nowhere.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The strangest thing about Correspondence 2 is that the most important ability it has is largely defined somewhere else (the Base Correspondence section). It\u2019s not that it isn\u2019t mentioned at all here, it is just piecemeal and narrowly stated.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll go through what is in Corr 2 before getting to the rest.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corr 2 can:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extend Senses (Sense Through Space)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exactly what it says on the tin. Also known as scrying. Note that this does not limit which senses, so as written it applies to Sphere given senses as well as natural ones. This is consistent with what we see of Corr 2\u2019s powers elsewhere.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the quest to come up with clever uses for a power I will sometimes deviate towards the esoteric and the sketchy. This ability gets one of each:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Extend Unconventional Senses</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are senses beyond the 5 we usually think of, and I don\u2019t mean ESP. Balance and Proprioception are senses, for instance. I don\u2019t know what precisely extending them beyond their normal range would accomplish, but it is certainly possible with this power.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Other Reference Frames</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the controversial one, so I put it forward as a potential application, not a certain one. There\u2019s nothing stating that scrying should be limited to the same viewpoint size as the mage. It is possible this power can be used to view the microscopic as well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You might disagree with me on that. That\u2019s fair. There\u2019s also nothing saying that this can be used for different viewpoint sizes. I would say, though, that this power should be available at some point in Correspondence so I\u2019d welcome suggestions of where else could fit.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Block Scrying (Thicken Space)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can use Thicken space to keep other people from using Correspondence to spy on him. He can also use this to cover his tracks when spying on others. These seem like the same thing but the latter implies a mage can do a bit more.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Cover Up</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage should be able to cover up detection of any spatial anomaly, not just their own actions. Stumble across a police box with an inside bigger than the outside, Corr 2 can probably keep Corr 1 senses from detecting that. This is a highly situational power based on the nature of the current game.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Effects?:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pull Things Through Tiny Holes (Reach Through Space)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Teleport small items by pulling it through small holes. Allegedly takes pattern spheres, despite what Base Correspondence says.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"color:#980000\">Conflict Resolution - A bad description of an effect we already have?</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ve been searching for a way to consider this a different effect than that described in Base Correspondence, one that would actually use Pattern Spheres, and I have only found one. The mage could be using pattern spheres to disassemble the target, pull it through many tiny holes and reassemble it on the other side. Opening holes in space is not normally a power associated with Corr 2 but I suppose it could be. But even if so, Corr 2 already lets a mage move things around in space directly, so this would be a harder and more Sphere intensive thing of accomplishing something the mage can already do. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All other explanations are just applications of range extension, which doesn\u2019t normally require pattern spheres. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Elsewhere in M20:</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, from the writeup in Corr 2, thickening space is the term for inhibiting correspondence senses, but it actually has one more use that is completely neglected here:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minor Ward (Thicken Space) from Common Magical Effects</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">HDYDT clearly says that Thicken Space is the basis for the first level of wards, and while I ordinarily ignore that book, M20s common magical effects table also lists Correspondence 2 as the rank Wards start at. HDYDT is not at its best here but Minor Wards basically increase the difficulty acting in certain ways within the ward.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since Wards are often cast to affect types of things rather than specific things that are already present, there is a good reason to incorporate other spheres to detect. Since Minor Wards were completely left out of this section, though, no guidance is given on how to select those.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">My default is that when a spell needs to sense something not present when the spell is cast, it takes one rank higher than the mage directly sensing the thing, so Appropriate Sphere 2. That is my take, though, not a clear ruling from M20.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The biggest oversight, though, is:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extend Range (Reach Through Space) from Base Correspondence</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is fundamental. It\u2019s used everywhere in M20. It\u2019s such a core part of Correspondence 2 that the Base Correspondence Section specifically calls it out. This is the fundamental basis of casting from a distance.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But it\u2019s not just about casting. This also extends the range of regular actions. If you want to punch someone from a distance, that\u2019s Corr 2. If you want to pick someone\u2019s pocket from across the street, that\u2019s Corr 2. If you want to whisper and be heard by someone across a busy street, that\u2019s Corr 2. If you want your senses to cover an area they ordinarily don't, that's Corr 2. Correspondence 2, it appears, can extend the range of anything.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the best explanation of all the manipulation of objects a mage can do at Corr 2 is that he is just extending the range of actions he can normally take at close quarters. He's literally reaching out and moving items as if they were right in front of him.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>We Get Signal</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extend Range should also apply to other things, like radio signals or wifi networks. Connecting to wifi as if your computer was in range or listening to radio broadcasts as if your radio was in range should be possible.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I'm Crushing Your Head</i></span></span></b><br /> \u200b<br /> Unfortunately, no, Corr 2 can't make the sketch from Kids in the Hall real. The indication is a mage is limited to the actions he can normally perform and he can't size them up or down, hence the limit of housecat size or less. He can reach out and actually squeeze someone's head, though, or do a variety of hostile actions. If he wants to up the effects beyond what he is easily capable of, though, he will need other spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T12:35:52-07:00","id":1549747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549721#post1549721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if you add other spheres<br /> &quot;Despite its ability to warp space and distance,<br /> Correspondence deals only with whole Patterns, unless a target<br /> has been altered by another Pattern Sphere; Correspondence<br /> alone, for example, cannot teleport someone\u2019s head off \u2013 the<br /> mage would need to use Life magick to separate the head from<br /> its body. A gun, on the other hand, could be snatched away by<br /> Correspondence alone.&quot;<br /> - 513 M20 Core</div> </div> </div> </div>So... still a no. It's not &quot;add other spheres&quot; it's, &quot;has been altered by another Pattern Sphere.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't cut someone's head off with Correspondence. You can cut someone's head of at range (in many ways, in this example a Life effect) and then you can use Correspondence to teleport just the head. I feel most STs would let you do this as a single magic casting and all where narratively it looks like the portal closes on the target's head and decapitates them, but mechanically that's not the order of events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549731#post1549731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first choice would be to make the rules themselves primary, but that's not exactly possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just asking because you left them out more than not. I'm not advocating for any specific application of them broadly.<br /> <br /> It's more for things like the base rules giving options like &quot;finding hidden objects&quot; to be less binary; whether its having it just be Abilities Enhancing magic for Alertness or Investigation rolls, or how to handle mages casting conflicting effects in the countermagic rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549742#post1549742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are senses beyond the 5 we usually think of, and I don\u2019t mean ESP. Balance and Proprioception are senses, for instance. I don\u2019t know what precisely extending them beyond their normal range would accomplish, but it is certainly possible with this power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Life or Mind might help this because the majority of our senses are internal and expanding them externally would be extremely difficult to process. We can sense temperature, but we lack any inherent senses for actively sensing heat signatures like some animals do. Without getting too much into a debate around when on sense starts and another ends, humans have a severely underdeveloped VNO (Jacboson's organ) compared to most animals we think of as having excellent senses of smell. The VNO doesn't inherently increase what you can or can't smell though, it increases the ability to pinpoint sources of smells (consider it similar to the benefit of having two eyes instead of one). Dogs aren't such good hunting companions because of the vastly increased number of smells they can differentiate compared to a human (though it does help of course), but because they have good VNOs to help them track one specific scent amongst all the rest and follow it.<br /> <br /> If you expanded what VNO senses humans do have, it wouldn't really turn us into scent hounds because ours don't really do that. Low level Life or Mind could help make up for the lack of actual physical organs or mental processing necessary for making such expansions useful (or at higher life just giving yourself some of the sensory organs humans lack or don't have strong versions of).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the controversial one, so I put it forward as a potential application, not a certain one. There\u2019s nothing stating that scrying should be limited to the same viewpoint size as the mage. It is possible this power can be used to view the microscopic as well. </div> </div> </div>We did have a whole thread about this... though I will point out your own statement on Correspondence 2 here though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately, no, Corr 2 can't make the sketch from Kids in the Hall real. The indication is a mage is limited to the actions he can normally perform and he can't size them up or down, hence the limit of housecat size or less. He can reach out and actually squeeze someone's head, though, or do a variety of hostile actions. If he wants to up the effects beyond what he is easily capable of, though, he will need other spheres. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T13:36:05-07:00","id":1549749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549747#post1549747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Life or Mind might help this because the majority of our senses are internal and expanding them externally would be extremely difficult to process. We can sense temperature, but we lack any inherent senses for actively sensing heat signatures like some animals do. Without getting too much into a debate around when on sense starts and another ends, humans have a severely underdeveloped VNO (Jacboson's organ) compared to most animals we think of as having excellent senses of smell. The VNO doesn't inherently increase what you can or can't smell though, it increases the ability to pinpoint sources of smells (consider it similar to the benefit of having two eyes instead of one). Dogs aren't such good hunting companions because of the vastly increased number of smells they can differentiate compared to a human (though it does help of course), but because they have good VNOs to help them track one specific scent amongst all the rest and follow it.<br /> <br /> If you expanded what VNO senses humans do have, it wouldn't really turn us into scent hounds because ours don't really do that. Low level Life or Mind could help make up for the lack of actual physical organs or mental processing necessary for making such expansions useful (or at higher life just giving yourself some of the sensory organs humans lack or don't have strong versions of).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, much like with handling multiple sense inputs or multiple locations, Mind and Life aren't mandatory parts of the spell, but they may be required to make it useful. Actually, I don't usually think of Life as a way of mediating inputs, but that was a really good example of how it could work. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We did have a whole thread about this... though I will point out your own statement on Correspondence 2 here though: </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that thread is why I stressed that the idea was controversial, not certain. Nor was the disparity between that and the Crushing Your Head idea lost on me, though there is enough of a difference between changing the size of a viewpoint and changing the size of a thing that I figured I'd put both in anyways. I'd certainly welcome other creative ways of using extend senses.<br /> <br /> I do think that changing the reference frame for senses should be available somewhere in Correspondence. The three potential points I see are Extend Senses, Co-Locality Perceptions (with some clever use of parallax), and Alter Size. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T15:52:47-07:00","id":1549755,"title":"","content":"Now i wonder what would it take to thanos someone. Cut them like onions, keep them still alive in this state and make it that gravity works on the separated parts so limbs fell of to the ground and cant be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T08:23:54-07:00","id":1549776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549755#post1549755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now i wonder what would it take to thanos someone. Cut them like onions, keep them still alive in this state and make it that gravity works on the separated parts so limbs fell of to the ground and cant be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 5 can do that, as it allows separation of position that doesn't separate the pattern. You'd likely need supporting spheres for the exact effect you describe, but the main part of it is Corr 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T08:38:58-07:00","id":1549777,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the entry that really cemented the value of this analysis, because Correspondence 3 has one of those lines that looked like a complete contradiction but in an effort to resolve it, I found an interpretation that not only made the line make sense, but was consistent with strange powers other parts of M20 gave this rank.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 3 </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Pierce Space/ Open or Close Gates/Co-locality Perceptions </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the mage can tear holes in space, large enough for her to step through. These minor gates are small and temporary, but they allow that character to step from one place to another, so long as she\u2019s alone and lightly encumbered. (Teleporting large items, or while carrying heavy loads, demands Correspondence 4.) Scoping out the new location is a good idea, of course. A close, familiar destination requires fewer successes than a distant, unfamiliar one.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using the Co-locality Perceptions Effect, the mage can also perceive several places at once. Those locations all appear as ghosts overlapping each other, as if they\u2019d been layered on top of the closest location.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 3 gves:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Limited Teleportation (Pierce Space or Open Gates)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Allows a mage to teleport himself (or others) along with any small items. Larger items explicitly have to wait until Corr 4. These holes or gates also only last long enough for one person or thing to pass through, so gates of significant duration are also not possible at this level. While the first paragraph makes it seem like this is limited to self transportation, the last paragraph makes it clear other things can be teleported.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Acme Brand Anvils</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Animaniacs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u201cAnd from this bag I can pull out most anything imaginable, like office desks or lava lamps or Burt, who is a cannibal.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animation is famous for characters pulling objects from seemingly nowhere. A mage can do this too. Smaller items would easily fall under Correspondence 2, but large anvils, office desks, and people would use Correspondence 3. If the effect includes physically pulling the object out of nowhere, as animation often implies, the mage will need spheres to augment or replace his strength for heavier targets.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Co-locality Perceptions (Co-locality Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perceive multiple places at once. It is not mentioned in this section, but handling multiple points of view at once is difficult without the addition of Mind. At least, I think that's the reason for why existing in multiple places (Corr 4) benefits from Mind 1. Possibly there is another explanation.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Infinite Zoom</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Similarly to what I said in earlier ranks, it is possible that the scale of perceptions of one location can be different than another. Overlaying local space with the image of something much larger would provide a helpful reference for making models or diagrams. Hollywood sometimes has computer geniuses solve puzzles by mapping an item and overlaying an image of it on some other part of reality, and this is one way that could work.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note that even if you reject the idea that one viewpoint can be a different scale than another, much of this effect is still possible through clever use of perspective and parallax.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now I need to cover this last paragraph separately.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Physical Contact</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now in previous threads I pretty much disregarded this as bad editing, because outside of teleportation this seems like a list of spells cast at a distance, which Corr 2 can already do. However, when looking for a reasonable interpretation I realized that \u201cwithout physical contact\u201d is key, because as far as I can tell Correspondence 2 can\u2019t do that. So, if that is a property of Correspondence 3 and not of the supporting Pattern Spheres, we get:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulate Position (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corr 2 was limited to things a mage could do with touch, that is, he could physically manipulate the object with Corr 2 extending his range. With Corr 3 the mage is directly altering the target\u2019s position without touching it. This opens up pure Correspondence effects to include things the mage couldn\u2019t do with his own strength. It also implies that levitation and flight are things that Correspondence can do by manipulating distance/position, which is something that previous editions and the Common Magical Effects chart have suggested.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As per Base Correspondence rules, Pattern Spheres aren\u2019t needed for Correspondence to manipulate full patterns. Unlike with Corr 2, though, these could be optional but highly recommended locking spheres.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other possible meanings could be:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Corr 2 meant to limit all its range extensions, both physical and spell casting, to house cat size or smaller and going above that requires Corr 3. I can\u2019t recommend this meaning as there\u2019s no indication of a size limit for casting at a distance, most spells don\u2019t have a size, and the spells indicated aren\u2019t obviously above said size limit. This version would arbitrarily curtail many uses of Corr 2, while not actually providing balance as many powerful spells have quite small effects.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 - This was supposed to be Corr 2\u2019s cast at a distance section accidentally placed in Corr 3. This means this paragraph is mostly meaningless and we have to discard it and that defeats the point of the thread.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Missing Powers:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Collapse Gates (Close Gates)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Open <i>or Close Gates</i> was listed as a power of Corr 3, but there\u2019s no indication of what Close Gate would mean. Creating lasting gates is a power of Corr 4, but this power should enable a mage to close one already made. This could be used to close (but not destroy) one opened by Corr 4 or block the Limited Teleportation of Corr 3.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Open or Close Existing Gate (Open and Close Gates)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gates aren\u2019t always open. Just because a mage or other powerful being decided to make a portal to some other place doesn\u2019t mean it can always be used. Some are only open at certain times or places, some are always closed unless they are needed. This power would let a mage bypass the normal rules of these gates and open them directly. It would also let a mage close (not end) a permanent gate that is normally open.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This shouldn\u2019t be limited to gates created by awakened magic. Other ways like Trods or Moon Bridges should be in the realm of possibility, though as they aren\u2019t purely spatial they may reasonably need other spheres too.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Knock</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another suspect application. Because of the lack of description, some STs could go so far as letting this work on physical doors or passages. I wouldn\u2019t, but if yours does this is a powerful ability.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tether/Forge Connection/Chain (???) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Somewhere along the line Correspondence should have the ability to forge, strengthen, or weaken connections between things. Revised called it Chain and put it under Corr 3. HDYDT has a related concept, Tether, but is specifically about making something always count as within immediate perceptions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m placing the ability here because of this line:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scoping out the new location is a good idea, of course. A close, familiar destination requires fewer successes than a distant, unfamiliar one. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That is just barely related to decreasing difficulty by increasing connection. I freely admit that\u2019s an incredibly tenuous connection but it is the closest thing anywhere in Correspondence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wherever you put this power, it is an important power for this sphere and has a profound impact on how mages use Correspondence. I welcome any arguments for another rank for this ability.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T07:47:46-07:00","id":1549813,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Rend Space/ Ward/ Co-locate Self </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Creating larger holes in space, the mage can now open permanent gates between locations (10 or more successes); isolate forces, spaces, objects, or people into their own tiny realms (by combining Correspondence 4 with Forces, Life, Mind, or Matter); and ward certain locations against specific Patterns (again, combining Forces, Life, Mind, or Matter with Correspondence) or Resonance energies (combining this Sphere with Prime 4). This warding effect can impede or even block the forbidden elements from crossing into, or out of, the protected space. (For extensive details about wards, see the sourcebook How Do You DO That?)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using the Co-location Effect, that mage can also appear in several different places at once. To function, however, she must add Mind 1 to that Effect. Each self mirrors the original\u2019s actions unless she also adds Life 2 to that Effect, granting independence to every self.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corr 4 has the following abilities:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lasting Gates (Rend Space)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Correspondence 4 mages can now create gates with duration which can be used by more than one person and can accommodate larger things. Strictly speaking the text only indicates permanent gates, but if Rank 4 can go all the way to permanent gates, it can do less too. There is no given limit on gates or the sizes of objects they can handle.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Speedy Thing Goes In, Speedy Thing Comes Out. </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A portal that opens above itself could create a situation where someone falls forever. Add a vacuum and it can accelerate indefinitely too. Pseudo perpetual motion machines and impromptu rail guns are possible applications. The exit of a portal doesn't have to be in the same direction as the entrance, so once the thing has reached appropriate velocity another portal can place and direct the object anywhere and any direction.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pocket Dimension (Rend Space or Ward)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Mage can isolate things in spaces removed from the rest of reality. Whether this involves creating a pocket dimension and moving a space there or just separating out an existing space from everything it normally connects to is unclear and could probably work either way.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Pattern Spheres</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once again, Correspondence doesn\u2019t need Pattern Spheres to affect whole patterns. That said, one common use of this power would be shunting a location into a pocket dimension, and that could easily involve separating buildings from foundations and other pattern splits. So there are situations that would call for pattern spheres and they come up frequently enough that it is worth pointing that out.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Rabid Weasel, I Choose You!</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The most pop culture application is holding an animal in a pocket dimension. A wise mage will make sure the pocket dimension also contains food and air, or include Life or Time to keep the animal alive or suspended until it is needed. This is another way that supplemental spheres would be useful.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Greater Ward (Ward)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Greater Ward can outright bar things entering (or leaving) a space. No rolls, no difficulty to overcome, just failure. It is a qualitatively more powerful effect than Minor Ward. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction and Ambiguity Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now Corr 4 directly mentions warding against specific patterns and adds additional spheres in that context, but again Correspondence doesn\u2019t need additional spheres to affect full patterns. The resolution I see is that Wards like this are not cast on their subjects. A ward against badgers isn\u2019t cast on all badgers everywhere, instead, it needs to respond to badgers if and when they get close. Corr 4 can ward against badgers on its own, but it can\u2019t ward against <i>only</i> badgers on its own. The extra spheres are used to tailor the scope so that it is more nuanced than \u2018everything\u2019 or \u2018nothing.\u2019</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately, there\u2019s not much guidance on what levels are needed. STs are going to have to figure that out for themselves. I gave my take on that back in Correspondence 2, [Relevant Spheres] 2. YMMV.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Automatic Sorting</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One unconventional use of Wards is as a sorting mechanism. A mage could set a series of wards up in certain ways to separate out one substance/creature/type of person from another.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Co-Locate Self (Co-locate Self)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can actually be in multiple places at once, which is quite useful. Well it\u2019s actually of limited use on its own since he is still limited to the same mind and can only make the same motion in each location. He needs Mind to process multiple locations and Life to act independently in each location. Needing these spheres is not a contradiction as Correspondence has no claim on those abilities.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Possible Contradiction</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On the other hand Life 2 doesn\u2019t have any listed abilities that would allow multiple motions. I\u2019m not sure what ability it is actually using here. Possibly the idea is that since Correspondence is giving the mage multiple bodies, it only takes a small alteration to make those bodies operate independently of each other, but Life 3 is Alter Self.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Alibi</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One use of being in multiple places is a mage can create an alibi for himself. My very next thought was that if one alibi is helpful, imagine what a mage could do with nine. Mwa ha ha ha.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Amusingly, that only seems stupid. While having multiple contradictory alibis might be super suspicious, it is also really difficult for a prosecutor to explain away.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From elsewhere in M20:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Teleport Anything (Rend Space) (from Corr 3)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 3 puts a cap on how large an item (and presumably creature) can be teleported. It states that Corr 4 is needed for larger things. So using the teleport or brief gate of rank 3 for larger things is possible at this rank. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T09:37:05-07:00","id":1549815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Speedy Thing Goes In, Speedy Thing Comes Out. </i></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A portal that opens above itself could create a situation where someone falls forever. Add a vacuum and it can accelerate indefinitely too. Pseudo perpetual motion machines and impromptu rail guns are possible applications. The exit of a portal doesn't have to be in the same direction as the entrance, so once the thing has reached appropriate velocity another portal can place and direct the object anywhere and any direction.</span>\u200b </div> </div> </div>Gravity is not an infinite source of velocity, a falling human for example maxes out after falling about 100m","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T10:09:30-07:00","id":1549816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549813#post1549813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Speedy Thing Goes In, Speedy Thing Comes Out. </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A portal that opens above itself could create a situation where someone falls forever. Add a vacuum and it can accelerate indefinitely too. Pseudo perpetual motion machines and impromptu rail guns are possible applications. The exit of a portal doesn't have to be in the same direction as the entrance, so once the thing has reached appropriate velocity another portal can place and direct the object anywhere and any direction.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Gravity in a vaccum could provide acceleration <b>up to</b> the speed of light (and that is implying relativistic effects due to an object having mass). That is the maximum speed of anything in our universe, anything includes information transmission not only physicial objects. Whether Sphere Magick breaks that limit, that a different thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549815#post1549815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gravity is not an infinite source of velocity, a falling human for example maxes out after falling about 100m</div> </div> </div> </div>You are confusing terminal velocity (due to air resistance) and the actual effects of gravity in a vacuum as per Ramnesis suggestion. In a vacuum gravity WILL accelerate you up to the maximum possible speed (lightspeed for us, with the afforementioned caveat that using magic might actually make it infinite).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T11:02:42-07:00","id":1549817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549816#post1549816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gravity in a vaccum could provide acceleration <b>up to</b> the speed of light (and that is implying relativistic effects due to an object having mass). That is the maximum speed of anything in our universe, anything includes information transmission not only physicial objects. Whether Sphere Magick breaks that limit, that a different thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, I was not considering light speed when I wrote the paragraph. Fortunately 'accelerate indefinitely' still works as a description due to those same relativistic effects. The object can be accelerated forever without ever reaching light speed.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know if sphere magic can get something moving faster than light speed, but this spell can't. The acceleration here is due to conventional gravity, not magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T15:52:34-07:00","id":1549829,"title":"","content":"I feel like the idea that Correspondence deals in whole patterns is getting stretched beyond what the base description of the Sphere really says regarding combining Correspondence with other Spheres. The base write-up says Correspondence alone lets you manipulate things at a distance as if they weren't at a distance, but you're limited by your natural abilities.<br /> <br /> So, as per the way the Sphere is written, you can use Correspondence to access a computer from a distance (esp. one that's not hooked up to a network) with just Correspondence as long as you're just doing things you could do if you were sitting at the computer: typing, turning devices on and off, plugging and unplugging things, etc. If you want to directly scan the digital code of the computer, you still need Forces despite the computer being a whole pattern.<br /> <br /> I think this differentiate addresses a lot of the potential contradictions or at least confusing bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T10:02:15-07:00","id":1549914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549829#post1549829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the idea that Correspondence deals in whole patterns is getting stretched beyond what the base description of the Sphere really says regarding combining Correspondence with other Spheres. The base write-up says Correspondence alone lets you manipulate things at a distance as if they weren't at a distance, but you're limited by your natural abilities.<br /> <br /> So, as per the way the Sphere is written, you can use Correspondence to access a computer from a distance (esp. one that's not hooked up to a network) with just Correspondence as long as you're just doing things you could do if you were sitting at the computer: typing, turning devices on and off, plugging and unplugging things, etc. If you want to directly scan the digital code of the computer, you still need Forces despite the computer being a whole pattern.<br /> <br /> I think this differentiate addresses a lot of the potential contradictions or at least confusing bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is a good illustration of the mechanics of range extension. Anything a mage would need spheres to do if he were in person, he still needs the same spheres to do from a distance. Basically, is he extending the range of his physical actions or the range of his spell.<br /> <br /> What applications of that do you think are getting stretched?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T10:08:53-07:00","id":1549915,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 5</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Spatial Mutation / Co-Location </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Distance and dimensions become child\u2019s play to a mage at this Rank. She can distort space; alter sizes and stretch or compress objects (Matter), bodies (Life), or forces (Forces); connect different Patterns to one another across intervening space; or even superimpose places or objects on top of one another (extremely vulgar).</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combining this Rank with Life 3, the mage may also expand her senses to perceive many different places at once. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I pulled the last sentence out because I have no idea what to do with it. A straight reading of it is that it is a complete duplicate of Corr 3\u2019s Co-Locality Perceptions (and Corr 3 doesn\u2019t need the Life 3 help). I don\u2019t think it is meant to be about seeing all of the superimposed locations mentioned in the previous sentence; if someone needed magic to perceive them the spell probably wouldn\u2019t be \u201cextremely vulgar.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do any of you have ideas?</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rest of Corr 5 is sparse on description. There are multiple abilities, but not much explanation of them:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Distort Space (Spatial Mutation)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Distort space is a very general description. The most direct interpretation is that a Correspondence master can twist and alter space in just about any way. That\u2019s reasonable, Correspondence Mastery should be capable of that, but there\u2019s not much suggestion of what to do with this. Here are some possibilities:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Change the Distance of a Road or Journey</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage could alter space such that a road so that a journey of a thousand miles begins <i>and ends</i> with a single step. Conversely, he could make a short walk down the hall nigh infinitely long. He could also connect two points or paths that are not ordinarily connected, so that a hiking path in New York leads to a trail in Germany, or a closet door in Rio opens into a small shack in Nepal. The mage could also turn space back on itself so that a road or path perpetually loops, or randomize doors so that they never lead to the same place twice.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Non-Linear Space</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage could mess with directions so that up is left and inward is down. It is, in fairness, very difficult to visualize these. The mage could also change reality to use non-euclidian geometry. I\u2019m hard pressed to see an advantage to doing this, but there are computer programs that simulate this kind of thing if you want to see what it is like. More classically, MC Escher and Inception style worlds are possible.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Added: Pluck an Airplane From the Sky (AKA I\u2019m Crushing Your Head Redux) (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level a mage really can act as if forced perspective were real and grab an airplane from the sky or crush someone\u2019s head as if it could fit between thumb and forefinger. Since earlier levels of Correspondence already allow position to be manipulated, the airplane trick might not even need other spheres, though the head crush would. Correspondence cannot directly attack by itself.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If this ends up with the mage holding a toy sized plane in his hands, it also involves Alter Size aspect of Correspondence 5, below.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Added: Space Warping Shield (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Correspondence 3 could let a mage manipulate the position of a bullet to direct it around him, Correspondence 5 lets him warp space so that bullets and other projectiles pass harmlessly around him. If he wants some things to pass around him and others not, he will likely need to set conditions much like a Ward spell.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Separate Objects and Perceptions</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage could change space so that everything sounds 10x further away than it looks, or everything appears to be 2 feet to the left of where it actually is.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Two Separate Effects</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because of the formatting here, it looks like Alter Size and Stretch/Compress are two different effects. Not only that, but it looks like the pattern sphere requirements are only applied to stretching and compressing things, but not to altering sizes. Those are the issues I am trying to cover.<br /> <br /> The resolution I see is that while these are quite similar powers in that both reshape space, they are different in how they treat the things occupying that space. If it appears from the outside that gross changes must be happening, but on the inside of the effect the patterns are unaltered it is Alter Size. If someone on the inside would feel themselves warping or otherwise impacted, it is Stretch or Compress Patterns. Both of these effects are things Correspondence 5 should be able to do, after all, though the latter would need help.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter Size (Spatial Mutation)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This one is a little more straightforward. The mage can alter the size of something by altering the space that it occupies. This would be something akin to the shrinking in Fantastic Voyage or Ant Man, or Honey, I Shrunk the Kids. This would also work for creating spaces that are bigger on the inside.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stretch or Compress Patterns (Spatial Mutation)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like with Alter Size, the mage can change the space a pattern is occupying, but this time in a way that changes the pattern itself. Because the pattern is altered by this, this ability would require pattern spheres. Examples of this include compressing the space so that there is no room for the pattern in question, or stretching it in a way that stretches the actual pattern. The Master\u2019s Tissue Compression Eliminator works this way\u2026 sometimes. I also remember an episode of Voyager where someone was injured by the shifting of space around them, though I can\u2019t remember the episode.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage could also change part of the space the pattern occupies and not the rest.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Connect Patterns Ignoring Distance (Spatial Mutation and/or Co-Location)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Normally connecting two patterns (e.g. installing a bionic implant) requires that they actually be in same place. At Correspondence 5 a mage doesn\u2019t need to concern himself with that triviality. There are many ways this could manifest. A mage could perform a life-saving heart transplant while leaving the heart and the recipient 1000 miles from each other. He could connect one side of a door to another door on the other side of the earth (another way of doing the previously mentioned door trick). He could potentially merge multiple people into one while leaving their bodies apparently intact.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note that Correspondence doesn\u2019t have pattern altering abilities, so actually fusing two patterns still requires the appropriate spheres. This just gets rid of the requirement they be in the same place.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Disembodied Teleportation AKA Teleport the Head Off an Elephant</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because two parts of a pattern no longer need to be in the same place to be the same pattern, a Correspondence 5 mage no longer needs Life to teleport someone\u2019s head without teleporting the rest of him. Unlike the Corr 3/Life 3 version, this doesn\u2019t kill or even injure the target as their pattern is still whole, it is just in two different places.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Superimpose Places (Co-Location)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One of the great extremes of Corr 5, anything can be made to occupy the same space as anything else. It is quite difficult to conceptualize how this would actually work, which I suspect is one reason it is described as highly vulgar. I can think of several, but they are neither exclusive or exhaustive</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Everything All At Once</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The simplest I can see is that anyone in the effect interacts with every location at once. From their point of view every location would appear to be fused into one, even if that technically wasn\u2019t true. If one location had a wall at one point and another had a passageway, the wall would still block a travellers way.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>A Change in Perspective</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here each location exists slightly out of phase. People inside can see them, but only interact with one or some of them at a time. They may be able to change which ones they interact with by changing perspective or taking specific actions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Added: This is a good explanation for defensive effects which make the mage seem intangible. He can be seen but attacks don\u2019t interact with him. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Added: A Step Diagon-ally (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can take a space and place it within another space but keep the two from interacting except at specific access points. This allows for the classic hidden pockets of reality: buildings hidden in the gap between other buildings, farms hidden in closets, entire train platforms hidden within a pillar, etc. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage could also take a pocket dimension and give it specific entrances which overlap with the world at specific points, creating something bigger on the inside (the TARDIS).</span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If you give me more suggestions I'll add them to this list.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Co-Locate Anything (Co-Location)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The reverse is also true, a mage can make a single object or place exist in multiple locations at once. He could already do this for himself at Corr 4, now he can do it for anything.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Corr 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. The existence of Archspheres could change this, but they aren\u2019t listed in M20. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-08-2025, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T05:31:32-07:00","id":1549937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage could mess with directions so that up is left and inward is down. It is, in fairness, very difficult to visualize these. The mage could also change reality to use non-euclidian geometry. I\u2019m hard pressed to see an advantage to doing this, but there are computer programs that simulate this kind of thing if you want to see what it is like. More classically, MC Escher and Inception style worlds are possible.</span> </div> </div> </div>I think this is about things like grabbing an airplane like someone would grab a toy airplane (still needed str to pull it off). Also going through keyholes, making projectiles rotate around to avoid you and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T06:30:32-07:00","id":1549939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Superimpose Places (Co-Location)</b><br /> <br /> One of the great extremes of Corr 5, anything can be made to occupy the same space as anything else. It is quite difficult to conceptualize how this would actually work, which I suspect is one reason it is described as highly vulgar. I can think of several, but they are neither exclusive or exhaustive </div> </div> </div>This could be used to make something that's bigger on the inside, since I don't think at this level you're limited by the &quot;anything&quot; having the same size as the &quot;anything else&quot;.<br /> <br /> Combined with &quot;A Change in Perspective&quot; you could have stuff like Harry Potter's Diagon Alley (a small comercial district hidden inside an alley, can only be interacted with after entering. Well, at leasst that's how I figure it works :P) <br /> <hr /><br /> Also this seems to be the magick behind Wards that make you seem intangible (rather than repelling the object the Ward protects against, it simply can't interact with the warded object)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T07:11:14-07:00","id":1549941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549937#post1549937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is about things like grabbing an airplane like someone would grab a toy airplane (still needed str to pull it off). Also going through keyholes, making projectiles rotate around to avoid you and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549939#post1549939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This could be used to make something that's bigger on the inside, since I don't think at this level you're limited by the &quot;anything&quot; having the same size as the &quot;anything else&quot;.<br /> <br /> Combined with &quot;A Change in Perspective&quot; you could have stuff like Harry Potter's Diagon Alley (a small comercial district hidden inside an alley, can only be interacted with after entering. Well, at leasst that's how I figure it works :P) <hr /><br /> Also this seems to be the magick behind Wards that make you seem intangible (rather than repelling the object the Ward protects against, it simply can't interact with the warded object)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I'll add these in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T09:40:17-07:00","id":1549946,"title":"","content":"On to Entropy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Entropy</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview</b>: Chance, Mortality, Fate, Flaws, the Low Umbra, Corruption. Fate and Chance are usually presented as two views of the same thing.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One main rule is listed here, Entropy can\u2019t be used to inflict direct damage until Rank 4, at which point it jumps straight to Aggravated. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T09:44:56-07:00","id":1549947,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Sense Flaws, Fate &amp; Fortune / Ring of Truth </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Basic Entropic understanding allows a mage to see the currents of probability, spot flaws in Patterns, and note the subtle yet telling details in a person\u2019s speech and behavior that suggest whether or not she\u2019s telling what she believes to be the truth. Although he cannot yet control such phenomena, the mage can predict dice throws, card draws, and other apparently random events; spot weak spots in objects, people, or arguments; and use those imperfect yet profound insights to his advantage</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy is considerably clearer in description and it is fairly easy. We are given three basic abilities at the start: Sense Flaws, Sense Fate and Fortune, and Ring of Truth. It is possible Sense Fate and Sense Fortune are two different things, but there isn\u2019t a clear distinction.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 1 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See Probabilities (Sense Fate and Fortune)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See the currents of probability is somewhat vague but at the very least that should give the mage the ability to know likely outcomes of random situations. Knowing the exact outcome of random events is listed as a possibility.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s no detail on how specific the information is or what counts as a random event, so this power could range from mildly useful to almost game-breaking depending on ST call. For my own part, I would limit knowing the exact outcome to purely random systems and have the information gleaned get more vague as the situation gets more open ended.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Predict Results</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can predict the outcome of games of chance and other purely random systems. This could also be used to guess random numbers or pixels in television static. In the event of a particularly unhinged mad scientist the mage could even know if the cat will be alive or dead.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Minor Prophecy </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prophecy is more of a time thing, and even that is uncertain. Nevertheless, where the outcome is in question the mage can see the currents of fate (or likely outcomes) and act accordingly.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Never Tell Me the Odds</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage should be able to quickly determine the exact likelihood of a random event, such as the odds of getting a royal flush. Added: This would also include knowing how random a system is, knowing if there is a disparity between expected odds and actual odds, and if something unknown is affecting the odds. (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unconventional Uses:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Detect Cheating</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because a mage can predict likely outcomes of random situations, he can also detect when the outcome wasn\u2019t actually random. Even without knowing what was supposed to happen, he should be able to tell that it didn\u2019t. Other aspects of Entropy 1 may even be able to add who had their fingers on the scale and how.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Flaws (Sense Flaws)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the initial description is limited to sensing flaws in patterns, the examples make it clear that this is a considerably more far-reaching power that can spot flaws in anything be it physical (like objects and people) or abstract (like arguments). A clever mage could use this in surprising ways, like figuring out exploits in the wording of a ward or curse, or the rules of a bureaucracy.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution (Sort of):</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The biggest weakness of this ability is how often the book forgets to have it have an effect. Finding a weak point or a way in is often a good course of action so Ent 1 gets added to a lot of examples, but those examples frequently forget to add any benefit for incorporating the Sphere.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Fine Print, CliffsNotes Edition</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can quickly scan the EULA and figure out what is relevant to him, what is not, what is a trap, and what is a flaw he can use.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Always Prepared at the DMV</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can navigate a bureaucracy with inhuman efficiency. He can easily find what forms he needs and who he needs to speak with, and is rarely if ever caught out by needing a previously unknown form.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is quite likely that the Technocracy constantly uses this on their own processes, giving them a skewed perspective of the efficiency of Bureacracy.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Detect Lies (Sense Flaws)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A peculiar application of Entropy, this power specifically detects whether the target believes they are lying and specifically relies on observation. This can be quite powerful but it is more effective at detecting attempts to deceive than actual truth or falsehood.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are some decisions STs will have to make for this one that will determine how powerful it is. The example specifies a lying human, but does this power also work on animals? On robots? Does it work on writings?</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing Abilities:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Detect Entropy Manipulation (Sense Fate and Fortune)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most spheres can detect the use of that sphere by other mages anyways, so this doesn\u2019t take much justification. That said, if Entropy can sense probabilities or fate, it should be able to sense when those are manipulated. It should be able to tell if someone is blessed or cursed through detecting fate, flaws, or both.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-09-2025, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T12:52:24-07:00","id":1549954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549946#post1549946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One main rule is listed here, Entropy can\u2019t be used to inflict direct damage until Rank 4, at which point it jumps straight to Aggravated. </span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is not true in practice. You can do damage with lower entropy, just not decay damage. Examples:<br /> <br /> - making an enemy slip of a roof by damagin a roof tile the enemy is standing on (entropy 2)<br /> - Making breaks fail when some one tries to stop a car before hitting your enemy (entropy 2)<br /> - Making a airplane fragment rip of and target the place where the enemy is while the visible plane is above (entropy 3)<br /> - Making that the pipe you hit is filled with hot steam and erupts at the enemy (entropy 2-3)<br /> - Making is so a car explodes after shooting the gas tank (entropy 2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T13:51:11-07:00","id":1549955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549954#post1549954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not true in practice. You can do damage with lower entropy, just not decay damage. Examples:<br /> <br /> - making an enemy slip of a roof by damagin a roof tile the enemy is standing on (entropy 2)<br /> - Making breaks fail when some one tries to stop a car before hitting your enemy (entropy 2)<br /> - Making a airplane fragment rip of and target the place where the enemy is while the visible plane is above (entropy 3)<br /> - Making that the pipe you hit is filled with hot steam and erupts at the enemy (entropy 2-3)<br /> - Making is so a car explodes after shooting the gas tank (entropy 2)</div> </div> </div> </div>But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> clearly stated <b>direct </b>damage in the very same text you are quoting, all of those are indirect.<br /> <br /> Are we reading the same text by Ramnesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T14:00:28-07:00","id":1549957,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to make it clear that you can in fact do damage with entropy 2 and 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T04:35:57-07:00","id":1549961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549947#post1549947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my own part, I would limit knowing the exact outcome to purely random systems and have the information gleaned get more vague as the situation gets more open ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would personally avoid the label &quot;purely&quot; random. Whether or not truly random events are even possible is a philosophic matter, and the vast majority of random number generators used by humans are pseudo-random either by imperfections in a system (no dice are made 100% perfectly and then roll with perfect technique on a 100% perfectly constructed surface), or by design limitations (computers aren't actually capable of generating truly random numbers on their own, and either use a pure algorithm that approximates randomness, or uses a sensor that can detect a suitably random external event; in high end computation usually both). Something that's probably more important than nitpicking over pure vs. approximately pure randomness, is the ability to sense odds shifting. Texas Hold Em poker is very popular because the odds shift as play proceeds. Knowing your starting odds is great, but knowing if your odds shift as other players fold is even stronger.<br /> <br /> Which also leads to an implied power here: the ability to detect how random a system is; which is sorta combining sense fate/fortune and sense weakness at the same time as a lack of randomness would be seen as a weakness in a RNG. Given the Syndicate's presence in the world of gambling, they'd likely have monitoring of large systems like lotteries or online betting for anomalies before they would be detectable by normal statistical quality checks. This isn't necessarily the same as detecting cheating though, as most games of chance are weighted so the house wins more than they lose. For mages trying to juice their odds of a payday, thigh would be more like scanning which slot machines have been set to be &quot;looser&quot; than the rest; something casinos do to increase the perception of having a chance at a big pay day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549957#post1549957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to make it clear that you can in fact do damage with entropy 2 and 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, none of this are actually doing damage with Entropy. They are, generally, just increasing the odds that an existing chance of danger is increased. If the person you're trying to send tumbling off a roof makes a successful check to keep their balance after stepping on a bad roofing tile... then they don't take any damage because they don't fall. And it's not like you can force someone on to a roof in the first place.<br /> <br /> We can wait for Ramnesis to get to Entropy 2 and 3 to discuss how much any of your examples really hold up to the text, but even if we entertain that they might be possible in extremely specific circumstances, the number of successes some of them would need makes it pointless to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T05:33:09-07:00","id":1549962,"title":"","content":"Dont really see why any of my examples would require more than 3 successes but ok.<br /> As for chances of danger that can be avoided its practically the same as dodging a magic projectile.<br /> The thing is those are legit metods to do damage with entropy spells (yes its not direct damage but in practice it is a damage possible by casting a spell).<br /> As for the need for the contidions to be met those were just some examples from the top of my head. There is almost always something you can do with entropy 2-3 to cause damage unless we are talking about a white room situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T09:12:10-07:00","id":1549964,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 2</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Control Probability </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the mage can control the factors he could only sense before. Pulling the strings of apparently random events, he can influence activities and results \u2013 directing the fall of dice or cards, repeatedly hitting weak spots, and directing people and things toward a conclusion of his choice. Of course, it\u2019s easier to control small events (the winner of a horse race) than large ones (causing a six-car pileup). In game terms, large alterations demand more successes than small ones do.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 2 really has one ability, but it is used in several ways. </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initially I separated directing the fall of dice and influencing activities and results. Intuitively it seems like the former is controlling the full events and the latter only bringing about a specific outcome. Functionally, though, they are used the same way and the main difference is scale. I can split these back apart, though, if you all think it is worth it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Influence People and Things (Control Probability)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can influence the results of random and/or chaotic systems. How this happens isn\u2019t quite explained, though it does involve pulling the strings of apparently random events. Given the examples, it appears the mage is stacking up the results of one or more events to bring about a specific result.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intuitively, this power tends towards focus on results rather than on process. Partly this is because most of Entropy\u2019s direct effects unlock with higher ranks, but also because this seems to work in situations with more factors than the mage could reasonably process.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I should point out that repeated use of this power is the poster child for the Domino Effect.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Side note: The wording here is interesting because \u2018conclusion\u2019 could mean an outcome or it could mean a judgement. Given the examples of horse races and car accidents, outcome is clearly an intended meaning. Influencing judgements is a trickier matter. Directly affecting thoughts is an Entropy 5 power, but affecting quick judgement calls, emotional responses, and instinctive reactions may be an intended meaning as well. That\u2019s an ST call.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>How to Win at Everything</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can repeatedly make things play out in his favor. He can win at gambling, carnival games, and at the cash register (hey, they gave me an extra $20, what luck*). Since even games of skill still have the potential for distraction and random chance, this should at least influence them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">*For him. Not so much for them when the till doesn\u2019t add up.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Look! A Convenient Distraction!</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can engineer events to provide a convenient event such as a distraction or a jammed door. The classic Hollywood example is making someone drop their groceries, which lets the mage slip by or start a conversation, depending on his intentions.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Penultimate Destination</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also manipulate trends and events towards damaging outcomes for a target. The car crash above was a clear example. On the flip side, a mage can manipulate events towards the miraculous and make situations that should have led to tragedy for himself or others instead be near misses.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Repeatedly Hit Weak Points (Control Probability)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is an interesting power because like the others it is listed as an extension of manipulating apparently random events. On its own, it appears to be a way of exploiting weak points. Now in theory that is a step up from finding those weak points with Entropy 1, but mechanically these two are often used the same way. (See Thunder Punch).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the context of manipulating probability, though, this gets a little bit more powerful and allows a mage to direct events towards flaws in a repeated fashion. Not only does this mean he can make the same rare event happen multiple times (the guy who keeps stepping on rakes) but he can also make multiple events land in the same place.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Why Is It Always the Eye!?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By manipulating events a mage can share the exploitation of a weak point with other people, even those who do not know about it. General attacks will tend towards those weak points without any conscious direction.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>It Keeps Happening</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can direct seemingly random events to repeatedly cause the same problems, whether that be physical strikes against an existing wound or mental reminders of past trauma.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a particularly dark example, a mage could probably make someone encounter repeated triggers for their PTSD. I should point out that may be extremely uncomfortable at the gaming table, so check with your fellow players first.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T09:32:43-07:00","id":1549965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549954#post1549954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not true in practice. You can do damage with lower entropy, just not decay damage. Examples:<br /> <br /> - making an enemy slip of a roof by damagin a roof tile the enemy is standing on (entropy 2)<br /> - Making breaks fail when some one tries to stop a car before hitting your enemy (entropy 2)<br /> - Making a airplane fragment rip of and target the place where the enemy is while the visible plane is above (entropy 3)<br /> - Making that the pipe you hit is filled with hot steam and erupts at the enemy (entropy 2-3)<br /> - Making is so a car explodes after shooting the gas tank (entropy 2)</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those are Entropy 3 because they rely on specific failures in materials or mechanics. The steam pipe arguably isn't even Entropy as it either has steam or it doesn't. Whether it breaks or not, could be Entropy 2, though. It is admittedly not always easy to see the line between directing events and decaying an object, but your focus on the specific method and materials pushes towards rank 3.<br /> <br /> More obviously Entropy 2 effects would come from directing an random or complex situation towards a reasonable, if unlikely, result. They would be more like:<br /> <br /> - Making an enemy stumble near the edge of a roof due to an inopportune wind gust or bird or any of a number of random factors.<br /> <br /> - Distracting someone with spilled coffee or windblown paper when they need to be pressing the brakes.<br /> <br /> - Having a swaying pile of crates fall over at an inconvenient time.<br /> <br /> I don't want to pigeonhole Entropy 2 into only working when the game world is undefined, but it is easiest to see opportunities for it when that is the case.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll add that as a system hack I'm not against treating some Entropy effects as attacks in order to use the rolled damage as a framework to narrate out the effects. That's explicitly an idea for a house rule, though. Also, as Entropy 2 specifically says that larger events take more successes, some of the successes would have to be spent there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T10:21:21-07:00","id":1549968,"title":"","content":"Yeah Entropy as writen is not easy to understand. Thats why i always simplified it to:<br /> 2 - Can decide the outcome of an ongoing process if the outcome is probable.<br /> 3 - like 2 but can create the process itself (cant affect will or living creatures yet)<br /> 4 - can affect living creatures<br /> <br /> In HDYDT p.133 we have:<br /> &quot;Up until Rank 4, the Entropy Sphere does not inflict<br /> damage. It can, however, lead to hazardous coincidences: a<br /> speeding car, a weakened floorboard, a falling candle, and so<br /> forth. Again, the circumstances must be present in order for them to<br /> be manipulated this way \u2013 a falling candle won\u2019t fall and start a<br /> fire if there hadn\u2019t been a candle there in the first place.<br /> Once again, the nature of the hazard and the damage<br /> it inflicts remain under the control of the Storyteller unless<br /> the player wants to invoke vulgar magick. Leading an enemy<br /> into speeding traffic so that he might get hit by a car involves<br /> the powers of coincidence, but yanking a car out of its way so<br /> that this particular car WILL hit the enemy is vulgar magick.<br /> And again, a very likely hazard (like a speeding car on a street)<br /> requires fewer successes than a very unlikely one (a lump of<br /> frozen poop falling from an airplane).&quot;<br /> <br /> Ill admint here that i see entropy as more modular fate. If consensus governs reality then so can probability. If its probable that the pipe can have hot steam inside we can make it a fact with entropy (though that is probably outside the scope of the sphere as writen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-09-2025, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T12:35:11-07:00","id":1549973,"title":"","content":"Entropy is by far the most overrated sphere due to people not understanding that <i>it works with things already present</i> and <i>must be something that actually stands a chance of happening</i>. <br /> <br /> You can't summon the taxi if there is no taxi around. So, you are constantly on the hands of the ST, much more than with other spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T13:29:42-07:00","id":1549975,"title":"","content":"Well, until you're at Entropy 4 and 5 anyway... the lines of &quot;already present&quot; and &quot;stands a chance of happening&quot; do justifiably get blurred as the Sphere goes up in mastery.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you can't shoot a car's gas tank and cause it to explode with Entropy. That's not how bullets or gasoline work. There is a zero percent chance of this happening. Under the most generous of conditions, using a highly compromised gas tank and incendiary bullets, you could cause the gas to start to burn - which is bad for someone in the vehicle, esp. if something more dangerous when exposed to flames is also present - but that's about it. Your ST might let you get away with a car tank exploding via applications of different magic as being coincidental because it's a common enough misconception even if it's been publicly debunked dozens of times, but that's not the same as tweaking probability so that something unlikely happens. Even if you use higher level magic to fate someone to die in an explosion while in a car, you're not dooming them to a car's gas tank exploding just from a stray bullet hitting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T14:29:34-07:00","id":1549979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549975#post1549975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, until you're at Entropy 4 and 5 anyway... the lines of &quot;already present&quot; and &quot;stands a chance of happening&quot; do justifiably get blurred as the Sphere goes up in mastery.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you can't shoot a car's gas tank and cause it to explode with Entropy. That's not how bullets or gasoline work. There is a zero percent chance of this happening. Under the most generous of conditions, using a highly compromised gas tank and incendiary bullets, you could cause the gas to start to burn - which is bad for someone in the vehicle, esp. if something more dangerous when exposed to flames is also present - but that's about it. Your ST might let you get away with a car tank exploding via applications of different magic as being coincidental because it's a common enough misconception even if it's been publicly debunked dozens of times, but that's not the same as tweaking probability so that something unlikely happens. Even if you use higher level magic to fate someone to die in an explosion while in a car, you're not dooming them to a car's gas tank exploding just from a stray bullet hitting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you and the Hypernarrative Influence Rote does not. Well strictly speaking it doesn't specify the gas tank exploding, but barring the presence of explosives there aren't any reasonable situations where a car would explode. Indeed, since the rote suggests a cliche of calculating the odds, barring very specific circumstances I'd insist the mage know about the presence of explosives to make that specific effect work.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Hypernarrative Influence isn't giving Entropy 2 new powers, just badly applying the ones it already has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T15:26:16-07:00","id":1549980,"title":"","content":"Hmm in demon the descent there is an embed called cause and effect. It makes successes from one action caunt twoards another effect that takes place imidiate after the action is completed.<br /> For example kicking the computer to hack it. Sounds like something in the realm of Entropy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T15:55:20-07:00","id":1549981,"title":"","content":"But it's not. DtD demons are manipulating the metaphysical Infrastructure of reality that lets them overwrite normal physics with narrative physics. Mages in Ascension don't have something like Infrastructure to take advantage of to justify such effects. Hacking a computer magically requires the Spheres that govern that (which is variable because there's lots of ways to hack something). Kicking the computer is just trying to leverage a a cultural myth to get an effect under the Paradox radar.<br /> <br /> Like most cultural myths, there is some truth in there. There are bits of technology where a smack can <i>temporarily</i> get past a minor fault. Chemical batteries near the end of their lifespan can be manipulated by physical force into a slightly better position to provide what electricity they have left to generate at normal levels instead of weakened ones. A loose contact point can be jostled into place. A fan might not be spinning fast enough because of a bit of debris and dislodging the debris will stop the heat fault detectors from limiting operations. Etc. There's no smacking a computer that will cause a password to randomly fill in, or a password prompt to disappear and allow you access to what's behind it. Software doesn't work like that.<br /> <br /> Mages have to deal with that reality, DtD demons don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T16:56:01-07:00","id":1549983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1549975#post1549975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, until you're at Entropy 4 and 5 anyway... the lines of &quot;already present&quot; and &quot;stands a chance of happening&quot; do justifiably get blurred as the Sphere goes up in mastery.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you can't shoot a car's gas tank and cause it to explode with Entropy. That's not how bullets or gasoline work. There is a zero percent chance of this happening. Under the most generous of conditions, using a highly compromised gas tank and incendiary bullets, you could cause the gas to start to burn - which is bad for someone in the vehicle, esp. if something more dangerous when exposed to flames is also present - but that's about it. Your ST might let you get away with a car tank exploding via applications of different magic as being coincidental because it's a common enough misconception even if it's been publicly debunked dozens of times, but that's not the same as tweaking probability so that something unlikely happens. Even if you use higher level magic to fate someone to die in an explosion while in a car, you're not dooming them to a car's gas tank exploding just from a stray bullet hitting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Exactly that. People think they can pull Entropy and expect the ST to just somehow deal with what you want to happen. You can't explode a car by shooting the tank with entropy (and as you said, it could be a coincident Forces effect). You can't summon a taxi, the ST might just say &quot;Well, there is no taxi around&quot;. You can't (or at least you would need a LOT of successes) make a ATM spew money around. Entropy is about changing probabilities and if you want to make something that has about 0% chance to happen, you're gonna need a Great Work, big ass ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T17:11:24-07:00","id":1549985,"title":"","content":"Of course, it's also one of those things where magic is such a silly choice.<br /> <br /> If you're already shooting bullets... why not just shoot the target instead of trying to combine magic and making a gas tank explode? Guns aren't hard to use in this game (and it's even easier to boost your shooting skills/weapon quality than setting up an explosion).<br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of people trying to go all Death from the Final Destination franchise with Entropy... but it's ultimately such a waste of time when you could just sneak up on someone and kill them like a normal murderhobo. I do get that there are circumstances where you want to do something impractical for character driven reasons. But the Euthanatoi aren't on the seat of Entropy because of the Sphere being great for killing people (and, in fact, they're the ones that are most sensitive to the dangers of using magic to kill instead of using personal combat skill).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T07:19:32-07:00","id":1550000,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Affect Predictable Patterns </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Things eventually break down. At this Rank, the mage can control the speed at which material objects fail or decay. That\u2019s easier to do with complex machines (cars, computers) than it is with simple ones (walls, stones) \u2013 after all, more things can go wrong with complicated things.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this Rank, the mage can also start controlling the fate and fortune of objects and people, giving them good or bad luck by controlling the probability of events around them. Again, large feats demand more successes than smaller ones.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two abilities are given here. Entropy 3 can:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed or Slow Decay (Affect Predictable Patterns)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By direct read this mainly concerns the speed at which things decay, however the examples bring up complex machines which can have sudden and dramatic failures. This would imply that both are within the realm of Entropy 3.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Tune Up/Grit in the Gears</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can tweak an object or machine so that it works for much longer without breaking down. Alternatively he can make it degrade much faster. There are a number of</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Jam Mechanism/Percussive Maintenance</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can trigger sudden failure modes like jamming guns and slipped belts. This could reasonably work in reverse as well with a problem suddenly clearing up. Mechanical problems suddenly clearing up without explanation may sound too unlikely for Entropy, which is why I used the name Percussive Maintenance. The repair abilities of a good thump are well known. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That said, in my troubleshooting experience unexplained improvement not only happens, it happens frequently enough to be irritating. After all, If I you can no longer figure out what the problem was, you can\u2019t prevent it from happening again. I know I am not alone in that experience, so I have no problems with a problem just clearing up. But I digress\u2026</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fortune and Misfortune (Affect Predictable Patterns)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power lets a mage make himself or someone else lucky or unlucky. What counts as good or bad fortune is going to vary. This is a very open-ended power that is highly customizable based on the intent and paradigm of the caster. In addition to that this either relies on Fate to guide it, or it is a spell that can make decisions. Entropy is like that.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Always Lucky</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The target always does better than average on games of chance, or in dangerous situations</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Never Hit a Red</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The target almost never encounters a specific inconvenience or problem. In reverse, this could curse someone to encounter those same problems much more frequently than normally.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Murphy\u2019s Rules Lawyering</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All actions, or all actions of a certain kind, are made at difficulty due to constant random accidents. A mage could curse someone to never be able to get out the door on time, or never get an uninterrupted night's sleep. In the same way, a mage could protect someone from interference with the same kind of random events just unleashed on others.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Recursive Entropy Manipulation</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While mucking about with fate and fortune should be detectable by Entropy 1 abilities, a mage should be able to manipulate his fortune to make it less likely anyone with Entropy 1 is looking. This might seem a little paradoxical, but one way it could work is by creating sudden bursts of good fortune in people other than the mage, thus causing the distraction.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>From Elsewhere in M20:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Destroy Durability (Affect Predictable Patterns) (From Magic vs Objects)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 What Rank?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Magic vs Objects speaks of damage inflicting effects on material objects. These attack the Durability trait of the object. The section does not mention what rank this is possible at, though. The two options are Rank 3, which controls the entropy in material objects, and Rank 4 which is explicitly when Entropy can attack a pattern directly.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">My best take on this is that decaying an object has to be capable of degrading its Durability, so it must be possible at this rank. It may not technically strike the object\u2019s pattern directly but it functions like a damage dealing spell anyways.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Missing Powers?</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed or Slow Decay\u2026 of Energies (Affect Predictable Patterns)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 What Counts as a Predictable Pattern?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now we come to a bigger dilemma that I didn't initially catch until I was looking over Forces: Does Affect Predictable Patterns also include forces and energies? On the one hand, the text clearly specifies material objects. However, the name Affect Predictable Patterns seems to apply to more than just objects. At the very least, it is a better fit for energies than Affect Living Patterns or Affect Thoughts, which are the next two ranks.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, maybe Entropy intentionally can\u2019t affect energy patterns at all. That doesn\u2019t seem likely to me, though.<br /> <br /> Overall, my take is that it should work on forces, but I'd like to hear what you all think.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T07:26:52-07:00","id":1550001,"title":"","content":"Entropy 3 seems enough to make it rain so i would say it can affect forces.<br /> Affecting predictable patterns should not only include making someone lucky or not. It should also include something specifically happening. For example the gun jaming thing could not only be a thing of decay but also a predictable pattern control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T07:44:14-07:00","id":1550002,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, It seems to me that rank 3 only affects objects (Matter) and can't affect living beings (Life) patterns (until rank 4).<br /> <br /> I couldn't find Entropy affecting Forces anywhere. So, i have to say it can't, although personally I would allow at rank 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T07:49:21-07:00","id":1550003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550001#post1550001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entropy 3 seems enough to make it rain so i would say it can affect forces.<br /> Affecting predictable patterns should not only include making someone lucky or not. It should also include something specifically happening. For example the gun jaming thing could not only be a thing of decay but also a predictable pattern control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Entropy can make it rain much less Entropy 3. Weather control requires Forces 4 or 5 and 5+ successes, depending on what you want.<br /> <br /> Entropy is about affecting luck, chaos, decay, etc. Jamming a gun can be specifically made with Entropy, because it is related to decay. Making the gunner trip and drop the gun directly into your hand can't be specifically made. At least not without a Great Work worth of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T09:20:48-07:00","id":1550004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550003#post1550003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Entropy can make it rain much less Entropy 3. Weather control requires Forces 4 or 5 and 5+ successes, depending on what you want.<br /> <br /> Entropy is about affecting luck, chaos, decay, etc. Jamming a gun can be specifically made with Entropy, because it is related to decay. Making the gunner trip and drop the gun directly into your hand can't be specifically made. At least not without a Great Work worth of successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rain may depend on luck. &quot;Maybe im lucky and it will be a sunny day&quot;. Even weather forecasts are somewhat luckbased.<br /> <br /> EDIT: There is currently a Q&amp;A with theonyxpath on reddit. It seems Entropy cannot make it rain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-10-2025, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T09:41:24-07:00","id":1550005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550003#post1550003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Entropy can make it rain much less Entropy 3. Weather control requires Forces 4 or 5 and 5+ successes, depending on what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weather is a chaotic system, though, so it reasonably would fall somewhere under Entropy. Small permutations like gusts of wind and patches of rain could easily be factors that set up the outcome of an Entropy 2 effect, for instance, at least if the day was already windy or rainy. Enhancing or degrading an existing storm or pattern would be at a higher level, possibly 3 since weather is predictable, possibly 4 as many people assume chaotic systems are unpredictable (though apparently that's a pet peeve for some).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T10:14:22-07:00","id":1550006,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Weather control requires Forces 4 or 5.<br /> <br /> Yes, the weather is a chaotic system, &quot;making&quot; a wind in a windy day it's ok. Making it in a sunny day is not. That is not making rain though. Entropy cannot make rain.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a>, again, that is not how Entropy works. You can't &quot;get lucky that X happens&quot; because you would be able to do anythinf with Entropy 2. <br /> <br /> My previous post about things needing to be already present and having a possible chance of happening applies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T10:49:27-07:00","id":1550007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550006#post1550006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Weather control requires Forces 4 or 5.<br /> <br /> Yes, the weather is a chaotic system, &quot;making&quot; a wind in a windy day it's ok. Making it in a sunny day is not. That is not making rain though. Entropy cannot make rain.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Spheres do have overlaps, so it isn't a problem if two spheres can do the same thing. In fact we have a clear example in Entropy 3. Entropy 3 can degrade an object. Matter can do that too. It isn't a contradiction. Life can heal creatures, but that doesn't stop Entropy from doing that too. So the fact that Forces can create and control weather does not mean that Entropy can't also manipulate weather.<br /> <br /> Also note, I chose examples of working with what already existed. Rain on a rainy day, wind on a windy day, and enhancing or degrading existing storms. These are not examples of creating something out of nothing, they are examples of manipulating what is already there. <br /> <br /> I do agree that Entropy cannot make <i>water</i>, indeed Forces can't do that either, but if there is enough water in a weather system that rain is reasonable then Entropy may be able to draw that water out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T11:09:56-07:00","id":1550008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550007#post1550007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spheres do have overlaps, so it isn't a problem if two spheres can do the same thing. In fact we have a clear example in Entropy 3. Entropy 3 can degrade an object. Matter can do that too. It isn't a contradiction. Life can heal creatures, but that doesn't stop Entropy from doing that too. So the fact that Forces can create and control weather does not mean that Entropy can't also manipulate weather.<br /> <br /> Also note, I chose examples of working with what already existed. Rain on a rainy day, wind on a windy day, and enhancing or degrading existing storms. These are not examples of creating something out of nothing, they are examples of manipulating what is already there.<br /> <br /> I do agree that Entropy cannot make <i>water</i>, indeed Forces can't do that either, but if there is enough water in a weather system that rain is reasonable then Entropy may be able to draw that water out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely you can do stuff with different combinations of spheres, I am aware. However, Entropy has never been described to change weather afaik, so I'm not sure it should just because &quot;it's a complex system&quot;. Iirc a chaotic system is a system where the outcome vary a lot with small variations of input. A lot of things work like that, including the human body. Can Entropy change moods and biological things like Life 3 as well? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Also, the comentary about my previous post was to quelsec","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T11:49:47-07:00","id":1550010,"title":"","content":"So, for me, the problem with Forces Patterns and what level of Entropy effects them is that IRL we don't really know how predictable these things are. Physics is full of things that act extremely predictably... until they don't. Part of it is that in reality, it's nearly impossible to find a &quot;pure&quot; energetic &quot;thing.&quot; Energy is always acting within a system. Particle wave duality means even the purest forms of energy sometimes get stuck bouncing around like particles instead.<br /> <br /> A classic (and recently culturally relevant) example is the three body problem. Even with Einstein literally rewriting the scientific consensus on mechanics from Newton's classical version, he didn't end up getting to a solution to this conundrum. We can accurately predict the relationship of the sun and the Earth, as well as the Earth and the Moon... but if we put all three together it becomes mathematical chaos. <br /> <br /> While normally it's a good idea to separate real world science and Mage when figuring out what level of Sphere to use, in this case I think it can help a lot. It's not hard to draw a line between when Forces falls under Entropy 3 as a Predictable Pattern and when you need higher level Entropy because you're dealing with an unpredictable Pattern: does classical mechanics have an easy to apply model to the system at hand. If yes, it's a generally predictable Pattern (even if within some assumed things like &quot;on Earth&quot;), if no, then it's probably too chaotic for Entropy 3.<br /> <br /> The energy of falling while a small object is under the sway of an overwhelming gravity well (aka the stuff around us subject to the gravitational pull of our planet) is easily predictable. Even Einstein's theories of relativity reduce down to Newton's laws of gravity under those circumstances. Bump things up to orbital relationships and we get into the nth-body problems and predictability goes out the window. Meteorology is similarly full of relatively simply predictive models and highly variable models. There's stuff we can predict with relative ease, and stuff that's always more guessing than not. We know pretty exactly what conditions generate tornadoes.... but we have zero idea how to predict where individual funnels will form, and if a given tornado system will result in lots of smaller funnels or less bigger ones (or whatever combination).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T14:11:36-07:00","id":1550012,"title":"","content":"To my mind there are two possible dividing lines between Predictable Patterns and those of higher Entropy ranks.<br /> <br /> The first as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> says, focuses on the practically predictable. Predictable Patterns are just that - things we can reliably describe and predict. If the system is unpredictable, or if it is functionally too complex, too reactive, or too difficult to calculate in any reasonable time frame, it goes in a higher rank.<br /> <br /> The second is more of a philosophical or theoretical distinction. Predictable patterns are those that, no matter how complex, are unwilled and mechanistic or probablistic. We may not be able to predict them easily, but we assume that with enough time and information and research we could. Higher ranks are for things that defy prediction. Things with wills, desires, identities. Most notably this includes life, which is why rank 4 is Affect Living Patterns. Of course this assumes that life is not deterministic, which some people will object to, but I think it works for the purposes of an RPG.<br /> <br /> I suppose there is a third option. Anything that either of the previous two would put in rank 4 or 5 goes in rank 4 or 5. So everything that is willed, responsive, or personal goes in Rank 4+, as does anything overly chaotic and anything with emergent behavior. Only those systems that are unwilled and coherently described go in rank 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure which of those, if any, Mage intended, but I do have two indications from M20, both from the Spheres writeups. Unfortunately they aren't the best sources. They do associate Entropy with forces and weather, but they don't do so clearly.<br /> <br /> Regarding Entropy and energy:<br /> <br /> Forces 3 gives the possibility of Forces 3/Entropy 3 to erode or enhance energies. This is the entry that made me realize Entropy never explicitly mentions energies at any rank.<br /> Now this is a rough entry to go through. For a start, it seems to be the wrong rank of Forces. Most interpretations of enhance or erode energies are possible at Forces 2+. Also, while it does indicate that Entropy 3 is the rank for affecting forces, it isn't clear how much Entropy is doing. The two main possibilities are:<br /> <br /> 1) This is one of those cases where M20 pairs two spheres that can accomplish the task on their own. Either Forces 2+ or Entropy 3 could accomplish the job.<br /> <br /> 2) While Entropy 3 can work on matter without help and Entropy 4 can work on Life without help, Entropy 3 can only affect energies with the addition of Forces. That's really janky, but it is a possibility.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Entropy and weather:<br /> <br /> Time 4 gives the ability to capture things in bubbles of time, and gives an example of using Time, Forces, and Entropy to capture a tornado. Again, we are blurring the lines between Forces and Entropy, so we face the same two options as above. Also, while we get some evidence weather and Entropy are connected, we don't get any indication of what rank is involved.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T15:16:52-07:00","id":1550013,"title":"","content":"My approach to those options is largely based on game-play considerations. While the developers might have a different opinion on things, I assume that the present paradigms in M20 are supposed to be equally coherent to the setting. Since we have example paradigms that hold that the world is deterministic, and ones that hold the world is not, option 2 would prejudice the game towards deterministic paradigms.<br /> <br /> In a deterministic paradigm all systems are predictable with enough knowledge. There is no random. There is no uncertain. There is a lack of knowledge and/or perspective necessary to know the predetermined outcome. This includes living creatures. While a deterministic paradigm would have to make some sort of exception for Awakened will as able to override determined reality, all unawakened Life Patterns would still be predictable with enough knowledge. We have sciences all about predicting animal behavior. It's not beyond some level of predictability.<br /> <br /> So, if we take a philosophic approach over a practical approach, the Sphere Rank needed varies by paradigm. And is something I think we can all agree shouldn't be the case for a host of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T02:40:19-07:00","id":1550029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550013#post1550013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My approach to those options is largely based on game-play considerations. While the developers might have a different opinion on things, I assume that the present paradigms in M20 are supposed to be equally coherent to the setting. Since we have example paradigms that hold that the world is deterministic, and ones that hold the world is not, option 2 would prejudice the game towards deterministic paradigms.<br /> <br /> In a deterministic paradigm all systems are predictable with enough knowledge. There is no random. There is no uncertain. There is a lack of knowledge and/or perspective necessary to know the predetermined outcome. This includes living creatures. While a deterministic paradigm would have to make some sort of exception for Awakened will as able to override determined reality, all unawakened Life Patterns would still be predictable with enough knowledge. We have sciences all about predicting animal behavior. It's not beyond some level of predictability.<br /> <br /> So, if we take a philosophic approach over a practical approach, the Sphere Rank needed varies by paradigm. And is something I think we can all agree shouldn't be the case for a host of reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradigms have nothing to do with how things actually work. Sphere ranks are not related to paradigms but that does not mean the mentioned paradigms are connected in any way to how reality of the setting is. Personally im all for the philosophical aproach, The only thing it defines is that free will of living creatures is not deterministic. Someone can think otherwise as his paradigm in mage but that would still require Entropy 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T03:06:39-07:00","id":1550031,"title":"","content":"Except that would be a flat out refutation of deterministic paradigms. As M20 firmly establishes, paradigms adapt to practical usefulness. If Entropy's ranks are based on non-deterministic philosophy, than all deterministic paradigms would have been cast aside centuries ago. Which then runs afoul of my assumption that by presenting non-deterministic paradigms in the books, than they are equally valid in play as deterministic ones.<br /> <br /> Since this thread is also about what the text actually says. The Entropy section itself never suggests that Life Patterns are targeted directly at rank 4 because of free will or anything of the sort. It doesn't actually justify why living things at 4, and then conceptual things at 5, are sorted in this fashion.<br /> <br /> This means that a mage with a deterministic paradigm can think that the Sphere operates in a &quot;practical&quot; fashion, while a non-deterministic mage can believe that the Sphere is influenced by free will, and neither is inherently advantaged by the rules siding with a philosophic position.<br /> <br /> Using the philosophic option goes against what we both agree on: paradigm doesn't dictate what rank an effect takes. That's why I'm against it, it's taking sides on paradigms instead of leaving them to address magic on their own terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T06:09:47-07:00","id":1550035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550012#post1550012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) This is one of those cases where M20 pairs two spheres that can accomplish the task on their own. Either Forces 2+ or Entropy 3 could accomplish the job.<br /> <br /> 2) While Entropy 3 can work on matter without help and Entropy 4 can work on Life without help, Entropy 3 can only affect energies with the addition of Forces. That's really janky, but it is a possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's option 2, and yes, this is kinda dumb, since Forces 3 should be enough to diminish or enhance energy...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I'm not sure I got the issue you have here. Is it because of the title of the sphere rank &quot;Predictable Patterns&quot;? If it is, I dont think the authors were thinking about determinism and non-determinism. Maybe we shouldn't get too attached by the name of the rank and more into the descrpitions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T06:58:52-07:00","id":1550036,"title":"","content":"Sphere levels do not exist in the game world (except maybe as a order of hermes paradigm) and therefore should not be used in connection to other paradigms in any way. Its just a mechanic.<br /> <br /> As for the two options i wote 1). Entropy has proven on base of matter and life (and maybe mind) that it can affect different patterns without other spheres.<br /> <br /> @Lord Revan<br /> Agreed If we have predictable patterns then we also have unpredictable patterns and that can be the basis. The core here is how do we define predictable patterns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T07:48:08-07:00","id":1550038,"title":"","content":"Just from the different approaches in how we are discussing this, I don't think we can come up with an authoratative ruling on where energies fit into Entropy. There's simply not enough indication one way or the other. What I would like to aim for, then, is a few reasonable options we could use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550013#post1550013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My approach to those options is largely based on game-play considerations. While the developers might have a different opinion on things, I assume that the present paradigms in M20 are supposed to be equally coherent to the setting. Since we have example paradigms that hold that the world is deterministic, and ones that hold the world is not, option 2 would prejudice the game towards deterministic paradigms.<br /> <br /> In a deterministic paradigm all systems are predictable with enough knowledge. There is no random. There is no uncertain. There is a lack of knowledge and/or perspective necessary to know the predetermined outcome. This includes living creatures. While a deterministic paradigm would have to make some sort of exception for Awakened will as able to override determined reality, all unawakened Life Patterns would still be predictable with enough knowledge. We have sciences all about predicting animal behavior. It's not beyond some level of predictability.<br /> <br /> So, if we take a philosophic approach over a practical approach, the Sphere Rank needed varies by paradigm. And is something I think we can all agree shouldn't be the case for a host of reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's a reasonable approach, though a potentially complicated one to discuss in depth. I want to ask, are you more focused on how the division affects mages in universe or how it affects players playing mages with those paradigms? For my part I'm mostly focused on the spheres as game mechanics, so the latter matters more to me.<br /> <br /> One other consideration. Entropy 3 makes it clear that the more complicated the object the easier it is to manipulate its decay. If that holds true for energies as well, then as systems get more complex they get easier to work with, right up until the moment they get too complex and bump up to the next rank. That being the case it is important that the demarcation between ranks be clear and easy to use. If weather is split amongst two ranks, how do we make the line clear?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T08:05:18-07:00","id":1550039,"title":"","content":"On another note, I should probably get Entropy 4 up as, unfortunately, energies are not the last undefined part of the Sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Affect Living Things </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this Rank, the mage assumes the awesome power of blessing, cursing, and conferring outright health or decay. By influencing the flow of entropy within a living body, that mage can grant outstanding vitality to, or inflict sudden disease upon, his subject. Such influence, as noted above, inflicts or heals aggravated damage and may grant long-term luck or misfortune. (Storyteller\u2019s option as to how this manifests.)</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately, \u2018blessing\u2019 and \u2018cursing\u2019 aren\u2019t as informative as they first appear. We probably shouldn\u2019t interpret Entropy 4 to be capable of any mythological curse we can find since some curses, like bad luck, are already possible at Entropy 3 and others, like transformations, are outside the realm of Entropy entirely. Given the examples I think we are meant to extend the possibilities of Entropy 3 to living systems.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Given that, Entropy 4 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Increase or Decrease Health (Affect Living Things)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most directly, Entropy 4 takes the ability to speed and slow decay from Entropy 3 and extends it to living systems. This includes both speeding or slowing breakdown and sudden failure. Even if this is an extension, though, it is a very powerful and versatile one.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Quick Healer</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since the body can heal itself, Entropy 4 can also speed or slow that function. Most obviously this can be used to speed up healing times. More darkly it can interfere with healing, leading to lingering wounds that are slow to close and heal.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Shrug It Off</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Given that entropy can slow damage and heal things, it should also be capable of making them resist damage. Entropy should be capable of giving someone a natural soak, though this could easily be flavored more as good fortune in how someone takes and moves with the hits rather than just greater durability.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Jam the Living Machine</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Much like before, Entropy should be capable of triggering sudden failure modes in people and animals. This would include sudden impediments like sprained ankles, thrown out backs, and stiff necks.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It could also reasonably include major life altering events like heart attacks and strokes, though that could disrupt a game in more ways than one so that\u2019s a table call. For my part, I would often handle those as magical attacks rather than events.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Eternal Youth</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By slowing down ageing to almost a stop, or even reversing it, Entropy can grant functional immortality, subject to the usual terms and conditions of immortality. Immortality is not legally responsible for suspicion, jealousy, the pain of outliving loved ones, or being dumped straight into the Deep Umbra when reality catches on. Do not take immortality if you have or may develop an incurable degenerative disease. Ask your doctor about immortality... or better yet, don't. He counts as a witness.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Direct Entropic Attacks (Affect Living Things)</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Entropy 4, the sphere is capable of direct attacks on the target\u2019s pattern. These are by default Aggravated. This is also a capability brough up in Base Entropy, and I should point out here that while Rank 4 specifically talks about it in the context of living things, Base Entropy does not. It is not clear, then, if Entropy attacks require supplemental spheres to affect other supernaturals.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Heal Aggravated Damage (Affect Living Things)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is one I usually forget about, but Entropy can heal patterns and specifically it can heal Aggravated Damage. There doesn\u2019t appear to be any restrictions on this, so it looks like it functions like Life healing, only more difficult (because of the higher rank)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Heal Vampires</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This came up in another thread. Normally, healing vampires requires adding Matter 2, but at this level Entropy can tune up both living and non-living systems, so even assuming Entropic Healing functions like Life healing, there is a case for letting Entropy 4 heal vampires without help. This same logic would apply to direct entropic attacks on vampires. Similar logic would apply to fae at Entropy 5 and fera at\u2026 whatever rank Entropy can affect spirits.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Missing Powers?</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Increase or Decrease Health\u2026 of Spirits (Affect Living Patterns)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 What Counts as a Living Pattern?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is basically the same dilemma as Entropy 3, only here the question is do spirits fall under Living Patterns. This is considerably less obvious than Predictable Patterns, though, and that didn\u2019t turn out to be obvious.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because the Low Umbra is one of Entropy\u2019s domains, we definitely can\u2019t make the claim that it doesn\u2019t affect spirits at all and we can\u2019t claim it always needs help. At the very least it needs to be able to affect ghosts at some rank, and it should probably be able to affect other spirits too.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think Entropy 4 is the better fit, but I could also see holding off until Entropy 5. What do you think?</span><br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T08:37:59-07:00","id":1550040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550036#post1550036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sphere levels do not exist in the game world (except maybe as a order of hermes paradigm) and therefore should not be used in connection to other paradigms in any way. Its just a mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550036#post1550036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the two options i wote 1). Entropy has proven on base of matter and life (and maybe mind) that it can affect different patterns without other spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's not stated directly it can affect Forces, I'd allow it as a ST, but only in high eanks (4 or 5) and only to decay/undecay (increase). No fine manipulation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550036#post1550036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Lord Revan<br /> Agreed If we have predictable patterns then we also have unpredictable patterns and that can be the basis. The core here is how do we define predictable patterns?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well that is just the title of the rank which doesn't even exist in-game, as you said yourself. We don't have to make this definition, we just have to see what is possible with the description and rotes examples.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T09:58:41-07:00","id":1550043,"title":"","content":"As for entropy healing i think its more like a retroactive &quot;flesh wound&quot;. It makes wounds magically heal retroactively so they appear serious but in fact were way lighter. Therefore helaing not with control over decay but healing with control over fate.<br /> <br /> I do not think entropy on its own should affect spirits, it cant affect werewolves without spirit so nor should it actual spirits.<br /> <br /> Whats missing here is the mind control aspect of entropy. At this lvl entropy should be able to control ongoing processes in living creatures decision making (Entropy 2 but for living things). For example if someone is hungry an entropy mage could direct in where and what he will go to eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T10:59:20-07:00","id":1550046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550039#post1550039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think Entropy 4 is the better fit, but I could also see holding off until Entropy 5. What do you think?</span><br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be 5. Spirits are the embodiment of ideas (or memories). Their bodies are not complex systems and aren't subject to decay in the same way as living bodies. They don't relate with time in the same way, and don't have an actual metabolism.<br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, I also think Forces should be covered by Entropy 3. In practical terms, most Entropy 2 effects are already dealing with Forces if you get to actual physics anyway. I don't think the sphere of Forces should be more protected than the sphere of Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:13:49-07:00","id":1550049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550046#post1550046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it should be 5. Spirits are the embodiment of ideas (or memories). Their bodies are not complex systems and aren't subject to decay in the same way as living bodies. They don't relate with time in the same way, and don't have an actual metabolism.<br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, I also think Forces should be covered by Entropy 3. In practical terms, most Entropy 2 effects are already dealing with Forces if you get to actual physics anyway. I don't think the sphere of Forces should be more protected than the sphere of Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Entropy can affect Matter, Life, Spirit, Mind and Forces. Maybe we should add Prime, Time and Correspondence to the list...<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, I completely disagree Entropy affecting Forces at rank 3. Rank 3 is for objects only (Matter), rank 4 for living beings (Life) and rank 5 for abstractions (Mind). Adding Forces and Spirit is not RAW at all, and if done, should be at rank 5.<br /> <br /> Also, want to remind again that Entropy does not grant fine control of those, it only affects their decay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:34:26-07:00","id":1550051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550049#post1550049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Entropy can affect Matter, Life, Spirit, Mind and Forces. Maybe we should add Prime, Time and Correspondence to the list...<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, I completely disagree Entropy affecting Forces at rank 3. Rank 3 is for objects only (Matter), rank 4 for living beings (Life) and rank 5 for abstractions (Mind). Adding Forces and Spirit is not RAW at all, and if done, should be at rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that necromancy and the low umbra are both explicitly part of Entropy's domain. At the very least it has to work on ghosts and similar types of spirits. It may not be mentioned in any of the five ranks, but it has to be somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, want to remind again that Entropy does not grant fine control of those, it only affects their decay. </div> </div> </div>That is well worth remembering. Entropy is largely limited to what could already theoretically happen. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:51:42-07:00","id":1550053,"title":"","content":"This topic is a lot of fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T14:45:47-07:00","id":1550061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550035#post1550035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I'm not sure I got the issue you have here. Is it because of the title of the sphere rank &quot;Predictable Patterns&quot;? If it is, I dont think the authors were thinking about determinism and non-determinism. Maybe we shouldn't get too attached by the name of the rank and more into the descrpitions?</div> </div> </div> </div>The descriptions are rather minimal and lacking in a lot of clarity. If you're running the game, you really do need to decide what counts as a &quot;predictable Pattern&quot; because the Sphere isn't actually as organized around when it intrudes on other Spheres as is being stated here. Entropy 1 and 2 work on all sorts of Patterns, then at 3+ the &quot;kind&quot; of Patterns start to matter more. Entropy 3 never explicitly says that it only works on Matter patterns, and even mentions giving people bad luck already... people are certainly not Matter patterns.<br /> <br /> Deciding what counts as a predictable pattern is going to be essential to consistently deciding what sort of fate/luck manipulations on people can be done on humans at Entropy 3 vs. what needs to wait until Entropy 4 or 5... because &quot;predictable&quot; is the only actual guidance we get. If you want a real wrench in this discussion the &quot;Common Magickal Effects&quot; chart lists cursing and blessing someone as an Entropy 3/Life 3 effect, despite what the Entropy section says.<br /> <br /> I agree the authors probably working thing in terms of specific philosophies, but this has lead to multiple editions of Entropy being a problem child in the game due to the vagueness of what the text says it can do; both by itself and in combination with other Spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550036#post1550036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sphere levels do not exist in the game world (except maybe as a order of hermes paradigm) and therefore should not be used in connection to other paradigms in any way. Its just a mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The numerical ratings don't exist in the game world. That said, mages are completely aware in-character that increasing skill in a Sphere equates to increasing control over the purviews of that Sphere. Every long standing group of mages, not just the Hermetics, understand that there's things an Entropy 1 mage can't do, but an Entropy 3 mage can, they just don't use numbered rankings to describe it. They give people titles or labels based on feats they can demonstrate.<br /> <br /> While it is important that &quot;Entropy 3&quot; doesn't actually exist in-universe, it's equal important that Entropy 3 is an abstraction of something that does exist in-universe, and that is something mages are aware of, discuss, and categorize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550038#post1550038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to ask, are you more focused on how the division affects mages in universe or how it affects players playing mages with those paradigms? For my part I'm mostly focused on the spheres as game mechanics, so the latter matters more to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, I'm not sure ho separable these considerations are. Players have to filter effects through their paradigms, and paradigms are shaped by how the game presents the functioning of magic. They're intertwined. A division of what counts as predictable that has a large impact on paradigms in universe inherently affects players playing mages with those paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that holds true for energies as well, then as systems get more complex they get easier to work with, right up until the moment they get too complex and bump up to the next rank. That being the case it is important that the demarcation between ranks be clear and easy to use. If weather is split amongst two ranks, how do we make the line clear? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't hold true for energies.<br /> <br /> Something I think is a functional analogy: energies are like a fluid. They conform to the shape of their container.<br /> <br /> The hard part is that the complexity of the &quot;shape&quot; of energy in the system is not directly correlated to the complexity of the system itself. Computers are fairly complex systems, but as a container of energy they're explicitly designed to make energy acting within them to be as predictable as possible. The Earth's surface is a fairly complex system as well, but weather as an energetic function of it varies wildly in predictability. Gravitational orbits are very simple systems... but then the nth-body problems set in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550040#post1550040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 3 is for objects only (Matter), rank 4 for living beings (Life) and rank 5 for abstractions (Mind).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is in direct contradiction with the text. Entropy 3 can explicitly affect living things, and abstractions only being a matter of Mind doesn't really fly with the rest of the metaphysics of the game.<br /> <br /> At best this line of progression only applies to Entropy's ability to directly harm/heal things, not to it's ability to perform gross manipulations of systems broadly.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree with Ramnesis that the text itself isn't going to resolve the Forces discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550051#post1550051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that necromancy and the low umbra are both explicitly part of Entropy's domain. At the very least it has to work on ghosts and similar types of spirits. It may not be mentioned in any of the five ranks, but it has to be somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah necromancy... the thing that somehow gets left out of every core book for the entire game line.<br /> <br /> M20 does treat ghosts and spirits as separate categories in the common effects chart. Like living things, Entropy can bless/curse ghosts and spirits at Entropy 3+, but harming ghosts actually takes Entropy 3/Prime 2 (sigh), while harming spirits directly is only listed as a Spirit effect.<br /> <br /> Take that for what you will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T04:44:13-07:00","id":1550066,"title":"","content":"I dont think we will ever agree here.<br /> The tradition seats in the council are made this way because the order of hermes organized it mostly. The same reason why dreamspeakers are even counted as a unified thing when in reality there just spiritual practices with no organisation or connections to each other. Yes the sphere realms exist in umbra, so does everything else imaginable.<br /> Spheres are the same as disciplines, changeling arts, demonic lores they do not exist as a factual thing in the narrative. They are a game mechanic. Saying spheres exist is like saying the order of hermes is right and others are wrong.<br /> <br /> As a sidenote keep in mind mages can believe the can do things they cant and also that the cant do things they can.<br /> <br /> As to Entropy 3 affecting life that is not true, you can give or take luck but you cant afect their will nor their body.Affecting life is making it do something or to work on a life pattern directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T06:24:22-07:00","id":1550068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550066#post1550066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think we will ever agree here.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but you're pretty much ignoring the text here, which is a bigger problem than disagreement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The tradition seats in the council are made this way because the order of hermes organized it mostly. </div> </div> </div>That has nothing to do with what I said, but agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same reason why dreamspeakers are even counted as a unified thing when in reality there just spiritual practices with no organisation or connections to each other. </div> </div> </div>The Dreamspeakers might have started as a hodge-podge of mages lumped together by the European focused Traditions (and not just the Hermetics), but they are also explicitly organized both from the positive example of their founders realizing the need for solidarity with each other before the age of colonial empires started, and the Tradition has been pushed into by necessity. As M20 says rather directly, &quot;Separation, after all, has been a liability. With stronger bonds between them, the \u2019Speakers share a greater voice.&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't mistake informality and an aversion to strict hierarchy for a lack of organization or social connections between members of the Tradition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spheres are the same as disciplines, changeling arts, demonic lores they do not exist as a factual thing in the narrative. </div> </div> </div>Except all of these things, Spheres included, are factual things in the narrative. Vampires don't just have vague concepts of mind control abilities, they know that Dominate and Presence are manifestations of their power and are separate Disciplines... that's how they can give them names. Considering most Disciplines require a tutor to learn, the Disciplines have to be part of the narrative of the game. You can't seek out training in something that doesn't exist.How can vampires ban Discipline use in Elysium if Disciplines aren't part of the narrative?<br /> <br /> M20 very clearly talks about how even if different groups of mages (esp. those outside the Traditions since the Traditions specifically developed a shared language for discussing magic) use different words to name them, and would explain them through their own beliefs, they all still inevitably describe the nine Spheres are the Traditions have identified them. Basically, every mage, regardless of their terminology has a conceptualization of the Sphere of Entropy. Every mage knows it's a thing. The only thing the Hermetics did was create a useful system for labeling what everyone already knew was the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are a game mechanic. </div> </div> </div>They're both, like most game mechanics.<br /> <br /> When a PC rolls Dexterity + Melee to attack with a sword, and then Strength + extra successes + sword dice of damage it's both a mechanic, and a part of the narrative because they're swinging a sword and hurting someone. The sword is not &quot;unreal&quot; because it has mechanics that define it. The damage dice provide are mechanics and the &quot;dice&quot; don't exist in the narrative but the aim and force of the swing they modify certainly do.<br /> <br /> I simply do not understand how you can look at the text and act like mages don't know what the Spheres are. They do. They're mechanics and narrative elements. Claiming otherwise is in direct contradiction to the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a sidenote keep in mind mages can believe the can do things they cant and also that the cant do things they can. </div> </div> </div>OK... what does this have to do with anything I said? This isn't a refutation of the idea that defining &quot;predictable pattern&quot; on a philosophic basis biases the game towards whichever philosophy you pick nor does it refute that such a philosophy could radically change the logic of the Sphere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to Entropy 3 affecting life that is not true, you can give or take luck but you cant afect their will nor their body.Affecting life is making it do something or to work on a life pattern directly. </div> </div> </div>This is just a goal post shift; esp. regarding the sudden declaration that &quot;affecting&quot; has some specific definition here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T07:59:23-07:00","id":1550069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550051#post1550051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that necromancy and the low umbra are both explicitly part of Entropy's domain. At the very least it has to work on ghosts and similar types of spirits. It may not be mentioned in any of the five ranks, but it has to be somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you provide a quote or page number, please? I'd like to read it to see if we can conclude anything based on text.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550051#post1550051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is well worth remembering. Entropy is largely limited to what could already theoretically happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that. Entropy is limited to luck, probability and decay. I wouldn't say it could, for example, change the direction of a flying arrow. At best, you could reduce it's speed by &quot;decaying&quot; the kinetic energy. You cannot control it's direction any more than you can mind control a human being at rank 4 or 5.<br /> <br /> I am very over the fence with all this affecting Forces thing, as it has never appeared in any book, iirc. Do we have any examples in previous editions? Or at least something in hdydt (yeah, I know...)?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T08:09:12-07:00","id":1550070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550061#post1550061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The descriptions are rather minimal and lacking in a lot of clarity. If you're running the game, you really do need to decide what counts as a &quot;predictable Pattern&quot; because the Sphere isn't actually as organized around when it intrudes on other Spheres as is being stated here. Entropy 1 and 2 work on all sorts of Patterns, then at 3+ the &quot;kind&quot; of Patterns start to matter more. Entropy 3 never explicitly says that it only works on Matter patterns, and even mentions giving people bad luck already... people are certainly not Matter patterns.<br /> <br /> Deciding what counts as a predictable pattern is going to be essential to consistently deciding what sort of fate/luck manipulations on people can be done on humans at Entropy 3 vs. what needs to wait until Entropy 4 or 5... because &quot;predictable&quot; is the only actual guidance we get. If you want a real wrench in this discussion the &quot;Common Magickal Effects&quot; chart lists cursing and blessing someone as an Entropy 3/Life 3 effect, despite what the Entropy section says.<br /> <br /> I agree the authors probably working thing in terms of specific philosophies, but this has lead to multiple editions of Entropy being a problem child in the game due to the vagueness of what the text says it can do; both by itself and in combination with other Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that exactly. I'd say that entropy 1 and 2 works on probabilities. Those probabilities *can* affect any kind of pattern, of course, but you are not directly affecting them. Just like levitation does not directly affect someone (you don't need Life to levitate someone unless you want to lock it).<br /> <br /> In rank 3 you are directly affecting objects patterns by introducing decay into the menu. Now, the mage can destroy, degrade, etc. things. At rank 4 that applies to living beings, which is why at this rank you can cause direct damage.<br /> <br /> My initial point is that you don't necessarily needs to define &quot;Predictable patterns&quot; to know how the sphere works. We can work with the text and rotes examples and see what is possible. Of course, not everything is covered by those, and a creative player would definitely want to create more, but hanging in the title of the rank doesn't help much. It's too vague.<br /> It is clear to me, based on the ranks descriptions, that 1 and 2 deals with probabilities, 3 affects objects and machines, 4 affects living beings and 5 ideas and concepts.<br /> <br /> None seem to affect energy or forces in any way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T08:18:22-07:00","id":1550071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550071#post1550071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you provide a quote or page number, please? I'd like to read it to see if we can conclude anything based on text.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the tables interacting with wraiths requires Entropy. Harming a ghost requires Entropy p. 508. Interestingly there is a bless/curse under spirit powers that also requires Entropy 3, that would mean that Entropy can affect spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550069#post1550069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only that. Entropy is limited to luck, probability and decay. I wouldn't say it could, for example, change the direction of a flying arrow. At best, you could reduce it's speed by &quot;decaying&quot; the kinetic energy. You cannot control it's direction any more than you can mind control a human being at rank 4 or 5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Luck also affects how is your aim or if the wind blows and changes the arrows trajectory a bit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550070#post1550070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a PC rolls Dexterity + Melee to attack with a sword, and then Strength + extra successes + sword dice of damage it's both a mechanic, and a part of the narrative because they're swinging a sword and hurting someone. The sword is not &quot;unreal&quot; because it has mechanics that define it. The damage dice provide are mechanics and the &quot;dice&quot; don't exist in the narrative but the aim and force of the swing they modify certainly do.<br /> <br /> I simply do not understand how you can look at the text and act like mages don't know what the Spheres are. They do. They're mechanics and narrative elements. Claiming otherwise is in direct contradiction to the text.\u200b<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Its simple, spheres are a game mechanic, the reality may be that a dwarf sits on a cloud and makes effects happen (for example).<br /> As all paradigms and none of them may be true there cannot be one true answer. There may be 9 spheres, there may be 6 elements, there may be 1 god but its not an absolute in the setting. Even the order of hermes paradigm is not necessary the exact 9 spheres as described in the mechanics. Thats why it should not matter in the main topic<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> to explain it even simpler in lord of the rings we have no idea how anyone does magic. The RPG One ring has rules on how to cast magic. Those rules are for the players only. In the same way Magic in MtAs is a soft magic system in the narrative. It does not work the same way as the mechanics. Its only a tool for the players to play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-12-2025, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T09:05:42-07:00","id":1550072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550068#post1550068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're both, like most game mechanics.<br /> <br /> When a PC rolls Dexterity + Melee to attack with a sword, and then Strength + extra successes + sword dice of damage it's both a mechanic, and a part of the narrative because they're swinging a sword and hurting someone. The sword is not &quot;unreal&quot; because it has mechanics that define it. The damage dice provide are mechanics and the &quot;dice&quot; don't exist in the narrative but the aim and force of the swing they modify certainly do.<br /> <br /> I simply do not understand how you can look at the text and act like mages don't know what the Spheres are. They do. They're mechanics and narrative elements. Claiming otherwise is in direct contradiction to the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, though I want to make sure we don't take too much from that connection. Game rules also have to consider balance and playability, and decisions made for those reasons probably shouldn't filter back down to the in universe game. Skill with a sword does not break down into five distinct and measurable levels of ability. Neither does strength. Those are artefacts of the system.<br /> <br /> In universe the Spheres are huge, complex fields of study that some mages think may be connected to the metaphysics of the universe (they may be right) and others think may just be an effective framework for describing it (similar to what some think math is). Progress along them will often be gradual rather than abrupt and some paradigms will access some capabilities better than others. That doesn't mean that there aren't accepted abilities for each rank, but it is more likely that those abilities were set down as requirements to achieve the recognition for that rank than that they are metaphysically the product of that rank.<br /> <br /> Out of universe there is no value in breaking down the spheres to match that smooth progression, and the distinction of what goes in what rank is at least partially one of intuition and game balance rather than deeply considered philosophical thought. Thus there is a limit to how much of what we define in the Sphere ranks is actually a metaphysical fact in universe. And if we do set abilities in a way that one or more paradigms can't fully use, that doesn't mean that in universe those paradigms are proved wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550069#post1550069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you provide a quote or page number, please? I'd like to read it to see if we can conclude anything based on text.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Base Entropy section on page 514 puts Necromancy as one of the specialties available to Entropy. It also lists 'tap into the energies of the Low Umbra, induce or remove corruption, and otherwise exert his Will through the inexorable process of mortality.' In addition to calling out the Low Umbra specifically, it also includes corruption which could reasonably include spiritual corruption.<br /> <hr /><br /> On another note, with most Spheres I'm going to put in an Everything Else section in rank 5 since at that point everything within the Sphere's purview should be possible (barring the existence of Archspheres). I'm not sure if I should with Entropy because it is harder to define the edges of Entropy. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T09:39:01-07:00","id":1550074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550071#post1550071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the tables interacting with wraiths requires Entropy. Harming a ghost requires Entropy p. 508. Interestingly there is a bless/curse under spirit powers that also requires Entropy 3, that would mean that Entropy can affect spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I stand corrected. Entropy can affect spirits and harm ghosts. However that is not the entirety of Necromancy. Animating the dead requires Life and Prime (no entropy). Resurrection requires Life, Spirit and Prime (again, no entropy).<br /> <br /> The entire section of Necromancy on Hdydt (<i>sigh</i>) has entropy only to slow the process of rotting of the body. So, the entry about necromancy is pretty much about harming/blessing/cursing spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550071#post1550071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... Luck also affects how is your aim or if the wind blows and changes the arrows trajectory a bit</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why people think that Entropy is the best sphere ever. It is not. If the arrow is already flying, you can't change its path, you can't create the amount of wind necessary to do that in a second . The best you can do is use &quot;luck&quot; to make the archer miss his target. However, you cannot make him shoot his friend that is behind him. That's impossible.<br /> <br /> You can't just wish for something and pull your Entropy card and shout &quot;luck!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And again, I am yet to see any rote or text about entropy affecting Forces.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-12-2025, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T10:34:51-07:00","id":1550075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550074#post1550074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why people think that Entropy is the best sphere ever. It is not. If the arrow is already flying, you can't change its path, you can't create the amount of wind necessary to do that in a second . The best you can do is use &quot;luck&quot; to make the archer miss his target. However, you cannot make him shoot his friend that is behind him. That's impossible.<br /> <br /> You can't just wish for something and pull your Entropy card and shout &quot;luck!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And again, I am yet to see any rote or text about entropy affecting Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well maybe it is the best sphere ever? :P<br /> How about Ahiu Nalu from Dead Magic 2 p.26? The description tells mage can alter the probability of the ocean to fight.<br /> Storm rune p.99 is used to calm storms. It has Forces 3 but also Entropy 3 so it could be sphere bloat or it could indicate entropy helps in changing the weather<br /> Shagos Grave MtAs 1ed p. 222 also seems to imply entropy can control who gets hit by lightning generated by an forces 5 effect storm.<br /> Dark streets from hollow ones revised p. 62 also has a spell taht seems to have sphere bloat hard to tell why it would use both entropy and forces<br /> <br /> In general it is hard to find a rote that uses entropy and not forces to afect forces is for 2 reasons:<br /> 1. Sphere bloat, the devs thought that if something touches the subject its main sphere should be included<br /> 2. Most of luck is based on forces, a gust of wind, a unlucky spark when the sword hits metal near a powder keg and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T12:14:32-07:00","id":1550076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550075#post1550075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well maybe it is the best sphere ever? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly not. I'd argue that it is one of the worst, imho. The main thing of the sphere (modifiers) can be done with practically every sphere. Every time I see someone that think otherwise, their take on what the sphere is capable is way wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550075#post1550075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Ahiu Nalu from Dead Magic 2 p.26? The description tells mage can alter the probability of the ocean to fight.<br /> Storm rune p.99 is used to calm storms. It has Forces 3 but also Entropy 3 so it could be sphere bloat or it could indicate entropy helps in changing the weather<br /> Shagos Grave MtAs 1ed p. 222 also seems to imply entropy can control who gets hit by lightning generated by an forces 5 effect storm.<br /> Dark streets from hollow ones revised p. 62 also has a spell taht seems to have sphere bloat hard to tell why it would use both entropy and forces<br /> <br /> In general it is hard to find a rote that uses entropy and not forces to afect forces is for 2 reasons:<br /> 1. Sphere bloat, the devs thought that if something touches the subject its main sphere should be included<br /> 2. Most of luck is based on forces, a gust of wind, a unlucky spark when the sword hits metal near a powder keg and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>All sphere bloat. Forces alone can affect weather. And Entropy alone cannot.<br /> <br /> And again, you can't summon wind. You can't change the path of an object by &quot;luckily&quot; having a gust of wind, unless the object is as light as a party balloon or paper.<br /> You second example requires a powder keg. Unless the ST said there is one around (which is extremely unusual except for very specific industries), you can't do that. It would also probably be vulgar, because just like the shooting of the gas tank, powder do not explode that easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-13T19:07:18-07:00","id":1550102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550076#post1550076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is certainly not. I'd argue that it is one of the worst, imho. The main thing of the sphere (modifiers) can be done with practically every sphere. Every time I see someone that think otherwise, their take on what the sphere is capable is way wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am curious, how would you rank the spheres on a list from best to worst? And what is the criteria for it? Versatility, raw power, ease of use?<br /> <br /> I was using <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207886-character-creation-and-progression-what-is-optimal-what-s-a-trap?p=1208226#post1208226\">this</a> ranking by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, but that link is admittedly for starting values, with some critique of how the spheres grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-13-2025, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T05:30:31-07:00","id":1550107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550102#post1550102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am curious, how would you rank the spheres on a list from best to worst? And what is the criteria for it? Versatility, raw power, ease of use?<br /> <br /> I was using <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207886-character-creation-and-progression-what-is-optimal-what-s-a-trap?p=1208226#post1208226\">this</a> ranking by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, but that link is admittedly for starting values, with some critique of how the spheres grow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends greatly on personal preference and probably the table game style. Also, I think all spheres are more or less in the same tier.Imo, versatility is the name of the game.<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion, the best spheres are Forces and Life, maybe Matter too. You <b>need</b> someone with Life(healing) in the group (or a wonder) or people will die too quickly. Life is also very, very versatile granting buffs, detecting living beings, controlling moods, etc.<br /> Forces is my favorite, so I'm a bit suspicious, but it is on of the most versatile sphere and that +1 sux in damage is good as well.<br /> Matter is also very versatile, since basically what is not Life nor Forces is Matter.<br /> <br /> Now, Prime is very useful but not on its own (at least in low levels). Correspondence is also very usefull and cool, but also depends on other spheres.<br /> <br /> Spirit and Time are good spheres in theory, but the rules kinda fuck Time and Spirit depends too much on the ST<br /> <br /> Mind is very cool, but the rules also kinda fuck it, unless you're dealing with sleepers only. And Entropy is too ST dependant, not very versatile (once you understand that you cant summon shit) and the main thing it does (modifiers) can be easily done by practically any sphere at low levels.<br /> <br /> Well, this is my short and quick analysis. But we are going off topic here and I'd suggest that we should go DM if you want to continue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T07:11:42-07:00","id":1550108,"title":"","content":"For my part, I think Entropy has to be able to affect forces and even moreso it has to be able to affect weather. Frankly, I find it unbelievable the Entropy couldn't be used to enhance or degrade a storm, or influence where rain lands or lighting strikes.<br /> <br /> Now I do think Entropy would be subject to the same restrictions as influencing material and living things: It can't create and it can't transmute, it can only push these patterns in ways they could already behave. A mage could intensify or degrade a blizzard, possibly turn it from snow to freezing rain, but he can't turn it into a hurricane or a tidal wave.<br /> <br /> What I am less sure of is if weather should be Entropy 3 or 4. I'm leaning 4 because Forces 4 is when that Sphere gets weather manipulation, and I think that was a game balance decision.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550061#post1550061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 does treat ghosts and spirits as separate categories in the common effects chart. Like living things, Entropy can bless/curse ghosts and spirits at Entropy 3+, but harming ghosts actually takes Entropy 3/Prime 2 (sigh), while harming spirits directly is only listed as a Spirit effect.<br /> Take that for what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed this when you first brought it up. This is one I've been wrangling with for a while now (at least since I started the Sphere Oddities thread. I initially dismissed it as just a bad sphere combination or an artifact from earlier drafts (and it may still be) but here is what I think is going on now:<br /> <br /> Prime 2 (and a point of quintessence) can upgrade an attack to aggravated damage. I think M20 sometimes uses this to instead upgrade a spell into an attack that causes Aggravated Damage. Looking at the Magical Damage chart, it can make <i>any</i> Sphere do aggravated damage, which would include Correspondence and Time, which cannot inflict damage at all without help. That's what I think Prime 2 is doing with Entropy 3 here, escalating a touch spell to a direct attack.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, the idea is first introduced on page 418, and that page also lets Spirit 2/Prime 2 affect spirits like Life magic.<br /> <br /> If this is the case, Entropy 3 would essentially function like Touch Ghosts, while Entropy 4 would be the Harm Ghosts level.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T07:28:45-07:00","id":1550112,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Affect Thought/ Shape Memes/ Binding Oath </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The most esoteric applications of Entropy allow the mage to alter ideas, strengthening or breaking down concepts. Although he does not affect the actual workings of consciousness, he can cause synapses to misfire (thus confusing perceptions and mental processing, inflicting penalties on an enemy\u2019s dice rolls), bind someone to an oath, or degrade the patterns of thought. By doing so, that Entropic Master can craft, perpetrate, reinforce, and undermine arguments, beliefs, and even memories.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To do such things, the Master merely speaks to, or glances at, the subject of his attention. Chaos Masters can scramble someone\u2019s perceptions with a few weird utterances, and Masters of Order can present arguments with apparently perfect logic. By offering compelling statements, the Master can create or destroy memes (see p. 594), thus influencing whole patterns of belief. An oath, meanwhile, ties the subject\u2019s fate to her loyalty; if she breaks the oath, then her luck goes really, really bad.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In game terms, such feats demand a certain number of successes. Inspiring a whim requires only one or two successes, sparking a fancy takes three, setting or undermining a conviction takes four or five successes, and setting up obsessions demands five successes or more. Such activities are usually coincidental and are typically rolled against a difficulty of the subject\u2019s Willpower, with a minimum difficulty of 4.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A much more meaty entry.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy 5 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulate Thought Processes (Affect Thought)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Correspondence master gains the ability to mess with the process of thinking, manipulating synapses and perceptions. This may sound like Entropy 4\u2019s Affect Living Things, but this rank has the power and deftness to create specific and intentional changes. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>S.E.P. Field </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The classic from Douglas Adams, this makes a person ignore something as Someone Else\u2019s Problem. This is most easily accomplished with Mind, but should be possible by the level of manipulation shown in Entropy 5.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulate Thoughts (Affect Thought)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m not sure if this is meant to be a different effect than Manipulate Thought Processes, but some of the listed effects seem to target the actual thought rather than the brain that is thinking it. A mage can plant impulses, ideas, and even beliefs in a subject with the use of Entropy. This is so much like mind manipulation that difficulty is calculated like mind effects. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is worth noting, though, that Entropy 5 is explicitly stated to leave consciousness alone. This can implant motivations, memories, and impulses, but it can\u2019t manipulate actual choices.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sudden Revulsion</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By imparting a sudden feeling of disgust or distrust, a mage can taint impressions of a person or thing.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Placebo</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage makes the target trust that a substance or treatment will have an effect (good or bad). This leverages the well known Placebo Effect to create physiological effects in the target in response to a stimuli or treatment, even if that thing shouldn\u2019t have any effect.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Placebo Domingo</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like the above but specifically giving the target a love of opera music and a certainty that it will make him feel better.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter Ideas (Shape Memes)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An Entropy Master can also skip the mucking about with brains and brain matter and skip straight to manipulating ideas themselves. What this means is a little vague and so utility will depend on the ST. At the very least, though, a mage can make an idea easier or harder to believe or understand.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is one I\u2019d like to see other people\u2019s takes on. How do you let this work?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Ear Worm</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While I named this after the song idea, the effect is an idea that keeps bringing itself to the forefront of someone\u2019s mind. This could be a distracting annoyance, or it could manifest as oddly compelling. Whatever the case, the idea, word, song, etc is unforgettable for a period of time. This is particularly useful paired with an effect like Placebo above.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bind an Oath (Binding Oath)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can take a specific type of idea or thought, a promise, and attach a curse to it such that if the promise is violated the curse activates. In a more general sense, the mage can tie someone\u2019s fate to an idea, thought, or belief.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Bind a Geas</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The condition doesn\u2019t have to be breaking your word. Folklore is filled with other conditions like refusing hospitality or eating dog meat.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This may require other spheres. For binding an oath, both the trigger (breaking an oath) and the consequence (bad luck) are in the purview of Entropy. Not every trigger will be. In the aforementioned \u2018eating dog meat\u2019 geas, Entropy 5 dooms can trigger if someone <i>knowingly</i> eats dog meat as that\u2019s a mental state, but a mage might need to add Life if the doom needs to kick in when they unknowingly do so.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> I usually add an Everything Else entry, but Entropy is hard to limit at the edges so I'm not going to do that here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T07:58:33-07:00","id":1550113,"title":"","content":"Tier lists aside, I don't think it's off topic to discuss what Entropy can do in the thread about what the Spheres say they can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the arrow is already flying, you can't change its path, you can't create the amount of wind necessary to do that in a second . The best you can do is use &quot;luck&quot; to make the archer miss his target. However, you cannot make him shoot his friend that is behind him. That's impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are pretty epic misses in the world of failures.<br /> <br /> I don't think the arrow rebounding on a hard object, flying upwards, and hitting the guy behind should be out of the cuesti\u00f3n. Maybe it would require many successes, but AFAIK there's no hard general RAW for &quot;make him shoot his friend that is behind him&quot; regardless of the Sphere used. So we would have to go a little sideways of strict raw anyhow to do that, even with Forces (I think there was a Correspondence Rote somewhere that does that and we could copy, but the point stands). <hr />Probability, as a concept, always deals with the undefined. As was said, if you know every element of a system there's no probability, everything works as determined.<br /> <br /> Now, Entropy can't create wind, so if you want to create a wind to carry an arrow somewhere, that's something Entropy alone can't do. But in practice the ST can't and will never describe everything that's in the scene. Ofc, different ST describe things differently, but there's always things left out. Like, I don't think there's been &quot;wind&quot; or even &quot;rain&quot; described more than once in the last D&amp;D campaign I played in, like, a whole year of &quot;game time&quot;. At this point, should we be more concerned about the impending drought than about the monster army? :P<br /> <br /> I think that's what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> was pointing out when saying that thing about there &quot;being enough water in the weather system&quot;? (regardless of the level being unclear, because Entropy doesn't affect Forces alone, albeit it should be able to because they're still part of a system, you can make statistic models about weather and such, etc).<br /> <br /> I think Entropy plays a lot with that element of uncertainty, and expect players and ST to play along. To not ask for anything too outlandish, nor to deny everything that it's plausible.<br /> <br /> That does make the Sphere very &quot;ST dependant&quot;, though perhaps a better expression would be that it makes the Sphere dependant on the dialogue between players and st. But, then, I think that &quot;too ST dependant&quot; could be a criticism valid about all of Mage. Entropy it's just a little worse on that end. <hr /><br /> I have a doubt of my own: Can I use Entropy 3-4 to create something like a protective effect on the PC that makes weapons that are used to attack them to break, regardless of the type of weapon?<br /> <br /> I could argue that I don't need to know exactly what patterns I'm affecting, because Entropy ain't a pattern sphere, I'm creating a &quot;protective aura of decay&quot; of sorts (in a similar way as I can affect the probability of attacks to miss, regardless of the type of attack) - a counter argument could be that I *DO* need to target these systems individually to cause them to break (because it's not the same as affecting probability, patterns are mentioned as targets)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-14-2025, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T08:48:04-07:00","id":1550114,"title":"","content":"I would also add manipulating fate here. It works like the vampire discipline that allows you to summon someone. You can make being in some place someones destiny. That person will sooner or later come there feeling the urge to. Its a afterthought from Affect thought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T11:56:21-07:00","id":1550117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550069#post1550069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am very over the fence with all this affecting Forces thing, as it has never appeared in any book, iirc. Do we have any examples in previous editions? Or at least something in hdydt (yeah, I know...)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your very example of decaying the speed of an arrow. And in fact, any way of affecting movement.<br /> <br /> To make an attack miss or hit, you're basically affecting its movement, and that's affecting its energy, either directly or through the energy of another thing.<br /> <br /> Fate, luck, probability, however you name it, in the <b>actual universe</b>, be it the game universe or our own, those things are the result of movements. Entropy simply can't affect them without affecting energy, and that means Forces.<br /> <br /> Of course, just like it affects the &quot;luck&quot; of matter before it affects Matter directly, it doesn't necessarily means that Entropy should affect Forces directly at any particular level, and while I said 3, I'm ok with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>' rule for Entropy 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T18:23:45-07:00","id":1550134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550117#post1550117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your very example of decaying the speed of an arrow. And in fact, any way of affecting movement.<br /> <br /> To make an attack miss or hit, you're basically affecting its movement, and that's affecting its energy, either directly or through the energy of another thing.<br /> <br /> Fate, luck, probability, however you name it, in the <b>actual universe</b>, be it the game universe or our own, those things are the result of movements. Entropy simply can't affect them without affecting energy, and that means Forces.<br /> <br /> Of course, just like it affects the &quot;luck&quot; of matter before it affects Matter directly, it doesn't necessarily means that Entropy should affect Forces directly at any particular level, and while I said 3, I'm ok with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>' rule for Entropy 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no. By that logic, everything in the universe is Forces, because matter=energy and life is made of atoms which is matter. So now I can do everything with Forces. <br /> <br /> That's not how the game works, you can't extrapolate that way. Entropy deals with the concept of luck and probability it is *not* necessarily messing with movement. You argument is fine for a in-game paradigm, though, just not for tje game rules.<br /> <br /> So, while I'm ok with a ST allowing to decay forces with Entropy 4 or 5, and weather with Entropy 5 (Entropy requiring the same as Forces is wrong imho), I still do not consider this as raw, simply by the fact that I can't find any text or Entopy (without Forces) rote to base that assumption.<br /> <br /> Also, my example is made up, it's not a rote, afaik. I will stand corrected if there are any example of that, I just don't know any\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T01:38:42-07:00","id":1550142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550134#post1550134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, no. By that logic, everything in the universe is Forces, because matter=energy and life is made of atoms which is matter. So now I can do everything with Forces.<br /> <br /> That's not how the game works, you can't extrapolate that way. Entropy deals with the concept of luck and probability it is *not* necessarily messing with movement. You argument is fine for a in-game paradigm, though, just not for tje game rules.<br /> <br /> So, while I'm ok with a ST allowing to decay forces with Entropy 4 or 5, and weather with Entropy 5 (Entropy requiring the same as Forces is wrong imho), I still do not consider this as raw, simply by the fact that I can't find any text or Entopy (without Forces) rote to base that assumption.<br /> <br /> Also, my example is made up, it's not a rote, afaik. I will stand corrected if there are any example of that, I just don't know any\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and thats a fine aproach. Everything can be done by every sphere. Just not that easy, sometimes in very inpractical ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T04:15:38-07:00","id":1550145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550142#post1550142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and thats a fine aproach. Everything can be done by every sphere. Just not that easy, sometimes in very inpractical ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, what??? No, not everything can be done with every sphere. There are several way to do some effect, sure, but not by every sphere.<br /> <br /> And are you saying that using Forces for basically everything is a fine approach? I'm sorry, but this just proves my point before about Entropy players, no offense intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T04:40:53-07:00","id":1550150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550145#post1550145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol, what??? No, not everything can be done with every sphere. There are several way to do some effect, sure, but not by every sphere.<br /> <br /> And are you saying that using Forces for basically everything is a fine approach? I'm sorry, but this just proves my point before about Entropy players, no offense intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just said that an aproach or theory that every sphere can do everything just on differnet levels and with different dificulty is perfectly valid.<br /> <br /> As for Entropy i would like to compare it to Fate from awakening. On 4 dots there si a rote called &quot;chaos mastery&quot; it allows the mage to control the probable outcome of a given situation including (as per examples in the awakening book):<br /> <br /> - Create a narrative effect such as controlling how vehicles behave in a multiple-car crash.<br /> <br /> - By directing once-random biochemical changes within a subject, cause seizures, hallucinations, and physical events, imposing suitable Conditions such as Blind or Disabled.<br /> <br /> - The mage reduces a subject\u2019s next action to a chance die.<br /> <br /> - Attack a subject by directing chance around them, or protect a subject from dangerous circumstances; this is not a direct-attack spell, and should use any rules for the<br /> hazard.<br /> <br /> Awakening powers are usually weaker than those from ascension so i see no reason to not include those possibilities in Entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T05:42:37-07:00","id":1550151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550142#post1550142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and thats a fine aproach. Everything can be done by every sphere. Just not that easy, sometimes in very inpractical ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there are many ways to do the same thing:<ul><li>Do you want your coin to land on a specific side? Entropy can do it, but also Forces.</li> <li>Do you want to See Auras? Mind or Spirit can do it.</li> <li>Do you want to boost attributes? Mind covers mental, and according to HDYDT Life could too.</li> </ul><br /> That does not mean that Forces can grant you healing, or that Mind can move a car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T05:50:07-07:00","id":1550152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550151#post1550151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, there are many ways to do the same thing:<ul><li>Do you want your coin to land on a specific side? Entropy can do it, but also Forces.</li> <li>Do you want to See Auras? Mind or Spirit can do it.</li> <li>Do you want to boost attributes? Mind covers mental, and according to HDYDT Life could too.</li> </ul><br /> That does not mean that Forces can grant you healing, or that Mind can move a car.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, just saying thats a valid theory (not that every effect can be replicated exactly but that you can achive simillar effects) and way of play<br /> I have no idea fow to use forces to heal (except for heating the wounds to stop bleeding but i bet someone could figure it out. As for mind moving a car you can dominate the car owner to move it with mind. Same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-15-2025, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T08:17:29-07:00","id":1550154,"title":"","content":"And Entropy it's specially guilty of this, because affecting probability, decay, etc ... it's always affecting something that's going to fall under the purview of other Spheres. These concepts just don't exist on their own as *things* (one could say similarly for *energy*, but &quot;fire&quot; can be seen as a thing, *decay* isn't ever a thing, it's a description related to a model that's more &quot;purpose-related&quot; than a &quot;thing&quot; - your decaying bread it's mold lush garden).<br /> <br /> That's why some people would argue to &quot;fold&quot; Entropy on the other spheres.<br /> <br /> But I like it to exist because fate it's a strong element of magical thinking, I think it makes the game more magical for it to exist as it's own thing.<br /> <br /> And on a more functional note Entropy it's the only Sphere that deals on &quot;unknowns&quot; - such as being able to detect &quot;danger&quot; w/o knowing or defining anything about the source. On that end, horoscope like undefined general effects such as &quot;good luck with money&quot; (w/o knowing how that will manifest) should also be possible.<br /> <br /> I think the game should play a lot more with that concept of being able to cast spells with &quot;undefined&quot; variable clauses using Entropy, and lament that it instead makes Entropy the &quot;dark&quot; Sphere, and puts it as a sort of &quot;sphere tax&quot; everywhere there's another Sphere doing something that falls within their purview, but that's also even remotely death or &quot;goth&quot; related, or that looks a bit chaotic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T09:19:02-07:00","id":1550155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550069#post1550069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am very over the fence with all this affecting Forces thing, as it has never appeared in any book, iirc. Do we have any examples in previous editions? Or at least something in hdydt (yeah, I know...)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this took a while since my copy of Revised is in storage, but in Entropy 3 in Revised:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> = MtA, Revised] At this level of skill, the mage can affect only set and predictable Patterns such as Matter and Forces. </div> </div> </div>So we do have evidence that, traditionally, Entropy 3 can manipulate forces patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T09:51:09-07:00","id":1550156,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy Errata</span></b></span><br /> <br /> This will be the section to cover methods of handling Entropy as it regards forces, weather, ghosts, and spirits. Having found that earlier editions (or at least Revised) do count forces patterns as Predictable Patterns, I need to rework how I format it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T09:53:38-07:00","id":1550157,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Forces</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview</b>: Energy Patterns. Actually the initial tag says \u2018Raising Storms\u2019 which is only the tiniest fraction of Forces.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two rules are given here:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Forces based attacks get an additional success of damage. While important, this doesn\u2019t change much about how the Sphere progresses.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 - Large scale effects require higher levels of expertise (and often more successes). This is less a rule and more an explanation of why larger uses of low rank abilities take higher ranks, and it has quite the effect on how Forces works.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T10:00:50-07:00","id":1550158,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Perceive Forces </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocking basic perceptions of the elements, a Forces savvy mage can sense the flow of forces in her environment. She can boost her perceptions into the infrared or ultraviolet spectrums, notice electrons, see in the dark, view X-rays, discern the flow of sound or radio waves, spot kinetic energies, and hear frequencies beyond the normal human range.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The descriptions here are mostly about expanding the senses that already deal with forces, sight and sound. There are a few possibilities left out, but from this description, Forces 1 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Expand visual range and sensitivity (Perceive Forces)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this power a mage can expand the spectrum he can see to just about any wavelength, letting him see heat (infrared), ultraviolet, radio waves, and even cosmic radiation. He can also increase his sensitivity to pick out the faintest of signals.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Stuck in a Skittles Commercial</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Despite being written as expanding vision, this could apply to any sense. If someone really wanted to be able to taste the rainbow, he could use Forces 1. Presumably, some CoXs frequently use sphere sensing to give themselves synesthesia. It seems like their thing.<br /> <br /> More seriously, being able to feel out heat or electromagnetic fields with touch or smell might suit many mages better than using vision.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><b><i>Added: Vastly Expand Spell Range (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a>)</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By default, a mage can cast on anything in sensory range. By dramatically zooming his sense of vision or enhancing his sense of hearing (or any other sense) a mage can increase his sensory range and thus cast much, much farther than usual without the use of Correspondence. </span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Expand aural range and sensitivity (Perceive Forces)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pretty much the exact same thing as expanding visual range, but with sound.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Echolocation</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By enhancing his hearing (and his processing with Mind 1) a mage can build a physical map of the surrounding area. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Other Mediums</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sound doesn\u2019t travel the same way in water or other mediums, but Forces 1 should be able to make adjustments for this.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Super Slow Play</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The human brain usually doesn\u2019t recognize beats below 33 beats per minute as rhythms. I\u2019m not sure how helpful it is, but a mage should be able to use Forces 1 to extend that limit down. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note: since writing this, I\u2019ve grown less convinced it works as a Forces effect. Let me know what you think.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See Other Forces (Perceive Forces)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A very important catch all, for two reasons. First, not every force is light or sound, and second, not every mage will think in terms of the electromagnetic spectrum. This power lets a mage set his senses to types of energy he can\u2019t normally sense. The two examples given are seeing kinetic energy and noticing electrons, but others, like seeing sources of gravity or magnetic fields would also be possible.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Neutrino Blinding</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fun fact, it is possible to share sphere senses with another person. The Spirit 2 writeup even suggests a method: tacking on Life 2 (though it is Spirit talking about Life, so take it with a grain of salt). An overwhelming input like, say, seeing neutrinos could effectively shut down someone\u2019s senses. It doesn\u2019t have to be neutrinos, just boosting sensitivity to light to extremes would work as well, but where\u2019s the fun in that?</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Missing Abilities:</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sense Forces Patterns (Perceive Forces)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes it isn\u2019t as important to be able to actually sense a force as to know it is there. Forces 1 is also capable of sensing patterns themselves, even ones the mage hasn\u2019t already keyed himself to see. For instance, with this ability a mage can detect the presence of a fire on the other side of a wall, without using his eyes. With more successes he can also tell if a force is being manipulated.</span><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-16-2025, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T10:44:16-07:00","id":1550159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>Super Slow Play</i></b><br /> <br /> The human brain usually doesn\u2019t recognize beats below 33 beats per minute as rhythms. I\u2019m not sure how helpful it is, but a mage should be able to use Forces 1 to extend that limit down.<br /> Note: since writing this, I\u2019ve grown less convinced it works as a Forces effect. Let me know what you think. </div> </div> </div>I think it's one of the places where Forces mixes with Time.<br /> <br /> But I'm OK with doing that with Forces as an alternative. Spheres allows to tune one's sense in weird ways. Forces sometimes seems to be able to provide senses like those of a machine. If one can adjust for sounds on water transmiting differently, maybe one could also adjust beats to see their rythm?. One sometimes forgets how much of a trip one can have with Sphere magick<br /> <br /> A &quot;problem&quot; i've tought about that may be similar: To &quot;Sense Speed&quot;. Speed it's a function of time and space. But movement it's usually regarded as a Force, at least as kinetick energy. So I would think Forces can sense speed<br /> <br /> (Or maybe not? &quot;No, it can't - you can only sense how hard you would crash, and need to extrapolate from that, discover/assume the mass of the vehicle, and do the math yourself to know how fast you're going&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , but I don't think Spheres are intended to be that granular . Now I'm remembering a talk I had with a friend years ago that said to create fire you needed Matter because of the combustible ... but that's clearly not the case)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-15-2025, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T10:50:34-07:00","id":1550160,"title":"","content":"I'm loving the love and care put into this topic, and it really helps me out maping out the never ending (even after almost 10 years of reading and sometimes playing Mage) Sphere questions.<br /> <br /> But... I'm certain that the more in-depth I study Ascencion, the more I appreciate and much prefer Awakening's magic. I feel it is way more organized, magical, and intuitive. Entropy generates so much freaking questions that at least separating Death and Fortune/Luck was a great enhancement for me (besides me loving a pure death sphere/arcanum). Yeah, of course, Storytellers might go to forums and q&amp;as to put down Sphere questions, but a game should be as self-fulfilling as it can by itself, and in comparison to Ascencion I think they corrected that a bunch in Awakening. <br /> <br /> Mage is wild and I'm very appreciative of the topic at hand!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T12:07:07-07:00","id":1550164,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I missed this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550113#post1550113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are pretty epic misses in the world of failures.<br /> <br /> I don't think the arrow rebounding on a hard object, flying upwards, and hitting the guy behind should be out of the cuesti\u00f3n. Maybe it would require many successes, but AFAIK there's no hard general RAW for &quot;make him shoot his friend that is behind him&quot; regardless of the Sphere used. So we would have to go a little sideways of strict raw anyhow to do that, even with Forces (I think there was a Correspondence Rote somewhere that does that and we could copy, but the point stands). <hr />Probability, as a concept, always deals with the undefined. As was said, if you know every element of a system there's no probability, everything works as determined.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, entropy is limited by &quot;something that actually stands a chance of happening under the given circumstances&quot;. And by stands a chance we all know those 1% probability of bouncing an arrow in to the sky to land in someone behind the archer does not stand a chance.<br /> <br /> Forces can literally maniopulate the movement and kinetic energy of an object the entire time. You can make the arrow do a barrel roll, fly upwards and land exactly on someone behind the archer. Would be vulgar, but you can. Entropy just <b>can't</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550113#post1550113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a doubt of my own: Can I use Entropy 3-4 to create something like a protective effect on the PC that makes weapons that are used to attack them to break, regardless of the type of weapon?<br /> <br /> I could argue that I don't need to know exactly what patterns I'm affecting, because Entropy ain't a pattern sphere, I'm creating a &quot;protective aura of decay&quot; of sorts (in a similar way as I can affect the probability of attacks to miss, regardless of the type of attack) - a counter argument could be that I *DO* need to target these systems individually to cause them to break (because it's not the same as affecting probability, patterns are mentioned as targets)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, but you'd need Life to lock it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T12:17:15-07:00","id":1550168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550158#post1550158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fun fact, it is possible to share sphere senses with another person. The Spirit 2 writeup even suggests a method: tacking on Life 2 (though it is Spirit talking about Life, so take it with a grain of salt). An overwhelming input like, say, seeing neutrinos could effectively shut down someone\u2019s senses. It doesn\u2019t have to be neutrinos, just boosting sensitivity to light to extremes would work as well, but where\u2019s the fun in that?</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Missing Abilities:</b></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need Spirit, according to BoS. By touching, you can share the senses. There are rules there for forcing the sharing to unwillingly targets and distant targets but I can't recall right now.<br /> <br /> Also, it's important to note that by expanding your sense, you also expand your sensory range and thus the range of your spella without Correspondence. That is valid for all rank 1 spheres sensing effects.<br /> <br /> Zoom in your vision to that dude 10km away and zap him with lightning. Or just explode the thugs that are inaide that locked room without even opening the door, via sonar or any other sensing that can ignore walls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T13:13:55-07:00","id":1550172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550164#post1550164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I missed this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it was greened. Hate when that happens, but that's how things are nowdays.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, entropy is limited by &quot;something that actually stands a chance of happening under the given circumstances&quot;. And by stands a chance we all know those 1% probability of bouncing an arrow in to the sky to land in someone behind the archer does not stand a chance.<br /> <br /> Forces can literally maniopulate the movement and kinetic energy of an object the entire time. You can make the arrow do a barrel roll, fly upwards and land exactly on someone behind the archer. Would be vulgar, but you can. Entropy just <b>can't</b> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that general definition of the limits of probability manipulation.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, I would say you could make an arrow go pretty much anywhere a Botch on part of the archer could potentially cause it to land. That DOES depend a lot on what the ST believes plausible, and the circumstance.<br /> <br /> And now we pretty much know it's Entropy 3, unless there's some reason to believe that was deliberately omitted as a retcon. It's amazing how the writeup of the Spheres of Revised keeps on giving.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T15:35:16-07:00","id":1550178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550172#post1550172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule of thumb, I would say you could make an arrow go pretty much anywhere a Botch on part of the archer could potentially cause it to land. That DOES depend a lot on what the ST believes plausible, and the circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an incredibly good way of putting it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, While this was omitted in M20, I'd say it's due to the author making a terrible work rule-wise, instead of retconing it. At least there is an argument now for Entropy to affect Forces. I'd still limit it to decay as we talked before and *definitely* not weather, since it's too big and very non predictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T07:06:35-07:00","id":1550189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550178#post1550178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, While this was omitted in M20, I'd say it's due to the author making a terrible work rule-wise, instead of retconing it. At least there is an argument now for Entropy to affect Forces. I'd still limit it to decay as we talked before and *definitely* not weather, since it's too big and very non predictable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be an area we have very different ideas of what is possible, and I'm curious what the actual difference is. Here's a list of effects. Do you think any of them are accomplishable with Entropy and enough successes (and Correspondence if necessary)?<br /> <br /> 1) There is an active thunderstorm going on. A mage wants to make one of the bolts of lightning hit a specific target.<br /> <br /> 2) It is a windy day with lots of sudden gusts. A mage wants to make one of the gusts blow at a convenient time.<br /> <br /> 3) There is an active tornado. Currently it is headed for a house, but tornados can change directions suddenly. A mage wants to get it to change directions to save the house.<br /> <br /> 4) There is an 80% chance of rain. A mage wants to make it rain on a specific spot.<br /> <br /> 5) There is an active rainstorm going on. A mage wants to cause the storm to fizzle out (decay) over the next hour.<br /> <br /> 6) There is an active rainstorm going on. A mage wants to cause the storm to escalate to damaging effects over the next hour.<br /> <br /> 7) A mage wants to bless a garden so that it consistently gets the right amount of rain for the plants planted there.<br /> <br /> 8) There is an active tornado. A mage wants to make it fizzle out (decay) over the next 10 minutes to prevent damage.<br /> <br /> 9) There is an active tornado. A mage wants to escalate it to a higher category.<br /> <br /> 10) There is a class 3 hurricane that just made landfall. A mage wants to downgrade it over the next hour.<br /> <br /> 11) There is a thunderstorm watch (i.e. the conditions are right for a thunderstorm to form). A mage wants to make it form.<br /> <br /> 12) There is a tornado watch (i.e. the conditions are right for a tornado to form). A mage wants to make one form.<br /> <br /> 13) It is a gentle, breezy day. A mage wants a sudden gust of wind for a quick distraction.<br /> <br /> 14) It is unlikely but possible for a thunderstorm to form. A mage wants to make a storm form.<br /> <br /> 15) The forecast calls for a foot of snow. A mage wants to triple the amount of snow that falls.<br /> <br /> 16) At sea, a mage wants a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rogue_wave\" target=\"_blank\">rogue wave</a> to strike a ship.<br /> <br /> 17) Rain is rare in this desert, the last time was a decade ago. A mage wants to fate it to rain sometime in the next year.<br /> <br /> 18) Rain is rare in this desert, the last time was a decade ago. A mage wants to fate it to rain sometime in the next day.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T08:56:24-07:00","id":1550191,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Manipulate Forces/ Elemental Touch </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Although she cannot conjure energies just yet, the mage may now alter the flow of existing forces. Sound can be muted or amplified; shadows can be gathered, shaped, or dispelled. The mage can warp light to make things invisible, change their colors by altering the spectrum of localized light, or render them silent by bending sound waves in their vicinity. With a wave of her hand, she can disrupt electrical currents; flare flames; or direct the course of winds, momentum, or gravity.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combining this Rank with other Spheres, that mage could also make an object (Matter) or organism (Life) attract or repel forces. Thus, she could weave minor protection spells or force-fields\u2026 or, conversely, turn that target into a magnet (perhaps literally) for the forces in question.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Despite its powers, this Rank is limited in scale. Assume that the mage can command energies around a single human sized character or within a small area (20\u2019 or less). To affect a larger area, you need a higher Rank in Forces.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For all the verbiage, this is basically one ability, which is Manipulate Forces. That one ability comes in a few flavors though. Forces 2 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enhance or Suppress Forces (Manipulate Forces)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can power up or down a given force, flaring matches into bonfires, dissipating the electricity of a circuit, or pulling the kinetic energy out of a moving object. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By a strict reading, there is no indication of a limitation on this power other than area, so the only thing standing between a lit match and a small blast furnace is successes.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>There Is Always Light</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There really is always light of some variety around, even if just that of ambient infrared. By shifting it up in frequency and amplifying it, a mage is never without a light source. More mystically inclined mages can do the same by dispelling darkness.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Power Surge</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enhancing the current within the wires of a building can easily pop a breaker and enhancing them within an electronic device can easily damage the device. Also, enhancing the static charge around someone could lead to quite a static shock.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Redirect Forces (Manipulate Forces) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can also move forces around and change their direction or flow. Moving objects can be redirected by changing their kinetic energy, electricity can be arced wherever the mage wants, and light can be concentrated or wrapped around a target.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By a strict reading, there is no given limit on the complexity of these manipulations, so barring some ST ruling the only thing between a mage and a very complex bit of manipulation is successes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the power behind the suggested force fields and magnets.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is barely an issue. It\u2019s clearly Forces 2 to direct forces towards a certain point, and it doesn\u2019t stop being Forces 2 if something is at that point. But if you want that point to move with something else\u2026 that is describing locking spheres. I don\u2019t like it when M20 pads out sphere descriptions with locking spheres, but that\u2019s what\u2019s going on.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Holograms</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By manipulating light, or sound, or momentum, or all three a mage can create physical illusions much like Star Trek\u2019s holodecks. There is some indication that this may be easier if Prime 2's Body of Light is used as a base, but as written Forces 2 should be capable of this on its own.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Flight</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By manipulating momentum with a small amount of finesse a mage can move himself or others around through the air. This is a spell that works much better with locking spheres. Without those it often turns into:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Yeet!</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By manipulating momentum to provide a short burst, a mage can launch a target in a given direction. He can also cast this on a location such that anything that enters that spot gets launched in that direction. </span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Vastly Augmented Spell Range</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 1 let a mage expand his visual range. Forces 2 lets him actually bend light, meaning he can now expand his visual range around corners and around the horizon. </span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T12:10:46-07:00","id":1550197,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> <br /> 1) Yes<br /> 2) Yes<br /> 3) No<br /> 4) No<br /> 5) No<br /> 6) No<br /> 7) Not exactly. The mage can bless the garden but it wont necessarily rain when the mage wants. Also would require Entropy 4 to affect Life.<br /> 8) No<br /> 9) No<br /> 10) No<br /> 11) No<br /> 12) No<br /> 13) Yes<br /> 14) No<br /> 15) No<br /> 16) No<br /> 17) No. He can bless it, though, and hope for the blessing to include rain.<br /> 18) Same as 17, but way harder.<br /> <br /> This is my answer without proper analysis and can chance with arguments. Basically, you cant do things that would require Forces 4+.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T12:20:47-07:00","id":1550199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550191#post1550191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Holograms</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By manipulating light, or sound, or momentum, or all three a mage can create physical illusions much like Star Trek\u2019s holodecks. There is some indication that this may be easier if Prime 2's Body of Light is used as a base, but as written Forces 2 should be capable of this on its own.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Vastly Augmented Spell Range</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 1 let a mage expand his visual range. Forces 2 lets him actually bend light, meaning he can now expand his visual range around corners and around the horizon. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 2 can create illusions (idk if that's what you meant with holograms) as well as make the mage invisible. <br /> <br /> You can also increase/decrease speed, which also means buff your physical capabilities.<br /> <br /> About the sensory range, I wonder how that would be ruled. How far can each Arete success zoom in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T07:09:02-07:00","id":1550213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550197#post1550197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a><br /> 1) Yes<br /> 2) Yes<br /> 3) No<br /> 4) No<br /> 5) No<br /> 6) No<br /> 7) Not exactly. The mage can bless the garden but it wont necessarily rain when the mage wants. Also would require Entropy 4 to affect Life.<br /> 8) No<br /> 9) No<br /> 10) No<br /> 11) No<br /> 12) No<br /> 13) Yes<br /> 14) No<br /> 15) No<br /> 16) No<br /> 17) No. He can bless it, though, and hope for the blessing to include rain.<br /> 18) Same as 17, but way harder.<br /> <br /> This is my answer without proper analysis and can chance with arguments. Basically, you cant do things that would require Forces 4+.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So would this be a fair description of how you see Entropy and weather: Entropy can influence the effects of the weather, but not the weather itself. So if the weather is already providing an effect, such as lightning, rain, or wind, Entropy can influence when and where that effect hits, but Entropy can't affect the weather pattern itself, and it can't make the weather produce an effect if it isn't already producing that effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T07:21:53-07:00","id":1550214,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 3</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Transmute Minor Forces/ Telekinetics/The Dragon\u2019s Touch </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now the mage can alter and invoke the energies she could only touch before. By adding Prime 2, she may conjure winds, fire, electricity, gravitational wells, and so forth. Combining this Rank with Life or Matter, she can transform people into electricity (Life 5/ Forces 3); change water into air (Forces 3/Matter 3), or attach elemental force to material forms \u2013 making them fly, pinning them to the ground, and having other, similar effects (generally with Life or Matter 3). And by adding an ephemeral Sphere to this Rank, she might erode or enhance energies (Entropy 3); manifest thoughts into energies (Mind 3); transmute spirit-stuff into physical energies (Spirit 3); or set triggers for energy fluctuations at some later interval (Time 4). </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this Rank, the scale of effect grows larger, now encompassing several dozen yards or a handful of characters.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now this is a tricky one. Again, there\u2019s only one real power here - transmuting forces - and I just realized it\u2019s not directly stated in the text, just the initial ability names. Apparently \u2018alter and invoke the energies she could only touch before\u2019 was supposed to mean that.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aside from that line everything else is a combination with other spheres. That\u2019s a problem because the suggestions range accurate, to inaccurate, to indecipherable. In particular, Forces 3 blurs the lines between the capabilities of Forces 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The upshot of all this is that I\u2019ll spend most of this section on dealing with contradictions and ambiguity. On that note, let me start with the most important:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction resolution - Forces 2 or Forces 3</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 2 can explicitly mute or amplify sound and flare fires, and by implication can enhance or suppress most forces. On several occasions, though, Forces 3 acts like suppressing and amplifying energies is a rank 3 power. While we could say that Forces 2 can only enhance and suppress heat and sound, and is limited to just redirecting all the other energies, I don't think that\u2019s reasonable.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead, we can focus on the fact that Forces 3, in addition to its new abilities, can do everything Forces 2 can but over a larger area. Thus, it is technically true that it can cause \u2018energy fluctuations\u2019 though it is generally more appropriate to say that is a Forces 2 ability, unless it exceeds the area limit of Forces 2. So:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Forces 2 Can Do but Up to a Few Dozen Yards in Area(???) </span></b><br /> <br /> That covers the times that Forces 3 is given Forces 2 powers without needlessly constraining Forces 2.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now on to the new ability:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Transmute Minor Forces (Transmute Minor Forces)</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this power a mage can turn one force into another, or with the help of other spheres, turn a force into something else, turn something else into a force, or conjure up a force from nowhere. Now this specifies minor forces, but that includes most forces we experience on a day to day basis.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Blocking Their Communications with Their Own Bullets</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can convert kinetic energy (say, of a Technocrat\u2019s bullets) into radio waves (say, the same frequencies they communicate on), thus reducing the damage of the bullets and disrupting communications. While this is a particular case, there are many times a mage may want less of one type of energy and more of another.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 3 also lists multiple conjunctional effects for this power. I\u2019m going to tackle them in order, except for one: Manifest thoughts into energies.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Manifest Thoughts into Energies (Forces 3/Mind 3)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The last time I took a trip through the Spheres, I missed the importance of this one. I correctly interpreted it as transmuting a thought or idea into energy, but I missed what that accomplishes. This is an alternative to Prime 2 for creating Forces from apparently nothing.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m so used to seeing Mind forced into psychic spells it doesn\u2019t belong in that it is honestly refreshing to find it actually having a use.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Change water into air (Forces 3/Matter 3)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Water to Air </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is allegedly Forces 3/Matter 3 to change water into air. Water and air are both forms of matter, so Forces is not involved. However, if we take this instead to mean water to wind, which has a kinetic component, Forces 3/Matter 3 makes sense.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Attach Elemental Force to Material Forms (Forces 3/Matter 3)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Attach Elemental Force</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or attach elemental force to material forms \u2013 making them fly, pinning them to the ground, and having other, similar effects (generally with Life or Matter 3). </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>From before, manipulation of forces is rank 2 unless the area gets to big.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This one is tricky, because the examples are of things that can be done with Forces 2. Indeed it looks exactly like the kind of effect that would be accomplished with locking, but with inflated spheres. The best explanation I have is that this is supposed to be a grafting effect. That is to say, the mage is creating a combination Forces/Life or Forces/Matter pattern. That would reasonably require Forces and the appropriate Pattern Sphere at transmutation levels. That would at least justify Forces 3/Life 3 for grafting a force into a frog, though it should be Forces 3/Life 5 for complex life, Forces 3/Matter 2 for simple objects, and Forces 3/Matter 4 for complex ones.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If it is a locked effect, though, the sphere requirements are suspiciously high. Matter 3 and Life 3 aren\u2019t contradicting the locking rules per se, as those never actually say what rank is required, and they don\u2019t contradict Matter or Life, because those don\u2019t cover locking ranks either. They do contradict the Common Magical Effects chart, though, which puts Levitation and Flight at Forces 2+/Life 2 or Forces 2+/Matter 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That\u2019s the best I\u2019ve found so far, anyways. Suggestions?</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Erode or Enhance Energies (Forces 3/Entropy 3)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction resolution - Enhance or Erode Forces</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>From before, manipulation of forces is rank 2, unless the area is too large.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A lot depends on what this means. Forces 2 can enhance or suppress energies with no need for additional spheres. Possibly, though, this is meant to replicate Entropy 3\u2019s ability to increase or decrease the rate something decays at, such as making a fire have a problem burning and go out faster, or making it burn more cleanly and efficiently so that it lasts longer, or making it more likely that the fuel source will collapse in a way that quickly makes it sputter out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, this is likely within the capabilities of Entropy 3 alone (see previous discussions in this thread). It also might be within the capacities of Forces 2 anyways. If neither, though, then maybe this is a valid way of accomplishing the effect?</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Set Time Triggers for Energy Fluctuations(Forces 3/Time 4)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity resolution - Time Triggers for Energy Fluctuations</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>From before, manipulation of forces is rank 2, unless the area is too large.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are two things this could mean. The first is energy effects on a time trigger. This would be things like flickering the lights at a certain time (Time 4/Forces 2) or having a car discharge it\u2019s kinetic energy as a lightning bolt at a certain time (Time 4/Forces 3).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is also possible that this is a trigger for some other event and the trigger event is the energy fluctuations. Here we have a problem, as there aren\u2019t clear instructions for how to set the required spheres for a trigger. That means it is up to the ST. I default to one rank higher than required for the mage himself to sense the trigger, so Forces 2. On the other hand, we could take the punishing requirement of \u2018setting the trigger takes the same spheres as making the trigger happen,\u2019 though that would still be Forces 2. Only if we go with the most punishing \u2018triggers cost whatever sphere governs the effect at <i>transmutation</i> levels\u2019 do we get to Forces 3. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T11:15:49-07:00","id":1550218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550213#post1550213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So would this be a fair description of how you see Entropy and weather: Entropy can influence the effects of the weather, but not the weather itself. So if the weather is already providing an effect, such as lightning, rain, or wind, Entropy can influence when and where that effect hits, but Entropy can't affect the weather pattern itself, and it can't make the weather produce an effect if it isn't already producing that effect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess it's a good description. I'd also add that Entropy couldn't influence large effects. A small gust of wind is ok, while huge strong winds aren't, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T11:26:44-07:00","id":1550219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550214#post1550214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Manifest Thoughts into Energies (Forces 3/Mind 3)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The last time I took a trip through the Spheres, I missed the importance of this one. I correctly interpreted it as transmuting a thought or idea into energy, but I missed what that accomplishes. This is an alternative to Prime 2 for creating Forces from apparently nothing.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, there are several alternatives of using Prime 2 with practically all other spheres. This one is a pretty good example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550214#post1550214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If it is a locked effect, though, the sphere requirements are suspiciously high. Matter 3 and Life 3 aren\u2019t contradicting the locking rules per se, as those never actually say what rank is required, and they don\u2019t contradict Matter or Life, because those don\u2019t cover locking ranks either. They do contradict the Common Magical Effects chart, though, which puts Levitation and Flight at Forces 2+/Life 2 or Forces 2+/Matter 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That\u2019s the best I\u2019ve found so far, anyways. Suggestions?</span> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>That one is locking, which requires rank 2 of the pattern of the locked subject. It is just wrong in the description, should be Life or Matter 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550214#post1550214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Erode or Enhance Energies (Forces 3/Entropy 3)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction resolution - Enhance or Erode Forces </i></span></span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Both Forces 2 or Entropy 3 can do that alone. Another example of the author not caring enough for the rules\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550214#post1550214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Set Time Triggers for Energy Fluctuations(Forces 3/Time 4)</i></b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Afaik, spell triggers require Time 2 and rank 2 of the trigerring condition, besides the spell itself.<br /> <br /> So, suspending a Forces spell is Time 4+ Forces 2 and the lightning per ae requires Forcea 3+Prime 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-17-2025, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T12:16:12-07:00","id":1550223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550218#post1550218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd also add that Entropy couldn't influence large effects. A small gust of wind is ok, while huge strong winds aren't, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most of your concerns about <b>Entropy</b>, specially this, are better modeled by increasing the necessary successes than by simply not letting <b>Entropy</b> do the thing.<br /> <br /> Even if one Sphere can do the same another can, it doesn't means it does with the same ease, or even that it is practical at all to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T12:40:43-07:00","id":1550225,"title":"","content":"Also to be honest dumping everything in forces to lvls 1-3 and then only increasing scale seems like they run out of ideas developing it. Weather manipulation should be Forces 2 at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T10:44:25-07:00","id":1550243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550223#post1550223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think most of your concerns about <b>Entropy</b>, specially this, are better modeled by increasing the necessary successes than by simply not letting <b>Entropy</b> do the thing.<br /> <br /> Even if one Sphere can do the same another can, it doesn't means it does with the same ease, or even that it is practical at all to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Forces 3 control weather with more successes? Can Mind 3 mind control with more successes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T14:36:21-07:00","id":1550247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550243#post1550243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can Forces 3 control weather with more successes? Can Mind 3 mind control with more successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It should at 2 to be fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T06:41:04-07:00","id":1550265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550243#post1550243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can Forces 3 control weather with more successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If the storm in question is only a few yards in diameter. That\u2019s the main barrier in M20. Maybe the intent was that weather manipulation should only start at Forces 4, but as written Forces 2+ can manipulate every relevant energy and it has no restrictions on power, number of energies, or complexity. The only given limit is area.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T08:26:07-07:00","id":1550270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550265#post1550265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. If the storm in question is only a few yards in diameter. That\u2019s the main barrier in M20. Maybe the intent was that weather manipulation should only start at Forces 4, but as written Forces 2+ can manipulate every relevant energy and it has no restrictions on power, number of energies, or complexity. The only given limit is area.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's about the same as controling a bit of wind or a single lightning. I already said that Entropy can do that (provided the conditions are already there).<br /> <br /> My point is that the number of successes cannot overlap a higher sphere rank. There are still limitations of ranks, and since there are not &quot;several dozen yards&quot; storms, you can't control weather.<br /> <br /> I guess maybe you could create a mini storm with Forces 3, but it would definitely be vulgar, since this doesn't exist\u2026<br /> <br /> PS: If the limitations are size only, this means that Forces 3 can mess with nuclear energy? I had the impression that weather is written as Forces 4 only, although this one makes sense due to the size of a storm, but nuclear control being Forces 5 only makes no sense.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll wait till you get to rank 5 lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-19-2025, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T12:03:36-07:00","id":1550275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550270#post1550270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's about the same as controling a bit of wind or a single lightning. I already said that Entropy can do that (provided the conditions are already there).<br /> <br /> My point is that the number of successes cannot overlap a higher sphere rank. There are still limitations of ranks, and since there are not &quot;several dozen yards&quot; storms, you can't control weather.<br /> <br /> I guess maybe you could create a mini storm with Forces 3, but it would definitely be vulgar, since this doesn't exist\u2026<br /> <br /> PS: If the limitations are size only, this means that Forces 3 can mess with nuclear energy? I had the impression that weather is written as Forces 4 only, although this one makes sense due to the size of a storm, but nuclear control being Forces 5 only makes no sense.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll wait till you get to rank 5 lol</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fairly certain that previous editions locked specific forces behind Forces 4 and 5, and weather was one of them. M20, though, just makes Forces 4 have the exact same powers as earlier ranks but at wider areas. That's the stated way controlling weather works.<br /> <br /> Here, I'll go ahead and post Forces 4 and 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T12:07:06-07:00","id":1550276,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Control Major Forces/ Gift of Zeus/Weather-Witching </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Larger Effects become possible. Our mage may now use the lower-Rank Effects over larger areas \u2013 a mile or more \u2013 to change weather patterns; conjure darkness; drop or raise temperatures; protect locations\u2026 or destroy them; and otherwise employ the previous levels on a much greater scale. For obvious reasons, such Effects tend to be vulgar and demand many successes to achieve.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this point Forces gets a little thin. Many of the high-level Forces effects are just low-level Forces effects but bigger. All of them, in fact. Previous editions would lock certain \u2018major\u2019 forces, like radiation and nuclear blasts, behind Forces 4. There are indications this is still meant to be the case, but none in the actual sphere writeups.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some STs will also put more complex workings into Forces 4, but on a direct read there is no indication of that here. Some also limit Forces 2 to single forces while effects that handle multiple forces are in 4, kind of like Matter\u2019s progression. Again, it\u2019s not in the text here or there.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The main features of Forces 4 are:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weather Control (Weather Witching)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One specific ability that really needed Forces 4 scales to accomplish is weather manipulation. Few pieces of weather are easily restricted to a handful of yards. Note that there is still a range limit here, so the really large storms have to wait until Forces 5, but there are still many weather effects that are possible on the Forces 4 scale. There are also a handful that are arguably possible at earlier ranks.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Forces 2 and 3 Can Do But Up to a Mile or More(???) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a common grammatical pitfall. On a technical level, there\u2019s no upper bound here; a thousand miles is \u2018a mile or more.\u2019 Here, though, I think it\u2019s meant to be a representative area, so we should take this to mean that Forces 4 can act over areas miles in radius, not hundreds or thousands of miles. Still, technically there is no actual limit, so STs should be prepared in case that argument is raised.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also note that this specifically scales Forces 2 and 3 up to this range, so even though Forces 4 is not, itself, a transmutation rank, it scales up Forces 3, which is.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Graft Kaiju</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage wanted to make a city smashing monster with giant wings of fire, this would be the level of Forces necessary to graft energy wings of that size to a living pattern. Life 3 or 5 would also be necessary depending on type of kaiju.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Control Major Forces (Control Major Forces)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most forces that we interact with regularly are accessed with Forces 2, but there are a few that are so exotic or powerful that mages can only access them at rank 4. What these are, offhand, I don\u2019t know as M20 doesn\u2019t list any.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, if a Master of Forces created a brand new force with Forces 5, Forces 4 should be capable of manipulating it, in theory.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T12:12:37-07:00","id":1550278,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Transmute Major Forces/Conjuring Infernos</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With godlike power, a Forces Master works her Will upon vast areas. She can conjure tornados on a clear day, calm tides, and ignite the very air into a firestorm. Such mages earn the title \u201cNuke,\u201d though few of them survive long enough to enjoy it. It\u2019s easier to invoke such forces under the right conditions, of course \u2013 a cold snap comes more easily in winter than in summer - and such radical alterations have repercussions that often outlast the original Effect. In game terms, massive Forces spells should disrupt the weather and leave massive Resonance echoes behind. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once again, the purpose is muddled as all the examples are possible at Forces 4, Forces 5 is just a much larger area. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Forces 2, 3, and 4 Can Do but With No Limit (???) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2018Vast areas\u2019 opens up the area to pretty much anything, limited only by successes. This could be interpreted to include some truly obscene distances. Consider the phrase \u2018the vastness of space,\u2019 for instance. Since there is no sphere above this unless optional archmastery spheres are used, this time the lack of limit makes sense.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmute Major Forces (Transmute Major Forces)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Convert one force into another or, with other spheres, into other patterns. This time there are no restrictions on size and if there are any exotic forces beyond the reach of Forces 2 or 3, they are available here. That\u2019s a big if, though, because there\u2019s still no indication of any such force.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When we get to rank 5 there shouldn\u2019t be much off limits.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Exotic Forces (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Forces 5, mages should be able to generate Forces that don\u2019t actually exist, like gravity that only attracts chickens, sounds that only interact with the ears of small mammals, etc.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Forces 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. The existence of Archspheres could change this, but they aren\u2019t listed in M20.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T08:41:18-07:00","id":1550285,"title":"","content":"Well, I looked over M20 and couldn't find anything restricting nuclear manipulation to Forces 5. Indeed Forces 4 and 5 seems to only increase the range of effects. And probably that's why, in earlier editions, nuclear powers were Forces 5: because nuclear blasts are just too damn big. <br /> However, one could manipulate the strong and weak forces without creating such a huge mess, and that would be possible with Forces 3. The same applies yo weather (although, again, that would be probably vulgar, making a few dozen yards storm with lightning and everything for example).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550278#post1550278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Exotic Forces (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Forces 5, mages should be able to generate Forces that don\u2019t actually exist, like gravity that only attracts chickens, sounds that only interact with the ears of small mammals, etc.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I never thought about creating a new Force\u2026 Your examples are easily achievable with Forces 3+Life 2. What would be the difference with Forces 5? Just not requiring Life? The range (obviously)?<br /> And why is it a Forces 5 to create new forces?<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, about the ranges, the book is extremely vague in the definitions:<br /> <br /> \u2022 No description of range<br /> \u2022\u2022 20 feet (6 meters) or less<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 several dozen yards<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 a mile or more<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 no limit<br /> <br /> This means that Forces 3 can affect things up to a mile? A mile is 146 dozen yards. 146 are several dozen yards. So, what is <b>really</b> the are limits of Forces 3?<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> The very same applies for Forces 4, except that it's harder to know, since rank 5 has no restrictions. So, we could say rank 3 can go up to 1 mile (with a Great Work ritual with tons of successes). But we dont know the limits of rank 4, since rank 5 should be able to affect\u2026infinity?<br /> <br /> Regarding rank 1, I'd like to know how the increased range would work mechanically, like how far each success on Arete can zoom the mage sight/hearing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T13:12:06-07:00","id":1550289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550285#post1550285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why is it a Forces 5 to create new forces?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would think by extrapolating from Matter 5 being able to create magical materials and Life 5 creating supernatural creatures. Also, this was a Forces 9! effect on MotA - most likely because of it's <i>reach</i> - if we're working under the assumption lvls 5 can do everything lvls 6-9 could, it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never thought about creating a new Force\u2026 Your examples are easily achievable with Forces 3+Life 2. What would be the difference with Forces 5? Just not requiring Life? The range (obviously)? </div> </div> </div>Recently I had a talk about this very subject about Matter 5. Why create matter that repels bullets with Matter 5 (it's among the examples, if I'm not mistaken) when Forces 2/Matter2 can make you a vest that repels bullets?.<br /> <br /> The answer I gave it's that locking an effect locks the effect to a pattern. It creates a Trinket. Magical materials have their own properties that may be present in different patterns.<br /> <br /> A good example it's Primium (Matter 5/Prime 3). Probably you could make a helmet that emits an anty-magick aura with Matter 2+ Prime, but you can't smelt it and make a sword that cuts trough magick. With Primium you can. This is good for a big organization, such as The Technocracy, which Masters can create a chunk of it, and then distribute the material so lesser scientists do whatever they want with it, from coating their walls to protect a Construct to making cyborgs with it.<br /> <br /> An example it occurs to me about what you could do if we extrapolate with Forces:<br /> <br /> A primitivist Forces mage could combine Forces with Matter, maybe Life, and make a supernatural flame that only burns man-made materials. Then use it to lit a house on a town he hates, and the fire could preserve this property as it grows bigger - burning trough houses and roads while leaving plants and animals relatively alone (though this won't protect from falling debris and such).<br /> <br /> Now, he could just do this at once with a big AoE &quot;smite&quot;, and less chances of the fire being stopped (he has Forces 5!).<br /> <br /> Not doing things the simple way might have some situational advantage. Like, you can save the &quot;special flame&quot; burning somewhere, as if it was an artifact, and use it again. Also big spells can be detected and traced, maybe the magical flame can be created on a safe place, then you can let it out trough less bombastic means, maybe give it to someone else, and it's own static magic won't be easy to detect until it's already too big to do anything about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T14:02:33-07:00","id":1550291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550285#post1550285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I looked over M20 and couldn't find anything restricting nuclear manipulation to Forces 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because it doesn't make sense anymore.<br /> <br /> Back in the day Radiation<sup>TM</sup> was the scariest thing around. And it was anathema to the Green movement, which even before Werewolf was very influential to WoD. It was also seen as almost unnatural, something only seen in its high-end applications.<br /> <br /> As a result, in the game it was the apex of Wyrm-Power, something that seared body, mind and soul, leaving blights in the land that wouldn't ever be receptive to life again.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, while most people still fear and doesn't understand shit about it, it doesn't occupy the same conceptual space anymore, more people (including RPG players) have access to info on how it works, and the Green movement is thorn on the matter, with an increasing faction defending nuclear power as the better alternative we have for now.<br /> <br /> Given that in practice radiation isn't really all that uncommon, nor particularly deadlier than the other forces/energies in similar proportions, it would just be an arbitrary obstruction in the way of making a working X-Ray machine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550285#post1550285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never thought about creating a new Force\u2026 Your examples are easily achievable with Forces 3+Life 2. What would be the difference with Forces 5? Just not requiring Life? The range (obviously)?<br /> And why is it a Forces 5 to create new forces?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a new idea for me too, but an interesting one.<br /> <br /> Being able to create those weird forces without relying on other Spheres isn't a bad deal, as most Mages won't have every Sphere at 2 or more by the time they get one at 5. But I think the best thing about &quot;creating a new Force&quot; is that you can prescribe means through which it spreads, and then let it go its own way.\u200b<br /> <br /> And it makes sense to be on 5. It's the level for creating new materials with Matter, and it isn't in any other level. 5 should be the level where you do anything within that Sphere, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550285#post1550285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bRegarding rank 1, I'd like to know how the increased range would work mechanically, like how far each success on Arete can zoom the mage sight/hearing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it applies to Rank 1. Perception effects are still limited to your actual perception range, which can only increase with Correspondence or with specific effects to enhance perception. It would be strange for Forces to be the exception where you notice things farther away just through the Sphere level you use.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, Forces is probably your best bet to enhance perception range through effects that create lenses and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T15:15:04-07:00","id":1550293,"title":"","content":"There's also increasing scientific literacy in the general population to know that &quot;radiation&quot; is a very broad category of energy (which includes light and heat). As has been discussed in a different thread, the books generally indicate that ionizing radiation is more special than non-ionizing radiation... which doesn't really make the Sphere very coherent but is at least a more functional definition and could at least have some basis to it (energy that starts mucking up the energies of other Patterns the way ionizing radiation does at least falls within the general concept of how the Spheres work to say is more complicated - thus higher ranked - than non-ionizing interactions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T15:54:37-07:00","id":1550294,"title":"","content":"Good answers from all. I agree with everything. <br /> <br /> So, what advantages would manipulating nuclear forces with Forces 3 grant?<br /> <br /> I mean, small nuclear blasts are still limited to the damage table. Radiation being able to pass through most matter could also be done with electromagnetic waves (gamma rays are radiatiom and EM waves).<br /> <br /> So, what exactly does controling nuclear forces brings to the table that Forces 3 already haven't? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550291#post1550291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it applies to Rank 1. Perception effects are still limited to your actual perception range, which can only increase with Correspondence or with specific effects to enhance perception. It would be strange for Forces to be the exception where you notice things farther away just through the Sphere level you use.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, Forces is probably your best bet to enhance perception range through effects that create lenses and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are completely right. Still, how far could Forces 2 bend, amplify, manipulate light rays or sound waves to extend the mage senses? Is there a per success rule or example?<br /> <br /> PS: Monteparmas, wdym bu creating a force and &quot;let it go its own way&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T11:13:53-07:00","id":1550301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550294#post1550294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what advantages would manipulating nuclear forces with Forces 3 grant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much, which is precisely why gatekeeping it behind Forces 5 was a nonsensical idea, and why the book simply chose to say nothing about it.<br /> <br /> <b>IF</b> it brought something special to the game, then the old decision on making it super-duper-special and level 5 would be a relevant decision. It isn't.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that this isn't just about a regular Mage using nuclear power and radiation in any of its myriad forms. It is about being able to use your Magic on radiation you find during the game. It's also about a Mage whose Paradigm uses nuclear power for certain tasks being able to work within their beliefs like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Other than that, being limited in the same way as other forces, like by the damage table, is kind of the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550294#post1550294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are completely right. Still, how far could Forces 2 bend, amplify, manipulate light rays or sound waves to extend the mage senses? Is there a per success rule or example?</div> </div> </div> </div>None I can think of, but we do have mundane equipment that does that. Binoculars and telescopes do exactly that to light, and that using just light that's already within reach (the amplified image is just light that reached the lenses). Amplification effects like that shouldn't be too hard to do, the most complex ones would just have to filter information on top of amplifying it.<br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;table&quot; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> arrived at is about the area of effect, not reach. All in all, Forces can be used to improve your perception, but it is cumbersome in comparison with Correspondence. Not too hard to do, but a lot of work for little gain, specially when you can do the same with mundane equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550294#post1550294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bPS: Monteparmas, wdym bu creating a force and &quot;let it go its own way&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> explained it better than me, but fire spreads, light excites materials, kinetic energy transfers upon impact. Forces interact with the environment, and depending on their nature they either transfer, spread or transform. Your artificial force will do the same, within your new parameters, and never ceasing to be how you made it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T18:30:18-07:00","id":1550306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550301#post1550301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None I can think of, but we do have mundane equipment that does that. Binoculars and telescopes do exactly that to light, and that using just light that's already within reach (the amplified image is just light that reached the lenses). Amplification effects like that shouldn't be too hard to do, the most complex ones would just have to filter information on top of amplifying it.<br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;table&quot; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> arrived at is about the area of effect, not reach. All in all, Forces can be used to improve your perception, but it is cumbersome in comparison with Correspondence. Not too hard to do, but a lot of work for little gain, specially when you can do the same with mundane equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, telescopes and binoculars have huge ranges as long as there isn't anything blocking the light path (wich isn't an issue for Forces 2 bending light). So maybe a couple successes should be enough to anywhere in several hundred kilometers range. I'd only ask for nore successes if a lot of bending is required. Bending seems to be the limits and not distance per se.<br /> <br /> So, like 3 successes and you can see what is happening in a room inside a building far, far away, considering you just have to make the light get out of the building and go into a straight line to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the nuclear forces manipulation, I made a quick search and there are lots of things that could be accomplished by it. The thing is that the majority of them is dangerously close to Matter, so I'd require a lot of successes. I guess about double that is required for Matter. In short, by manipulating the strong and weak nuclear forces (considering your paradigm includes them):<br /> <br /> - Disitegrate objects (and beings) by simply removing the strong nuclear force and letting attoms be undone.<br /> <br /> - Generate energy from mass (e=mc\u00b2). That is a good one to avoid needing Prime 2, although you would need mass to be undone<br /> <br /> - Make objects radioactive or radiocative objets non-radioactive<br /> <br /> - Make object superstable, lightweight and nigh indestructible objects<br /> <br /> - Change objects shapes and/or composition, by manipulating nuclear bonds/position (EM force) and changing nuclei (weak and strong forces) respectively.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T20:18:45-07:00","id":1550309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550306#post1550306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, telescopes and binoculars have huge ranges as long as there isn't anything blocking the light path (wich isn't an issue for Forces 2 bending light). So maybe a couple successes should be enough to anywhere in several hundred kilometers range. I'd only ask for nore successes if a lot of bending is required. Bending seems to be the limits and not distance per se.<br /> <br /> So, like 3 successes and you can see what is happening in a room inside a building far, far away, considering you just have to make the light get out of the building and go into a straight line to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say each &quot;mirror&quot; you make has to be &quot;in reach&quot; of the spell, so if you need more than one, then you need multiple castings to build your chain. That's by itself plenty of limitations for the entrepreneur Forces user who wants to ditch Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550306#post1550306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the nuclear forces manipulation, I made a quick search and there are lots of things that could be accomplished by it. The thing is that the majority of them is dangerously close to Matter, so I'd require a lot of successes. I guess about double that is required for Matter. In short, by manipulating the strong and weak nuclear forces (considering your paradigm includes them):</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I prefer to stick to <b>radiation</b> instead of <b>nuclear force</b>. The <b>four forces</b> are a physics concept, not the game's concept of <b>Forces</b> as it is manipulated by the Sphere. So Forces control the radiation (which is actually a range of phenomena, many of them involving charged particles instead of &quot;pure&quot; energy, but heck, fire isn't an energy either, it's a chemical reaction), not the Nuclear Forces <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> Instead, the two nuclear forces are part of the belief system of the Mage when using Matter to do that stuff. If you let Forces directly control any force at all at a subatomic level, then you'll let the Mage do anything Matter does, so as a rule of thumb the Mage can cause radiation that includes charged particles, but can't otherwise control <b>Forces</b> at a subatomic level, only at the macro level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T22:03:05-07:00","id":1550310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550309#post1550309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say each &quot;mirror&quot; you make has to be &quot;in reach&quot; of the spell, so if you need more than one, then you need multiple castings to build your chain. That's by itself plenty of limitations for the entrepreneur Forces user who wants to ditch Correspondence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wdym by &quot;mirror&quot;? Each bending? I can see a single spell bending light more than once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550309#post1550309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I prefer to stick to <b>radiation</b> instead of <b>nuclear force</b>. The <b>four forces</b> are a physics concept, not the game's concept of <b>Forces</b> as it is manipulated by the Sphere. So Forces control the radiation (which is actually a range of phenomena, many of them involving charged particles instead of &quot;pure&quot; energy, but heck, fire isn't an energy either, it's a chemical reaction), not the Nuclear Forces <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> Instead, the two nuclear forces are part of the belief system of the Mage when using Matter to do that stuff. If you let Forces directly control any force at all at a subatomic level, then you'll let the Mage do anything Matter does, so as a rule of thumb the Mage can cause radiation that includes charged particles, but can't otherwise control <b>Forces</b> at a subatomic level, only at the macro level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, forces should definitely control the four fundamental forces (and more). I understand your point of the forces being a scientific paradigm thing, but Gravity is present in the sphere text and it seems you can manipulate it independently of your paradigm, so why not the weak and strong forces as well (specially if you have a scientific paradigm)?<br /> <br /> That is one thing I dislike about some people views about the settings, as if entire Reality depends on each mage's paradigm, while I believe that is not true. What I read from thre books, is that there are fixed Reality traits (like gravity) that can be bent by magick. Regardless of your paradigm, the fundamental forces does exist\u2026<br /> <br /> PS: radiation is still a physics concept that involves atoms, electrons etc. The game rules itself is based on a somewhat physics concept","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T02:15:11-07:00","id":1550314,"title":"","content":"There is definitely a certain amount of there being a difference between &quot;My Focus is built around compelling spirits to enact my will, but a fireball is still Forces 3/Prime 2,&quot; and, &quot;I'm trying to use Spirit 3 to convince a fire-spirit to burn something,&quot; going on here.<br /> <br /> While Forces can certainly influence fundamental subatomic interactions (gravitation and EM are already explicitly so), there's still a difference between manipulating the gravitational interaction between a person and the Earth (allowing for levitation/flight, or pressing someone into the ground) with just forces, and completely altering a human's personal gravity well (would require Life to lock on at a minimum if not more-so as you're altering the Forces within a Life pattern).<br /> <br /> Unraveling a target by destroying the forces holding their atoms together just sounds like a basic Forces attack with a unique choice of energy due to Focus rather than anything else. Trying to completely restructure aluminum into combat viable steel without using Matter would - like cajoling a fire-spirit into burning something - require a specific set of circumstances where you can control such interactions on a fine basis without any interference or any collateral impact (and frankly without Mind or Time, even that's a bit of a stretch considering how fast everything is going at that scale). The idea that you could go beyond that into fictional hypertech materials with just Forces is pushing it... manipulating strong and weak interactions isn't going to let you make Vibranium or Adamantium because if they could, those materials would actually exist. Convincing a fire-spirit to burn something for you with Spirit doesn't mean you can get the spirit to exceed its own capabilities.<br /> <br /> I don't have much problem with the idea that a Forces 5 character that's done the work to create a highly specific prepared ritual, can copy what a Matter 2 or 3 mage could do with a fraction of the successes and no need of all those extra steps. Just like I don't mind if a Spirit focused mage puts in the work to rely on spirits to do stuff they don't have the Spheres (or don't want to risk the Paradox) to do. The costs are generally going to avoid breaking the game by letting one Sphere do too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T20:52:19-07:00","id":1550329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550314#post1550314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is definitely a certain amount of there being a difference between &quot;My Focus is built around compelling spirits to enact my will, but a fireball is still Forces 3/Prime 2,&quot; and, &quot;I'm trying to use Spirit 3 to convince a fire-spirit to burn something,&quot; going on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I don't think I got what your point is here. When talking about rules, I tend to try my best to &quot;ignore&quot; paradigm, in the sense that &quot;let's all agree that we are talking about a paradigm that supports that&quot;. Saying that, I believe both your statements are true. The default fireball does requires Forces+Prime and Spirit can summon a fire spirit to burn something. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550314#post1550314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Forces can certainly influence fundamental subatomic interactions (gravitation and EM are already explicitly so), there's still a difference between manipulating the gravitational interaction between a person and the Earth (allowing for levitation/flight, or pressing someone into the ground) with just forces, and completely altering a human's personal gravity well (would require Life to lock on at a minimum if not more-so as you're altering the Forces within a Life pattern).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. You can change gravity in an area (which would affect your target if he's inside that area) or you could directly affect the pattern's gravity which would require locking if you want to stick with the target. You wouldn't need Life/Matter to affect someone's/something's nuclear forces within an area, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550314#post1550314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unraveling a target by destroying the forces holding their atoms together just sounds like a basic Forces attack with a unique choice of energy due to Focus rather than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also agree. I would translate that attack as the damage table for living beings. For objects something similar to the core damaging objects rules, but I'd make it easier as you are not really breaking them with brute force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550314#post1550314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to completely restructure aluminum into combat viable steel without using Matter would - like cajoling a fire-spirit into burning something - require a specific set of circumstances where you can control such interactions on a fine basis without any interference or any collateral impact (and frankly without Mind or Time, even that's a bit of a stretch considering how fast everything is going at that scale). The idea that you could go beyond that into fictional hypertech materials with just Forces is pushing it... manipulating strong and weak interactions isn't going to let you make Vibranium or Adamantium because if they could, those materials would actually exist. Convincing a fire-spirit to burn something for you with Spirit doesn't mean you can get the spirit to exceed its own capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we are in a paradigm (focus) conversarion. The amount of time and effort and how it will be done depends on paradigm. But limiting that to labs and high tech seems wrong (if that's what you mean). The time and effort are translated into the mage's instruments and the required successes (which wouldn't be few for those feats I listed, imo).<br /> <br /> And tbh, Vibranium and Adamantium do exist in mage, they are Trinkets or Wonders. Simply magickally modified objects to last. <br /> <br /> The difference from your Spirit analogy is that you need to find a fire spirit to control. The nuclear forces are just there already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550314#post1550314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have much problem with the idea that a Forces 5 character that's done the work to create a highly specific prepared ritual, can copy what a Matter 2 or 3 mage could do with a fraction of the successes and no need of all those extra steps. Just like I don't mind if a Spirit focused mage puts in the work to rely on spirits to do stuff they don't have the Spheres (or don't want to risk the Paradox) to do. The costs are generally going to avoid breaking the game by letting one Sphere do too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, you don't need Forces 5, as per M20. And the in-game effort will depend on the paradigm, not being limited by technology (although if the mage doesn't believe in nuclear forces, he couldn't manipulate them). And I agree on the succeeses, it should require more successes than Matter due to complexity of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T03:00:10-07:00","id":1550332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550329#post1550329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't think I got what your point is here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to understand but assume that there's something I didn't say:<br /> <br /> &quot;The default fireball does requires Forces+Prime and Spirit can summon a fire spirit to burn something.&quot;<br /> <br /> That was my point, though I bring it up because both can be true. Forces should be able to manipulate nuclear interactions because those are energetic systems, and this could encroach on Matter, but like the fire ball vs. spirit issue, each has it's own set of considerations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You wouldn't need Life/Matter to affect someone's/something's nuclear forces within an area, though. </div> </div> </div>Well, as you seem to agree to, there are limits to this. Disrupting strong force interactions to break something apart is different from altering strong and weak force interactions until atoms transmute into different atoms with different properties. Just like reducing gravity in an area is different than giving a living thing the ability to levitate.<br /> <br /> [quote]...but I'd make it easier as you are not really breaking them with brute force.<br /> <br /> I struggle to consider this anything but the most brute force Forces attack possible. You are talking about literally ripping apart the bonds that hold elementary particles that make up atoms together to destroy something. There is no more &quot;brute&quot; than just shredding a target apart. There's no finesse. There's no by products that are left in a repurposable form. You used the word &quot;disintegrate&quot; and that's entirely appropriate. It's just destruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The amount of time and effort and how it will be done depends on paradigm. But limiting that to labs and high tech seems wrong (if that's what you mean). The time and effort are translated into the mage's instruments and the required successes (which wouldn't be few for those feats I listed, imo). </div> </div> </div>I... don't think you really understand what it would mean to attempt to change a single atom, let alone a whole object's worth of atoms, from one set of elements to another by just manipulating strong and weak interactions. Besides the very idea being a matter of Focus in the first place (the current model of subatomic elementary particles and interactions was only considered proven scientifically 13 years ago, before that this was all hypothetical in the minds of physicists and there was a lot of hand wringing around the Higgs boson tests about what it would mean if they couldn't confirm its existence), the sheer mental processing you're talking about is beyond what a human mind could handle. All of the variables you'd need to adjust are constantly in flux. The interaction fields within an atom are generated by constant changes between states, and those are constantly being influenced by the fields of every nearby quantum field on top of it. This extends beyond the human mind... it's literally the point of Heisenberg's uncertainty principle. You're dealing with paired properties that cannot be simultaneously known. And multiples of them.<br /> <br /> Can magic make up for that? Sure. But I don't see how Forces can by itself. That's my point about needing an appropriately prepared space. It doesn't matter what the character's style is, if you're trying to just use Forces you need a dedicated space to isolate your target and active measures to keep everything in place. I don't care if it's magic circles or a hypertech lab. The energies you're trying to control with Forces are insanely complicated and delicate. It's one thing to talk about taking a sledgehammer to them and breaking them, it's an entirely different matter to be talking about doing the equivalent of a dozen cardiac bypass surgeries a nanosecond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And tbh, Vibranium and Adamantium do exist in mage, they are Trinkets or Wonders. Simply magickally modified objects to last. </div> </div> </div>The equivocation is noted and not appreciated.<br /> <br /> Do they exist in Mage due to the natural functions of atomic interactions? If no, my point stands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference from your Spirit analogy is that you need to find a fire spirit to control. The nuclear forces are just there already. </div> </div> </div>Hence I didn't compare it to summoning a spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, you don't need Forces 5, as per M20. </div> </div> </div>Technically, M20 doesn't say either way. As per the heuristic at the start of this thread, if M20 is unclear about something, and previous editions offer clarity, they are valid sources. M20 never defines what the line between minor and major Forces patterns is. Previous editions clearly put manipulating radioactivity (and by necessity strong and weak interactions) into the major category. M20 doesn't say you don't need Forces 5, M20 doesn't say anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T09:47:32-07:00","id":1550337,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Life</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview: </b>Living Things and Biology</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Anything with enough living cells in it to transplant, preserve, or cultivate counts as Life, if it has passed that point it is Matter. This line seems to vary over the book, but that's the distinction given here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 - Life attacks naturally inflict Aggravated Damage.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 - Any radical alteration that is not part of a creature\u2019s original pattern causes Pattern Bleed unless the change is made permanent or the target is supplied with quintessence.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T09:58:32-07:00","id":1550339,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Sense Life </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basic Life knowledge allows a person to read the presence and health of nearby life-forms. With such knowledge, the mage can discern a living being\u2019s age, sex, and overall health. By combining those perceptions with other Spheres, he can also sense distant organisms (Correspondence 2), guess their potential for sickness or misfortune (Entropy 1), perceive them through past or future states (Time 2), or read the streams of Quintessence that bind them to the universe (Prime 1). </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> This is one of the shorter rank 1 sections and it is padded out with conjunctional effects. Nevertheless, the two main abilities are quite versatile:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Nearby Life (Sense Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can sense the presence and patterns of nearby lifeforms regardless of visibility. As with many sphere senses, we can assume the information can be curated in some way, such that the mage can sense the ubiquitous surrounding bacteria but is not overwhelmed by the sheer amount.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Changed: Recognize Non-life</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In being able to sense life, a mage should also be able to tell when something he expects to show up on Life senses doesn\u2019t fully. That is, if he\u2019s looking at a wax statue, or a vampire, or an animatronic, or something else that looks alive by his other senses, Life can tell him that it isn\u2019t alive in the classic sense. This wouldn\u2019t tell him much about why it isn\u2019t, that still requires other spheres. This also wouldn\u2019t detect strangeness from things that are fully alive and have special properties.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vital Statistics (Sense Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also use Life 1 to sense biological information about nearby lifeforms. The examples include demographic data like age and sex, but should also reasonably include things like pulse rate, blood pressure and really anything that can be measured about a life form.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Replacement: A Certain Kind of Scientific Mood Ring <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a></i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By parsing the various physiological reactions of the target, the mage can get a general sense of their mood and preparedness for action. Thes will give a mage an advantage in social situations, as well as advanced notice if the target is preparing for physical action.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Human Polygraph Machine</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also read all the vital statistics that a polygraph test reads, like pulse, blood pressure, breathing rate, and skin conductivity. This wouldn\u2019t tell a mage if someone is lying, it would give him the results a real polygraph test would which, if he had the skill to read one, would be exactly as accurate as a real polygraph. How accurate that is depends on the story. Realistically, they are suspect, but many a movie treats them as nigh infallible, so depending on ST this might be quite a useful power.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Added: Sense Natural Weapons</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can use Life 1 to sense the various offensive (and for that matter, defensive) capabilities that a target has. This can tell a mage the abilities of creatures he's not familiar with, as well as hidden weapons like retractable claws and venom. This normally only applies to natural weapons, though with enough successes a mage may be able to detect a non-living weapon hidden within (not on, within) a pattern.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Effects</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It doesn\u2019t usually work well when M20 pads out the capabilities of spheres by tacking on well-known augments. Casting through space and time is one of the signature purposes of Correspondence and Time respectively. It\u2019s not wrong to say this is a combo, it just is a combo for almost every possible spell and it doesn\u2019t say much about Life 1. I\u2019m also struggling to see what Entropy is adding here, although if the text was \u2018sickness <i>and</i> misfortune\u2019 that would make more sense.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deathsight, Life Edition (Sense Life + Sense Fortune) Life 1 / Entropy 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Sickness and Misfortune</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At first glance it seems like Entropy can do this on its own and Life can do most of it. However, they do pair well. A mage can sense the health of a target with Life 1, as well as the strength of their immune system. He can sense their likelihood of being exposed to sickness, or developing a disease by chance, or being injured with Entropy. The two together can sense both, creating an ability something like a Wraith\u2019s Deathsight</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One With the Living Quintessence (Sense Life + Sense ???) Life 1 / Prime 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Bindings of the Universe</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think the big problem here is that this doesn\u2019t appear to be a Prime augment to Life, but a Life augment to Prime. Reading Prime 1 carefully, it doesn\u2019t actually mention the ability to see the flows of quintessence within patterns. We could take this to mean that seeing the quintessence within patterns requires a pattern sphere. This could also be pure padding. What I'd most want to see is what the main utility of this is.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Missing?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Added: Detect Life Augmentation (Sense Life)</b><br /> <br /> Many Spheres have the ability to detect uses of that Sphere. It's unclear if Pattern Spheres normally can, and Life is not specifically given this capacity but... the existence of Pattern bleed shows that there is some important difference between an untouched pattern and a pattern that has been altered. It is reasonable that Life should be able to detect this difference, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> The full capabilities of this would be up to the ST, but it is worth noting that if this ability is based on the disparity that causes pattern bleed it would be harder to sense changes that don't cause that bleed.<br /> <br /> Alternately, this could be the important use of <b>One With the Living Quintessence</b> above.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-24-2025, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T11:48:04-07:00","id":1550342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550332#post1550332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as you seem to agree to, there are limits to this. Disrupting strong force interactions to break something apart is different from altering strong and weak force interactions until atoms transmute into different atoms with different properties. Just like reducing gravity in an area is different than giving a living thing the ability to levitate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, definitely. Disrupting doesn't need fine control while transmuting or reshaping does. That is translated into more successes needed. I wouldn't compare to giving a living thing the ability to levitate because that requires locking to the pattern.<br /> <br /> A better analogy would be to push something with full force versus picking a lock with telekinesis. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550332#post1550332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I struggle to consider this anything but the most brute force Forces attack possible. You are talking about literally ripping apart the bonds that hold elementary particles that make up atoms together to destroy something. There is no more &quot;brute&quot; than just shredding a target apart. There's no finesse. There's no by products that are left in a repurposable form. You used the word &quot;disintegrate&quot; and that's entirely appropriate. It's just destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to break an object, you can use Forces to literally create forces hitting it into pieces. Or you can just mess up the nuclear force so they don't hold the object integrity anymore. Neither require finesse nor fine control, the mage just makes a big mess. My point is that, maybe, you need less &quot;force&quot; to do that with nuclear control.<br /> An analogy would be a knot in a string. You can undo it by pulling it hard and snapping the string. Or you can pull the end and undo the knot. Undoing is a lot easier and requires less strength. Instead if causing X newtons of force unto the object, you just &quot;pull&quot; one nuclear string and it undo into itself, idk\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550332#post1550332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't think you really understand what it would mean to attempt to change a single atom, let alone a whole object's worth of atoms, from one set of elements to another by just manipulating strong and weak interactions. Besides the very idea being a matter of Focus in the first place (the current model of subatomic elementary particles and interactions was only considered proven scientifically 13 years ago, before that this was all hypothetical in the minds of physicists and there was a lot of hand wringing around the Higgs boson tests about what it would mean if they couldn't confirm its existence), the sheer mental processing you're talking about is beyond what a human mind could handle. All of the variables you'd need to adjust are constantly in flux. The interaction fields within an atom are generated by constant changes between states, and those are constantly being influenced by the fields of every nearby quantum field on top of it. This extends beyond the human mind... it's literally the point of Heisenberg's uncertainty principle. You're dealing with paired properties that cannot be simultaneously known. And multiples of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imho, you are going too deep into real life scientific paradigm. And while that might be ok for a specific paradigm that involves all that, I think it's not the only way of doing it.<br /> <br /> Would that be a thing for all etherites with Matter that shapes objects by changing their atomic structure too?<br /> <br /> If we think about all the real life hindrances in physics, biology, etc there will be no spells in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550332#post1550332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can magic make up for that? Sure. But I don't see how Forces can by itself. That's my point about needing an appropriately prepared space. It doesn't matter what the character's style is, if you're trying to just use Forces you need a dedicated space to isolate your target and active measures to keep everything in place. I don't care if it's magic circles or a hypertech lab. The energies you're trying to control with Forces are insanely complicated and delicate. It's one thing to talk about taking a sledgehammer to them and breaking them, it's an entirely different matter to be talking about doing the equivalent of a dozen cardiac bypass surgeries a nanosecond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if there is one sphere that should be able to control nuclear forces is Forces. <br /> I agree about the complexity. And the high amount of successes probably translate into a ritual(unless you have a very high Arete), which requires time, space and the tranquility necessary for a ritual. My point is that this is already taken into consideration by the number of successes.<br /> The mage wants to reshape something in the heat of battle? Good luck trying that and getting all the successes. Just hope you don't botch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550332#post1550332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The equivocation is noted and not appreciated.<br /> <br /> Do they exist in Mage due to the natural functions of atomic interactions? If no, my point stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum\u2026If a Matter crat does it this way, why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550332#post1550332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, M20 doesn't say either way. As per the heuristic at the start of this thread, if M20 is unclear about something, and previous editions offer clarity, they are valid sources. M20 never defines what the line between minor and major Forces patterns is. Previous editions clearly put manipulating radioactivity (and by necessity strong and weak interactions) into the major category. M20 doesn't say you don't need Forces 5, M20 doesn't say anything about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, the edition that makes a distinction between minor and major forces based on their nature is only 1st edition. Which also have a lot of different rules, being almost a whole different game.<br /> <br /> What 2E and revised called minor and major forces are just the magnitude and area of the effect. So, wind is minor forces while weather or tornado major. By this logic, nuclear fine control is minor while nuclear blasts (atomic bombs) are major.<br /> <br /> Also, just by the fact that Forces is said to control nuclear forces, and later isn't specified that you need rank 5 for that, means that you don't need it. That's the whole (and quite well done) analysis Ramnesis is doing in this thread. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, what one might also wonder is *why* would a Forces mage need to reshape or change an object like that? Outside very specific situations, things like the example of making and aluminum rod hard so you can strike with it, doesn't require nuclear manipulation. Just a &quot;coat&quot; of hard forces. Hell, the mage could create a forces bat to strike, no need for the aluminium at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T12:22:48-07:00","id":1550345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550339#post1550339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Human Polygraph Machine</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also read all the vital statistics that a polygraph test reads, like pulse, blood pressure, breathing rate, and skin conductivity. This wouldn\u2019t tell a mage if someone is lying, it would give him the results a real polygraph test would which, if he had the skill to read one, would be exactly as accurate as a real polygraph. How accurate that is depends on the story. Realistically, they are suspect, but many a movie treats them as nigh infallible, so depending on ST this might be quite a useful power.</span> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>Life can also read hormones and moods. So, more than lying, you can read raw emotions: fear, rage, lust, hapiness, sadness, etc. Plenty of info for the mage to take advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T14:27:54-07:00","id":1550347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550339#post1550339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sense Unlife</i></span></span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd relabel this to &quot;Sense Facsimile.&quot; Unlife is a weird term that doesn't really explain what you're doing. A facsimile is a something that appears to be something else. So a Matter pattern that appears to be alive in how it functions could be senses as not being alive because it's just a facsimile. It doesn't have the quality of &quot;unlife&quot; whatever that means (some fantasy authors treat &quot;unlife&quot; as the opposite of &quot;undeath&quot; so it's living creature that has supernatural properties to emulate dead things rather than a dead thing that has supernatural properties to emulate living things).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Read Muscles</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Human Polygraph Machine</i></span></span></b> </div> </div> </div>I would combine these into one broader effect of &quot;Sense Mood.&quot; I don't think it's justified to go farther to the extent of specific emotions (I don't think Life 1 can sense the differences between happy tears and sad tears for example, both operate on the same systems, though it can tell the difference between tearing up because of allergies vs emotions).<br /> <br /> Reading Muscles is kinda insufficient as a stand-alone effect. It takes a tiny fraction of a second for an arm to interpret the instruction of &quot;punch&quot; and execute it (the entire process of the thought of throwing a punch to impact can take as little as 1/10th of a second for a trained fighter). Given the constant background noise of non-aggressive impulses in the nervous system, this really isn't helping you more than just watching someone and seeing their arm start to move into a punch. Maybe a niche situation of seeing through things like using a cloak or shield to hide what strike is coming.<br /> <br /> What's more useful is reading the subconscious signals that humans are broadly less sensitive towards than most other animals. &quot;Reading muscles&quot; to read attacks is pretty fallible just like polygraphs are (and they've been rather thoroughly knocked off their pedestal in pop culture). Being able to sense all of the subtle cues caused by things like agitation, relaxation, and so on are more useful because it helps filter specific actions accurately. Is someone coming towards you to give you a big hug or to tackle you? Knowing they're aggressive vs. happy is a good way to know how to respond before it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T15:01:17-07:00","id":1550348,"title":"","content":"So a raw steak is life or matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T17:49:38-07:00","id":1550352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550337#post1550337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Anything with enough living cells in it to transplant, preserve, or cultivate counts as Life, if it has passed that point it is Matter. This line seems to vary over the book, but that's the distinction given here.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about this for quite some time, but can't remember ever seeing it stated in the books.<br /> <br /> So, am I to assume that, for the purposes of Sphere Magic, viruses and bacteria are Matter rather than Life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T18:40:50-07:00","id":1550354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550352#post1550352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about this for quite some time, but can't remember ever seeing it stated in the books.<br /> <br /> So, am I to assume that, for the purposes of Sphere Magic, viruses and bacteria are Matter rather than Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those should be Life. The raw steak is Matter <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T07:46:19-07:00","id":1550359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550347#post1550347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would combine these into one broader effect of &quot;Sense Mood.&quot; I don't think it's justified to go farther to the extent of specific emotions (I don't think Life 1 can sense the differences between happy tears and sad tears for example, both operate on the same systems, though it can tell the difference between tearing up because of allergies vs emotions).<br /> <br /> Reading Muscles is kinda insufficient as a stand-alone effect. It takes a tiny fraction of a second for an arm to interpret the instruction of &quot;punch&quot; and execute it (the entire process of the thought of throwing a punch to impact can take as little as 1/10th of a second for a trained fighter). Given the constant background noise of non-aggressive impulses in the nervous system, this really isn't helping you more than just watching someone and seeing their arm start to move into a punch. Maybe a niche situation of seeing through things like using a cloak or shield to hide what strike is coming.<br /> <br /> What's more useful is reading the subconscious signals that humans are broadly less sensitive towards than most other animals. &quot;Reading muscles&quot; to read attacks is pretty fallible just like polygraphs are (and they've been rather thoroughly knocked off their pedestal in pop culture). Being able to sense all of the subtle cues caused by things like agitation, relaxation, and so on are more useful because it helps filter specific actions accurately. Is someone coming towards you to give you a big hug or to tackle you? Knowing they're aggressive vs. happy is a good way to know how to respond before it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call about reading muscles and really any attempt to read future action. Regardless of where a mage reads it, his reaction will start significantly after the read action is already in progress.<br /> <br /> I am going to keep the Human Polygraph effect, though, because it is such a specific application of the exact abilities of Life 1. The only drawback being that, like many people, I have very little respect for actual polygraph tests. I will add a separate Sense Moods section, though, as you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> have both pointed out the wider use. I also changed the name of Sense Unlife to Sense Nonlife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T07:52:55-07:00","id":1550360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550352#post1550352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about this for quite some time, but can't remember ever seeing it stated in the books.<br /> <br /> So, am I to assume that, for the purposes of Sphere Magic, viruses and bacteria are Matter rather than Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well many (if not most) biologists don't consider viruses to be alive. That said, I don't think that's a good argument to bring into Mage. <br /> <br /> We can cultivate viruses and bacteria in a lab, so for the purposes of the Sphere they count as Life. Also treating disease was the province of life well before viruses and bacteria were ever identified and a paradigm doesn't need to recognize their existence to do that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T10:13:25-07:00","id":1550362,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Alter Simple Life-Forms/ Heal Self </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple organisms \u2013 viruses, mollusks, insects, plants, etc. \u2013 become clay in the mage\u2019s hands. He learns to adjust their Patterns (giving a crab wings, for example), and heal or kill them. Although he can\u2019t yet transmute them into other states of being, he can cause flowers to bloom or wither, help trees bear fruit, and so on. Focusing on his own Pattern, he can also heal himself or perform small alterations (hair color, skin tone, height, weight, and so on) to his basic form.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are multiple significant abilities mentioned here and I am going to split them apart even if they are usually considered part of the same ability.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One important consideration is the difference between simple and complex lifeforms. We are given examples but no clear dividing line. Some classic possibilities include warm blooded vs cold blooded, chordates (animals with spinal cords) vs everything else, and live birth vs eggs. This is really a table decision.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adjust Simple Life Forms (Alter Simple Life Forms)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The start of the simple life progression track. The mage can adjust patterns to some degree. The exact limits of that degree are unclear. Pushing a creature to do something it can do naturally is in (bloom, grow fruit, etc). Full transmutation is out, though dramatic changes like the addition of wings (limbs) are possible. The dividing line is unclear.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is also unclear if this level allows for changes dramatic enough to cause pattern bleed. Most of the examples would not be as they don\u2019t alter the target outside of its normal form and function. The winged crab might be. How the ST draws that line will have an effect on the utility of this power.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Them! </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By dramatically enhancing the size of ants, a mage can reproduce the giant ants from the movie Them! How difficult this is depends on how far into the weeds we want to get; stories don\u2019t usually get into the adjustments that need to be made to make gargantuan creatures physically work. We can reasonably ignore that and just size up. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the table does want to get into specifics: Two big factors are the square cube law and the way insects breathe. The first means that volume (and therefore weight) increases much faster than cross sectional area (and therefore strength of its muscles and equivalents). The second means insects don\u2019t actually have a breathing system that works at those sizes, so the mage will need to enhance that system or give the ants lungs. Those changes could reasonably be done at Life 2, though they may take more successes.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heal or Harm Simple Life (Alter Simple Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The start of the healing progression track. Here it lines up with the alteration of simple life, but it will rapidly diverge so it gets its own entry. At this level a mage can heal simple life forms or directly attack them with Life magic. At least, I presume that's what kill them means in this context.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Side question: Do were-spiders count as Simple Life (+Spirit) in any of their forms? If so they are sometimes Life 3/Spirit 2 to attack and sometimes Life 2/Spirit 2. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Muscle Control</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attacks can include more than just physical damage. At the level that a mage can damage a living pattern he can also seize control of its various systems to change behavior or action. In particular he can usurp control of its musculature and move it around against its will. This is less like mind control and more like puppeteering. </span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heal Self (Heal Self)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage is a complex life form, but healing doesn\u2019t have to wait until Alter Complex Life, especially not personal healing. A mage can heal himself at Life 2. Presumably this means he can directly attack his own pattern for Aggravated damage too, though that might not come up too frequently.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I\u2019m My Own Bio-Weapons Lab (the gentler name could be Generate Antibodies)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On some sidebars it is stated to be difficult to target patterns inside of other patterns. Though bacteria and viruses are simple life, the ones mages are most interested in are often found inside complex life, which may require higher ranks (at least enough for healing). Not so here, a mage can heal himself and affect bacteria at the same rank of Life, so he should be able to isolate strains within himself and either alter them or make minor alterations to himself in response.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minor Self Alterations (Heal self?)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The examples given are more minor than the ones given for altering simple creatures. The changes seem to be limited to those found within the mage\u2019s species. Still that is quite powerful, and includes a lot of possibilities for both disguise and physical adaptation. Thicker skin, faster clotting, and limbs adapted for running, climbing, or swimming should all be possible here.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Universal Donor</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can quite literally grow more of himself to give to other people. He can produce more blood quickly, in whatever type is necessary. He can grow excess skin for skin grafts, as well as regrow organs he donates. He can even alter his organs to match the various markers needed for transplant.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One important consideration. Spells have a duration, so some of the modifications to prevent rejection could wear off. That said, STs and players often implicitly ignore that limit when it comes to things absorbed by a body. We don\u2019t usually have the molecules from conjured food or air disappear from the body when the spell runs out, for instance. Whether this happens with transplants is a table call, just make sure the players know the ruling in advance.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Elsewhere in M20</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Share Senses (From Spirit 2)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 2 claims that Life 2 has the ability to share magical senses and abilities with other creatures. Seeing spirits and contacting the spirit world are the examples. There is no complexity distinction in the writeup and contextually the ability would mostly be used on humans, so the indication is that Life 2 can share senses with any creature. Since this is not an effect that alters the creature\u2019s pattern it does make sense it wouldn\u2019t follow the standard alteration progressions.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T11:02:13-07:00","id":1550363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550360#post1550360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well many (if not most) biologists don't consider viruses to be alive. That said, I don't think that's a good argument to bring into Mage.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Its a great idea consensus compliant undead!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T11:15:48-07:00","id":1550364,"title":"","content":"The &quot;are viruses and bacteria covered by Life or Matter&quot; seems pretty conclusively answered in Life 2 for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T09:58:53-07:00","id":1550381,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 3</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Transform Simple Life-Forms/Alter Self/ Heal Others </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Advanced understanding allows the mage to radically alter simple organisms (turning a tree inside-out); transform one into another (changing fruit into insects); or \u2013 with Prime 2 \u2013 conjure them from raw energy.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Working with his own Pattern, that mage can work substantial alterations on himself, growing gills, claws, armor and so forth. He remains essentially human, but begins to master the definition of \u201chuman.\u201d Meanwhile, he also gains the ability to heal damage to other complex organisms, put them to sleep, or inflict harm upon their living Pattern forms.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life continues its trend of being fairly direct about what it can do. Meanwhile, I continue my descent into disturbing, Cronenbergian examples. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once again, I\u2019m going to split powers that really should be considered the same thing.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmogrify Simple Life (Transform Simple Life) </span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transform Simple Life (Transform Simple Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The continuation of the Simple Life track. These are essentially two different presentations of the same idea and the only reason I\u2019m separating them is to make sure neither gets lost. A mage can transform one life pattern into another (transformation), like changing a bug into a tree, and can also grossly reshape a pattern (transmogrification), like the aforementioned turning a tree inside out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any change great enough that it can only be done at this level should be large enough to cause Pattern Bleed.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Pulling a Pokeball out of a Squirtle</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can shape hidden compartments in living things as ways of concealing objects. Large enough creatures could even hold entire rooms. If you set your expectations correctly, a vacation house in </span><s>Monstro the Whale</s> an oversized whale shark <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">could be quite lovely.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Living Mech: Battletoad</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this degree of control over simple creatures, a mage could grow and transmogrify a creature into a living, pilotable biomachine with a cockpit and organic control system. Actual controls will be rather direct and jerky as they use the direct muscle control from earlier, unless Mind is involved or the mage spends a lot of time practicing driving the creature. Possibly instincts could be instilled to help, but that depends on if instincts are Life or Mind or both.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The nautical version of this would be Submersible Fortress: Megalodon.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The names assume frogs and sharks are simple life. Substitute beetles and squids if that is not the case in your game.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Unrestrained Growth</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can induce absurd levels of growth in a crab, causing rapid, semi-formed, cancerous growth like something from a John Carpenter Film. This growth might continue until it overruns and envelops an area. The subject doesn\u2019t have to be a crab, it just sets up a hidden double meaning for \u2018cancer\u2019 if it is.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heal or Harm Complex Organisms (Heal Others)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The continuation of the healing track. At this point a mage can heal anything and anyone. There are no limits anymore. He can also harm anyone, which is why Life 3 is so often associated with Life attacks. That said, attacks aren\u2019t limited to damage and most effects that inflict some kind of normal debuff are possible here. Sleep is given as an example, but confusion, ennervation, lack of balance, etc should be possible.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I\u2019ve Got Your Strings, To Hold You Down</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rather horrifyingly, at Life 3 a mage can puppet just about any living creature. This is exactly the same as the Life 2 version but it works on anything living.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter Self (Alter Self)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The continuation of the alter self track. The mage is no longer limited to features found within humanity and can now add small changes from other things. The intention appears to be that if the change can be described as \u2018human with bonuses\u2019 it is within the realm of Life 3, whereas if it becomes something else it requires greater ranks. It\u2019s a good limit, though not quite as clear as it seems. Is a mermaid a human plus a fish tail, or is it something else? A human with hooves and a human with a bull head are both human-plus, but what about a minotaur? That\u2019s going to be a call for the ST.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also a call for the ST: are gills radical enough to result in Pattern Bleed? It\u2019s unclear.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I\u2019m All Ears</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Features don\u2019t have to be in quite the same place as they normally are. A mage can grow extra eyes and ears in strange places to improve his senses. He can also grow different kinds of ears and eyes to see and hear different things.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T10:41:39-07:00","id":1550382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550381#post1550381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter Self (Alter Self)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The continuation of the alter self track. The mage is no longer limited to features found within humanity and can now add small changes from other things. The intention appears to be that if the change can be described as \u2018human with bonuses\u2019 it is within the realm of Life 3, whereas if it becomes something else it requires greater ranks. It\u2019s a good limit, though not quite as clear as it seems. Is a mermaid a human plus a fish tail, or is it something else? A human with hooves and a human with a bull head are both human-plus, but what about a minotaur? That\u2019s going to be a call for the ST.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also a call for the ST: are gills radical enough to result in Pattern Bleed? It\u2019s unclear.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I\u2019m All Ears</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Features don\u2019t have to be in quite the same place as they normally are. A mage can grow extra eyes and ears in strange places to improve his senses. He can also grow different kinds of ears and eyes to see and hear different things.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This &quot;essentially human&quot; things is kimda nonsense to me. I believe the intention of the author was to limit conplete transformations. So, turning into a bull requires Life 4, but turning your head into the one of a bull is Life 3. Or giving you hoofs. But then, you could cast several spells and transform into a bull step-by-step. <br /> There is no issue here, since doing it with a lower sphere rank will be balanced by the multiple paradox and rolls (possibility of botches too) the mage will need to do what Life 4 can in one roll. Since a minotaur is a human with bull legs and head, I'd say it's totally doable with Life 3<br /> <br /> It's interesting to add that at this rank, Life can buff <b>all</b> attributes. It can also make the mage capable of resisting harsh environments (extreme cold/heat/pressure etc) and withstand the strains of a Forces 2 speed up spell, which possibly grants extra actions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T13:08:12-07:00","id":1550383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550382#post1550382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This &quot;essentially human&quot; things is kimda nonsense to me. I believe the intention of the author was to limit conplete transformations. So, turning into a bull requires Life 4, but turning your head into the one of a bull is Life 3. Or giving you hoofs. But then, you could cast several spells and transform into a bull step-by-step.<br /> There is no issue here, since doing it with a lower sphere rank will be balanced by the multiple paradox and rolls (possibility of botches too) the mage will need to do what Life 4 can in one roll. Since a minotaur is a human with bull legs and head, I'd say it's totally doable with Life 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me. The Alter Self track has three steps, not two, with the middle one (Life 4 - Transform Self) being self transformation. The middle step allows full shapeshifting with one specific limit: he can only shift into things of similar size and mass (such as large dogs, deer, etc). <br /> <br /> But Life 3 doesn't state either restriction. Sure, an ST could reasonably say that growing to the size of an elephant puts the mage past the point of 'essentially human' but that's his ruling, it isn't from the book and it isn't obvious. Indeed in stories of a regular person growing to titanic proportions.(Attack of the 50 Foot Woman, Honey I Blew Up The Kid, Monsters Vs Aliens, etc.) we generally still consider the new titan to be human. Much more so than in stories where the person is transformed into an animal or animal hybrid (The Fly, Emperor's New Groove, The Witches, etc.)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, though, it is hard to enforce a limit for Life 4, when it can already be surpassed by an earlier rank of Life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T13:32:41-07:00","id":1550385,"title":"","content":"I think it would be worth collectively just agreeing that the Spheres, broadly, need a serious overhaul just on clarity itself (the fan reaction to HDYDT? saying that plenty clearly without any specific debates here) instead of debating each ambiguity?<br /> <br /> While I appreciate the desire to get into the weeds here, I'm plenty guilty of doing it, there's a point where we're getting away from what the books say and into personal interpretations or personal patches rather than relying on direct statements. If one of the authors didn't put down their intentions in writing (either in the books or at least somewhere else) we don't know what they were specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T15:47:43-07:00","id":1550386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550383#post1550383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me. The Alter Self track has three steps, not two, with the middle one (Life 4 - Transform Self) being self transformation. The middle step allows full shapeshifting with one specific limit: he can only shift into things of similar size and mass (such as large dogs, deer, etc).<br /> <br /> But Life 3 doesn't state either restriction. Sure, an ST could reasonably say that growing to the size of an elephant puts the mage past the point of 'essentially human' but that's his ruling, it isn't from the book and it isn't obvious. Indeed in stories of a regular person growing to titanic proportions.(Attack of the 50 Foot Woman, Honey I Blew Up The Kid, Monsters Vs Aliens, etc.) we generally still consider the new titan to be human. Much more so than in stories where the person is transformed into an animal or animal hybrid (The Fly, Emperor's New Groove, The Witches, etc.)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, though, it is hard to enforce a limit for Life 4, when it can already be surpassed by an earlier rank of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair it would be way easier to do full transformations on life 3 and partial shapeshifting (so mixing parts of different animals) on 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T16:29:09-07:00","id":1550388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550364#post1550364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;are viruses and bacteria covered by Life or Matter&quot; seems pretty conclusively answered in Life 2 for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected.<br /> <br /> As for debating ambiguities, I'm with Heavy Arms. Lets split some hairs, but not all of them, we're trying to clarify the game as it is. There are other games if one wants an actually better defined magic system, including MtAw (to stay with a familiar system) and GURPS (a favorite of at least one forum member, where you can take your sweet time to adjust it precisely to your specifications to any degree you want).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T19:38:40-07:00","id":1550391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550382#post1550382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to add that at this rank, Life can buff <b>all</b> attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question, Mind 1 can boost Mental attributes too... Does anywhere state that is the limit? Up to human limits or can it go beyond? For example, if someone has Perception 1, Intelligence 4, Wits 5... Can they Boost Wits? Can Intelligence go only up to 5?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> your opinions are appreciated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T20:47:20-07:00","id":1550392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550385#post1550385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be worth collectively just agreeing that the Spheres, broadly, need a serious overhaul just on clarity itself (the fan reaction to HDYDT? saying that plenty clearly without any specific debates here) instead of debating each ambiguity?<br /> <br /> While I appreciate the desire to get into the weeds here, I'm plenty guilty of doing it, there's a point where we're getting away from what the books say and into personal interpretations or personal patches rather than relying on direct statements. If one of the authors didn't put down their intentions in writing (either in the books or at least somewhere else) we don't know what they were specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not perfect because such a broad affecting system is bound to have this sort of thing, I've always found that Mage Awakening (1st or 2nd edition) solved much of these problems for me.<br /> It is clearer at least. <br /> <br /> I don't even think we should NOT debate the Spheres. There is merit in this. But this merit is the op and everyone participating in this, not the book author's. Be it Brucato or some else, I've always found Mage Ascencion rules very poor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T01:07:27-07:00","id":1550393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550391#post1550391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, Mind 1 can boost Mental attributes too... Does anywhere state that is the limit? Up to human limits or can it go beyond? For example, if someone has Perception 1, Intelligence 4, Wits 5... Can they Boost Wits? Can Intelligence go only up to 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>If should be noted that by the book Life only boosts physical Attributes and Mind the rest (as dubious as that logic is).<br /> <br /> The book never sets a specific limit. M20 makes it clear that increasing Attributes over your current rating results in Pattern Bleed. In past editions 6+ dots from this also result in Permadox as long as the effect is in place. This implies there isn't really a hard limit, but rather a soft limit of how much you want Paradox on your ass until you let the powers drop or spend XP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550392#post1550392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even think we should NOT debate the Spheres. There is merit in this. But this merit is the op and everyone participating in this, not the book author's. Be it Brucato or some else, I've always found Mage Ascencion rules very poor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that we shouldn't have discussions of how to handle the rules as they are... the point of the thread though, is what are the rules as they are in the first place? So constantly getting on tangents that get away from that core point isn't probably productive to the thread.<br /> <br /> Yeah, we could have the Nth thread about how to fix the game... I'm not sure it'll do much the countless previous ones haven't. Trying to build up a consensus on what the RAW actually are seems more fruitful.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, the authors do matter. They're part of the thread even if indirectly. It's their words we're parsing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-26-2025, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T07:22:10-07:00","id":1550396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550393#post1550393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>If should be noted that by the book Life only boosts physical Attributes and Mind the rest (as dubious as that logic is).</b><br /> <br /> The book never sets a specific limit. M20 makes it clear that increasing Attributes over your current rating results in Pattern Bleed. In past editions 6+ dots from this also result in Permadox as long as the effect is in place. This implies there isn't really a hard limit, but rather a soft limit of how much you want Paradox on your ass until you let the powers drop or spend XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in Ascension Life makes sense, specially if you have a scientific paradigm:<br /> <br /> Physical attributes are dependant on (or representing) your body, Appareance is literally your body shape and physiognomy so that HAS to be Life. And how perceptive, smart, quick thining, charismatic and manipulative you are, are based on what your brain does. There is no other organ that controls your charisma...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am reading from the M20 core that only the Mental attributes (Perception, Intelligence, Wits) can be boosted with Mind. From where are you getting Social <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> ?<br /> <br /> <br /> I get that in AWakening the Mind Arcana does Mental and Social, due what the Arcana represent and do is not really related to paradigm but how the underlying reality works, so in Awakening even though Life could modify your brain in all ways, the boosting-the-brain-instantaneously Arcana is Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-26-2025, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T11:26:03-07:00","id":1550398,"title":"","content":"First of, lets remember for the Nth time that the game works under the assumption of the Mind-Body duality, regardless of Focus/Paradigm. Regardless if we agree that in rl practice the brain is an organ and the traits we regard as mental and social come from its biochemistry (and actually the biochemistry of the whole body, the brain is just the main piece), in the end any &quot;deep&quot; mental trait is governed in the game by Mind.<br /> <br /> So I can agree that Appearance is a physical attribute, but Manipulation and Charisma are certainly under the purview of Mind. Otherwise, what do we even have a Mind Sphere for?<br /> <br /> Now, regardless of how you parse the bonuses between the Spheres, the system is very clear the one <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said: any bonus will cause Pattern Bleed as long as it is maintained by Magic instead of bought with XP (you can still justify this buying with Magic without further penalties). And any <b>value</b> beyond 5 causes Permadox <b>if achieved with Sphere Magic</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T13:09:49-07:00","id":1550401,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble finding where social Attribute boosting is covered... in might not be M20 core (though it was that way in previous editions).<br /> <br /> The problem is that the Physical/Social/Mental Attribute divide has nothing to do with the way Spheres are designed, but the Sphere rules use those clusters anyway. The Attributes aren't designed with any sort of philosophic position on the relation of mind and body. If you want to perform a Feat of Strength greater than your current Strength allows, you roll Willpower to see if you can pull it off. Appearance is both your literal physical appearance and your intuitive understanding of non-verbal communications and norms (how you dress is not a physical activity but absolutely impacts how people perceive you). Perception is a neural process even if the mind is what makes sense of the raw data the body picks up.<br /> <br /> So the Attributes categories are meant to be broad generalities that allow for lots of edge cases (specifically to allow for fun Attribute + Ability combos where in the right situations any can be paired up). Solidly pegging some Attributes to Life and some to Mind is always going to cause dissonance within the rules. But that's what we're stuck with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T20:26:42-07:00","id":1550402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550383#post1550383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me. The Alter Self track has three steps, not two, with the middle one (Life 4 - Transform Self) being self transformation. The middle step allows full shapeshifting with one specific limit: he can only shift into things of similar size and mass (such as large dogs, deer, etc).<br /> <br /> But Life 3 doesn't state either restriction. Sure, an ST could reasonably say that growing to the size of an elephant puts the mage past the point of 'essentially human' but that's his ruling, it isn't from the book and it isn't obvious. Indeed in stories of a regular person growing to titanic proportions.(Attack of the 50 Foot Woman, Honey I Blew Up The Kid, Monsters Vs Aliens, etc.) we generally still consider the new titan to be human. Much more so than in stories where the person is transformed into an animal or animal hybrid (The Fly, Emperor's New Groove, The Witches, etc.)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, though, it is hard to enforce a limit for Life 4, when it can already be surpassed by an earlier rank of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I completely forgot about the size limitations. That makes very clear the differences between ranks. And although Life 3 has no raw size limitation, I can't think of a reason for it to have a better limitation than Life 4.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> , Life 3 can buff all attributes as per hdydt. Yeah, we all hate this book, but this one makes sense. <br /> <br /> physical attributes are obvious. As is appearance. Charisma and manipulation can be buffed by pheromones other traits (including having good looks helps a lot). Mental attributes can be buffed by increasing brain capacity and sensorial organs. Hdydt has some explanation in the shapechanging section.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the thread, I pretty much appreciate the effort to reach a common ground on what the spheres can do, although I understand we cant cover everything, especially effects of conjunctional spheres. It's ok if some people don't want to participate on this, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T23:54:00-07:00","id":1550403,"title":"","content":"I mostly agree about the size limitation. Most alterations affect mass if you want to be too strict, but I think that goes against the intent. But that can be said of <b>Life 4</b>, too.<br /> <br /> But <b>Life 4</b>'s explicit citation about size and mass seems to infer it was implicit, but already there, on <b>Life 3</b>, and makes sense to similar effects on other Spheres.<br /> <br /> At most I'd say that conjunctional effects should be able to bypass this by converting mass to and from other Patterns.<br /> <br /> That does bring up two considerations, though:<br /> <br /> 1 - What are the limits for healing? Eventual healing may be easily handwaved as per my first paragraph, but regrowing entire organs too quickly too frequently may start to be too much to ignore the game's version of the Conservation laws.<br /> <br /> 2 - Can we transfer mass from a life form to another through an effect? For every other &quot;similar&quot; Sphere that's a &quot;yes&quot;, so what about <b>Life</b>? Can we increase the size of an animal or plant by drawing living mass from other creatures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T02:55:21-07:00","id":1550404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550402#post1550402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charisma and manipulation can be buffed by pheromones other traits (including having good looks helps a lot).</div> </div> </div> </div>What pheromones can buff Charisma and Manipulation? As well, how would any such alterations not fall under Appearance (since Appearance handles things like first impressions where subconscious processing of subtle body signals has any strong impact)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T03:05:16-07:00","id":1550405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550403#post1550403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly agree about the size limitation. Most alterations affect mass if you want to be too strict, but I think that goes against the intent. But that can be said of <b>Life 4</b>, too.<br /> <br /> But <b>Life 4</b>'s explicit citation about size and mass seems to infer it was implicit, but already there, on <b>Life 3</b>, and makes sense to similar effects on other Spheres.<br /> <br /> At most I'd say that conjunctional effects should be able to bypass this by converting mass to and from other Patterns.<br /> <br /> That does bring up two considerations, though:<br /> <br /> 1 - What are the limits for healing? Eventual healing may be easily handwaved as per my first paragraph, but regrowing entire organs too quickly too frequently may start to be too much to ignore the game's version of the Conservation laws.<br /> <br /> 2 - Can we transfer mass from a life form to another through an effect? For every other &quot;similar&quot; Sphere that's a &quot;yes&quot;, so what about <b>Life</b>? Can we increase the size of an animal or plant by drawing living mass from other creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Mass seems to be a good limit. Most people have at least 30% of body as fat. You can use that to regenerate (although i would save regrowing limbs to Life 4. Reataching severed ones is fine)<br /> 2. I dont see why not but to transfer something to ourselves again we need Life 4 as that is the limit of transforming complex lifeforms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T09:39:01-07:00","id":1550407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550403#post1550403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At most I'd say that conjunctional effects should be able to bypass this by converting mass to and from other Patterns.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's an excellent point. Prime 2 allows the mage to create things from nothing and it should help here as well. The size Prime 2 would allow for the transformation would depend on the ST, though, since we have no reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550403#post1550403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That does bring up two considerations, though:<br /> <br /> 1 - What are the limits for healing? Eventual healing may be easily handwaved as per my first paragraph, but regrowing entire organs too quickly too frequently may start to be too much to ignore the game's version of the Conservation laws.<br /> <br /> 2 - Can we transfer mass from a life form to another through an effect? For every other &quot;similar&quot; Sphere that's a &quot;yes&quot;, so what about <b>Life</b>? Can we increase the size of an animal or plant by drawing living mass from other creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div> 1- The game practically has no conservation laws, lol. Forces 2 can accelerate things massively even without Prime 2, for example.<br /> Healing has no limits. Small healings are coincident while full organs are just vulgar.<br /> <br /> 2- You don't need to get mass from somewhere else to increase the size of an animal or plant. But if you are talking about really massive increase, I don't see why you couldn't get that from other creatures. It all fall under Life sphere. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550404#post1550404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What pheromones can buff Charisma and Manipulation? As well, how would any such alterations not fall under Appearance (since Appearance handles things like first impressions where subconscious processing of subtle body signals has any strong impact)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, charisma can be buffed by body language, a good posture or even voice resonance. Anything that makes you stand out and be noticed, showing a relaxed stance and confidence at the same time.<br /> <br /> Manipulation buff could be subtle scents that can trigger some instinctive feeling of trust on people or something like that.<br /> <br /> I'd say appearance should affect every social interaction. It is just too relevant in society, but the game doesn't work that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T10:59:53-07:00","id":1550408,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> I think on a Life can boost attributes (again, under a scientific paradigm), there is no need to go with Pheromones.<br /> <br /> Everything that you are behaviourally is in the brain. The gut feels you have? The instinctual responses and body posture? Your brain (and nervious system plus muscle actuators) do all that.<br /> <br /> IF we were to have in the real world the capabilities that Life Sphere expouses, then modifiying the bodies will make you more intelligent, charismatic, manipulative, funny, witty, etc. In game terms, only on this topic I agree with HDYDT.<br /> <br /> Of course understanding that the mind body duality the game exposes is better represented by the Mind + Life SPheres makes total sense in the context of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the end mages are (or should be) more defined by Paradigm that by Sphere. Some Hermetic magus would boost his Intelligence with Mind, but a Technocrat Biologist would go for Life for the same effect; for each one of them the reasoning would make perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> My question was started when <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> stated that Mind boosted Social attributes, and I found unreasonable that Appearance would go mainly to Mind when it has an undeniable physical component, even if you consider Mind / Body duality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T12:00:08-07:00","id":1550411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550408#post1550408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> I think on a Life can boost attributes (again, under a scientific paradigm), there is no need to go with Pheromones.<br /> <br /> Everything that you are behaviourally is in the brain. The gut feels you have? The instinctual responses and body posture? Your brain (and nervious system plus muscle actuators) do all that.<br /> <br /> IF we were to have in the real world the capabilities that Life Sphere expouses, then modifiying the bodies will make you more intelligent, charismatic, manipulative, funny, witty, etc. In game terms, only on this topic I agree with HDYDT.<br /> <br /> Of course understanding that the mind body duality the game exposes is better represented by the Mind + Life SPheres makes total sense in the context of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the end mages are (or should be) more defined by Paradigm that by Sphere. Some Hermetic magus would boost his Intelligence with Mind, but a Technocrat Biologist would go for Life for the same effect; for each one of them the reasoning would make perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> My question was started when <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> stated that Mind boosted Social attributes, and I found unreasonable that Appearance would go mainly to Mind when it has an undeniable physical component, even if you consider Mind / Body duality.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, paradigm shouldn't determine which spheres an effect needs, what the effect does should. That is exactly where hdydt gets wrong, when adding spheres according to paradigm.<br /> <br /> Having said that, both Mind and Life can boost attributes. Mind can do at rank 1 (which is unusual, but raw) and boosts mental attributes only (maybe some case can be made for manipulation too).<br /> While Life 3 can do to all attributes. How the mage increases charisma amd manipulation falls for the player and ST to be imaginative. My first thought was pheromones because that's an easy answer and if your table doesn't require deep scientific explanations that's enough.<br /> <br /> Now, if you neeyomore specific answer, you can use my examples in my previous post and develop from there. <br /> <br /> Basically, anything that makes you more trustworthy would buff manipulation and anything that makes you stand out and attract attention would buff charisma.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T14:07:59-07:00","id":1550412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550404#post1550404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What pheromones can buff Charisma and Manipulation? As well, how would any such alterations not fall under Appearance (since Appearance handles things like first impressions where subconscious processing of subtle body signals has any strong impact)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, even ignoring that pheromones don't do all the things people seem to think they do <i><b>for humans</b></i>, that would be better handled as affecting Appearance than Charisma and Manipulation. Those two have more to do with behavior. I'm not completely against them being buffed by <b>Life</b>, but I'm yet to be convinced it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550407#post1550407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say appearance should affect every social interaction. It is just too relevant in society, but the game doesn't work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL it's true, but also far more complicated than what a simple number can represent.<br /> <br /> But we're talking a game, and in this case a game with a ill thought-off attribute. Appearance-the-Game-Trait is another can of worms, but it is what it is, we're not rewriting the actual rules. So it makes sense for all those <b>Life</b> alterations to go into it, and it doesn't affects every social roll.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550408#post1550408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything that you are behaviourally is in the brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the game doesn't work like that.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if at the end behavior and thought are physical processes irl. And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> said, <b>Paradigm</b> shouldn't affect what Spheres you use, just how you explain your Magic within the fiction of the game. A <b>Mind</b> effect can be explained with chemistry, spirits, electrical currents, it doesn't become anything other than a <b>Mind</b> effect.<br /> <br /> And the write-up of <b>Life</b> doesn't say it buffs every Attribute. Actually it doesn't say anything about buffs. I can't search for other passages about buffs right now, so if someone can point out what the book actually says, I'd be grateful.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550407#post1550407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game practically has no conservation laws, lol. Forces 2 can accelerate things massively even without Prime 2, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not completely true. The game certainly doesn't have <b>Physics</b>' Laws of Conservation (which are actually Laws of Symmetry), but it is adamant to state in every Sphere that makes &quot;things&quot; that you can't create something out of nothing below level 5.<br /> <br /> Even Prime doesn't actually makes things out of nothing, but instead establishes a means to take &quot;creation stuff&quot; from the environment (or maybe in the form of Quintessence) and turn it into other things. <b>Forces</b> is the only Sphere of the type that lets you amplify without a source for the extra &quot;stuff&quot;, but that's an exception <b>and</b> even then you can't simply create a new force out of nothing.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, we're talking <b>Life</b>, and it does have such limitations. We already agreed that <b>Life 4</b>'s limit on mass should be followed by lower levels. Why shouldn't it be followed by healing? Again, that's not about demanding extra mass for any healing, but someone will stretch this at some point, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> already proposed an effect (at <b>Life 2</b>) where you become a living organ factory just using healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T14:47:37-07:00","id":1550413,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>:<br /> <br /> I have provided some examples and explanations on how to buff manipulation and charisma. If you think they are wrong, we could discuss exactly *what* manipulation/charisma represent in game and then think how to buff them. If there is one sphere that should be able to buff them is Life.<br /> <br /> about raw, we have this in hdydt:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rank 3 Life Arts (Rank 4 for other characters) can boost or lower body-based Attributes by one dot per success rolled. Altered Physical and Social Attributes generally reveal themselves in obvious ways: rippling muscles, beautiful features, straighter posture, rapid reflexes, and so forth. Mental Attributes might be increased the same way, either by altering the character\u2019s sensory organs (raising Perception) or his brain matter and capacity (raising Intelligence or Wits). Those mental augmentations, however, might not be obvious to someone looking at the transformed character unless they involve some radical change from the way that person normally appears. </div> </div> </div>Notice how lame is their explanation for buffing Wits and Intelligence even using the same explanation (brain matter and capacity). That was my point before, we don't need to dig so deep into explanations. Stuff like pheromones, scent or even &quot;straighter posture&quot; (as in the raw text) should be enough to boost charisma and manipulation.<br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer explanations just a bit better than the provided by raw, so I stick with the ones I posted before. Let me know if you think any of them makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> About the conservation of energy, raw says that creating from &quot;nothing&quot; requires Prime 2 and not rank 5 afaik. All pattern spheres can increase/decrease stuff: Forces can insanely accelerate an object, Life can make you grow wings or make trees bear fruit and matter can change an object weight or density. And all that without Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Healing doesn't even change your shape or size, so there's no reason to have a size limit. If you can grow huge claws or wings, you can regrow your arm. It's no big deal. Otherwise healing would require Prime 2, which isn't raw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T16:33:30-07:00","id":1550414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550407#post1550407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, charisma can be buffed by body language, a good posture or even voice resonance. Anything that makes you stand out and be noticed, showing a relaxed stance and confidence at the same time.<br /> <br /> Manipulation buff could be subtle scents that can trigger some instinctive feeling of trust on people or something like that.<br /> <br /> I'd say appearance should affect every social interaction. It is just too relevant in society, but the game doesn't work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My first thought was pheromones because that's an easy answer and if your table doesn't require deep scientific explanations that's enough.<br /> <br /> Now, if you neeyomore specific answer, you can use my examples in my previous post and develop from there.<br /> <br /> Basically, anything that makes you more trustworthy would buff manipulation and anything that makes you stand out and attract attention would buff charisma. </div> </div> </div>So, here's the thing. You don't need a deep scientific explanations. You need the most basic of science explanation and leave the cultural myths to the Mythic Thread/Hypernarrative mechanics.<br /> <br /> Here's the simple science: there are zero human pheromones, and zero non-human pheromones that cause pheromone responses in humans. It is likely impossible for humans to be impacted by pheromones because what few mammalian pheromones we have identified in other species are processed by the VNO... something that's near vestigial in humans and in humans doesn't have the ability to access the neural pathways that non-human pheromones operate on.<br /> <br /> Using Forces to manipulate ambient light levels and colors &quot;buffs&quot; social rolls (Magick Enhancing Abilities exists for a reason) more than pheromones ever will when dealing with humans... but I don't think anyone's going to claim that Forces can give you extra dots of Charisma or Manipulation (even with a literal glow up!).<br /> <br /> As is usually important to note here, this isn't to say that the chemical excretions of humans don't matter to social interactions. Obviously they do. If someone walks in and you perceive them as smelling bad, you are negatively inclined towards them socially. The problem is that &quot;bad&quot; is an experiential memory mediated response. What you think makes someone smell good or bad in ways that impact your impressions of them are formed from a lifetime of unique personal experiences, direct socialization, and cultural norms that vastly overwhelm any potential instinctive reactions to specific chemical signals (which is also a real thing, but pheromones aren't just chemicals you have a response to).<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;trust&quot; smell, there are the smells you associate with the people that you trust(ed) deeply and the situations you associate with them. If you really trusted your grandfather, and you grandfather was a woodworker, you likely have strong positive associations with the smell of fresh wood shavings. If you were forced into shop class because you were AMAB and the shop teacher was the football couch treated you like shit because you did theater instead of playing sports like a boy should... you probably don't think of the smells of woodworking the same way.<br /> <br /> The same broadly holds true of things like body posture. There isn't a single &quot;good&quot; body posture that makes you more positively attention grabbing or trustworthy. It's your ability to modulate your posture to the social context you're in that matters.<br /> <br /> Again, the Magick Enhancing Abilities is an obvious place for a lot of these things. The problem is stretching them to a full &quot;increase dots in&quot; effect when they're so contextual.<br /> <br /> The logic of why Mind 1 can boost Attributes is beyond me, but Mind lets you directly influence emotional responses without having to mediate for specific individual associations. While we're not there in the thread yet, I don't think it's jumping the gun to say Mind can do, &quot;everyone look at me,&quot; or, &quot;aura of trust&quot; effects that don't need to worry about the nuances that attempting such influences with Life would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550408#post1550408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF we were to have in the real world the capabilities that Life Sphere expouses, then modifiying the bodies will make you more intelligent, charismatic, manipulative, funny, witty, etc. In game terms, only on this topic I agree with HDYDT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we take a scientific paradigm on this (something I don't agree with for reasons both Darth Revan and monteparnas have elaborated on), the science doesn't back this up.<br /> <br /> Every attempt to come up with a scientifically valid definition of &quot;intelligence&quot; has failed utterly and most tests of intelligence are testing much more specific things that humans culturally associate with the concept of intelligence. For example there's a neural cluster in the brain that's frequently larger in &quot;smart&quot; people... but it has nothing to do with how well you understand concepts, or whether or not you can solve a problem. It essentially governs how many different thoughts you can consciously juggle at once. The ability to get to the solution faster because you can handle more parts of the problem at once is seen as &quot;smart&quot; and thus intelligent but... it by WoD definitions it's really Wits not Intelligence since we're talking about speed of thought instead of depth of problem solving skills.<br /> <br /> Increasing perceptiveness runs into similar problems. We already sense orders of magnitude more stimuli than our brains can handle. We spend far more brain power sorting noise to find important details than we do scanning our environment. Those filtering processes are complicated, use multiple parts of the brain, and there's no simple way to increase their effectiveness across the board.<br /> <br /> M20's Enhancement Background touches on an important thing here (interestingly Vicissitude also deals with this): living organisms are hard to flat out &quot;improve.&quot; While not a zero-sum situation, drastic alterations generally improve one thing at the cost of something else. Dwayne 'The Rock' Johnson once put out the diet he ate during his wrestling career, and the specific needs to attain a current physical appearance and the physical ability to perform the high intensity stunt-athletics of it. It's an insane diet to try to replicate without including the years of working up to it, but it's also a necessary style of diet for that kind of physique. It would an extremely unhealthy diet outside of that context (he doesn't keep it up now that he's an actor and has stunt teams to do cinematic magic instead of needing to perform things himself live). If, in a scientific lens, you gave someone what the WoD defines as haveing 2/2/2 in physicals Strength 5 and didn't modify them into not just inhuman but impossible biological ways, it would either not work (the rest of their body wouldn't be able to actualize the increased power) or would destroy the body that can't handle the radical changes.<br /> <br /> A fictional example I like is one from the X-Men and specifically a scene where Quicksilver is in a therapy session, because he's an antisocial asshole and people think he needs to work on that. Something he points out though, is that his powers extend to his mind, and he can't completely turn them off. His social problems are because his mind is constantly moving at the speeds necessary to function so that he can physically move as fast as he does and still know what he's doing. Having conversations with normal people is so excruciatingly slow for him that he just... can't stand most social situations. <br /> <br /> Yes, we're talking about magic, and magic doesn't have to be constrained by such things, but if you want to rely on a scientific POV you end up having to consider them. If you want to use magic to manipulate real world events and increase the impact by taking advantage of scientific principles, the magic doesn't change what those scientific principles are (unless you can use more magic to address those, but that voids the point of taking advantage of existing science in the first place).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My question was started when <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> stated that Mind boosted Social attributes, and I found unreasonable that Appearance would go mainly to Mind when it has an undeniable physical component, even if you consider Mind / Body duality. </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, I never liked the idea of it much either. But Mage has let Mind boost the Social Attributes, and as I expounded on in a previous post, the whole idea of mapping the Attributes to the Spheres like that is inherently a game design issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550411#post1550411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, paradigm shouldn't determine which spheres an effect needs, what the effect does should. That is exactly where hdydt gets wrong, when adding spheres according to paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>As usual, agreed that this needs to be front of mind when discussing what the books say the Spheres do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T17:45:05-07:00","id":1550417,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> This is a great post and I would agree with you, except that this a game. We can't go that deep into science otherwise the game won't work. It's like saying if you use Correspondence to teleport you will end up in the void of space because Earth is moving at 30 km/s.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I agree that voice resonance or body language doesn't have much effects irl, but is a good enough excuse to work in-game. Raw used &quot;brain matter and capacity&quot; to buff Int and Wits. That's the kind of explanation that are needed. Raw also states that social attributes can be buffed with Life. And has &quot;straighter posture&quot; (besides &quot;beautiful features&quot;, which clearly represents appearance) as a buff. To me, this translates into Charisma.<br /> <br /> So, instead of tryiof to convince you, let me ask you this:<br /> <br /> -Which sphere, if any, do you think could buff manipulation and charisma? (Note that mind, by raw, only buffs mentals)<br /> <br /> - What do you think Charisma and Manipulation represents in real life and how do you think someone could buff them? (Not by rules, but with in-game explanations)<br /> <br /> And lastly, inducing hormonal and moods reaction is on the area of Life, so, why couldn't Life create a scent that triggers oxycotin (or any other hormone or bodily function that relates to pleasure, relaxarion and trust) and makes the mage more trustworthy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T19:18:41-07:00","id":1550419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550413#post1550413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>:<br /> <br /> I have provided some examples and explanations on how to buff manipulation and charisma. If you think they are wrong, we could discuss exactly *what* manipulation/charisma represent in game and then think how to buff them. If there is one sphere that should be able to buff them is Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with them, yes. Heavy Arms made a good explanation that I agree with, but let me try to be more concise.<br /> <br /> Manipulation and Charisma are ultimately behavioral in nature. It's not about the body you have, but about how you use what you have. A big part of them is knowing how to read the room to know what's appropriate and what's not.<br /> <br /> Forget about pheromones or similar stuff, humans aren't much driven by &quot;instinct&quot;, we're driven by memory. Sensory cues affect us through memory and experience, especially (but not only) social experience.<br /> <br /> So there's nothing you can do to your body that'll have the same effect on everyone. Charismatic people <b>behave</b> in a way that capitalizes trends and common experiences. Manipulative people <b>read</b> the target and adapt their behavior accordingly. And any &quot;personal gift&quot; for those things has more to do with personality than smell or appearance.<br /> <br /> There are more complications and nuance to that irl, and the very idea of Charisma and Manipulation as distinct Attributes is weird. But then again, that's the game as we have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550413#post1550413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Healing doesn't even change your shape or size, so there's no reason to have a size limit. If you can grow huge claws or wings, you can regrow your arm. It's no big deal. Otherwise healing would require Prime 2, which isn't raw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm not talking standard healing. I'm talking about pushing healing to extreme cases, like regrowing enough organs to build five new bodies from scratch in minutes and without food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T20:34:22-07:00","id":1550422,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> ,So, it is not possible to increase manipulation and charisma through magick?<br /> <br /> What does a &quot;straigther posture&quot; increase in social attributes by raw? Certainly not appearance as it was already described as &quot;beautiful features&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't inspire trust into people increase manipulation?<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't a heavenly charming voice increase charisma? There are even merits that are similar to that.<br /> <br /> I also would prefer a single CHA attibute like in DnD where all social traits are in one. But WoD is not like that, and according to raw, you don't need anything deeper than &quot;altering brain matter&quot; to increase Wits. It's that easy.<br /> <br /> About the excessive healing, yeah, making several organs is the same as creating them from scratch. That\u2019s a loophole a ST will have to deal\u2026or maybe not, the best that can happen is the mage get a few bucks from organ black market which isn't so much and is dangerous, so\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T22:25:47-07:00","id":1550423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550417#post1550417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> This is a great post and I would agree with you, except that this a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is getting rather frustrating. I've been accused, multiple times, of advocating positions that oppose the necessities of game design. It's not my fault the rules have massive flaws in them. It's not my fault if a suggesting interpretation causes big issues if you break out some reading glasses, let alone a magnifying glass, or a microscope.<br /> <br /> If you're fine at your table hand-waving simple truths away, cool, you and your friends do what's fun. That doesn't change what the books say, or how any given way to try to ready the rules might interact with other things.<br /> <br /> I have repeatedly pointed out that magic can override real world considerations. The point of that is that the <b>correct</b> magic does that. Bending other magics to take advantage of real world science (even outdated science) to make a case that X Sphere can do Y effect doesn't get the hand-wave of magic that magic directly intended for something does. You don't get to use a pure Forces effect to create new metals because you read somewhere that you can change atomic structures by controlling subatomic energetic interactions and thus it's a Forces thing too. If you just want to magic it, take Matter. If you want to combine magic and science, you need to include the actual science; at least if you want to have a functional conversation with people that aren't your personal play group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like saying if you use Correspondence to teleport you will end up in the void of space because Earth is moving at 30 km/s. </div> </div> </div>And yet I've been heavily criticized on this forum for pointing out that Correspondence doesn't actually deal with &quot;empty space&quot; as science describes it, but functions on connections, which very easily makes sure this is never a problem for the base Sphere system. The bridge between two connected patterns doesn't care about the real distances covered, or the relativistic positions of astronomical bodies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I agree that voice resonance or body language doesn't have much effects irl, but is a good enough excuse to work in-game. </div> </div> </div>I... didn't say that.<br /> <br /> The problem, as monteparnas has built on, is that they don't have much <u>universal</u> effect. They have extremely strong effects if adequately personalized to the target audience. The lack of universal impact is what makes Life a bad choice. You need greater flexibility and in-the-moment adaptation that's based on interpreting social responses from your target audience. Thus, there's no &quot;I smell like X, you feel Y&quot; universal chemical. Even if you use Life and Matter to magic up something like that, it would still only effect one emotional response. Creating a supernatural scent molecule that magically makes other humans more relaxed around you isn't going to help if you want to rile people up to go attack someone; both of which can be done with Charisma based rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Raw used &quot;brain matter and capacity&quot; to buff Int and Wits. That's the kind of explanation that are needed. </div> </div> </div>That's the kind of explanation that's considered good enough in a book we all agree is horrible bad at explaining what's needed. Those explanations make no sense, Mind 1 being able to buff Mental Attributes doesn't really make much sense either. I'm not saying that the HDYDT? doesn't say what it clearly says. I'm saying it makes the game harder to operate if you value a modicum of consistence in what the Spheres are capable of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Which sphere, if any, do you think could buff manipulation and charisma? (Note that mind, by raw, only buffs mentals) </div> </div> </div>Just a note, can you specific &quot;buff&quot; here? I'm assuming you mean, &quot;gain X dots in Attribute for duration&quot; but there's other bonuses you can grant.<br /> <br /> Entropy and Mind are the only Spheres that address the need to be adaptive that indicates high levels of social competence. Entropy's opening effects of Ring of Truth and Sense Weakness clearly give it the ability to provide valuable information that would help ensure social influence attempts land with maximum effect, even if what level of Entropy you'd need to justifying increasing dots in those Attributes instead of justifying Abilities Enhancing Magic would be difficult to determine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - What do you think Charisma and Manipulation represents in real life and how do you think someone could buff them? (Not by rules, but with in-game explanations) </div> </div> </div>I don't think any of the Attributes coherently represent any real world traits. They are, as written, nothing more than narrative archetypes in dot form. They exist to help actualize character concepts in the mechanics, not simulate real life. These archetypes of course stem from the imaginations of real life people, so they correlate to real life traits; just not in ways that make sense on any level of inspection.<br /> <br /> Consider, for a moment, vile figures like serial killers, personality cult leaders, and dictators. They illustrate quite clearly that there is no real line between &quot;charisma&quot; and &quot;manipulation.&quot; Ted Bundy charmed jury members sitting in judgement of him for murder. Is that insane Charisma? Insane Manipulation? Both?<br /> <br /> The closest thing these Attributes have to something we see is studying human interactions is the difference between pathos and ethos in the concept of classical Greek rhetorical classification. Pathos is rhetoric that appeals to the emotional desires of the audience; coinciding with Charisma. Ethos is rhetoric that appeals to a positive social position of the speaker (authority, expertise, reputation, etc.); coinciding with Manipulation. The third type in this is logos, rhetoric that relies on fully reasoned statements (which you can say is Intelligence in the few examples in the books that touch on it, but it never really comes up in terms of social influence). You notice that none of this is about what's true or not true, or the motivations of the speaker. It's just about how the strategy to appeal to the audience.<br /> <br /> If one wants to improve their &quot;Charisma&quot; and &quot;Manipulation,&quot; like anything else, you are either addressing flaws in your current skill set, or seeking to improve on your existing strengths. In either case, you're seeking out formal or informal ways to influence other people where you can get effective feedback. Taking part in community theater or modern dance classes are easily accessible ways to work on presentation and evoking emotional responses in your audience, and you'll get feedback on your efforts without too much pressure compared to professional oriented classes. Finding a course on extemporaneous speaking is another avenue for building up your social skills where you'll receive feedback that doesn't have the same complexities of doing things in public where it would be kinda weird to ask people to rate your style.<br /> <br /> Other options are to expand your horizons. Immersion in other subcultures or traveling to places with significantly different cultural norms helps you reflect on your own ways of behaving when it's taken out of the normal you've adjusted it too. A simple example is &quot;personal space.&quot; Most people don't really think about what size the bubble of space around them is that dictates how close they are comfortable with other people getting to them, and how much gradients it might have based on personal social dynamics. One of the best ways to start thinking about this (and then applying it to social interactions purposefully) is to spend time in a community where your sense of personal space is wildly different from everyone else's. People that living densely populated areas rarely intuitively understand that part of what people from more rural areas find them rude, is because urban living shrinks the sense of personal space. You can't walk down busy streets, use mass transit, and so on if you can't be very close to other people. It's not uncommon for urban living people to get &quot;too close&quot; and upset people used to having a wider personal space. This also goes in the other direction where rural people don't realize they're coming off as unsociable in urban situations by trying to claim too much personal space when people expect to be physically closer.<br /> <br /> For those less inclined to being careful about ethical or moral considerations, you can also just study con artistry. South Park did a great primer on this by taking down John Edwards (a formerly prominent TV &quot;medium&quot;) by showing how basic the tactics of influencing people can be if you pick the right targets that Stan accidentally convinces Edwards's audience that Stan is the real medium despite him openly saying he's just manipulating them (it is South Park's kind of humor). Cold reading training coupled with mastering how to use the Forer effect and subjective validation is going to make you very good at getting people to do things they wouldn't think they'd do for a complete stranger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And lastly, inducing hormonal and moods reaction is on the area of Life, so, why couldn't Life create a scent that triggers oxycotin (or any other hormone or bodily function that relates to pleasure, relaxarion and trust) and makes the mage more trustworthy? </div> </div> </div>Because there isn't a universal scent that triggers any such responses; nor are the specific reactions to such activated responses predictable. Now, a mage could certainly do that on a single target and wouldn't even need a scent trigger in the first place. The problem is that the more people you target the less effective one chemical pathway activation can possibly be. So it can never be good enough as a single chemical output to make everyone more likely to trust you (aka increasing your Attribute).<br /> <br /> Consider that many antidepressants have warnings of suicide risks (esp. in younger patients). Even if the risk is actually extremely low, it's not zero. So if you're a walking antidepressant chemical emitter, most people are going to feel nothing special (they're not depressed or not in a fashion that responds to medication), a good number of people are going to feel mildly better than usual around you (hey, a place for a bonus to your roll), and some people are going to hurt themselves just because they're around you too much.<br /> <br /> This is why I go back to science mattering if you're going to use science to justify things. This is why direct emotional manipulation is generally a Mind effect even if Life can do some emotional effects as well. Mind is the Sphere of, &quot;aura of trust.&quot; Life isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T23:42:45-07:00","id":1550426,"title":"","content":"I would say that you can affect minds with Mind, Forces and Life. Its just way harder with the last two. The mind is comopsoed of electric impuleses like software and gut bacteria can and will severly affect your mind.<br /> <br /> As for quicksilver its one of the most badly writen characters in the whole marvel universe. If he can percive time as fast as he moves (like in the movies) then he is unbeatable. Literally no one thats not fast as him can do anything to him. Also i think you mistake him with red rush from invnincible (that guy actually cant shut down hes mind speed).<br /> <br /> As for what increases social attributes? Life for Appearance and Data fo Manipulation, Charisma and abilities (i use Data as a 10th sphere). Raw i dont think there is any way to increase social attributes. I was asking about this on this forum and thats the answer i got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T03:12:15-07:00","id":1550431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550426#post1550426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mind is comopsoed of electric impuleses like software...</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot being to overstate how badly this comparison shakes out. The immensity of how different digital data is computed and associated memory works are just... apples and bricks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for quicksilver its one of the most badly writen characters in the whole marvel universe. If he can percive time as fast as he moves (like in the movies) then he is unbeatable. Literally no one thats not fast as him can do anything to him. Also i think you mistake him with red rush from invnincible (that guy actually cant shut down hes mind speed). </div> </div> </div>Claiming any character that's been in publication for that long is &quot;one of the most...&quot; [anything] is always going to be difficult to justify. Quicksilver in the comics is, while incredibly fast, generally depicted well below the Fox X-Men franchise portrays with Evan Peters. The comics usually cite - baring boosts from other characters such as a power up he got from the High Evolutionary - Mach 10 as Quicksilver's top speed. That's ~7,700 mph, which is ridiculously fast for sure, but nothing in the realms of comics where there are multiple characters that can travel at near the speed of light, which is ~100,000 times faster than Mach 10.<br /> <br /> Also, no, I'm not mixing him up with Red Rush. Quicksilver's therapy session is from 1993, so it's safe to say Red Rush is more likely taking inspiration from Quicksilver on this one.<br /> <br /> Boxed for size:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img title=\"a6h5syqisete1.jpg\" data-tempid=\"temp_1853_1745834815064_565\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1853\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1853\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1853&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"a6h5syqisete1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for what increases social attributes? Life for Appearance and Data fo Manipulation, Charisma and abilities (i use Data as a 10th sphere). Raw i dont think there is any way to increase social attributes. I was asking about this on this forum and thats the answer i got. </div> </div> </div>As noted, at least one M20 book cites Life for Charisma and Manipulation even if some of us find the reasoning highly suspect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T03:34:21-07:00","id":1550433,"title":"","content":"I cant see anything in the box","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T04:29:56-07:00","id":1550435,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, Yes, by buffing I mean increasing the dots with duration, and not affecting difficulties. <br /> Which spheres and how, including your scientific explanation, can do that?<br /> <br /> While I agree with your arguments, I feel that it is going to be a very different and harder game if we use real life logic and science here. We are going to find a <b>lot</b> of bs explanations in raw.<br /> <br /> I believe you are also against increasing intelligence and wits dots by &quot;altering brain matter and capacity&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> I kindly ask you to just avoid deep explanations and try to dive into what raw says, especially that one quote I posted from Hdydt. The list is:<br /> <br /> &quot; Rippling muscles, beautiful features, straighter posture, rapid reflexes, and so forth.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I believe translate into: strength, appearance, charisma or manipulation, dexterity . What do you think straigther posture is doing in that list, if not by charisma or manipulation?<br /> <br /> We all know a straight posture shouldn't help prsctically nothing irl, but it seems to be a good enough excuse to increase attributes dots by <b>raw</b>. Not in any personal table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T05:18:43-07:00","id":1550437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550433#post1550433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cant see anything in the box</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If that doesn't do it, just Google X-Force 87 and Quicksilver. Or just take my word for it that I'm not confusing characters instead of acting like my example is flawed because you don't know about the character in question very well.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550435#post1550435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;617&quot;]...including your scientific explanation,...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to continue this, drop the condescending bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T08:22:21-07:00","id":1550441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550402#post1550402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I completely forgot about the size limitations. That makes very clear the differences between ranks. And although Life 3 has no raw size limitation, I can't think of a reason for it to have a better limitation than Life 4.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550403#post1550403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly agree about the size limitation. Most alterations affect mass if you want to be too strict, but I think that goes against the intent. But that can be said of <b>Life 4</b>, too.<br /> <br /> But <b>Life 4</b>'s explicit citation about size and mass seems to infer it was implicit, but already there, on <b>Life 3</b>, and makes sense to similar effects on other Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the reason I brought up the issue outside of one of my main posts is that I was pointing out an exploit that could affect how we use the spheres in play. I was not advocating using Life 4 to infer limitations on Life 3. Indeed, that's one of the initial guidelines for the thread.<br /> <br /> For what it is worth, the reason I think this is happening is because the Change Self track is spread over 4 ranks rather than the 2 the other change tracks uses. So there needed to be limitations on the rank 4 transform self to separate it from the rank 5 perfect metamorphosis. It had nothing to do with limiting alter self and especially not alter others.<br /> <br /> Of course that's way too much inference to put in the writeups for either Life 3 or Life 4. Life 4 has enough of that anyways even when I'm trying to avoid it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T08:27:46-07:00","id":1550442,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Alter Complex Life-Forms/ Transform Self </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this Rank, the mage may enact radical changes on any complex organism \u2013 people, dogs, horses, and so forth. He can uplift other species with new limbs, opposable thumbs, increased brain capacity, etc., so long as he doesn\u2019t change their intrinsic nature.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Working with his own Pattern, that mage can transform himself into other life-forms of similar size and mass; he could become a Great Dane, for example, but not a hummingbird. Special abilities of that form (flight, water breathing, and the like) do not carry over, however, unless he builds them into that new form with additional Life Effects, and the new body might require an adjustment period before the mind and reflexes reflect the new form.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter Others (Alter Complex Lifeforms)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The start of the alter complex life track. Everything the mage could do to Simple Life at Life 2 and himself at Life 3, he can do to anything at Life 4. Unfortunately, all three use different terms for the limitations. Rank 2 uses \u2018state of being\u2019 for the limits on Simple Life, rank 3 uses \u2018essentially human\u2019 for Alter self, rank 4 here uses \u2018intrinsic nature.\u2019 While the words differ, though, all three seem to indicate that the mage can make a vast array of changes so long as the target is still the same kind of creature it started as. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Changed: What Good is a Phone Call if You Are Unable to Speak? (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disturbing transformations like removing someone's mouth or even entire face disappear at this level. </span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transform Self (Transform Self)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The continuation, but oddly not culmination of the Alter Self track. This track does not appear to follow the pattern of Transform Simple Life, or at least that\u2019s what the text looks like. The examples list changing from one life form into another, not turning inside out or pulling a Tetsuo (from Akira), and the transformation is limited to similar sizes and masses. One line in particular stands out:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Special Abilities</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Special abilities of that form (flight, water breathing, and the like) do not carry over, however, unless he builds them into that new form with additional Life Effects </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This line may read as more far reaching than intended. On a direct read this sounds like if a mage turns himself into a form that ordinarily has a special ability, he doesn\u2019t get that ability unless he uses a separate Life Effect to give it to himself. It sounds like if he turns himself into a big fish he doesn\u2019t automatically get water breathing unless he also gives himself gills even though those come with the form. That\u2019s probably not the intended meaning.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I suspect that this is meant to apply to more mythological transformations. If he turns himself into a merman (specifically one without gills), he doesn\u2019t get water-breathing because that was a supernatural, not natural ability. If he turns himself into a bonnacon he doesn\u2019t get the burning flatulence. Etc. I also suspect that the additional effect line isn\u2019t supposed to mean that the ability must be part of a separate spell, but is there to cover cases where the extra ability requires Life 5 or another sphere to achieve.<br /> <br /> Added:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> also have a good point that this could reasonably mean that the special abilities of forms have to be paid for in successes. Those successes would cover the cost of forming the necessary organs and the instincts/skills to use those special abilities. The fish does come with gills, and those gills need to be paid for as part of the cost of transforming into a fish.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-29-2025, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T09:43:42-07:00","id":1550447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550437#post1550437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to continue this, drop the condescending bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not being condescending. I was genuinely asking you what spheres could increase dots in manipulation and charisma and what would be the scientific explanations, since you think my explanations weren't good.<br /> <br /> My point being that if some sphere can do that at all, it should be Life.<br /> <br /> The second point I tried to make is that the game doens't run into deep explanations for the effects when described by raw. And hdydt already says Life can increase Social attributes, being two explanations about &quot;beautiful features&quot; (which is clearly Appearance increase) and &quot;straighter posture&quot; (which I believe fits Charisma increase). I was simply asking you to give your opinions about this line of thought regarding raw.<br /> <br /> But it's not the fist time we talk and you read my posts in an offensive, condescending way. It was not my intention. I just want to have a good conversation about the topic. If you feel offended and can't continue without being rude, maybe we should stop right here.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T09:45:24-07:00","id":1550448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550422#post1550422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> ,So, it is not possible to increase manipulation and charisma through magick?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that, I already stated that I think this should be a <b>Mind</b> effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550422#post1550422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does a &quot;straigther posture&quot; increase in social attributes by raw? Certainly not appearance as it was already described as &quot;beautiful features&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't inspire trust into people increase manipulation?<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't a heavenly charming voice increase charisma? There are even merits that are similar to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no universal &quot;trust inspiring scent&quot;. There's no universal &quot;charming voice&quot;. There's no universal &quot;charming posture&quot;.<br /> <br /> And science matters because you're using science to justify doing this with <b>Life</b>. <b>Mind</b> is a best &quot;Because Magic&quot; Sphere to do those things.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b> creates a specific scent/color/posture/whatever. For it to give a bonus, it would have to have a universal effect. They don't.<br /> <br /> Outside HDYDT, which this thread exists precisely to substitute, the game rarely used <b>Life</b> for those bonuses, either. In fact, the game completely avoids bonus to Social Attributes, giving preference to do it with <b>continuous Mind effects</b>.<br /> <br /> You're otherwise constantly picking statements out of context and ignoring most of the things I said. I'm growing impatient with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T10:38:40-07:00","id":1550452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550448#post1550448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say that, I already stated that I think this should be a <b>Mind</b> effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went back to your posts but couldn't find the statement. Just to be sure, you're talking about attributes increase?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550448#post1550448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no universal &quot;trust inspiring scent&quot;. There's no universal &quot;charming voice&quot;. There's no universal &quot;charming posture&quot;.<br /> <br /> And science matters because you're using science to justify doing this with <b>Life</b>. <b>Mind</b> is a best &quot;Because Magic&quot; Sphere to do those things.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b> creates a specific scent/color/posture/whatever. For it to give a bonus, it would have to have a universal effect. They don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about something like a scent that would trigger trust into people who smells it. The same way you could make a scent that would put dogs to sleep, or calm them down. It's not a real life scent, it's a spell that makes people mood change.<br /> <br /> To be honest I'm also not sure this should increase the attributes or change difficulties... I just think it's weird to mages having all that &quot;unlimited&quot; power and not being able to increase those two attributes.<br /> <br /> If you did meant increasing the atributes with Mind, do you have any suggestion on how that would translate in-game?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T10:44:29-07:00","id":1550454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550442#post1550442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Makes no sense to me transforming into a fish and not being able to breath underwater. Well, to be fair, you <b>could</b> transform into a air breathing fish with lungs. Just make the spell this way. What i believe they meant was exactly what you said, and is further demonstrated a bit in hdydt (I really hate that they could've made an amazing book from this one): if you want some special ability to your new form, you need to add it separately.<br /> <br /> So, you won't breath fire just because you turned into a dragon, you need to add that special power, which would require Forces (and probably Prime) as well as Life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T11:27:42-07:00","id":1550457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550442#post1550442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure. The text doesn't seems to imply that the body itself doesn't have the proper organs, but that you don't have the brain processes that govern those abilities.<br /> <br /> But I always thought this line weird and badly explained. That, and we're talking the Level 4 of a Sphere that was already able to give you such traits. Overall it's a confusing piece.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550452#post1550452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about something like a scent that would trigger trust into people who smells it. The same way you could make a scent that would put dogs to sleep, or calm them down. It's not a real life scent, it's a spell that makes people mood change.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you <b>can't</b> make a scent that would put dogs to sleep with <b>Life</b> alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b> can't create a substance that doesn't exist. Period. It creates biological tissue, at most it can make a tissue that produces a given organic compound.<br /> <br /> Now, you <b>can</b> make an organ that produces a narcotic that works on dogs, but that's because such a substance is already possible and not because it &quot;smells of doggy sleepyness&quot;. Even then you should preferably already know of a real substance that does that.<br /> <br /> Creating new substances is <b>Matter</b>. And to put dogs to sleep you need <b>Mind</b>. If you want to make someone have a &quot;smell that puts dogs to sleep&quot; you need a conjunctional spell of <b>Life</b> and <b>Mind</b>, possibly with <b>Matter</b> if you want the lingering smell to affect dogs after the person left.<br /> <br /> Scents don't trigger trust in humans. They simply don't do that. And since <b>Life</b> can't create a substance that don't exist, nor make a thing have an emotional effect it can't naturally have, the whole idea of doing it with <b>Life</b> alone is outside the scope of the Sphere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550452#post1550452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> If you did meant increasing the atributes with Mind, do you have any suggestion on how that would translate in-game?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One way would be to increase your ability to read social cues, and the speed with which you do so and reacts to it.<br /> <br /> But most similar effects in the game are actually continuous <b>Mind</b> effects affecting the people you want to trust you instead of affecting yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T12:36:11-07:00","id":1550458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550457#post1550457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you <b>can't</b> make a scent that would put dogs to sleep with <b>Life</b> alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b> can't create a substance that doesn't exist. Period. It creates biological tissue, at most it can make a tissue that produces a given organic compound.<br /> <br /> Now, you <b>can</b> make an organ that produces a narcotic that works on dogs, but that's because such a substance is already possible and not because it &quot;smells of doggy sleepyness&quot;. Even then you should preferably already know of a real substance that does that.<br /> <br /> Creating new substances is <b>Matter</b>. And to put dogs to sleep you need <b>Mind</b>. If you want to make someone have a &quot;smell that puts dogs to sleep&quot; you need a conjunctional spell of <b>Life</b> and <b>Mind</b>, possibly with <b>Matter</b> if you want the lingering smell to affect dogs after the person left.<br /> <br /> Scents don't trigger trust in humans. They simply don't do that. And since <b>Life</b> can't create a substance that don't exist, nor make a thing have an emotional effect it can't naturally have, the whole idea of doing it with <b>Life</b> alone is outside the scope of the Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectufly disagree. It's within Life reach to put dogs (and humans) to sleep. As well as Mind. Life can affect moods and any other bodily functions such as spells to sleep, vomit, stun, etc. How exactly it does that depends on the explanation and paradigm/instruments.<br /> <br /> You can put all dogs in the area to sleep and if you want you can lock that effect on you (since that would also require Life). You could make some sort of aura of sleepiness. You don't need to create a whole new substance to do that, although you can do it with Matter as you said, but then you need to make it go inside the dog system to work. With Life, you are just tweaking the dog biology to &quot;shut it off&quot;. Or you could make them bark, or attack too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550457#post1550457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way would be to increase your ability to read social cues, and the speed with which you do so and reacts to it.<br /> <br /> But most similar effects in the game are actually continuous <b>Mind</b> effects affecting the people you want to trust you instead of affecting yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed a good explanation, and one that is also in reach of Life, as we saw earlier in this thread. Life can read moods and physiological stuff. It's not as good as Mind (which can read thoughts), but maybe it's enough to help in this effect? Like, making the mage able to read peoples emotions and stress levels (or any other bodily trait), that allows the mage to be the &quot;perfect&quot; friendly shoulder to cry on or to confide secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T13:02:33-07:00","id":1550460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550458#post1550458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Life, you are just tweaking the dog biology to &quot;shut it off&quot;. Or you could make them bark, or attack too.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, but that would be fundamentally distinct from making a &quot;scent that does&quot;.<br /> <br /> Buffing an attribute means targeting the beneficiary of the effect with a spell that causes <b>this target</b> to be more &quot;something&quot;. Lets say, &quot;sleep inducer&quot;.<br /> <br /> Causing a dog to sleep with <b>Life</b> means targeting <b>the dog</b> with the spell to <b>directly</b> cause it to sleep. Same result, but reached through entirely different means.<br /> <br /> If I make you exude an aura of <b>Life</b> Magic that causes people to feel a certain way, I'm not targeting you with the spell, I'm not buffing you, I'm targeting <b>other people</b> with the effect and <b>incidentally</b> giving you an advantage.<br /> <br /> However this advantage is mechanically represented (which can be as bonus dice), it isn't buffing your Attributes in the same sense. With <b>Life</b> I can buff your <b>Strength</b> by making you <i>actually stronger</i>, with <b>Mind</b> I can buff your <b>Wits</b> by making your brain <i>actually faster</i>. Using <b>Life</b> to create an &quot;aura of charisma&quot;, if even accepted as a valid effect, isn't making you <i>actually</i> anything, it's making <i><b>other people</b></i> more susceptible.<br /> <br /> And the complexity of human interactions and reaction to experience is such, and so individualized, that it simply goes beyond what can be done with the sensorial/emotional stimuli that <b>Life</b> creates. At this point it is basically being as good at mind manipulation as the <b>Mind</b> Sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T14:45:28-07:00","id":1550465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550442#post1550442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I Have No Mouth\u2026</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The full change described in the Harlan Ellison story has to wait until Life 5, but taking away someone\u2019s mouth or other features is possible at this level.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>What good is a phone</i> call if you are unable to <i>speak</i>?&quot; might be a better cultural reference for what Life 4 says it can do... same practical point though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transform Self (Transform Self)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">...</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts?</span> </div> </div> </div>The rules say what they say, and what they say is dumb. Everything is is people trying to read into it to find something more functional.<br /> <br /> I would say that it is more in-line with the RAW to say that the intent is for transformations into forms with non-human abilities should take more successes (since that's ultimately all having to do multiple Life effects to do it would really result in).<br /> <br /> If it said something to the extent of, &quot;The farther from human the animal you shift into, the more successes it will take,&quot; and features such as flight or being able to respire through water were just examples of what makes something farther from human, I'm not sure people would like it, but there wouldn't be a lot of debating about authorial intent.<br /> <br /> If we look at HDYDT? we... do get confirmation that the intent was not have turning into a fish require you to also have to put magical resources into growing gills as well... but HDYDT? also leans much more into Life 4 being limited as monteparnas pointed out in the sense that transforming into a fish when you're a human results in significant penalties because you have no idea how to breathe with gills or swim with true fins.<br /> <br /> So the intent if we include HDYDT? is that turning from a human into a chimpanzee should be easier than turning from a human into a fish. Core book is really oddly framed in how it expresses that. HDYDT? is clearer, but also adds a number of unique complications (increased difficulties on all actions while adjusting to the new form, having to spend WP to avoid getting lost in the form, or having to spend XP to &quot;learn&quot; a form and avoid those risks). I think it's reasonable to say the core &quot;simple&quot; version is more successes, but HDYDT? offers alternative costs if you want to explore them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550447#post1550447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not being condescending.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, you managed. Intentions and results can be like that. &quot;Your science,&quot; is generally a very rude and dismissive thing to say to someone with scientific training because it either implies (a) their specific training is suspect and/or an inferior field of study, or (b) they are advocating their pet hypotheses over the scientific goal of consensus theories.<br /> <br /> And maybe consider that you have now how two people express displeasure in your rhetorical approach in this so... maybe some self-reflection is in order?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was genuinely asking you what spheres could increase dots in manipulation and charisma and what would be the scientific explanations, since you think my explanations weren't good. </div> </div> </div>I've already answered what Spheres I think would be best (Mind most directly, Entropy has a compelling case that could be made instead).<br /> <br /> Asking for a scientific explanation is a bad faith tactic and I will not reply to that; I've already detailed my feelings on when science should be applied to these considerations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point being that if some sphere can do that at all, it should be Life. </div> </div> </div>You've had two people try from multiple different angles that Life can't do all of that, but Mind can. You have presented no real counterpoint to any of the reasons put forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second point I tried to make is that the game doens't run into deep explanations for the effects when described by raw. </div> </div> </div>I also already addressed this: I feel this is a negative aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And hdydt already says Life can increase Social attributes, being two explanations about &quot;beautiful features&quot; (which is clearly Appearance increase) and &quot;straighter posture&quot; (which I believe fits Charisma increase). I was simply asking you to give your opinions about this line of thought regarding raw. </div> </div> </div>If you don't want to engage with my willingness to use vulgarity (which is not the only form of rudeness, and how rude it is is very subjective), so be it, but this is bullshit.<br /> <br /> You're asking me to engage with the RAW (which doesn't assign specific Attributes to any of these), while you are using RAI (claiming they clearly apply to specific ones). Hell, your reading is pretty suspect. The things you're listing are not explanations of how magic improves Attributes, they're a list of potential perceivable consequences from boosting your Attributes. That is, if you increase your Strength rating with magic, your physical appearance will change in response. It's a list of side effects, not explanations. If you use Life to boost your Strength, you get muscles to go along with it; not you give yourself muscles to increase your Strength via Life Magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T17:54:29-07:00","id":1550468,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I don't think M20 actually stated whether or not something can be created from nothing, even with five dots. The Prime 2 thing for conjuring fireballs out of nowhere is pretty heavily implied to be a creatio ex materia situation where you're converting Quintessence into matter and energy. As an aside, actually having straight up creatio ex nihilo would be a pretty big thing to see, given how the possibility of it really depends on the paradigm (for an LDS mage, for example, it won't fly - even God constructed the universe out of pre-existing materials).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T01:05:59-07:00","id":1550475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550437#post1550437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/a/peter-david-giving-us-best-quicksilver-characterization-RvwlnNn </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If that doesn't do it, just Google X-Force 87 and Quicksilver. Or just take my word for it that I'm not confusing characters instead of acting like my example is flawed because you don't know about the character in question very well.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to continue this, drop the condescending bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now i see. As for if something is badly writen or not is quite obvious in almost every speedseter in any of the printed universes otherwise they could not possibly lose to anyone slower than them (same problem we have with extra action powers in the game but bigger). Not a topic for this place though.<br /> <br /> I have to defend lord Revan here. He did no such thing. Reflect if youre not projecting here.<br /> <br /> Going back to the topic.<br /> Shouldnt the i have no mouth example work at life 3? I mean its just skin and maybe bones if someone is determinated.<br /> <br /> As for the line about transformations it seems to me that it just means that fife has to work within nature. That would also suggest that someone increasing strenght with life has to get bigger for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T03:46:03-07:00","id":1550476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550475#post1550475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to defend lord Revan here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm exceedingly confident that if you DMed Travis and asked him what to do if you felt it had come to the point of &quot;having&quot; to defend another poster, he'd tell you to report it and let the mods handle it instead of jumping in yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reflect if youre not projecting here. </div> </div> </div>I'm certainly not being my best self... if I'm aiming crass language at someone that's sort of the point. I attempted to express my reactions calmly, and it was not listened to. While I know plenty of folks around here would rather I work harder on alternative methods of dealing with things, it's not something I have perceive in myself as a distinctly negative trait even if I'd rather the Internet be a nicer place that hasn't convinced me that it's a responsible response.<br /> <br /> As I'm self-aware of all of that, however a trained analyst might label my behaviors in a clinical setting, it fails to meet the classical or most of the modern definitions of psychological project as those involve the subconscious assumptions of one's personal negative traits onto another person's motivations. You might not agree with my emotional response to Lord Revan's post as being condescending - even after my explanation of why - but I think you'd be hard pressed to argue that I think he's acting the way I would act when he clearly isn't.<br /> <br /> And I'll go a bit farther just to turn this back to the tangent that spawned it: it's a great example of how Charisma and Manipulation don't mesh well with the majority of the Spheres because they're so contextual in application. I was raised with, among other things, a sense of &quot;you can't trust people that never curse,&quot; as people that are never willing to use such strong language in front of others are inherently hiding their true emotions. It's not a particularly uncommon attitude in plenty of areas/backgrounds. It's not particularly healthy for interacting with diverse groups, but being able to be disarming to a wide variety of cultural backgrounds is clearly part of both traits. It's similar to the cliche of voters wanting to think of their elected leaders as people they could imagine going to the bar and having a few drinks with. It's objectively not really a valuable sign of character, but culturally it's a signal of shared norms and understanding on basic mannerisms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shouldnt the i have no mouth example work at life 3? </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, despite M20 formalizing the &quot;+1 success to target others&quot; rule to make casting negative effects a bit harder like that, it retains the previous editions' decision to have the &quot;Alter Self&quot; and &quot;Healing/Harm&quot; progressions to also require one higher Rank to use on other &quot;complex&quot; targets. This event extends to Life 5's ultimately &quot;Alter Self&quot; abilities not actually be something you can do to others directly unless your ST allows Archspheres (so better luck just grabbing enough Prime to make Wonders that cast specific Life 5 effects on the user instead).<br /> <br /> I don't think the increased rating to do things to others that you can do to yourself is well supported by the logic of the system, but it's how Life is written. Take that as you will for what &quot;should&quot; be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T06:15:16-07:00","id":1550478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550460#post1550460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could, but that would be fundamentally distinct from making a &quot;scent that does&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Maybe the scent part is more into instruments than the rules. Still, Life can do sleeping area effects for specific species and you can lock that area effect into your pattern. Mechanically, it is doable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550457#post1550457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buffing an attribute means targeting the beneficiary of the effect with a spell that causes <b>this target</b> to be more &quot;something&quot;. Lets say, &quot;sleep inducer&quot;.<br /> <br /> Causing a dog to sleep with <b>Life</b> means targeting <b>the dog</b> with the spell to <b>directly</b> cause it to sleep. Same result, but reached through entirely different means.<br /> <br /> If I make you exude an aura of <b>Life</b> Magic that causes people to feel a certain way, I'm not targeting you with the spell, I'm not buffing you, I'm targeting <b>other people</b> with the effect and <b>incidentally</b> giving you an advantage.<br /> <br /> However this advantage is mechanically represented (which can be as bonus dice), it isn't buffing your Attributes in the same sense. With <b>Life</b> I can buff your <b>Strength</b> by making you <i>actually stronger</i>, with <b>Mind</b> I can buff your <b>Wits</b> by making your brain <i>actually faster</i>. Using <b>Life</b> to create an &quot;aura of charisma&quot;, if even accepted as a valid effect, isn't making you <i>actually</i> anything, it's making <i><b>other people</b></i> more susceptible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good point, and I concede. In practice, this may be similar to increasing the attribute because that's kinda what giving extra dices are... Or even better if it translates into extra successes. But I understand that this is not exactly raw and very ST dependant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550457#post1550457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the complexity of human interactions and reaction to experience is such, and so individualized, that it simply goes beyond what can be done with the sensorial/emotional stimuli that <b>Life</b> creates. At this point it is basically being as good at mind manipulation as the <b>Mind</b> Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you mean with the last sentence. You mean one need to read thoughts for that? My idea was to make the mage capable of reading moods and emotions so he can take advantage of this. For example, if someone is afraid, you can manipulate the person into doing something out of fear. Same for love. Think of Palpatine manipulating Anakin all over by knowing how he felt about all that was happening.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, you managed. Intentions and results can be like that. &quot;Your science,&quot; is generally a very rude</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said &quot;your science&quot;. I said &quot;your scientific explanation&quot;. I was asking for <b>your</b> explanation, with a scientific view about the subject at hand. You simply chose to read my sentence in a rude way, as if I was trying to offend you or your science knowledge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already answered what Spheres I think would be best (Mind most directly, Entropy has a compelling case that could be made instead).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see Entropy affecting modifiers, but how could it increase any attribute?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking for a scientific explanation is a bad faith tactic and I will not reply to that; I've already detailed my feelings on when science should be applied to these considerations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would asking for an explanation be bad faith??? I was asking to understand what you think would be a plausible way to do it and try to fit that in Life. To be honest, it's the opposite of bad faith, since I was trying to fit the effect into your way of viewing the game...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've had two people try from multiple different angles that Life can't do all of that, but Mind can. You have presented no real counterpoint to any of the reasons put forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not entirely true. I didn't presented any counterpoint to Mind because I'm ok with it being capable to increase those attributes. I also concede that the pheromones/scent/aura idea isn't exactly an attribute buffs (although it might be the same mechanically).<br /> <br /> My main counterpoint, was that we don't need much to explain an effect. And I can provide you another solution:<br /> <br /> - Reading the manipulation text again, it includes hiding your intentions, having a good poker face. There are several body traits that can show a liar, like sweat, stuttering, looking to a certain direction, accelerated heartbeat, increased blinking, voice pitch shifting,and so on. The list is big. By taking control of his body, the Life mage could simply avoid all of that and have the perfect poker face, not showing any sign of nervousness, even a very confident and honest behavior. On top of that, you can use Life senses to catch that and to be capable of reading moods so you can know when people is lying to you and use their feelings to manipulate them.<br /> <br /> - Charisma is described as having <i>it</i>, as some sort of presence, being noted. A true (not forced) smile, a confident behavior, a commanding body language, often present in leaders and good speakers can do that.<br /> <br /> That is way more than is provided to increase Wits and Intelligence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also already addressed this: I feel this is a negative aspect of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, this is how it works. I think it is made this way exactly to allow more versatility to the game. And also to not require too much knowledge from the players. Not all players are real life scientist or want to dig deep to play the game. Hence, things like &quot;altering brain matter&quot; is acceptable and enough to increase mental attributes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't want to engage with my willingness to use vulgarity (which is not the only form of rudeness, and how rude it is is very subjective), so be it, but this is bullshit.<br /> <br /> You're asking me to engage with the RAW (which doesn't assign specific Attributes to any of these), while you are using RAI (claiming they clearly apply to specific ones). Hell, your reading is pretty suspect. The things you're listing are not explanations of how magic improves Attributes, they're a list of potential perceivable consequences from boosting your Attributes. That is, if you increase your Strength rating with magic, your physical appearance will change in response. It's a list of side effects, not explanations. If you use Life to boost your Strength, you get muscles to go along with it; not you give yourself muscles to increase your Strength via Life Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, the list do represent what attributes are being increased, even if they are consequences. The consequences are related to the explanations.<br /> <br /> My reading is suspect?? The book says &quot;Altered Physical and Social attributes generally reveal themselves in obvious ways: rippling muscles, beautiful features, straighter posture, rapid reflexes and so forth.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is not a matter of RAI. The book is clearly listing different attributes. Rippling muscles can only be addressed to Strength. Beautiful features can only be addressed to Appearance. Rapid Reflexes must be Dexterity and Straighter Posture is related to Charisma, which is often described by having presence. What else could it be? The consequence of increasing Strength? Who the hell would describe increasing Strength with good posture? If anything, your lack of text interpretation in this case is suspect. I bet that if the book wasn't completely clear on the mental attributes increase you would say it wasn't possible with Life too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T07:28:35-07:00","id":1550479,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;<i>What good is a phone</i> call if you are unable to <i>speak</i>?&quot; might be a better cultural reference for what Life 4 says it can do... same practical point though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I waffled back and forth between that exact reference and &quot;I have no mouth.&quot; Also the Helvetica Scenario, though that is less well known. I think you are right. I can save &quot;I have no mouth&quot; for the rank that can pull off the whole transformation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules say what they say, and what they say is dumb. Everything is is people trying to read into it to find something more functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's often the case, yes. But in the past I've been too quick to discard lines as contradictory and badly edited when in fact they are describing an ability I hadn't thought of or a recommendation of how an ability is supposed to work. That's why my goal is to try to find interpretations that work with the text as much as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550465#post1550465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that it is more in-line with the RAW to say that the intent is for transformations into forms with non-human abilities should take more successes (since that's ultimately all having to do multiple Life effects to do it would really result in).</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is the exact kind of thing I am looking for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550476#post1550476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, despite M20 formalizing the &quot;+1 success to target others&quot; rule to make casting negative effects a bit harder like that, it retains the previous editions' decision to have the &quot;Alter Self&quot; and &quot;Healing/Harm&quot; progressions to also require one higher Rank to use on other &quot;complex&quot; targets. This event extends to Life 5's ultimately &quot;Alter Self&quot; abilities not actually be something you can do to others directly unless your ST allows Archspheres (so better luck just grabbing enough Prime to make Wonders that cast specific Life 5 effects on the user instead).<br /> <br /> I don't think the increased rating to do things to others that you can do to yourself is well supported by the logic of the system, but it's how Life is written. Take that as you will for what &quot;should&quot; be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went into Life thinking that was the way it was written, but M20 specifically says that all of the ways a Master of Life can change himself, he can also apply to other complex organisms. At Life 5 the full range of transformation/transmogrification is available to the self and all others. It's HDYDT that makes the claim otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T07:52:02-07:00","id":1550480,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Transform &amp; Create Complex Life-Forms/Perfect Metamorphosis </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the Master of Life may adopt any form he wishes to achieve and may transform other complex organisms the same way. His expertise allows him to make permanent changes to life-Patterns, create complex life-forms from energy (with Prime 2), give them consciousness (with Mind 5), transmute them into other elements (Forces or Matter 3) or raw energy (Prime 5), radically age or de-age them (Entropy 4 or Time 3), or instill them with spirits (Spirit 3 or 5). Without such measures, however, his creations remain mindless, soulless sacks of life \u2013 alive, but nothing more.</span> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transform Others (Transform Complex Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmogrify Others (Perfect Metamorphosis)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmogrify Self (Perfect Metamorphosis)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The culmination of the Alter Self and Alter Complex Life tracks. At this point a mage can manipulate, change, and transform lifeforms in near limitless ways. There is no given limit for size or any other attribute.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I Must Scream\u2026</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There was a striking description from one of the Abyssal Exalted books (2<sup>nd</sup> ed I think) of a Necrotech airship kept aloft by screaming mouths. That is, the mouths on the top were convinced they were suffocating and sucked in air at a furious pace, while the ones on bottom constantly screamed the air out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Well at this rank, that kind of Biotech engineering becomes possible. Of course, there would need to be considerably more modification for the mouths/lungs to put out enough force to support themselves, let alone an airship, but that\u2019s also within the scope of Life 5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have no idea why any mage would want to make this idea work, but it is a good illustration of the level of creation possible at Life 5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A less horrific version is the Skewer from Expedition and the third form creatures from Tremors, both of which produce their own chemical propulsion.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His expertise allows him to make permanent changes to life-Patterns </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Permanent Changes</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is one of those descriptions that should be clearer than it is. Per normal magic rules, duration can be made permanent with enough successes. There\u2019s not usually a rank requirement. Except that Life and Matter both mention permanent changes at Rank 5. Now there is one other part of Life that mentions Permanent Changes, and that is Pattern Bleed. So, the one thing we can be certain of is that Life 5 allows changes that bypass the problem of Pattern Bleed. As for the rest, I see three options.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 1 - The most unsatisfying is that Permanent Change doesn\u2019t have anything to do with permanency and is solely a tag to overcome Pattern Bleed. I\u2019m not going to spend much time on this other than to say that it would be terrible game design if permanent didn\u2019t in any way mean permanent.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 2 - Life (and Matter) are special and permanent spells are not possible until Rank 5. This is a reasonable approach. That said, if this were the case, I really would have expected it to be said directly somewhere.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also, by the methodology set forth at the beginning we\u2019d need it to be said in the Base Life section. Life 5 can\u2019t tell Life 2, 3, and 4 what they are not capable of. But that's just a limit on how we look at the rules in this thread, not how we look at them in general.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 3 - The duration rules are about the permanence of spells. Life 5 is talking about a permanent alteration of the life pattern. The spell is over and done and the change is the new normal. This has the advantage of making sense within the context of pattern bleed. Permanency ends Pattern Bleed because the target\u2019s form actually matches their true pattern.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If you have any other options, let me know. I\u2019m going to write this up based on option 3 for now.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is My Life Now (Perfect Metamorphosis)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can change a target\u2019s pattern permanently. Unlike spells of permanent duration, there is no magic keeping the target\u2019s pattern this way, and this cannot be dispelled or unwoven because the magic is over and done with already. The new pattern is simply reality now.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>\u2026and I Have No Mouth</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cI am a great soft jelly thing. Smoothly rounded, with no mouth, with pulsing white holes filled by fog where my eyes used to be. Rubbery appendages that were once my arms\u037e bulks rounding down into legless humps of soft slippery matter. I leave a moist trail when I move. Blotches of diseased, evil gray come and go on my surface, as though light is being beamed from within.\u201d </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, the permanent transformation at the end of I Have No Mouth and I Must Scream is possible at this rank. It is unclear if the narrator is simple life, complex life, or something unknown, but that doesn\u2019t matter at Rank 5. He also appears to be functionally immortal, and though he has no eyes he can tell what he looks like, and these too are possible at Rank 5.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Abilities</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Life (Transform Complex Life + Fuel Pattern)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is such a well-known power that it barely needs description. By adding Prime 2 a mage can divert quintessence to create an entirely new pattern. One important element is that at this rank these created life forms can be made permanent in a way that rank 3 could not accomplish. </span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instill Mind (Transform Complex Life + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is getting into a hazy area of Mage because it isn\u2019t automatically obvious what it takes to attach a mind or a soul to a body and what sphere is doing what. That will probably need its own section. For now, this is likely a grafting effect, hence the need for Life 5 for complex creatures.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m at a loss for the next two. They both seem like something that the supplemental sphere can do on their own. We\u2019re looking for some kind of effect that can only be done with both, or at the very least will work significantly better if both are involved.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution \u2013 Prime/Raw Energy</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So what exactly is intended here with this \u2018transmute them into other elements (Forces or Matter 3) or raw energy (Prime 5)? On its face, this seems like a standard transmutation of complex life into some other form, essentially destroying the person and turning them into something else. Life 5/Forces 3 and Life 5/Matter 2 work for that.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmute Complex Life to Elemental Substance (Transform Complex Life + [Other])</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Standard transmutation effect.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution Continued \u2013 Prime/Raw Energy</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This doesn\u2019t work for Life 5/Prime 5, though. Converting someone into quintessence and sending it back wherever it goes would be Life 5/Prime 2 at most. Also, Prime 5 can actually pull all the quintessence out of a person on its own. I actually can\u2019t think of an application for Life 5/Prime 5 that could reasonably fit \u2018turn someone into raw energy.\u2019 Any ideas?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Added: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> pointed out that Life 5\u2019s impossible/exotic life ability would mean it can transform someone into another substance while keeping them alive. This could in theory use just Prime 2 for Body of Light, but perhaps the idea is that <u>the Life 5/Prime 5 version turns someone into a periapt of their own quintessential form, or as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> suggests, an actual Node.</u></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Age and De-age</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s a similar problem here. Shouldn\u2019t Life 4 be able to age or de-age on its own. And shouldn\u2019t Entropy 4? To be a conjunctional effect this should achieve something neither one can do on their own.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maybe Life 5 is here to bring permanence to an otherwise impermanent effect (though as far as I\u2019m aware, nothing says Time and Entropy can\u2019t do permanent effects). However, it still seems that Life 5 could bring both de-ageing and permanency on its own.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The challenge here is to find an effect that Life, Entropy, and Time can\u2019t do on their own, but that both Time and Entropy can accomplish equally effectively with Life.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts?</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When we get to rank 5 there shouldn\u2019t be much off limits.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Exotic Life (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Forces 5, mages should be able to generate Life patterns with impossible physics (like Matter can make substances with impossible physics) and Life patterns with completely alien biological principles. The former would include people with organs that phase through each other, allowing impossibly large organs to fit inside of them by overlapping. The latter would include silicon-based biology and non-nucleic forms of genetic storage.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Life 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. The existence of Archspheres could change this, but they aren\u2019t listed in M20.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-07-2025, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T09:40:59-07:00","id":1550483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who the hell would describe increasing Strength with good posture?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, having a good posture will do a whole lot more to increase your effective strenght than your charm (any sort of task related to strength requires having a good posture, as any weigth-lifter can confirm, whereas I can think about many leaders with cult-like followers that don't have a particularly good posture) <hr /><br /> In my opinion, indeed, Mind or Entropy would fit better, because society it's a complex construct of interactions that can't be easily reduced to this or that trait of your body. I.E, being &quot;militarly straigh&quot; may be the &quot;good posture&quot; to be charismatic arround military people, but would work the other way arround with many social groups.<br /> Sensing stress and reducing it could work to ease social interaction in the sense it makes you look friendly, but people very often don't look for a &quot;friendly shoulder&quot; on a leader - most leaders I know are very unsavory people, that cause a lot of stress and just happen to direct that stress towards a goal people already agreed it's worth pursuing.<br /> And what Attribute should go into writting an inflamatory <b>text</b>, if not Manipulation or Charisma?, there's no way Life would affect <i>that</i> (except, maybe, to better your caligraphy :P), and there's no aura that would affect people at that &quot;range&quot;<br /> <br /> Mechanically, all the effects suggested to raise Charimsa and Manipulation with Life look more like they could justify a circumstantial bonus to a specific roll than the persistent constant bonus of an Attribute. These traits are something so immateral that, while Life could certainly *help* at many things related to them, I don't think it should be their &quot;rulling sphere&quot;, so to speak.<br /> <br /> A better argument could be made for Mind and Entropy. These could &quot;affect&quot; social interactions directly, and an argument could be made for a spell that makes 'em go &quot;your way&quot; all the time in a way functionally similar to that of raising an Attribute does:<br /> <br /> Mind can feel the social cues that allow to manipulate each individual, it can create&quot; Pressence like&quot; auras, and it has relation to stuff like language and meaning (debatable).<br /> <br /> Life has to shift biology to accomodate to the desired interaction better, and it has no way of knowing the 'rules' of the interaction as they change, outside of what the mage itself knows (it WOULD need to be able to read minds to do that on it's own).<br /> <br /> And I think Entropy should be <i>better </i>than both Mind and Life. There's a lot of unexplained factors about these Attributes (what the heck it's &quot;having<i> <b>it</b></i>&quot;?, what is <b><i>it</i></b>?), and I'm not clear being better at getting social cues would do a whole lot to being <i>substantially </i>better at taking advantage of them all the time...<br /> <br /> ... but Entropy 5 does affect directly the undercurrents of tought and social development. If something could give you a permanent enhancement to your capability <i>to move people </i>w/o any sort of direct mind control being involved, the sphere that it's all about the movement of ephemeral things should be it.<br /> <br /> It can allow you to sense social cues, to affect them even at unknown ranges and targets (trough memes), and it could ensure the &quot;focus&quot; (so to speak) it's always following you and what you do w/o anything circumstantial about what you're trying to do mattering. This is the closest to having &quot;magical charisma&quot; I can think off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-29-2025, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T10:38:37-07:00","id":1550485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a similar problem here. Shouldn\u2019t Life 4 be able to age or de-age on its own. And shouldn\u2019t Entropy 4? To be a conjunctional effect this should achieve something neither one can do on their own.<br /> <br /> Maybe Life 5 is here to bring permanence to an otherwise impermanent effect (though as far as I\u2019m aware, nothing says Time and Entropy can\u2019t do permanent effects). However, it still seems that Life 5 could bring both de-ageing and permanency on its own.<br /> <br /> The challenge here is to find an effect that Life, Entropy, and Time can\u2019t do on their own, but that both Time and Entropy can accomplish equally effectively with Life.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 5 should be enough on it's own. Same for Time, but with potential complications? . Not so sure about Entropy.<br /> <br /> *Entropy ... I would argue that since age it's natural, merely reversing decay wouldn't be enough. You would need to change what ageing means to cells to alter that, and that I think could require Life. I used to interpret that with only Entropy you would become an extremelly healthy old dude, but not a young dude.<br /> <br /> *Time can age and de-age, if I'm not remembering bad, ain't very granular when it affects patterns. Time 3 needs Mind to rewind time on your body remembering what happened. In a similar vein, de-aging with just Time would send your body (and mind) to a previous state, that may net you more than just a younger body. Like, if you had a phisical condition back then that got better, you would get that back too.<br /> <br /> *Life 5, perhaps, could be unable to make you <b><i>unaging </i></b>w/o extra Spheres. There are living beings that don't age, and Life can make your body like them, but I'm not sure you can issolate that &quot;property&quot; w/o transmuting your body into something inhuman, or can it?. I know Life 5 allows to give yourself supernatural powers (such as breathing fire), but only with conjunctional Spheres. For an ageless body that's not also made of jellyfish, I think it could be similar and require an extra Time/Entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T10:53:49-07:00","id":1550486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550483#post1550483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, having a good posture will do a whole lot more to increase your effective strenght than your charm (any sort of task related to strength requires having a good posture, as any weigth-lifter can confirm, whereas I can think about many leaders with cult-like followers that don't have a particularly good posture) <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it helps. But when you think of someone increasing his strength you won't think posture. You think muscles. I think that maybe a mage could increase his strentgh by getting a better posture instead of better muscles (Idk if one could go to 5 str only with posture, though), but that is not what the text is telling us. It is providing examples of different attributes changes. And Strength is already there with &quot;rippling muscles&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550483#post1550483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A better argument could be made for Mind and Entropy. These could &quot;affect&quot; social interactions directly, and an argument could be made for a spell that makes 'em go &quot;your way&quot; all the time in a way functionally similar to that of raising an Attribute does:</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be an option for Life too. I believe we all feel this way because the books never present a direct indication of social attributes increase (except for appearance). And I think that's one way of running it. You simply can't increase those attributes, you can only affect dice pool and difficulties (but for matters, your dots don't change).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550483#post1550483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind can feel the social cues that allow to manipulate each individual, it can create&quot; Pressence like&quot; auras, and it has relation to stuff like language and meaning (debatable).<br /> <br /> Life has to shift biology to accomodate to the desired interaction better, and it has no way of knowing the 'rules' of the interaction as they change, outside of what the mage itself knows (it WOULD need to be able to read minds to do that on it's own).<br /> <br /> And I think Entropy should be <i>better </i>than both Mind and Life. There's a lot of unexplained factors about these Attributes (what the heck it's &quot;having<i> <b>it</b></i>&quot;?, what is <b><i>it</i></b>?), and I'm not clear being better at getting social cues would do a whole lot to being <i>substantially </i>better at taking advantage of them all the time...<br /> <br /> ... but Entropy 5 does affect directly the undercurrents of tought and social development. If something could give you a permanent enhancement to your capability <i>to move people </i>w/o any sort of direct mind control being involved, the sphere that it's all about the movement of ephemeral things should be it.<br /> <br /> It can allow you to sense social cues, to affect them even at unknown ranges and targets (trough memes), and it could ensure the &quot;focus&quot; (so to speak) it's always following you and what you do w/o anything circumstantial about what you're trying to do mattering. This is the closest to having &quot;magical charisma&quot; I can think off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that increasing those attributes should have a &quot;rulling sphere&quot;, as it isn't specified in any of them in raw and all we can debate here is what are the possibilities of doing that in a custom way, which won't be exactly raw.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also,reading your post something made me thougth: all attributes have several characteristics to them. Stamina, for example, represents your fatigue resistance, your immunologic system and your tolerance for pain, among others. The same way, manipulation is described as &quot;having a poker face&quot;, &quot;spotting when being manipulated&quot; and &quot;bending other to her whim&quot;. Charisma includes being &quot;likeable&quot;, &quot;able to impress others&quot; and to &quot;stand out&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, my question is, when you increase your immunologic system, do you get dots in stamina? How many of those descriptions one need to consider an increase in stamina?<br /> <br /> And that is on point with what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you use Life to boost your Strength, you get muscles to go along with it; not you give yourself muscles to increase your Strength via Life Magic. </div> </div> </div>But then how would one boost Strength? How would be the effect detailed? The player can't just &quot;I want to increase 2 dots in strength&quot;, there should be an in-game explanation of the effect, which probably won't cover all aspect that an attribute involves, right?<br /> <br /> As I see it, increasing one aspect of the attribute is already enough to increase dots, just like I want my body tissues to be more resistant to impact does not affect directly you immune system, but is enough to boost Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T11:06:44-07:00","id":1550487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 3 - The duration rules are about the permanence of spells. Life 5 is talking about a permanent alteration of the life pattern. The spell is over and done and the change is the new normal. This has the advantage of making sense within the context of pattern bleed. Permanency ends Pattern Bleed because the target\u2019s form actually matches their true pattern.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I believe this is the exact idea. And your example bellow fits perfectly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is My Life Now (Perfect Metamorphosis)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can change a target\u2019s pattern permanently. Unlike spells of permanent duration, there is no magic keeping the target\u2019s pattern this way, and this cannot be dispelled or unwoven because the magic is over and done with already. The new pattern is simply reality now.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Matter and Life transformations are not permanent, so if you turn lead into gold, it will turn back after a while. You need to apply the required successes for permanency and even then it is still a spell that can be unwoven.<br /> <br /> What rank 5 seems to do is to directly change the pattern, not needing all those successes anymore and not being possible to uneave them, as the spell changed the pattern directly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution \u2013 Prime/Raw Energy</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> \u2018turn someone into raw energy.\u2019 Any ideas?[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe turning someone into Quintessence available to others? Maybe something like a node? To be honest, I believe this is just the book not knowing it own rules...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Age and De-age</i></span></span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't think of anything besides pure sphere bloat. Time alone should age-deage, as should Life 5. And Entropy 4 can grant vitality and I would consider that as staying young for a long time, as aging is the decay of the body...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T11:41:36-07:00","id":1550488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it helps. But when you think of someone increasing his strength you won't think posture. You think muscles. I think that maybe a mage could increase his strentgh by getting a better posture instead of better muscles (Idk if one could go to 5 str only with posture, though), but that is not what the text is telling us. It is providing examples of different attributes changes. And Strength is already there with &quot;rippling muscles&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you're comming, I think that's a strong RAI about <b>that </b>text (not RAW, because it is a stronlgy implied relation, and not an explicit one). But that text ain't core, and by any common sense it expands the functions of the Sphere far beyond &quot;what the sphere says it can do&quot; (think about my example of writting a text).<br /> <br /> I'm unconvinced we should treat the &quot;intent&quot; of what's being said there as such gospel as to infer a whole new area within a Sphere, an area that deals with things that aren't biological at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That seems to be an option for Life too. </div> </div> </div>Not really, &quot;social interactions&quot; aren't covered in anything Life can do in the core. You're reverse-engineering that from somewhere else.<br /> <br /> I gave examples, that you're ignoring, about social interactions. At least one could <b>never </b>fall uppon Life. A lot of people gave examples of how while your biology may influence social interactions, nothing related to Life can be interpreted a single way and it always depends on the observer and the medium<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, my question is, when you increase your immunologic system, do you get dots in stamina? How many of those descriptions one need to consider an increase in stamina? </div> </div> </div>Stamina it's going to be implied in all of them. If you don't &quot;increase your immunologic system&quot;, then the bonus wouldn't apply to sickness?, only to punches? . One needs to make a house-rule that woud increment Attributes in a granular fashion for that to work otherwise.<br /> <br /> Life just happens to cover nearly all of them, if not all of them, insofar as it applies to Stamina. Even it's few mental aspects are neatly covered by biological responses.<br /> <br /> Life covers a lot less when considering the Social Attributes. Hence why I think it's much more problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T14:24:55-07:00","id":1550491,"title":"","content":"I can see the argument for Life needing Time to actually revert a being to a younger state, but halting aging itself should just be Life, given how senescence itself is a biological mechanism. In terms of just age regression and age progression, I think that Time 4 should be enough for that, sphere bloat is not really needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","user":"Verlan","date":". 04-29-2025, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T21:52:55-07:00","id":1550500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550478#post1550478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand what you mean with the last sentence. You mean one need to read thoughts for that? My idea was to make the mage capable of reading moods and emotions so he can take advantage of this. For example, if someone is afraid, you can manipulate the person into doing something out of fear. Same for love. Think of Palpatine manipulating Anakin all over by knowing how he felt about all that was happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>What capability is <b>Life</b> giving you to read moods? <b>Life</b> doesn't do that. It can read only the most basic emotions and sensations, but only if the spell is aimed at the target of the reading.<br /> <br /> You want to give yourself a hormone-sensing nose? That isn't all that effective, it's a really shallow understanding of the target's mood, and it can confuse you more than help as it shifts your attention from actually useful cues.<br /> <br /> My paragraph meant two things:<br /> <br /> 1- Reading people has a lot more to do with experience than with a more or less robust sensory equipment. That has been explained to you several times by different people, you just refuse to acknowledge it;<br /> <br /> 2- Giving <b>Life</b> this level of emotion-reading intrudes too much on <b>Mind</b>'s purview. Basically, to justify <b>Life</b> buffing Social Attributes you're giving it a lot of powers that should be under <b>Mind</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550478#post1550478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Reading the manipulation text again, it includes hiding your intentions, having a good poker face. There are several body traits that can show a liar, like sweat, stuttering, looking to a certain direction, accelerated heartbeat, increased blinking, voice pitch shifting,and so on. The list is big. By taking control of his body, the Life mage could simply avoid all of that and have the perfect poker face, not showing any sign of nervousness, even a very confident and honest behavior. On top of that, you can use Life senses to catch that and to be capable of reading moods so you can know when people is lying to you and use their feelings to manipulate them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Reading body cues to get a liar is known to be actually quite ineffective to begin with. While there are still lots of badly trained cops and internet charlatans that use this method, well trained officials that have to caught lies are currently being trained at focusing on the story, not the body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 3 - The duration rules are about the permanence of spells. Life 5 is talking about a permanent alteration of the life pattern. The spell is over and done and the change is the new normal. This has the advantage of making sense within the context of pattern bleed. Permanency ends Pattern Bleed because the target\u2019s form actually matches their true pattern.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the correct option, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution \u2013 Prime/Raw Energy</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So what exactly is intended here with this \u2018transmute them into other elements (Forces or Matter 3) or raw energy (Prime 5)? On its face, this seems like a standard transmutation of complex life into some other form, essentially destroying the person and turning them into something else. Life 5/Forces 3 and Life 5/Matter 2 work for that.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmute Complex Life to Elemental Substance (Transform Complex Life + [Other])</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Standard transmutation effect.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution Continued \u2013 Prime/Raw Energy</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This doesn\u2019t work for Life 5/Prime 5, though. Converting someone into quintessence and sending it back wherever it goes would be Life 5/Prime 2 at most. Also, Prime 5 can actually pull all the quintessence out of a person on its own. I actually can\u2019t think of an application for Life 5/Prime 5 that could reasonably fit \u2018turn someone into raw energy.\u2019 Any ideas?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I think could conceivably require <b>Life 5/Prime 5</b> would be to make <b>living quintessence</b>. You're converting a person into pure energy, <i><b>but not killing them in the process</b></i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Age and De-age</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s a similar problem here. Shouldn\u2019t Life 4 be able to age or de-age on its own. And shouldn\u2019t Entropy 4? To be a conjunctional effect this should achieve something neither one can do on their own.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think here it's just Sphere bloat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T03:26:28-07:00","id":1550502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550478#post1550478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Entropy affecting modifiers, but how could it increase any attribute?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy 3 lets you improve the performance of machines and tools. Entropy 4 lets you apply that to living Patterns. Entropy 5 to conceptual Patterns.<br /> <br /> While the game models a car or a sword as a series of modifiers to your character's actions, in then end your boosting the object specific &quot;attributes&quot; of them. Can Entropy go above 5 dots? Probably not since it can only remove flaws to make something its ideal self. But if it can make my body run at peak performance all the time... why not grant dots in Physical Attributes to represent that? If I can constantly sense the flaws in my social presentation and rhetorical techniques... why not dots to model that?<br /> <br /> It's by no means RAW. But as I said, I think it has a compelling case I think can be made for it that covers the needs of the complexities of social interactions because it can provide live and responsive feedback that adapts as social contexts shift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would asking for an explanation be bad faith? </div> </div> </div>Anything can be done in bad faith. Say I need to provide scientific explanations to things I have stated I don't think need scientific explanations doesn't become a better thing if you frame it as a request for explanations instead of some other phrasing. The problem is you not listening to what I said and trucking on as if I haven't addressed things you have come back to multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be honest, it's the opposite of bad faith, since I was trying to fit the effect into your way of viewing the game... </div> </div> </div>No, you're trying to fit things into a strawman of my views of the game, because you're ignoring my expressions of my view of the game and asking for things that don't fit within it. Hence I consider it a bad faith request.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main counterpoint, was that we don't need much to explain an effect. </div> </div> </div>This is a fairly strong statement that requires a lot more backing than simply asserting can establish; esp. if an effect isn't explicitly detailed in the books or the books contradict themselves (as I just got to feel dumb about missing something I've pointed out to others in other threads).<br /> <br /> The books, as much as they try to set guidelines to this, is that the explanation for the effect has to be sufficient to explain the Sphere rank(s) first, and then how the mage accomplishes it within their Focus. This can be pretty minimal for common effects that are well established in the games and easy to fit into most magical systems. Healing magic is primarily Life magic, and healing people is such a common desire that every style of magic comes with some basic concept of how to go about it. Which means very little explaining is needed from us as we play the game. Using Forces to transform material from one element into another isn't a common effect that's simple to slot into the Forces write-up, and isn't something magical styles are going to have simple to understand theories about to fast track out of character explanations of what's going on. <br /> <br /> I would vastly prefer the game be better constructed so explanations could all be as simple as possible even when players start getting creative. But if that was the case this thread probably wouldn't exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are several body traits that can show a liar, like sweat, stuttering, looking to a certain direction, accelerated heartbeat, increased blinking, voice pitch shifting,and so on. The list is big. By taking control of his body, the Life mage could simply avoid all of that and have the perfect poker face, not showing any sign of nervousness, even a very confident and honest behavior. On top of that, you can use Life senses to catch that and to be capable of reading moods so you can know when people is lying to you and use their feelings to manipulate them. </div> </div> </div>1) These are the things polygraphs are supposed to catch as &quot;lie detectors&quot; and have long been known to fail utterly at that task consistently. All of these are simply signs of anxiety and stress. If you put an expert and a practiced public speaker on the spot suddenly and unprepared, they'll likely show some or all of those signs even when they honestly and directly answer whatever question you sprung on them. Basically, all these signs actually show is that someone's brain has kicked into high gear. Ina highly constrained context like poker where there isn't anything else to be responding to but the game, it makes sense to hide stress responses as much as possible. Otherwise these grow meaningless very quickly when it comes to specific things like detecting lies.<br /> <br /> 2) Avoiding lie detection by suppressing small visual cues of mental activity runs right back into the &quot;OK but this doesn't help everything else the Attribute does, so how can it justify a dot increase?&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) Having a flat affect (aka a clinical psychological state of having muted to no outward responses to emotional stimuli) absolutely sucks. It actively harms socialization because it goes from &quot;cool and collected&quot; straight into triggering uncanny valley responses in people that don't understand why they're getting zero feedback. &quot;Honest&quot; communication is imperfect and flawed. If you never pause, or &quot;um,&quot; or stumble, or misspeak, or or any of that people get more distrustful, because all of us make small mistakes and zero mistakes spikes the weird-meter in our brains. Instead of authentic and trustworthy you become practiced and rehearsed.<br /> <br /> To pull another pop-culture example: in Reservoir Dogs, Mr. Orange is actually rehearsing a story so he can tell it off the cuff. He isn't given a complete script precisely to avoid him just learning a story by rote and it coming off as fake. He doesn't practice lines, he practices reliving the fake story in his head until he can tell people the story as if he actually had lived it. Like a real memory it has flaws, stuff that's not important if he tells it 100% the same every time. Like a real memory some things are hyper-detailed because our brains focus on stressors and stimuli, while forgetting specifics that weren't deemed important in the moment. And as an undercover cop, that's him being trained in his Manipulation skills. That balancing act of good liars where even a completely fake story can be imbued with enough truth by the liar's mastery of talking like a real honest person, not just sticking to the same story and never changing it, or not acting like people expect you to act when you're recounting something emotional to that happened to you.<br /> <br /> You notice that his body doesn't really come into play here? Sure, yes, his brain because he's a human. But the skills, the activities, what counts? It's all mental stuff. You take away the flaws and quirks and individuality... you get Data from Star Trek who's wooden and stilted if he's not obviously just copying original artists directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Charisma is described as having <i>it</i>, as some sort of presence, being noted. A true (not forced) smile, a confident behavior, a commanding body language, often present in leaders and good speakers can do that. </div> </div> </div>OK. So where does Life provide &quot;it&quot; for the character?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet, this is how it works. </div> </div> </div>I've already gone, in detail, about how the game design of Attributes and Spheres don't mesh well because they have different goals and desired results. Telling me in more detail how Charisma and Manipulation are defined doesn't get around that Spheres weren't designed the same way and that results in messy application of Spheres to directly adjust Attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it is made this way exactly to allow more versatility to the game. And also to not require too much knowledge from the players. Not all players are real life scientist or want to dig deep to play the game. Hence, things like &quot;altering brain matter&quot; is acceptable and enough to increase mental attributes. </div> </div> </div>OK, that's your RAI. That's not RAW.<br /> <br /> The RAW would put this as a matter of Focus. An Akashayana is unlikely to even entertain the notion of just &quot;altering brain matter&quot; to gain intelligence as the most hardcore Mind-Body dualist Tradition. A Progenitor is never going to accept such a pat oversimplification of biological functions and anatomy.<br /> <br /> If the book actually held that statement up as an explicit example of the maximum amount of effort expected to explain an effect... that would be different. The truth is you don't know if it says that because there was a need to trim word count, or Brucato wasn't even thinking about people reading it to try to decipher other parts of the game and was just trying to focus on detailing effect mechanics, or lots of other possible reasons it was written that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, the list do represent what attributes are being increased, even if they are consequences. The consequences are related to the explanations. </div> </div> </div>No, they don't. If it listed Attributes with the examples, it would be different. A broad list without any other context is just that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book says &quot;Altered Physical and Social attributes generally reveal themselves in obvious ways: rippling muscles, beautiful features, straighter posture, rapid reflexes and so forth.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yep. And if it wanted to say &quot;rippling muscles (Strength), beautiful features (Appearance), straighter posture (Charisma), rapid reflexes (Dexterity) and so forth.&quot; it could have said that. It didn't say that. It left specific Attributes-consequence designations out. This is by definition RAI to claim the book is clearly listing different Attributes. Here's a great example of why:<br /> <br /> &quot;Rippling muscles&quot; is a side effect of Appearance for someone that's going for a body builder aesthetic. Such muscles aren't actually practical in work or athletics. They come from styles of exercise that don't include conditioning for long term repeated use, unhealthy dehydration schemes to really get those ripples to pop, and dangerously low body fat to better show off muscle definition. Olympic athletes that compete in heavily Strength regulated events don't have rippling muscles. Whether you want to look at the large stocky weight lifters that need to keep up healthy body fat levels that hide their muscles to help with their center of gravity and overall mass for the best leverage, or gymnastics are their insane core muscle strength that allows them to excel in things like the still rings. People that look like Arnold Schwarzenegger in his body building prime are trying to impress judges, not be athletes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beautiful Features&quot; is Charisma. They're your &quot;it&quot; factor that draws in every eye making you the center of attention. Your looks make your smile come naturally and it pleases everyone around you when they see it. You know you're the hottest person in the room, and it fills your actions with confidence that lets command everyone's attention with the simplest gestures and requests.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rapid reflexes&quot; is Wits. Wits literally covers quick reflexes as part of its purview, Wits might normally be harder to spot when boosts, but this is where it leaks out.<br /> <br /> &quot;Straight Posture&quot; is Stamina. Proper posture is essential for endurance from being able to exercise for long periods or not have your body fall apart from sitting at a desk all day. Bad posture robs your body of energy as your overall health declines from repetitive stresses that lead to things like carpal tunnel syndrome, and with less overall energy your immune system suffers as well. Bad posture on the toilet can even kill over time you because it strains your heart. The straight posture at the end of a long day while everyone else is slumping over is your Stamina talking.<br /> <br /> Is my list better than yours? Doesn't matter. It matters that it's just as valid as yours. My versions fit the physical descriptions and Attribute write-up just as much as yours. As the books do not explicitly say one way or the other, RAW doesn't apply. Both are RAI, and those your assertion that they aren't isn't defensible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything, your lack of text interpretation in this case is suspect. I bet that if the book wasn't completely clear on the mental attributes increase you would say it wasn't possible with Life too. </div> </div> </div>Oh please. If HDYDT? hadn't put that to print, would you be adamantly arguing that Life could, or just suggesting it as a possibility even as the books never say so? It's the only book in any edition that says that it isn't Life for Physicals and Mind for Mentals, while Socials are kinda iffy over the editions. I'm not going to deny that you found RAW that says it, but if you expect clinging to HDYDT? for putting a preference you had before into the rules is some sort of valiant hill to die on... I have no idea what to say to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550479#post1550479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is the exact kind of thing I am looking for</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I went into Life thinking that was the way it was written, but M20 specifically says that all of the ways a Master of Life can change himself, he can also apply to other complex organisms. At Life 5 the full range of transformation/transmogrification is available to the self and all others. It's HDYDT that makes the claim otherwise. </div> </div> </div>Damn it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550480#post1550480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per normal magic rules, duration can be made permanent with enough successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not technically true. The chart ends with ST discretion, not permanence. There is no guaranteed permanent effects in the base magic rules.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think it's really impressive for one of the abilities of Life 5 to be &quot;force the ST to let you have a permanent effect,&quot; and I find the &quot;option 3&quot; position far more compelling for what Life 5 should be as otherwise described.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage can change a target\u2019s pattern permanently. Unlike spells of permanent duration, there is no magic keeping the target\u2019s pattern this way, and this cannot be dispelled or unwoven because the magic is over and done with already. The new pattern is simply reality now. </div> </div> </div>A small wrinkle... Unweaving explicitly calls out transformations as something it can undone if successful.<br /> <br /> Of course another Life 5 mage could also just transform someone back to how they were before too... so it's not like there's no counter to this anyway.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>\u2026and I Have No Mouth</i></span></span></b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Contradiction Resolution \u2013 Prime/Raw Energy </div> </div> </div>To expand from the &quot;living quintessence&quot; idea, Prime 5 would allow a living <b>Node</b>. Prime already includes the ability to turn a living pattern into a Node but is otherwise still just a living thing. This could get rid of the pesky problem of your ambulatory Node being susceptible to being shot and killed as you've replaced their living tissues with raw quintessence and their only forms of physicality are bits of Tass. I'm sure some Etherite or Progenitor has a fully written text defending the ethics of this idea being put into place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At Forces 5, mages should be able to generate Life patterns with impossible physics (like Matter can make substances with impossible physics) and Life patterns with completely alien biological principles. The former would include people with organs that phase through each other, allowing impossibly large organs to fit inside of them by overlapping. The latter would include silicon-based biology and non-nucleic forms of genetic storage. </div> </div> </div>Some of these feel like a bit of a stretch even for Life 5. Realizing hypothetical or mythical living patterns into reality is one thing. Completely ignoring all laws of physics feels a bit much. Having a TARDIS body where you have all these extra organs feels like it should take some Correspondence.I would aim for some level of &quot;extreme bending&quot; over fully breaking physics. Dragons with flight wings that really shouldn't work for their size but at least follows the conceptual idea of wings = flight feels OK in a way that &quot;nothing is off the table&quot; doesn't.<br /> <br /> Another metric could be... does just Life 5 &quot;exotic&quot; invalidate things like need Forces to create living flames, or Matter to create living statues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T07:06:17-07:00","id":1550514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of these feel like a bit of a stretch even for Life 5. Realizing hypothetical or mythical living patterns into reality is one thing. Completely ignoring all laws of physics feels a bit much. Having a TARDIS body where you have all these extra organs feels like it should take some Correspondence.I would aim for some level of &quot;extreme bending&quot; over fully breaking physics. Dragons with flight wings that really shouldn't work for their size but at least follows the conceptual idea of wings = flight feels OK in a way that &quot;nothing is off the table&quot; doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you believe that was the toned down version?<br /> <br /> Here was my thinking. The easiest thing to extend to Life 5 is the living equivalent of something possible for objects at Matter 5. One of the classic examples of the impossible substances of Matter 5 is matter that can pass through other patterns. It's one of the rotes in Revised. The examples were bullets that don't interact with armor and coroners tools that phase through bodies, but the same non-interaction would also let those objects continuously occupy the same space at the same time.<br /> <br /> Applying the same power to Life 5 meant life patterns that could occupy the same space as other life patterns without interacting (technically the Revised rote indicated phasing with any pattern was possible but I didn't want to open that door). That meant people who could phase through other people and organs that could phase through other organs. While using people was more direct, I thought organs was more useful and better leveraged the power.<br /> <br /> For all the strangeness it is just a power Mage has already tackled before applied in a different context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another metric could be... does just Life 5 &quot;exotic&quot; invalidate things like need Forces to create living flames, or Matter to create living statues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if the transmutation examples from Life 5 were meant to keep the target alive on the other side of the transformation then it would be an indication that other Spheres are required where the effect steps into other purviews. It's a reasonable spell effect though it is hard to say Life 5 was intending to reference it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T08:44:46-07:00","id":1550517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550500#post1550500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What capability is <b>Life</b> giving you to read moods? <b>Life</b> doesn't do that. It can read only the most basic emotions and sensations, but only if the spell is aimed at the target of the reading.<br /> <br /> You want to give yourself a hormone-sensing nose? That isn't all that effective, it's a really shallow understanding of the target's mood, and it can confuse you more than help as it shifts your attention from actually useful cues.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can, we just saw that in this very thread at rank 1. Also, rank 1 spheres doesn't require a specific sensory organ. Although you can use them (smell temporal manipulations with Time 1) you can also just &quot;feel&quot; things (feeling quintessence flow with Prime 1) not necessarily with your skin. So, it is possible for the mage to just feels people's emotions in the area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550500#post1550500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Reading people has a lot more to do with experience than with a more or less robust sensory equipment. That has been explained to you several times by different people, you just refuse to acknowledge it;<br /> <br /> 2- Giving <b>Life</b> this level of emotion-reading intrudes too much on <b>Mind</b>'s purview. Basically, to justify <b>Life</b> buffing Social Attributes you're giving it a lot of powers that should be under <b>Mind</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- I understand. The issue is when it is said that Life can't increase those attributes because reading people is not enough for that and is situational and then it's said that Mind should do it\u2026by reading people. If Life can't increase them because it has to do with experience and less about people's input, then Mind can't either.<br /> <br /> 2- Yes, Life and Mind do have several overlaps. Just a few examples: Life can control body (puppettry) similarly to Mind control, Life can put to sleep as much as Mind, Life can buff mental attributes as much as Mind. I understand that you might not like that, but it is raw, and Mind being able to get emotions reading doesn't invalidate Life's capability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entropy 3 lets you improve the performance of machines and tools. Entropy 4 lets you apply that to living Patterns. Entropy 5 to conceptual Patterns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy can bless/curse, which by no means translates into Attributes increase and are often described as difficulty modifiers. Entropy can see &quot;quirks of behavior&quot;, according to Hdydt, which to me, is enough to grant the attribute increase.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Forces to transform material from one element into another isn't a common effect that's simple to slot into the Forces write-up, and isn't something magical styles are going to have simple to understand theories about to fast track out of character explanations of what's going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and my point is that even for those non common effects we don't need a deep explanation or knowledge. You don't have to study and know quantum fields to affect nuclear forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) These are the things polygraphs</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they aren't completely efficient because they can't provide <b>perfect</b> information about the subject body, and the reader is not directly scanning the body. It's just a machine plugged into someone's body making line in a paper that will later be interpreted by the reader.<br /> A Life mage can read <b>exactly</b> what is going on in the target body. With high precision of any trait instantly. On top of that, the Life mage has a very different way of seeing biology, much more efficient than a sleeper reading lines in a paper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Avoiding lie detection by suppressing small visual cues of mental activity runs right back into the &quot;OK but this doesn't help everything else the Attribute does, so how can it justify a dot increase?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I pointed out in my last post. A mage uses Life to increase his hearing. Is his Perception increased? Or he just gets lower diffs? What if he increases his hearing and sight? Does he have to increase all 5 senses to get an increase in Perception? That is not clear in raw and I believe it's one of the main things that should be solved to reach to a conclusion on the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Having a flat affect (aka a clinical psychological state of having muted to no outward responses to emotional stimuli) absolutely sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to turn into a robot. You just need to make those imperfections and flaws look natural. The Life mage has <b>full</b> control of his body, and great part of lying is acting. You can perfectly stutter, sweat, cry, etc.<br /> <br /> Still, the mage will have to roll Manipulation+Subterfuge, but it's way easier to lie when you have full control of your facial expressions and body. Think of it as the perfect actor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, that's your RAI. That's not RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that is raw because they did put the attribute in parenthesis this time:<br /> <br /> &quot;Mental Attributes might be increased the same way, either by altering the character\u2019s sensory organs (raising Perception) or his brain matter and capacity (raising Intelligence or Wits).&quot;<br /> <br /> This is obviously one way of doing that, and Akashic might do it differently. What really matters is that it is in reach of Life to do it. I also believe the author didn't want to waste words with more explanations and then just said &quot;brain matter&quot;. But you shouldn't need much more than that to get the boost and definitely not any kind of deep analysis of how the brain works, which region of the brain is being boosted and what are the different aspects of intelligence (a really difficult thing to define). The level of analysis you guys are making is way too deep and I'll show you why in the emd of this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550502#post1550502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. And if it wanted to say &quot;rippling muscles (Strength), beautiful features (Appearance), straighter posture (Charisma), rapid reflexes (Dexterity) and so forth.&quot; it could have said that. It didn't say that. It left specific Attributes-consequence designations out. This is by definition RAI to claim the book is clearly listing different Attributes. Here's a great example of why:</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they didn'tdo it to not waste words and the relationa are pretty obvious, unlike &quot;brain matter and capacity&quot;, which each could mean both Intelligenceand Wits (that'swhy in this case they specified).<br /> <br /> I concede it's RAI because <b>it isn't written exactly what I said</b>, but we both know that you are making a huge mental gymnastic and that the list is intuitive for what attribute they mean. Don't bother saying otherwise, if you had a test where you should link the desceiptions with the attributes you definitely would do the same links as I did.<br /> <br /> Also, notice that Charisma is still in your list. Even if you change the relations, social attributes are still on the list, and social atts besides appearance. This is the point im making, is on reach of Life to increase social attributes.<br /> <br /> <br /> While writing this answer I found another piece of raw that I'd like to share:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tiny adjustments of physical chemistry can trigger emotional reactions, both from the chemical triggers and from the conscious reactions to those triggers. (\u201cHey, I feel scared. WHY do I feel scared? There must be something scary around here that I haven\u2019t noticed yet\u2026\u201d) Although such adjustments can\u2019t actually control a person\u2019s mind the way that Mind-Sphere magick can do, it\u2019s still a form of influence that a Life-trained mages can perform.<br /> A related form of Life magick lets the mage control his own physical chemistry in ways that might influence other organisms: boosting pheromone production so that he \u201csmells right,\u201d augmenting his endorphins or testosterone in order to ward off pain or radiate aggressive strength, and so on.<br /> In game terms, both techniques use Life as a coincidental modifier for mundane die-rolls. As detailed under Magick Enhancing Abilities, this allows the player to adjust the difficulty of a related die-roll by -1 to -3. Unless he\u2019s trying to do something that\u2019s hard enough to demand a high difficulty, this adjustment M-I-G-H-T (Storyteller\u2019s option) let the character succeed automatically. A guy who enhances his testosterone just before a big meeting, for instance, could simply dominate lesser characters by default. </div> </div> </div>This piece is the perfect example of what I was saying.<br /> Notice how the game clings to cinematic pop-culture stuff like pheromones to explain the effects. It doesn't go deep into how they work (or don't), it's just an excuse to have the effect. They even go further with a bs explanation of &quot;smelling right&quot;. And someone boosting testosterone in a meeting is enough to dominate others (manipulation).<br /> <br /> So, it alls boils down to game mechanics. By raw, you can affect modifiers this way. Another common way of running this is giving dice bonus. How exaclty is that different from an attribute increase?<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I could understand a ST restricting the boost for dice (or successes) bonus only, as much as another ST granting attribute increases. This will vary from table to table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-30-2025, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T09:57:07-07:00","id":1550518,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Matter</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview: </b>Objects and Materials</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No special rules</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T10:00:40-07:00","id":1550519,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Matter Perceptions </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Primary understanding of Matter allows the initiate to perceive the intrinsic properties of base materials \u2013 their underlying structure, innate properties, and integral stability or lack thereof. With that knowledge, she can view the material composition of an object, note its less-obvious structures, find its hidden layers or \u2013 when combining this perception with Entropy \u2013 spot its weak points. Combined with Life, this Sphere detects implants, enhancements, and other integrations of living tissue and inert materials.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I find it interesting what each of the pattern sphere senses focus on. Forces focuses on perceiving actual forces, Life on both sensing the presence of them and analyzing details about living things, Matter just on the analysis. Is that intentional? I don\u2019t think so but it\u2019s hard to say.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 1 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know Material Properties (Matter Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can get detailed material information on matter. This is stated to include structure, properties, integrity or lack thereof, composition, hard to see structures, and hidden layers. We can reasonably infer that other properties like mass, melting and boiling points, chemical and elemental composition are possible as well. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is an implication that matter that is integrated with living matter cannot be sensed, or at least cannot be analyzed, without Life. The wording here is key, as it indicates the difficulty lies in situations where it is difficult to tell where one pattern ends and the other begins. This would include magical fusions, cybernetics, medical implants, and also, possibly, matter that has spread throughout the body such as inorganic toxins. It would not include clearly distinct patterns like bullets, hidden microfiches, and Terminators.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sense Hidden Compartment</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since Matter 1 can explicitly see structure and hidden layers it is quite clear that it can sense things hidden within objects, or at the very least sense places where things can be hidden.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sense Weak Point</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 1 can also see where the structure of a substance is weaker or stronger, or where it might have special properties.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See Weak Points (Matter Perceptions + Sense Flaws) Matter 1 / Entropy 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - See Weak Points</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You might have noticed, I already put Sense Weak Points as a power of Matter 1. It really appears from the wording of both Matter 1 and Entropy 1 that either one can detect the weak points of an object. Matter 1 can explicitly sense integral stability, after all. What Entropy can bring to the table that Matter can\u2019t do is see probable places an object will be damaged, or to put it another way, to sense the object\u2019s fortune. <u>So the combination would show both where it is easy to damage an object and where an object is likely to be damaged.</u> It might be better to call this <b>Deathsight, Object Edition</b></span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Analyze Cybernetics and Medical Implants (Matter Perceptions + Sense Life) Matter 1 / Life 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When something is both matter and life it is difficult to analyze without both. This is a problem with any integrated pattern, but in the case of life and matter there are many situations in the modern world where this can arise, so it makes sense that it get special mention.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Matter Patterns (Matter Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strictly speaking, there is no mention at all of mages using Matter 1 to sense objects around them. That said, an absence doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s not possible and if Life can do this for living things, probably Matter can do it for objects. At the very least, if a player were to ask to scan for nearby Matter patterns, I would assume that to be a Matter 1 effect.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since it isn\u2019t directly stated, though, this is definitely an ST call.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Expand Senses (Matter Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Forces can expand the energy sensing senses (vision and hearing), Matter should be able to expand the matter sensing senses (touch, taste, and smell). Taste and smell should be able to be tailored to substances and concentrations that can\u2019t ordinarily be tasted or smelled, and touch can be refined to sense textures and qualities that are normally imperceptible. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is not stated in the Matter 1 writeup, but in this case it is just another way of perceiving the information Matter 1 can already give.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T12:35:49-07:00","id":1550521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Tiny adjustments of physical chemistry can trigger emotional reactions, both from the chemical triggers and from the conscious reactions to those triggers. (\u201cHey, I feel scared. WHY do I feel scared? There must be something scary around here that I haven\u2019t noticed yet\u2026\u201d) Although such adjustments can\u2019t actually control a person\u2019s mind the way that Mind-Sphere magick can do, it\u2019s still a form of influence that a Life-trained mages can perform.<br /> A related form of Life magick lets the mage control his own physical chemistry in ways that might influence other organisms: boosting pheromone production so that he \u201csmells right,\u201d augmenting his endorphins or testosterone in order to ward off pain or radiate aggressive strength, and so on.<br /> In game terms, both techniques use Life as a coincidental modifier for mundane die-rolls. As detailed under Magick Enhancing Abilities, this allows the player to adjust the difficulty of a related die-roll by -1 to -3. Unless he\u2019s trying to do something that\u2019s hard enough to demand a high difficulty, this adjustment M-I-G-H-T (Storyteller\u2019s option) let the character succeed automatically. A guy who enhances his testosterone just before a big meeting, for instance, could simply dominate lesser characters by default.</i><br /> <br /> This piece is the perfect example of what I was saying.<br /> Notice how the game clings to cinematic pop-culture stuff like pheromones to explain the effects. It doesn't go deep into how they work (or don't), it's just an excuse to have the effect. They even go further with a bs explanation of &quot;smelling right&quot;. And someone boosting testosterone in a meeting is enough to dominate others (manipulation).<br /> <br /> So, it alls boils down to game mechanics. By raw, you can affect modifiers this way. Another common way of running this is giving dice bonus. How exaclty is that different from an attribute increase?</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving a flat dice bonus with an Effect it's exceedingly rare, AFAIK, unless I'm very mistaken it doesn't happen outside a couple of obscure Rotes. While I do believe Sphere system <i>should </i>provide tools for interacting with all - or nearly all - Mage game mechanics (since it's a game about changing reality, and reality it's partially represented by those systems), I'm not aware about any general rule about providing flat dice bonuses with an Effect outside of increasing Attributes<br /> <br /> Rules wise, this example proves that the book considers those vague explanations are an excuse to adjust difficulty on a specific task (well, for a specific dicepool, and these are combinations of Traits that are decided by the ST for each roll or dramatic action). Attribute increases are a <u>very </u>different mechanic.<br /> <br /> Your question about &quot;how many descriptors&quot;, while it doesn't have a RAW answer, <i>it risks to</i> <i>contradict RAW</i>. Attributes modify a huge number of actions, RAW. If your descriptors don't include them, they're either a mere excuse devoid of substance or they're contradicting the RAW of Attributes. Pick your poison.<br /> <br /> And a good part of the problem it's that all of these descriptors Life can modify (&quot;hormones&quot;, &quot;the best smile&quot;, etc), even if taken at it's face pop-cultured value, would be relevant to a very small amount of tasks at best.<br /> <br /> I can see powerful muscles affecting roughly all Str does, even if that may not really be enough if we're delve too deep into Str science. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> made an astoundingly good case for posture alone being a good descriptor for raising Stamina ... But even the most vaguely magical alteration of the body presented in the thread seems like awfully inefficient to replicate even a fraction of what the Social stats &quot;represent&quot;. One needs a christmas three of alterations of yourself combined with sensory effects to even <i>begin </i>making a case for the increase.<br /> <br /> I would be much more accommodating with the idea of Life increasing the dice of concrete dicepools related to the &quot;descriptors&quot; in question. Unfortunately there isn't any rule, AFAIK, that explains how to increase &quot;specific&quot; dicepools with magick (or when to do that vs. giving a difficulty reduction).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-30-2025, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T13:23:59-07:00","id":1550524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550521#post1550521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Giving a flat dice bonus with an Effect it's exceedingly rare, AFAIK, unless I'm very mistaken it doesn't happen outside a couple of obscure Rotes. While I do believe Sphere system <i>should </i>provide tools for interacting with all - or nearly all - Mage game mechanics (since it's a game about changing reality, and reality it's partially represented by those systems), I'm not aware about any general rule about providing flat dice bonuses with an Effect outside of increasing Attributes</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they are rare and I dont know why, but they exists, which can be the premise that it is possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550521#post1550521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules wise, this example proves that the book considers those vague explanations are an excuse to adjust difficulty on a specific task (well, for a specific dicepool, and these are combinations of Traits that are decided by the ST for each roll or dramatic action).</div> </div> </div> </div>My main argument was that people was going too deep into the explanations and too harsh, when raw provides us only shalow reasonings. The arguments were that Life could not create a &quot;right smell&quot; or use pheromones efficiently. Independently if it was to increase attributes or to give any other kind of bonus. It was argued that those things do not work irl (which I can agree). But in this game, those stuff works, as many other things that work in pop culture and if you dig just a bit we see that it's not like that irl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550521#post1550521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atribute increases are a <u>very </u>different mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Is that raw? Asking genuinely, because I've tried to get an answer for my atts question and couldn't find on the book.<br /> <br /> What do you say about my Perception question? Does the mage needs to increase all 5 senses to increase dots in perception? What about other senses that also roll Perception, like awareness?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550521#post1550521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your question about &quot;how many descriptors&quot;, while it doesn't have a RAW answer, <i>it risks to</i> <i>contradict RAW</i>. Attributes modify a huge number of actions, RAW. If your descriptors don't include them, they're either a mere excuse devoid of substance or they're contradicting the RAW of Attributes. Pick your poison.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand your point.<br /> <br /> To me, it seems that when you increase a major aspect of the attribute, you increase its dots. The strength example is the easiest. Like heavy arms posted, posture can affect how much you can lift, but I wouldn't require posture boost to increase Strength. If a player says that he's boosting his muscles (which by no means necessarily include a good posture) , that's enough to increase Str, because it's the core of the attribute.<br /> <br /> However some attributes involve more than one aspect (like Stamina and Perception). The case of Perception seems to be worst, because there are 3 very important (sight, hearing and smell) and at least 2 important (touch and taste) aspects. There is no raw about that and it's a hard call, that will definitely vary from tables.<br /> <br /> The last sentence of the quote in my previous post is enough for me to consider an increase in Manipulation. It would work for lying, convincing and even intimidating someone, so the majority of aspects are covered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550521#post1550521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a good part of the problem it's that all of these descriptors Life can modify (&quot;hormones&quot;, &quot;the best smile&quot;, etc), even if taken at it's face pop-cultured value, would be relevant to a very small amount of tasks at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Just this small piece of text that I quoted provided examples of &quot;triggering emotional reactions&quot;, &quot;radiate aggreasive strength&quot; and &quot;dominate lesser characters&quot;. A player is not restricted by that and can build a lot of similar effects. This list pretty much covers manipulation. If one can radiate aggressiveness, why not radiate loveliness for Charisma? We only have to be creative\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550521#post1550521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind can read much more than just physiological reactions and emotions. Also it can directly influence emotions, thoughts, dreams, beliefs, internal concepts, etc - Life can only push people with emotions and biological chems that alter the conscience. So, Mind has a much better case at giving such a &quot;complete&quot; bonus. At least it should be better at this than Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>The solutions provided were based only ononlnd reading people (rank 1) and not directly influencing others.<br /> <br /> Not that this matters anymore, as by the raw example, tweaking your own chemistry is capable of affecting others and we dont need to read people anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-30-2025, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T14:27:56-07:00","id":1550526,"title":"","content":"My patience is worning out...<br /> <br /> I don't like to be rude on purpose because I have a hard time measuring what's just rude and what's completely reprehensible, but I may not be able to hold myself for long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can, we just saw that in this very thread at rank 1. Also, rank 1 spheres doesn't require a specific sensory organ. Although you can use them (smell temporal manipulations with Time 1) you can also just &quot;feel&quot; things (feeling quintessence flow with Prime 1) not necessarily with your skin. So, it is possible for the mage to just feels people's emotions in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's targeting the spell at the person to be read. Not giving you the ability to do so by yourself. You ignored what I actually said.<br /> <br /> We're talking about giving Attribute buffs. Reading stuff <i><b>directly</b></i> with the spell isn't giving yourself a buff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- I understand. The issue is when it is said that Life can't increase those attributes because reading people is not enough for that and is situational and then it's said that Mind should do it\u2026by reading people. If Life can't increase them because it has to do with experience and less about people's input, then Mind can't either.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Mind </b>does more than read people, and it reads more than hormone levels, like in reading the actual mind.<br /> <br /> So you think if <b>Life</b> can't do <b>Mind</b> stuff, <b>Mind</b> shouldn't either?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b2- Yes, Life and Mind do have several overlaps. Just a few examples: Life can control body (puppettry) similarly to Mind control, Life can put to sleep as much as Mind, Life can buff mental attributes as much as Mind. I understand that you might not like that, but it is raw, and Mind being able to get emotions reading doesn't invalidate Life's capability.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>They have <i><b>some</b></i>, not <i><b>several</b></i>, and as far as reading emotions is concerned, <b>Life</b> does it within limits.<br /> <br /> But tell me about how you think <b>Entropy</b> shouldn't touch storms because it is a <b>Forces</b> effect, but <b>Life</b> should take most of <b>Mind</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and my point is that even for those non common effects we don't need a deep explanation or knowledge. You don't have to study and know quantum fields to affect nuclear forces.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is talking about deep explanations but yourself. We're talking about which Sphere should do a given effect within the game rules.<br /> <br /> Science was only brought up in the sense that <i><b>WHEN YOU JUSTIFY AN EFFECT THROUGH SCIENCE, THEN THIS SCIENCE HAS TO BE SOUND</b></i>.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying <i><b>justifying</b></i> in the sense of Focus/Instrument, either. I'm saying it in the sense of <i><b>justifying which game traits to use</b></i>. That's a game justification, not a fiction justification.<br /> <br /> Most of <b><i>your</i></b> explanations about how <b>Life</b> would do <b>Mind</b> stuff rely on scientific principles, but only as sound as you find convenient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMaybe they aren't completely efficient because they can't provide <b>perfect</b> information about the subject body,<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're <i><b>completely</b></i> unreliable because <b><i>the science behind the idea isn't sound</i></b>.<br /> <br /> It is simply BS, as any psychologist can tell you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat's what I pointed out in my last post. A mage uses Life to increase his hearing. Is his Perception increased? Or he just gets lower diffs? What if he increases his hearing and sight? Does he have to increase all 5 senses to get an increase in Perception? That is not clear in raw and I believe it's one of the main things that should be solved to reach to a conclusion on the matter.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is clear in RAW: most spells to aid rolls do so reducing the difficulty of specific rolls.<br /> <br /> Buffing Attributes is exceedingly rare and require effects which very broad applications.<br /> <br /> So unless your effect reasonably affects every single situation an Attribute would be called for, it can't buff that Attribute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYou don't need to turn into a robot. You just need to make those imperfections and flaws look natural. The Life mage has <b>full</b> control of his body, and great part of lying is acting. You can perfectly stutter, sweat, cry, etc.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>But your first suggestion was to use an effect that would completely eliminate such cues. That's an exemple of an error a character would commit because they don't actually have <b>Charisma</b>.<br /> <br /> If you have complete real time control over your physiological cues, you still need actual <b>Manipulation</b> to know how to use it. It's maybe a good excuse to reduce difficulties, but not a buff to <b>Charisma</b> or <b>Manipulation</b>. And seriously, wouldn't even be that great as a dif modifier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNo, that is raw because they did put the attribute in parenthesis this time:<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another quote. Your interpretation of the other quote isn't RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI believe they didn'tdo it to not waste words and the relationa are pretty obvious, unlike &quot;brain matter and capacity&quot;, which each could mean both Intelligenceand Wits (that'swhy in this case they specified).<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever you believe isn't stated, if it even matters since it is in the book it is.<br /> <br /> You should stop quoting HDYDT since this thread exists precisely because it isn't a good book at doing what it should do.<br /> <br /> And I don't find your links particularly convincing, no.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550517#post1550517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWhile writing this answer I found another piece of raw that I'd like to share:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wholly about reducing difficulties of specific rolls.<br /> <br /> Zero people here challenged that <b>Life</b> can give circumstantial advantages on specific social rolls.<br /> <br /> None of this is about buffing Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T17:08:48-07:00","id":1550529,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> we just got into the 5th Sphere, so we are halfway there!<br /> Great job getting this thread going and being very thorough. I wouldn't have had the patience to put such a clear chart for each Sphere level even in my best days. Some considerable clearing of contradictions (could we say paradoxes?) came out of the discussions in this thread, and thank you for the goat initiative and work put into this. =) Mage is a handful, everytime, and I can appreciate this content and the people involved","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T20:56:07-07:00","id":1550533,"title":"","content":"Double posted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 05-01-2025, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T10:26:26-07:00","id":1550540,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Basic Transmutation </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With advanced knowledge, the mage can transmute one substance into another, so long as she doesn\u2019t alter its essential shape, temperature, or basic state (gas, liquid, solid). Depending upon that mage\u2019s practice, she might reshape lead into gold through alchemy, wood into stone through a hyperpetrification process, or water into wine (and, with Life 3, wine into blood) through a sacred miracle. Rare and/ or complex materials are more difficult to fabricate than simple ones; it\u2019s easier to turn stone into iron, for example, than into gold. To reflect that challenge, such refinement requires a greater number of successes than a transmutation into a common material.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(On a related note, the mage cannot yet fabricate radioactive materials. Such elements merge their essence into the Sphere of Forces, and thus demand a greater level of expertise.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When combined with other Spheres, this basic level of understanding allows a mage to conjure base materials from energy or dissolve them into Quintessence (Prime 2), transmute matter into living tissue (Life 4 or higher), move an object through space (Correspondence 2 or higher) or time (Time 3 or higher), change ephemera into matter and matter into ephemera, or awaken the slumbering spirit within material objects (Spirit 3 or higher). In all cases, Matter 2 allows the mage to work with simple, homogenous, non-living substances. Complex mixtures of various elements usually require Rank 3 or higher, although simple combinations (like those found in bread, milk, paper, or gunpowder) are possible if the player rolls plenty of successes.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is one major power for Matter 2, but it has a lot of utility and it comes with some strong limitations. Between those two, this is going to be a long section. Matter 2 has:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Limited Transmutation of Substance (Basic Transmutation)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can transmute one simple substance into another one of the same temperature, shape, and state (solid, liquid, gas, plasma). Simple mixtures are possible but may require more successes. Radioactive materials are also explicitly off limits, with the specific rationale that their connection to another sphere (Forces) means it takes higher levels of Matter to work with them. </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 2 doesn\u2019t claim to be able to make substances that don\u2019t exist and it only uses examples of substances that already do exist. Matter 5 claims jurisdiction over substances that don\u2019t exist so that is likely intentional.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Despite the many restrictions, this can be quite powerful depending on what does and does not count as simple.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>What Did They Make This Out Of?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By changing an object or section of object into something easily degradable a mage can quickly destroy something solid. Sand or powder is a good choice. Choosing something reactive, like white phosphorous, could easily make this a quite pyrotechnic endeavor.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Quick Conduction</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By changing insulation and wall materials to something conductive like copper a mage can quickly change the flow of power. The simplest use of this is to pop breakers and drop a house into darkness. With more finesse a mage could also electrocute a target or turn on a device that is not plugged in.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Added: (from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>) the same effect can be used on air (or really on plasma) to change it into a highly conductive pathway. Matter 2 can\u2019t change a gas to a plasma, but a laser pointer can do that in small quantities, and a mage can change the plasma from there. At Matter 3, a mage can forego the laser pointer.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><b><i>Removed: Non Newtonian Fluids</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Quick Dali</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Take a model of a clock and turn it into something that melts easily, like wax or butter. Aim for a duration such that it hasn\u2019t finished melting by the time the spell ends. The object will revert back to what it was before but retain the sagging and melted appearance.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Build Your Own Archaeological Fraud</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since radioactive material is specifically off limits, anything a mage conjures will show up as older than 50,000 years old if it can be carbon dated, or 4.5 Billion years old if it can be uranium dated. This was probably not the intention behind the radiation restriction, but it is fun nonetheless.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note: Even if we say that a mage can replicate reasonable levels of common radioactive material, like Carbon 14, he doesn\u2019t have to and can deliberately create an obvious forgery.</span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Explosive Decompression</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Interestingly enough a mage is only restricted to the current temperature, not the current pressure. That means a mage can create a liquid under pressure that would (and does) rapidly expand into gas when that pressure is removed. That is an ability with an explosive potential.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Added: (from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>) By creating a situation that changes when a spell ends the explosion can be put on a time delay. Examples include mentos turned into an inert stone and turns back into mentos when the spell ends. Put that in a bottle of diet soda. The same effect also works with sodium turned into an inert rock and put in a bottle of water.</span><br /> \u200b <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Simple Object (Basic Transmutation + Fuel Pattern) Matter 2 / Prime 2</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is such a well-known power that it barely needs description. By adding Prime 2 a mage can divert quintessence to create an entirely new pattern. Prime 2 specifically uses the terminology of diverting quintessence into patterns, by the way, so arguably it is just providing the energy while Matter is doing all the transmutation.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dissolve Simple Object (Basic Transmutation + Fuel Pattern) Matter 2 / Prime 2</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution: Dissolve Simple Object</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That terminology becomes important here. From the description this is a reverse process to creating matter, so instead of diverting quintessence from somewhere to fuel or weave a new pattern, this is unweaving a pattern and <i>diverting the quintessence back to wherever it came from</i>. Matter 2 is just leaving that second part out of the description. Perfectly reasonable, and I mention the ambiguity only because it leaves open the question of what Matter 2 can do on its own.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stone to Flesh (Basic Transmutation + Transmute Simple or Complex Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution: What level of Life?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stone to flesh itself is straightforward, though this section doesn\u2019t distinguish between simple and complex life and doesn\u2019t choose the proper level of life for transmuting either (Life 3 or Life 5, respectively). Life 4 could reasonably be the level for a mage to transmute a stone into himself, though. So, <u>if he had a co-location effect or split his mind among multiple clones, and one of his bodies was turned to stone, Life 4/Matter 2 would be the correct combo to turn it back.</u> The more classic giving life to the statue of Galatea would be Life 5/Matter 2 (or Life 3/Matter 2 if Galatea was a crab).</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Move Object Through Space (??? + Reach Through Space) </span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - What\u2019s Doing What Now?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence explicitly doesn\u2019t need Matter to work on whole patterns in this context, but sometimes a locking sphere is useful so we can get to the Correspondence/Matter combo that way. Unfortunately, Corr 2 works by letting the mage physically reach out and pick up the object manually, so it doesn\u2019t use locking. Correspondence 3 based levitation and motion matches the description and does benefit from locking, so we can assume Matter 2 just got the Correspondence rank wrong.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Move Object Through Time (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution \u2013 What is Happening Here?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Much of this depends on what is happening. Actual time travel is Time 5, and it\u2019s not at all clear that it needs Matter to send an object forward or backwards. Time 3 lets a mage cast through time and Correspondence can move objects through space at the same rank it can cast through space, but there\u2019s really no evidence Time is meant to have the same progression. <u>The best match I\u2019ve found is a rewind time spell locked to an object so that it rewinds time just for that object rather than a specific area</u>. That\u2019s not really moving an object through time, though, and it would be the second time Matter 2 is reduced to a locking sphere in its own writeup.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Convert Matter to Spirit or Back Again (Basic Transmutation + Step Sideways?) Matter 2 / Spirit 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Awakening Spirits</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a contradiction I almost missed. Spirit 3 can already turn things to ephemera and vice versa without Pattern Spheres. That\u2019s what it does in gauntlet crossings. Possibly the intention was it can only do this on its own during gauntlet crossings, but if so that is not a stated limitation of Spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t have a good application for Spirit 3/Matter 2 in this context.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Awaken the Spirit of an Object (??? + Rouse and Lull Spirit) ???</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Awakening Spirits</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This normally doesn\u2019t require Matter either, neither in Spirit 3 or in the sidebar Spirit 3 references. I\u2019ll add that the sidebar does say that awakening the spirit of a poison involves Life 3 if it is currently spread out in a life pattern, so <u>if there was a situation where the substance a mage wanted to awaken was suffused in another object, for instance awakening the spirit of the trace bits of gold in a piece of ore, Matter 2 would be involved. </u></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-07-2025, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T11:07:39-07:00","id":1550541,"title":"","content":"Isnt the disolve simple object redundant? Prime should be able to do that alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T12:03:25-07:00","id":1550543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science was only brought up in the sense that <i><b>WHEN YOU JUSTIFY AN EFFECT THROUGH SCIENCE, THEN THIS SCIENCE HAS TO BE SOUND</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the Etherites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T12:58:50-07:00","id":1550544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550541#post1550541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt the disolve simple object redundant? Prime should be able to do that alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>At Prime 4 it can. Not at Prime 2. <br /> <br /> However, Prime 2 describes its role in ex nihilo creation as 'the mage may <i>divert</i> Quintessence into new or existing forms.' It doesn't say 'change,' or 'transform,' or 'transmute,' or any other verb that would imply that Prime is part of the transmutation itself. So it is at least a plausible reading that Prime 2 provides the Quintessence and Matter 2 does the complete job of transmuting Quintessence into objects.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, then in the reverse process Matter 2 would do the complete work of transforming the object into Quintessence, and Prime 2 would divert that Quintessence back to wherever it pulls Quintessence from. So what happens if a mage leaves off the Prime 2?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T13:26:35-07:00","id":1550546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550544#post1550544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At Prime 4 it can. Not at Prime 2.<br /> <br /> However, Prime 2 describes its role in ex nihilo creation as 'the mage may <i>divert</i> Quintessence into new or existing forms.' It doesn't say 'change,' or 'transform,' or 'transmute,' or any other verb that would imply that Prime is part of the transmutation itself. So it is at least a plausible reading that Prime 2 provides the Quintessence and Matter 2 does the complete job of transmuting Quintessence into objects.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, then in the reverse process Matter 2 would do the complete work of transforming the object into Quintessence, and Prime 2 would divert that Quintessence back to wherever it pulls Quintessence from. So what happens if a mage leaves off the Prime 2?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, Prime 2 has an effect of sacrificing an object for 1 Quintessence, while Prime 2+Matter 2 gets you 1 Quintessence per success.<br /> <br /> Matter 2 alone could dissolve the object into anything other than Quintessence, like air or sand, as you pointed.<br /> <br /> I wonder how many successes are required for that, as the Feats table doesn't seem to include Matter examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T13:35:24-07:00","id":1550547,"title":"","content":"Somehow my post was lost in an unapproved state after an editing. So here it goes again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My patience is worning out...<br /> I don't like to be rude on purpose because I have a hard time measuring what's just rude and what's completely reprehensible, but I may not be able to hold myself for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I could say the same, as you are ignoring my arguments as well. The game clearly doesn't follow the same real life science explanations, as I already showed in the book quote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's targeting the spell at the person to be read. Not giving you the ability to do so by yourself. You ignored what I actually said.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm talking about a spell cast on the mage himself, not a targeting spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about giving Attribute buffs. Reading stuff <i><b>directly</b></i> with the spell isn't giving yourself a buff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said that a mage giving himself the ability to read people (with Mind) would be a good explanation to get an attribute increase. I'm saying this should work with Life as well. We both are arguing opinion right now, and this doesn't even matter, because I think this explanation can be dropped and we're better debating the raw one I posted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have <i><b>some</b></i>, not <i><b>several</b></i>, and as far as reading emotions is concerned, <b>Life</b> does it within limits.<br /> <br /> But tell me about how you think <b>Entropy</b> shouldn't touch storms because it is a <b>Forces</b> effect, but <b>Life</b> should take most of <b>Mind</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said Entropy 3 shouldn't touch weather control, because Forces 3 (the sphere of weather control by raw) can't. Increasing manipulation or charisma had no specific sphere by raw, you're putting Mind in this place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is talking about deep explanations but yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you are arguing the efficiency of polygraphs or pheromones, you are going deeper than the explanations given in the books. Again, pop culture stuff are true in mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of <b><i>your</i></b> explanations about how <b>Life</b> would do <b>Mind</b> stuff rely on scientific principles, but only as sound as you find convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is on board with the raw that considers &quot;smelling right&quot; and &quot;pheromones&quot; as effective enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they're <i><b>completely</b></i> unreliable because <b><i>the science behind the idea isn't sound</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're ignoring my argument. Neither are pheromones (even less so than polygraphs), yet they are a thing in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is another quote. Your interpretation of the other quote isn't RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was talking about the &quot;brain matter&quot; stuff. This is raw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever you believe isn't stated, if it even matters since it is in the book it is.<br /> <br /> You should stop quoting HDYDT since this thread exists precisely because it isn't a good book at doing what it should do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to ignore hdydt when it <b>directly contradicts</b> something from M20 core. In this case there is nothing about that in M20, so no contradiction. If you want to completely ignore hdydt as raw, then we can't go on. However, hdydt has already poped in this thread in other posts and I bet it will pop later again, as it <b>is</b> useful for some things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't find your links particularly convincing, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah? What relation of attribute to consequence do you think would fit better? Even if you work some mental gym, social attributes (besides appearance) will still be in the list.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So unless your effect reasonably affects every single situation an Attribute would be called for, it can't buff that Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, this is not completely clear, but makes sense. Considering that you accept the shalowness of the raw explanations, and that a player could extrapolate from there (like radiating &quot;being likeable&quot; ), one could cover all major situations, enough to get the increase. That's my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550526#post1550526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's wholly about reducing difficulties of specific rolls.<br /> <br /> Zero people here challenged that <b>Life</b> can give circumstantial advantages on specific social rolls.<br /> <br /> None of this is about buffing Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the point completely. You said that pheromones and buffing hormones and etc. would do <b>anything</b> as they are not effective in real life. You never said that they could grant a modifier, but not an att increase.<br /> <br /> The whole argumentations were based on how this stuff is not real. But they are real enough for the game, by raw.<br /> <br /> Now, you could argue that they are not enough to grant an increase in atts, but that is your opinion and neither of us can base our point in raw.<br /> <br /> I could argue that giving modifiers in diff is similar to getting dice boosts (even though we already know they are rare) and thats good enough for a boost in the social attributes even if a particular table wouldn't accept a direct increase.<br /> <br /> At the very worst, even if we agree to disagree, we have to agree that Life can give a good boost in Manipulation and Charisma rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> PS: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>, great example, Etherites uses the most bs scientific explanations all the time lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T13:37:01-07:00","id":1550548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550540#post1550540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one major power for Matter 2, but it has a lot of utility and it comes with some strong limitations. Between those two, this is going to be a long section. Matter 2 has:</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one glaring problem with the limitations of Matter 2: &quot;...<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">are possible if the player rolls plenty of successes</span>.&quot; IIRC this is the only time the core book allows you to do this explicitly. The Spheres are full of poorly explained and arbitrary lines the separate what rank you need to target specific categories of patterns or perform specific alterations, but they're solid lines. The ST gets the shitty job of picking what side of a line the situation is, but then you go from there.<br /> <br /> Punting that to a mid-ground of &quot;add some extra successes&quot; causes a lot of oddities in play (esp. since there's no guideline of how many to add).<br /> <br /> But then again, this is a section that labels milk as a homogeneous simple combination... which is kinda baffling when most people reading this text are people that buy milk that has been homogenized during processing. Milk, naturally, isn't homogeneous, we process it to be so because we like it better that way (and generally buy milk in large enough quantities, and formerly sold it in glass that shaking the bottles all the time got messy frequently). There's a whole rabbit hole this example opens up if the homogeneous requirement is contextual. While the idea of being able to use Matter 2 on oil and water that were just given a strong mixing before they separate back isn't that impressive, there's a lot of potential chemistry insanity this opens up that seems entirely out of keeping with the rest of the description of Matter 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Despite the many restrictions, this can be quite powerful depending on what does and does not count as simple.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Further, there's two important kinds of simple/complex that this level of material workings: ingredients and structure. And the write-up doesn't address this at all. Chocolate for example, has six different crystal structures it can form when cooling from a liquid to a solid, all of which have different properties based on those crystal structures despite the ingredients staying the same (and it gets even more complicated when you start adjusting the proportions of the base ingredients of chocolate). If someone does chocolate art (fun YouTube stuff to watch IMO), they're generally mastering chocolate mass and cocoa butter, which readily homogenize, and then tempering (how to get the crystals they want for what they're making). So you could argue that this is a simple combination of two ingredients that are only two ingredients because you separated them out from the same starting ingredient (fermented cocoa beans) in the first place. And you can argue that chocolate is very complex because it can take on so many crystal structures with so many different properties.<br /> <br /> A different culinary trip would be trying to decide if spices are simple or complex. Most spices are simple in the sense that they're just a refined part of a plant. But what makes spices valuable and desirable are the intensely complicated array of aromatic compounds they contain (some spices have over 200 individual aromatics that make up the flavor experience you get when eating them).</span><br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Quick Conduction</i></span></span> </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By changing insulation and wall materials to something conductive like copper a mage can quickly change the flow of power. The simplest use of this is to pop breakers and drop a house into darkness. With more finesse a mage could also electrocute a target or turn on a device that is not plugged in.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This gets even worse with a laser pointer (or Forces if you don't have one handy, but then Forces could just zap someone), as lasers produce an thin homogeneous zone in air around the beam that is mildly conductive. Mage the Awakening 1e had a conductivity spell that was very heavily debated because as written you basically could buy a laser pointer and a cattle prod and zap people from a pretty substantial distance without all of the normal considerations for trying to do that (and being able to completely skip Forces).</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Non Newtonian Fluids (aka Make That Vein On Your STs Face Pop) </div> </div> </div></i></span></span></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are things that are neither solid nor liquid but behave like both depending on circumstances. Turning a wall into oobleck is a quick way of melting it. Turning a pool into oobleck is a quick way of running across it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, an ST is well within his rights to say if it isn\u2019t a solid or a liquid you can\u2019t turn a solid or liquid into it. That said, most of the same effect could be accomplished by transforming a solid into something that will rapidly melt, or a liquid into something that will rapidly solidify.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think this is a bit of a misconceptions about non-Newtonian fluids. &quot;Fluid&quot; in physics is not a state of matter. Matter in any state can act as a fluid, even if most people think fluid = liquid. Solids rarely act as fluids until acted upon by external forces, while liquids, gases, and plasmas usually act as fluids unless an external force acts on them.<br /> <br /> Sorry to get a bit gruesome, but it's a simple explanation: When a building gets blown up, the solids that get flung around act as a fluid. Thus, experts in investigating these things can actually analyze the debris fields using the same basic science as crime scene investigators analyzing the liquid blood splatters from a stabbing or shooter. In both cases the rules of fluid dynamics don't change.<br /> <br /> When we talk about non-Newtonian fluids, we're talking about materials that don't follow the normal rules for fluid dynamics. This can mean things like inducing a state-change instead of normal fluid motions (rapid compression of obleeck results in the liquid solidifying instead of flow out of the way of the kinetic impact). At rest all non-Newtonian fluids are whatever state of matter they normally occur at under those conditions. Obleeck is a liquid (if a very thick one). Since you can't change states with Matter 2, only liquids can be turned into obleeck (at least at rest, see my rant about milk).<br /> <br /> So I'd say turning a wall into obleeck really shouldn't work because walls are solids and obleeck is a liquid (but I'd also be against temporary suspensions of water and oil counting as a homogeneous liquid); but there are non-Newtonian fluids that are solids at rest a wall could be turned into. Turning a pool of water into obleeck is fine by me (hard enough to pull off just to run across something you could run around, and with Matter and Prime you could just summon up a lot of starch over the pool and make the obleeck that way instead).</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Build Your Own Archaeological Fraud</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since radioactive material is specifically off limits, anything a mage conjures will show up as older than 50,000 years old if it can be carbon dated, or 4.5 Billion years old if it can be uranium dated. This was probably not the intention behind the radiation restriction, but it is fun nonetheless.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think this is a bit of a poor application of the radioactive material stipulation. If you take it to this extreme Matter 2 is useless because everything is radioactive in the sense that all matter is constantly undergoing radioactive decay. I firmly standby interpreting any reference to radioactivity in this context as meaning ionizing radioactivity or matter irradiated by it.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't see any reason why Matter wouldn't let you create specific mixtures of isotopes to fool decay-based dating systems. If I can summon carbon out of nothing with Prime, and I have an appropriate Focus, why can't I control how much is C13 and how much is C14?</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Explosive Decompression</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Interestingly enough a mage is only restricted to the current temperature, not the current pressure. That means a mage can create a liquid under pressure that would (and does) rapidly expand into gas when that pressure is removed. That is an ability with an explosive potential.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can even time delay this without Time. Think Mentos and Diet Pepsi, but you turn the Mentos into something inert to the Diet Pepsi with a duration to expire when you want the reaction to go off.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Convert Matter to Spirit or Back Again (Basic Transmutation + Step Sideways?) Matter 2 / Spirit 3 </div> </div> </div></span></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Awakening Spirits</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a contradiction I almost missed. Spirit 3 can already turn things to ephemera and vice versa without Pattern Spheres. That\u2019s what it does in gauntlet crossings. Possibly the intention was it can only do this on its own during gauntlet crossings, but if so that is not a stated limitation of Spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t have a good application for Spirit 3/Matter 2 in this context.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;</span>He may carry a few material possessions, although transmuting them as well raises both the difficulty of the roll and the number of successes required for the trip. (Normal clothing and items raise both factors by +1; bulky clothing and items raise them by +2.) That traveler must step sideways on his own; bringing large items or other people across demands a higher Spirit Rank.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would say that the application of Spirit 3/Matter 2 is for when you don't have higher Spirit magic. I think Spirits limitations are pretty clearly only when crossing, and then are quite limited to a few items on your person. Spirit 3/Matter 2 would override the limitations of it being part of Step Sideways and the difficult increases on the Step Sideways roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550543#post1550543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell that to the Etherites.</div> </div> </div> </div>When one exists in reality, and comes to my games to play Mage having agreed to follow the rules of the game, I will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T13:37:27-07:00","id":1550549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550546#post1550546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iirc, Prime 2 has an effect of sacrificing an object for 1 Quintessence, while Prime 2+Matter 2 gets you 1 Quintessence per success.<br /> <br /> Matter 2 alone could dissolve the object into anything other than Quintessence, like air or sand, as you pointed.<br /> <br /> I wonder how many successes are required for that, as the Feats table doesn't seem to include Matter examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 3 is the level for gaining Quintessence through sacrifice. It does require Matter 2 for objects though not Life for living things. Possibly that is because a mage can kill a living sacrifice but not a material one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T13:41:28-07:00","id":1550550,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a><br /> <br /> I'm not going line by line on this, it's not worth it.<br /> <br /> But I'm going to point out something: pheromones not working on humans don't make them not real. A Life mage can absolutely give themselves the ability to excrete bee pheromones and take control over a bee hive. Bee behavior is highly regulated by chemical signals and to them the line between chemistry and mind control might as well not exist. The world is a big place. Some times work great in one application, and do nothing in others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T13:55:48-07:00","id":1550551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550549#post1550549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime 3 is the level for gaining Quintessence through sacrifice. It does require Matter 2 for objects though not Life for living things. Possibly that is because a mage can kill a living sacrifice but not a material one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 3 for living beings and Prime 2 for objects. Tbh, neither should require the Pattern spheres, since the object sacrificed has to be destroyed (or dissolved, buried, etc). Adding Matter only provides more than a single Quintessence while living sacrifices already provide successes based amounts. It seems mechanically balanced this way.<br /> <br /> But we can talk more about that when we reach Prime =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T15:05:43-07:00","id":1550553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550544#post1550544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At Prime 4 it can. Not at Prime 2.<br /> <br /> However, Prime 2 describes its role in ex nihilo creation as 'the mage may <i>divert</i> Quintessence into new or existing forms.' It doesn't say 'change,' or 'transform,' or 'transmute,' or any other verb that would imply that Prime is part of the transmutation itself. So it is at least a plausible reading that Prime 2 provides the Quintessence and Matter 2 does the complete job of transmuting Quintessence into objects.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, then in the reverse process Matter 2 would do the complete work of transforming the object into Quintessence, and Prime 2 would divert that Quintessence back to wherever it pulls Quintessence from. So what happens if a mage leaves off the Prime 2?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 2 cant divert quintessence to the werer, thats Prime 3 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T15:13:15-07:00","id":1550554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550548#post1550548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is one glaring problem with the limitations of Matter 2: &quot;...<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">are possible if the player rolls plenty of successes</span>.&quot; IIRC this is the only time the core book allows you to do this explicitly. The Spheres are full of poorly explained and arbitrary lines the separate what rank you need to target specific categories of patterns or perform specific alterations, but they're solid lines. The ST gets the shitty job of picking what side of a line the situation is, but then you go from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong. And the other side of the coin is a problem too. Matter 2 says that complex mixtures require Rank 3 or higher, yet neither rank 2 nor 3 say where the dividing line is, nor where the line between 3 and 4 is. For my own part I tend towards the idea that mostly solid objects made of multiple different materials are Rank 3, while complex mechanism or complex integration of materials is Rank 4. That's all guesswork, though, and there are still a lot of holes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550548#post1550548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a bit of a misconceptions about non-Newtonian fluids. &quot;Fluid&quot; in physics is not a state of matter. Matter in any state can act as a fluid, even if most people think fluid = liquid. Solids rarely act as fluids until acted upon by external forces, while liquids, gases, and plasmas usually act as fluids unless an external force acts on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, and I was aware that Oobleck was a liquid. I may remove that example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550548#post1550548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a bit of a poor application of the radioactive material stipulation. If you take it to this extreme Matter 2 is useless because everything is radioactive in the sense that all matter is constantly undergoing radioactive decay. I firmly standby interpreting any reference to radioactivity in this context as meaning ionizing radioactivity or matter irradiated by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this probably wasn't the intent of the radioactivity ban. Likewise, I don't think Matter 4 is supposed to be incapable of making smoke detectors. This was an example rote meant to illustrate what a strict a letter of the law interpretation of Matter 2 would mean.<br /> <br /> Though, even with a more charitable interpretation of Matter 2, a mage could still build an easily identifiable archaological forgery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550548#post1550548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;He may carry a few material possessions, although transmuting them as well raises both the difficulty of the roll and the number of successes required for the trip. (Normal clothing and items raise both factors by +1; bulky clothing and items raise them by +2.) That traveler must step sideways on his own; bringing large items or other people across demands a higher Spirit Rank.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would say that the application of Spirit 3/Matter 2 is for when you don't have higher Spirit magic. I think Spirits limitations are pretty clearly only when crossing, and then are quite limited to a few items on your person. Spirit 3/Matter 2 would override the limitations of it being part of Step Sideways and the difficult increases on the Step Sideways roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the limitation on size is mostly about what can be carried across at the time, but I don't see an indication that going past those limitations should suddenly involve Matter when they didn't before. Also, Spirit seems to have a unique approach to transmutation, with a corresponding limitation that I'll tackle when we get to Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T15:41:15-07:00","id":1550556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550554#post1550554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not wrong. And the other side of the coin is a problem too. Matter 2 says that complex mixtures require Rank 3 or higher, yet neither rank 2 nor 3 say where the dividing line is, nor where the line between 3 and 4 is. For my own part I tend towards the idea that mostly solid objects made of multiple different materials are Rank 3, while complex mechanism or complex integration of materials is Rank 4. That's all guesswork, though, and there are still a lot of holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this then is that it makes nothing new. Whats stops you from making just the basic components and asimilating them manualy or with matter 3? Makes lvl 4 really underwelming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T16:25:15-07:00","id":1550558,"title":"","content":"The primary thing that stops you from making components and assembling them yourself has always been the mage's personal skills in that regard. Would you rather have a watch that a mage who's never assembled a watch before cobbled together for individual parts? Or a watch that mage conjured up by just making the watch as one item?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T20:53:13-07:00","id":1550563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550548#post1550548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one exists in reality, and comes to my games to play Mage having agreed to follow the rules of the game, I will.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's with the hostility? The comment wasn't directed towards you, or anything you've been saying. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T01:48:15-07:00","id":1550567,"title":"","content":"Dude, we've been on these forums together for long enough that I think you know that's not me being hostile.<br /> <br /> However, monteparnas and I have said the same exact thing to the same exact other poster, so directing that at her isn't really that different from directing it at me. So yeah, it was a bit reactive, but I don't see it as unaimed in my direction as you seem to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T02:27:10-07:00","id":1550568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550558#post1550558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary thing that stops you from making components and assembling them yourself has always been the mage's personal skills in that regard. Would you rather have a watch that a mage who's never assembled a watch before cobbled together for individual parts? Or a watch that mage conjured up by just making the watch as one item?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again you can make the components with Matter 2 and asemble them with Matter 3, that still makes 4 redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T03:52:42-07:00","id":1550572,"title":"","content":"The only thing Matter 3 would allow is not needing tools as you can command the components directly. You still need to know how the components fit together. Nothing in Matter 3's write-up replaces the ability to create complex machines from nothing but having a general idea of how they work present in Matter 4. Matter 3 doesn't tell you which components go where, or how tightly a screw needs to be, or any of all of those little details that goes into assembling a complex machine. Matter 3 also doesn't allow for permanent changes. So it would be really useful for fixing something without having to take it completely apart because you can turn a fixed part into something easier to maneuver into place and then let the effect expire. But if Matter 3 is the only thing holding your item together, it's got a short lifespan before it falls apart (which could be fine in plenty of circumstances).<br /> <br /> Matter 4 isn't redundant because with a single effect you can just summon up a complex machine. It's done. It's not an alteration that expires. You don't need to spend time assembling things yourself or casting additional effects to put it together.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, all the conjunctional effects that Matter 4 lists that Matter 2 and 3 combined can't replicate no matter how much time and skill you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T04:33:38-07:00","id":1550579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550572#post1550572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing Matter 3 would allow is not needing tools as you can command the components directly. You still need to know how the components fit together. Nothing in Matter 3's write-up replaces the ability to create complex machines from nothing but having a general idea of how they work present in Matter 4. Matter 3 doesn't tell you which components go where, or how tightly a screw needs to be, or any of all of those little details that goes into assembling a complex machine. Matter 3 also doesn't allow for permanent changes. So it would be really useful for fixing something without having to take it completely apart because you can turn a fixed part into something easier to maneuver into place and then let the effect expire. But if Matter 3 is the only thing holding your item together, it's got a short lifespan before it falls apart (which could be fine in plenty of circumstances).<br /> <br /> Matter 4 isn't redundant because with a single effect you can just summon up a complex machine. It's done. It's not an alteration that expires. You don't need to spend time assembling things yourself or casting additional effects to put it together.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, all the conjunctional effects that Matter 4 lists that Matter 2 and 3 combined can't replicate no matter how much time and skill you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would believe its the same with matter 4. Nothing in matter 4 says you have the knowledge how to create everything. So i would assume the mage still needs to know the laptops components and placement to build it. Also knowing that would be Matter 1 forte.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T05:09:11-07:00","id":1550584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550550#post1550550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> <br /> I'm not going line by line on this, it's not worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. We both have different ways of viewing this matter that will probably not change.<br /> <br /> The aftermath of the conversation is that it is definitely doable via modifiers and it all boils down to deciding if an effect that grants modifiers could be made in a way to grant dice bonus or attributes increase (let the player's mental Olympics begin, lol). Since there are no hard rules about that, I don't see why we should argue further as it will be a &quot;your table rule vs. my table rule&quot;\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550550#post1550550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;3153&quot;]<br /> But I'm going to point out something: pheromones not working on humans don't make them not real. A Life mage can absolutely give themselves the ability to excrete bee pheromones and take control over a bee hive. Bee behavior is highly regulated by chemical signals and to them the line between chemistry and mind control might as well not exist. The world is a big place. Some times work great in one application, and do nothing in others.</div> </div> </div> </div> In the game, through magick, pheromones can work with humans just like with bees and even better, not limited at all by the real world pheromones capabilities. <br /> <br /> That's the point Dataweaver was making. Etherites use stuff that we know that are not real or doesn't work irl (like orgone energy). So the science does not has to be sound.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T05:19:49-07:00","id":1550585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550579#post1550579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would believe its the same with matter 4. Nothing in matter 4 says you have the knowledge how to create everything. So i would assume the mage still needs to know the laptops components and placement to build it. Also knowing that would be Matter 1 forte.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the mage does have to know how the stuff he is creating work, at least in a basic level. I believe you could create each piece of a complex machine and assemble it instead of creating the machine itself, but you will need a lot more rolls, get a lot more dox (creating from scratch is vulgar) and you will need way more knowledge of the subject, since you're going to assemble it piece by piece. I would definitely call for a knowledge roll.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by the Matter 1 thing, is that it should grant the mage knowledge of how to build a laptop? I guess it would help if he have another laptop and uses rank 1 to get info about it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T05:42:24-07:00","id":1550586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550585#post1550585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the mage does have to know how the stuff he is creating work, at least in a basic level. I believe you could create each piece of a complex machine and assemble it instead of creating the machine itself, but you will need a lot more rolls, get a lot more dox (creating from scratch is vulgar) and you will need way more knowledge of the subject, since you're going to assemble it piece by piece. I would definitely call for a knowledge roll.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by the Matter 1 thing, is that it should grant the mage knowledge of how to build a laptop? I guess it would help if he have another laptop and uses rank 1 to get info about it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats exactly what i ment<br /> The thing is thats nothing new, there is little benefit to create those things fast as matter is more of a downtime sphere. Therefore Matter 4 is still redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T06:40:00-07:00","id":1550588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550584#post1550584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the game, through magick, pheromones can work with humans just like with bees and even better, not limited at all by the real world pheromones capabilities.<br /> <br /> That's the point Dataweaver was making. Etherites use stuff that we know that are not real or doesn't work irl (like orgone energy). So the science does not has to be sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrase &quot;through magick&quot; is doing enough heavy lifting to push the Earth out of orbit of the Sun without a lever.<br /> <br /> If it's &quot;through magick,&quot; then you're talking about a character's Focus and that doesn't matter to what Sphere ranks it takes to do something. An Etherite can call it pheromones all they want, but it might still be a Mind X effect in the end. Calling it pheromones doesn't automatically make it a Life effect, just like an Akashayana meditating doesn't automatically make something a Mind effect, or a Dreamspeaker invoking the spirits make it a Spirit effect.<br /> <br /> This whole debate you've been blurring the lines between Focus and manipulating science. And that's why the Etherite example doesn't mean anything, and when monteparnas and I say the science has to be sound if you're incorporating science into the effect still means the science has to be sound. Pseudoscience Focuses don't get to use real world science to get extra bang for their buck. The pseudoscience is just another paradigm within another Focus that just tells us the way the mage thinks about magic and then does it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T06:45:07-07:00","id":1550589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550588#post1550588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The phrase &quot;through magick&quot; is doing enough heavy lifting to push the Earth out of orbit of the Sun without a lever.<br /> <br /> If it's &quot;through magick,&quot; then you're talking about a character's Focus and that doesn't matter to what Sphere ranks it takes to do something. An Etherite can call it pheromones all they want, but it might still be a Mind X effect in the end. Calling it pheromones doesn't automatically make it a Life effect, just like an Akashayana meditating doesn't automatically make something a Mind effect, or a Dreamspeaker invoking the spirits make it a Spirit effect.<br /> <br /> This whole debate you've been blurring the lines between Focus and manipulating science. And that's why the Etherite example doesn't mean anything, and when monteparnas and I say the science has to be sound if you're incorporating science into the effect still means the science has to be sound. Pseudoscience Focuses don't get to use real world science to get extra bang for their buck. The pseudoscience is just another paradigm within another Focus that just tells us the way the mage thinks about magic and then does it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree here but would use consensus instead of science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T08:10:00-07:00","id":1550591,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 3</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Alter Form </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At this Rank, the mage can alter the shape of materials in whatever ways she desires, and she can temporarily transform their essential state into a different one \u2013 steel, for example, into fog or water into glass. (Permanent changes require Matter 5.) That crafter may change an item\u2019s density, fuse broken pieces together, or rip solid ones apart. </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By mixing Matter 3 with other Spheres, the mage can join inert matter with living tissue, disintegrate it into dust, shift objects with the power of thought, or otherwise perform amazing transformations upon apparently solid materials.</span> </div> </div> </div>There are several major powers here:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Full Transmutation of Substance (Alter Form)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 3 expands the transmutation powers of Matter 2 to include any material regardless of state. Water to ice, stone into air, all of these become possible. Note that unlike Matter 2, Matter 3 doesn\u2019t say anything about temperature or radiation restrictions. Matter 5 claims radioactive materials so that restriction is likely still off limits. Temperature changes are apparently fair game, though.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Vanished Into Thin Air</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can quite literally turn an object into normal air such that it is completely gone. As this is the most literal possible meaning of vanishing into thin air, there's not much more I can add.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>A Very Nasty Surprise</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spells have durations. If a mage turns something poisonous or mind affecting, such as Ether, into thin air that air will dissipate into the rest of the air in a room. When the spell runs out, those air molecules will turn back, leaving a lot of Ether vapor in the room to be inhaled.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>How to Boil Water</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now that temperature is on the table we no longer have to worry about if a substance is possible at a given temperature because mages can change the temperature if necessary. A mage can transform ice cold water to boiling water, or boiling water to typical liquid nitrogen. This may sound a lot like Matter stepping on Forces territory, but this does have to wait until Matter 3 to accomplish the temperature changes Forces can do at rank 2.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sculpt Material (Alter Form)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition to transmuting an object, a mage can also use Matter 3 to reshape it. There does not appear to be a limit to what can be shaped or what shape it can be put in.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Paint With All the Colors of the Wind</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sculpt Material appears to apply to gasses as much as anything else, which means he can reshape the air in a room. He could even shape it over time, which is functionally the same as moving it around though more cumbersome than using Forces to actually blow it about.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>\u201cI Shapeshift the Closed Door into One That\u2019s Open\u201d</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As silly as that statement sounds, that is an actual thing Matter 3 can do. Matter 3 may not be able to move objects, but to a limited degree it can sculpt them into the states they would be in if they did move.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><b><i>Added: A Direct Indirect Attack With Matter (from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a>)</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also shape materials in offensive ways. This may include rapid sculpting into damaging shapes like spikes shaped through someone, and can definitely include sculpting spikes right into their path with no time to move.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fuse or Rend Materials (Alter Form)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Importantly, Matter 3 can now merge objects, allowing a mage to perfectly repair broken objects as if they never broke, weld unweldable substances (like glass to non-living bone). He can also sever, rend, or shatter materials in pretty much any pattern he wishes.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Seven Years Good Luck</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can perfectly repair broken glass and mirrors, regardless of how thoroughly they were destroyed. Actually getting the good luck would require the use of Entropy, though.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Change Density (Alter Form)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can alter the density of a substance. No limitation is given so this applies to any substance and any state of matter, which has a lot of applications. This specifically gives Matter 3 to create substances that 'transcend the limitations of scientific possibility\u2019 (with regards to density) and \u2018materials unknown to Earthly reality\u2019 (again with regards to density). Matter 5 claims it is the rank for those two categories, but Matter 5 cannot contradict Matter 3 on what Matter 3 can do.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Harden Armor</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By increasing the density of a substance, a mage can increase its durability and soak. This does also increase weight, but if the mage chooses the right substance this isn\u2019t a big consideration.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Thalassophobia</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Humans float because they are less dense than water. If a mage lowers the density of water around a swimmer, they are going rapidly slip below the surface. This can quite easily drown someone, but even if it is only done over a small volume and a short duration it can easily cause panic and disorientation.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately, this is another case of quick padding. There\u2019s very little description and no ranks or spheres given so I\u2019ll do my best.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fuse Matter and Life (Alter Form + Transmute X Life) Matter 3 / Life 3/4/5</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I admit I assumed this was a Matter 2 effect. In every other case grafting is transmutation levels\u2026 but Matter 2 can\u2019t change shape and it can\u2019t fuse materials, both of which have a role in grafting.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disintegrate Into Dust (Alter Form + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - ???</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t actually know what other Sphere is being suggested. It\u2019s not Prime, as that was covered in the Matter 2 section. Maybe Entropy? Maybe Time? Whatever the case, Matter 3 is explicitly capable of rending material apart, including down to dust. It\u2019s also capable of transmuting things to dust (well, Matter 2 for transmuting solids to dust and Matter 3 for everything else).</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shift Objects With the Power of Thought (Alter Form + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - A Bit of Mind</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have a deep dislike of attempts to incorporate Mind into any effect that sounds vaguely psychic. That said, M20 doesn\u2019t say Mind here, so I\u2019m not going to assume it. Shift could mean reshape, move, or both. Matter 3 can handle the reshape. Forces and Correspondence can each accomplish the movement. <u>Matter 3 combined with Forces or Correspondence can do both.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, if a mage wanted a psychic attack that also damaged any surrounding matter, then I can see Mind being involved. We could take Mind 3 for a Psychic Blast and add Matter so it affects objects as well as things that have a mind, and Forces to add an element of movement. That doesn\u2019t really fit the description of this effect, though. It\u2019s more of a Psychic Attack That Tangentially Moves Objects than a direct Shift Objects With Thought.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>From Elsewhere in M20</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmute Semi-Complex Matter from Matter 2</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 2 indicates that more complicated forms of matter can be transmuted at rank 3, though it\u2019s not clear what counts. Initially it sounds like rank 2 can only handle simple, homogenous substances, but bread, paper, stone, wine, and wood are clearly possible. Meanwhile assemblies of multiple types of matter appear to be the province of Matter 4. Possibly substances that involve more than one state of matter start here? Like a glass of ice water, or quicksand. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another possibility is substances that require specific interactions or specific layouts of the different substances in play. Matter 2 could handle a disorganized or homogeneous mixture of substances, but Matter 3 would be necessary for the specific structure of a compound bow.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the end, tables will have to decide this one for themselves.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-07-2025, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T08:27:23-07:00","id":1550592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550586#post1550586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats exactly what i ment<br /> The thing is thats nothing new, there is little benefit to create those things fast as matter is more of a downtime sphere. Therefore Matter 4 is still redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think that getting a lot less paradox and requiring less knowledge and probably less successes is good enough? Also, I'd say some machines, like a smartphone, is made of several complex components that would require Matter 4 themselves. If you want to really build a complex device such as computers, wouldn't you need like a LOT of Mater 3 spells to make each one of the complex parts and build them? Tbh, I'm not sure Matter 3 could even do that, as those pieces aren't &quot;simple combinations&quot;...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550588#post1550588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The phrase &quot;through magick&quot; is doing enough heavy lifting to push the Earth out of orbit of the Sun without a lever.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, every effect is &quot;magick&quot; either the caster call it that way or not. When I said &quot;through magick&quot; I mean an Effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550588#post1550588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's &quot;through magick,&quot; then you're talking about a character's Focus and that doesn't matter to what Sphere ranks it takes to do something. An Etherite can call it pheromones all they want, but it might still be a Mind X effect in the end. Calling it pheromones doesn't automatically make it a Life effect, just like an Akashayana meditating doesn't automatically make something a Mind effect, or a Dreamspeaker invoking the spirits make it a Spirit effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with that. In fact, that's the thing I really, <b>really</b> hate about hdydt and the things that I promptly ignore from this book, because it's a direct contradiction to all the Mage core. But I'm not basing it on instruments. Life can do that simply because Life can manipulate &quot;body chemistry&quot; and by raw that is enough to affect social situations (as I showed in previous posts, if that's enough for an attribute increase or not were exhaustly debated).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550588#post1550588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole debate you've been blurring the lines between Focus and manipulating science. And that's why the Etherite example doesn't mean anything, and when monteparnas and I say the science has to be sound if you're incorporating science into the effect still means the science has to be sound. Pseudoscience Focuses don't get to use real world science to get extra bang for their buck. The pseudoscience is just another paradigm within another Focus that just tells us the way the mage thinks about magic and then does it.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD physics and science is not exactly like our real world science. Again, the Etherite example means that the game accepts stuff that is not real (or does not work irl), like orgone, pheromones, Ether,etc. So, if one effect is inside of the sphere ranks (changing your biology to affect others are, by raw) and your mage has a way of doing that within his paradigm, then it is doable. Doesn't matter if pheromones aren't a thing in real life or how they're supposed to work, just as orgone doesn't exists but the mage can use it. The Etherite very, very often incorporate science into their effects and very often it is not sound.<br /> <br /> To be honest, the blurring you described is intrinsic to the game, because the Spheres limits and explanations do follow a lot of our real life science. For example, the very Matter sphere we're discussing now: The sphere description says things like matter states, radioactive materials, density. Life sphere talks a lot about body chemistry, viruses, bacterias, etc. All those things are part of our real life science. But then, they go way further what's is possible irl science to explain effects. If you were to make an analysis about body chemistry and hormones, we would see that a lot of effects shouldn't work like they do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T08:47:56-07:00","id":1550594,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> <br /> <br /> Another use of Matter 3 is to change the shape of nearby objects (including the ground) to deal direct damage. Things like concrete spike or anything of the sort. I believe the damage table is to be followed, but the damage is only lethal, unless you add Prime and 1 point of Quintessence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T11:27:50-07:00","id":1550598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't think that getting a lot less paradox and requiring less knowledge and probably less successes is good enough? Also, I'd say some machines, like a smartphone, is made of several complex components that would require Matter 4 themselves. If you want to really build a complex device such as computers, wouldn't you need like a LOT of Mater 3 spells to make each one of the complex parts and build them? Tbh, I'm not sure Matter 3 could even do that, as those pieces aren't &quot;simple combinations&quot;... </div> </div> </div>Nope its not good enough. Doing something faster is not good enough. A higher sphere should do something different and more compex, not larger (looking at you forces 4 and 5) or faster.<br /> At the moment Matter 2 or 3 is way better than Matter 4 when it comes to usability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T22:14:14-07:00","id":1550617,"title":"","content":"Note that one quirk about the way Magick works is that the higher the Sphere requirement is, the fewer successes you're likely to get; because the base difficulty is derived from the Sphere level required, and higher-difficulty rolls are less likely to achieve successes. As such, there's some impetus to build <i>some</i> sort of scale benefit into the Sphere level, so that the power of the Sphere available is always greater the number of dots you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T09:15:36-07:00","id":1550628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550598#post1550598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope its not good enough. Doing something faster is not good enough. A higher sphere should do something different and more compex, not larger (looking at you forces 4 and 5) or faster.<br /> At the moment Matter 2 or 3 is way better than Matter 4 when it comes to usability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can create a gun, a computer or a car with Matter 2 and 3. Even the internal parts (like a combustion motor) is already too complex to be made with rank 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T09:53:42-07:00","id":1550630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550628#post1550628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you can create a gun, a computer or a car with Matter 2 and 3. Even the internal parts (like a combustion motor) is already too complex to be made with rank 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree to disagree a medieval blacksmith could make that if he knew how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T10:15:57-07:00","id":1550631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550630#post1550630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree to disagree a medieval blacksmith could make that if he knew how.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2026don't know what you're trying to argue. Anyone could do it too if they had all the equipment, material and knew how. What does that have to do with Mage and Matter sphere? Are you saying that a combustion motor is not complex?<br /> <br /> Honestly, we need to define what &quot;complex&quot; means and I don't think &quot;something a blacksmith can do&quot; is the right one. In rank 4 guns, cars and computers are listed as complicated. So if you want to make them with a lower rank you need to create the internal parts and assemble, but aren't the internal parts complicated as well?<br /> <br /> If you want to make a computer you would need to create a motherboard, ram memory, cpu, HD, source, etc. Each of these seems pretty complex.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think rank 3 should already be able to make those things, but that's just not how it seems it works in raw\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T11:38:59-07:00","id":1550635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550631#post1550631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2026don't know what you're trying to argue. Anyone could do it too if they had all the equipment, material and knew how. What does that have to do with Mage and Matter sphere? Are you saying that a combustion motor is not complex?<br /> <br /> Honestly, we need to define what &quot;complex&quot; means and I don't think &quot;something a blacksmith can do&quot; is the right one. In rank 4 guns, cars and computers are listed as complicated. So if you want to make them with a lower rank you need to create the internal parts and assemble, but aren't the internal parts complicated as well?<br /> <br /> If you want to make a computer you would need to create a motherboard, ram memory, cpu, HD, source, etc. Each of these seems pretty complex.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think rank 3 should already be able to make those things, but that's just not how it seems it works in raw\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>In a gun? no they are not. They are solid pieces of metal combined together.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T14:50:34-07:00","id":1550639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550635#post1550635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a gun? no they are not. They are solid pieces of metal combined together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Matter 3 can deal with those pieces, but you still have to assemble it and you need that expertise (I'd ask for a roll). While Matter 4 can create the gun in one go. Matter 3 would require several rolls, more dox, more risky [b]and[/quote] there are things you might not be able to create, like a computer or a smartphone (hence why I ised the computer example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T15:18:18-07:00","id":1550646,"title":"","content":"There's also a quality issue. Could a Medieval blacksmith make a functional gun with the right knowledge? Sure. Could they make a semi-auto? No. That's a few different kinds of smiths to handle the intricate blowback mechanics.<br /> <br /> But you know what a that means? You have a paperweight. The hard things with guns is the ammunition and fuel. The first black powder projectile weapon was recorded in history during Europe's Medieval period (though in China of course). It did not take long for the vast majority of what goes into the body of the gun to start getting figured out. Modern gun bodies are basically tweaks of designs 100+ years old or older. Ammo is what's radically changed (and changed what the body of the gun looks like more than anything else). And no Medieval smith can make modern smokeless powder or modern primers. It's not that you can't make them yourself, but smokeless powder involves a bunch of dangerous chemicals in a complex process to maximize the pressure that expels the bullet (and has to be tweaked between revolvers, gas operated blowback, and impact operated blowback). Making primers is making a miniature explosive device and even preppers advocate just stockpiling primers instead of trying to learn how to make your own because it's too hard to do by hand at home.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, maybe Matter 4 listing &quot;gun&quot; is a bad idea because instead of &quot;gun with ammo&quot; (honestly a basic combustion engine isn't that different either, but a modern ICE to run a modern vehicle is a separate level of complexity), because the gun isn't the hard part of making functional firearms.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T07:32:07-07:00","id":1550685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550568#post1550568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again you can make the components with Matter 2 and assemble them with Matter 3, that still makes 4 redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking about this a lot. The need to assemble a device is itself a constraint on how the device is designed. I've worked with designers who have struggled to make sure there is enough room for tools to fit in and fasten parts in place, and with enough assemblers cursing because the designers missed an important dimension. <br /> <br /> Matter 4 doesn't have that constraint. It can make devices that are physically impossible for a person to assemble in the first place. It can mount pieces so close together it would be physically impossible for anyone to get a tool in to fasten or unfasten the connectors. It can make interlocking parts that pass through each other in ways that are geometrically impossible to put together (like those interlocking piece puzzles, only there isn't a secret trick). Instead of using screws and threaded holes to hold pieces in place, it can instead make the screws and frame all one piece so that there is no way of taking the mounted part off (or of ever putting it on in the first place). It can make outer shells that are a single piece with no way of opening or closing them. Etc.<br /> <br /> So yes, Matter 4 can make things that Matter 2 and competent assembly cannot. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T07:50:25-07:00","id":1550686,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Complex Transmutation </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Complex and radical transformations now become possible, especially with the addition of other Spheres. Pumpkins can be changed into carriages (Life 2), people into thrones (Life 5), cars into robots (combinations of Forces and Prime), or thin air into banquets, so long as the mage doesn\u2019t mind racking up a little (or a lot\u2026) of Paradox. Different principles can be combined in complicated ways, creating cybernetic machines or electrified gold. Complicated devices (guns, cars, computers) may be conjured out of empty space if the mage understands the principles behind such things (in game terms, possesses the proper Abilities). As usual, though, complicated creations demand extended rituals and many successes.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Full Transmutation of Complex Matter</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this point a mage can use Matter to create complex arrangements of matter that involve multiple different forms of matter. Examples include carriages, thrones, cars, robots, banquets etc. There appears to be no limit to the complexity. Unlike Matter 2 there are no limitations on temperature, though radioactive materials may still be off limits. Even Matter 4 cannot make smoke detectors and glow in the dark watches.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I was having the hardest time coming up with an application not already covered in the examples, but thanks to recent conversation I do have this:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Impossible Mechanisms</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The design of complex mechanisms and computers is functionally limited by a lot of design constraints: what shapes can be made easily, how difficult is it to assemble, etc. Matter 4 doesn\u2019t have to concern itself with manufacturing techniques or step by step assembly. It can make mechanisms of interlocking pieces that can\u2019t be taken apart (and indeed couldn\u2019t be assembled together in the first place, at least by hand). It can fit things close enough together that there is no room to assemble in any kind of step by step manner.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On a similar note, Matter 4 is also free from price constraints. Bespoke circuit boards that elegantly curve in just the right ways to fit into the device that no company would make (at least not for any reasonable price. Intricately complex gears that would be ridiculously expensive to to make in one piece can be not only made by Matter 4 but made already in position and ready to work.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a game mechanic, I doubt this will come up in play, but in universe it would be highly prized. </span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thing to Life to Thing (Complex Transmutation + Transmute X Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this point any type of matter can be transformed into something living with either Life 3 (transmuting pumpkins is Life 3, not Life 2), Life 4 (for self), or Life 5, or back. I would point out that by the rules in Base Life, only fresh pumpkins count as life. Desiccated pumpkins or canned pumpkin would be Matter.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I want to take a moment to point out that the example for complex life is a regular person into a piece of furniture meant to be sat on. Matter 4 uses a throne, but lawn chairs are also possible. I bring this up because it will be relevant in Matter 5.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cars to Robots (Complex Transmutation + ??? + Fuel Pattern?)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Where\u2019s All the Prime Gone?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is no problem at all with cars to robots at Matter 4. I think that the spell is assuming a running car turning into a running robot, hence the addition of Forces. However, an unpowered car should turn into an unpowered robot with Matter alone. There\u2019s no need at all for Prime, though, as nothing is being conjured. Even in the case of an unpowered car turned into a powered robot, the addition of Forces is enough.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is possible, though, that this spell is supposed to be interpreted in more of a science fiction or cartoonish sense, i.e. <u>turning a car into an animated robot servant capable of obeying limited commands or having a small amount of instinct or agency.</u> Prime 2 never says anything about animation, but the magical effects table ties it in to that ability anyways, so possibly that is what is going on here.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T09:58:32-07:00","id":1550696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550685#post1550685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been thinking about this a lot. The need to assemble a device is itself a constraint on how the device is designed. I've worked with designers who have struggled to make sure there is enough room for tools to fit in and fasten parts in place, and with enough assemblers cursing because the designers missed an important dimension.<br /> <br /> Matter 4 doesn't have that constraint. It can make devices that are physically impossible for a person to assemble in the first place. It can mount pieces so close together it would be physically impossible for anyone to get a tool in to fasten or unfasten the connectors. It can make interlocking parts that pass through each other in ways that are geometrically impossible to put together (like those interlocking piece puzzles, only there isn't a secret trick). Instead of using screws and threaded holes to hold pieces in place, it can instead make the screws and frame all one piece so that there is no way of taking the mounted part off (or of ever putting it on in the first place). It can make outer shells that are a single piece with no way of opening or closing them. Etc.<br /> <br /> So yes, Matter 4 can make things that Matter 2 and competent assembly cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can fit those parts perfectly with Matter 3. As it allows you to change shape of matter however you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T13:03:04-07:00","id":1550704,"title":"","content":"I would argue the difference between Matter 2/3 and 4 is a Ship of Theseus situation; the sum of the parts is more than the parts themselves. On a metaphysical level, a mechanical clock has a different pattern than the parts of a clock - even if all the parts are created in the right place. Manual assembly of the parts would <i>create </i>the emergent mobile clock pattern, which is different from shaping the parts into existence: you're creating 'clock parts', not a 'clock'. tldr: the difference is metaphysical, not physical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 05-06-2025, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T19:36:00-07:00","id":1550716,"title":"","content":"Ok, it was established that smaetphone (or computer) parts are &quot;simple&quot; enough to be made with Matter 3? Genuinely asking, any hint from raw?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T20:32:13-07:00","id":1550719,"title":"","content":"Nothing\u2019s been established because Matter 3 never even says it can transform matter into more complex forms than Matter 2. Only Matter 2 says that, and it gives no guidelines. That said, if Matter 3 can transform things directly into smartphones then there\u2019s not much that\u2019s too complex for it and Matter 4\u2019s sole improvement to the track is multiple parts.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other end of the scale Matter 2 could have just meant Matter 3 can conjure multiple states of matter at once. That would certainly be consistent with the rank, and it\u2019s likely closer to the intent.<br /> <br /> Of course, Matter 3\u2019s other abilities can make an integrated circuit board. A mage with that rank can definitely sculpt one from the appropriate materials, but that\u2019s a fundamentally different effect than conjuring them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T23:53:50-07:00","id":1550728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550716#post1550716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, it was established that smaetphone (or computer) parts are &quot;simple&quot; enough to be made with Matter 3? Genuinely asking, any hint from raw?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I picked a bad example. I changed it to mechanical clock. IMO simple electronic components like resistors or diodes could work, but anything that itself is made of sufficiently complex components (displays) shouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 05-06-2025, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T08:16:22-07:00","id":1550738,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Alter Properties </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With Mastery, the crafter can create substances that transcend the limitations of scientific possibility, conjure materials unknown to Earthly reality, or share the deadly legacies of radioactive matter. Such Masters can shape armor out of air (with Prime 2), turn vampires into lawn furniture (Life 5), or melt steel with a thought (Mind 3). Again, such deeds remain incredibly vulgar, but they recall the godlike feats of legendry.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A very thin section with questionable examples. Matter 5 can:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transform and Alter Special Materials (Alter Properties)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level, no material is off limits. A mage can use Matter 5 to create and transmute any known substance. Radiation is now explicitly on the table, and since none of the others claimed it we can infer it was off limits until rank 5. That said, by the methodology of this thread Matter 5 cannot tell Matter 3 and 4 what they cannot do.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Radioactive Materials</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages can now create all forms of radioactive materials, which already means he can create nuclear fuel and nuclear weapons, but it can actually skip those steps too.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Transuranic, Heavy Elements May Not Be Used Where There Is Life</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Certain heavy elements have half lives so short they would fully decay in seconds. In the words of XKCD\u2019s Randall Munroe \u201cThe result wouldn\u2019t be <i>like</i> a nuclear explosion \u2013 it would <i>be</i> a nuclear explosion.\u201d So mage with Matter 5 can skip the bomb and go straight to the nuclear explosion, and it doesn\u2019t take much material to get to the level of a medium sized nuclear bomb.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, if he did this without Correspondence or a method of soaking <i>a lot</i> of damage, it would be the last spell he ever cast.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Alpha Radiation</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alpha radiation itself is helium nuclei, meaning there\u2019s a good case it is the province of Matter rather than Forces. Of course, Alpha particles are easily blocked by skin and clothing, but turning matter already inside of someone into alpha particles could be a lot of radiation damage. Since the target's skin is an effective shield, this is much safer for the casting mage.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Impossible Materials (Alter Properties)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level a mage can also create materials that are impossible. This would include bricks that don\u2019t interact in any way with glass (they pass right through), or magnets that attract specific things, or objects that are quantum locked.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note that many impossibilities were already possible at earlier levels, for instance ice that is lighter than air could be created by Alter Density, so the statement that Matter 5 can create things \u2018unknown to Earthly reality\u2019 cannot be used to limit the stated power of earlier ranks even outside the methodology of this thread.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Neutronium and Psuedoneutronium</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The exotic state of matter that neutron stars may be made of is possible at Matter 5, as is normal matter that somehow has the density of neutronium. The distinction between those two is sometimes quite important since neutron star material would catastrophically expand outside the gravity of the star.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Alter Density is a Matter 3 ability, keeping the atomic structure of the material intact while bringing something to that density is the impossible part that makes psuedoneutronium Matter 5.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These next one is here because I\u2019m going to use it in an upcoming contradiction analysis.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Heliophobic Materials</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Otherwise ordinary materials with the unusual quality of combusting or degrading in sunlight (and only sunlight) are the stuff of Matter 5.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue Properties (Alter Properties)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition to being able to create special materials, a mage can also give properties to materials. This is mostly a semantic difference as functionally, giving a brick a special power and transforming a brick into a brick that has a special power are the same.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because it is functionally the same, its examples are interchangeable with <b>Impossible Materials</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Psychoreactive Materials</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Otherwise ordinary materials with the unusual property of heating, melting, or combusting when exposed to concentrated mental energy would also be the stuff of Matter 5.</span> This is another example I am using because it will come up in contradiction analysis. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Matter 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Added: From Matter 3:</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 3 says Matter 5 is necessary to make permanent changes, which puts Matter alongside Life as the two spheres that directly lock permanent changes behind Rank 5. There is the same uncertainty of what this means as with Life (though Matter doesn\u2019t have to deal with Pattern Bleed), so I\u2019m not going to go through the possibilities again. Here is the permanent change possibility:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Here to Eternity (Alter Properties)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can change a target\u2019s pattern permanently. Unlike spells of permanent duration, there is no magic keeping the target\u2019s pattern this way, and this cannot be dispelled or unwoven because the magic is over and done with already. The new pattern is simply reality now.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately, the suggested conjunctional effects for Matter 5\u2026 aren\u2019t. Not good ones anyways.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Impossible Materials From Nothing (??? + Fuel Pattern) - Matter 5 / Prime 2</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Armor Out of Air</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>If we assume that the armor in question is made of impossible materials, and is created ex nihilo rather than from actual atmosphere, then yes this is Matter 5/Prime 2.</u> It would have been good to have a suggestion of what impossible material would make for really good armor.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regular armor converted from breathable air would be at least Matter 3 (for gas to solid) and possibly Matter 4 (for complex arrangements of materials), and no Prime would be necessary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Armor composed of actual air that nonetheless had the properties of combat armor would be Matter 5, and if for some reason it was conjured in a place with no atmosphere would also take Prime 2, so that\u2019s another niche option.</u></span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vampires to Lawn Furniture (??? + Perfect Metamorphosis - Matter 5 / Life 5?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Lawn Chairs Are Not Impossible Matter</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transforming a human to a chair was already established to be Life 5/Matter 4 in the Matter 4 section. The complexity of the chair has not changed, only the target. Life attacks on Vampires do require a Matter augment, but it is Matter 2, not 5. Even if we required Matter at 1 less rank than Life to affect Vampires (and that\u2019s not stated anywhere) that would still mean Matter 4.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Perhaps the goal is to change the target into a chair made of typical materials that nevertheless combusts in sunlight. That wasn\u2019t part of the brief, but it would take Life 5/Matter 5 to do that to a human.</u> Ironically, though, a mage shouldn\u2019t need Matter 5 to do the same to a vampire, since the indication is that the chair would automatically keep its vampiric nature regardless of what the mage does. In that one regard, the spell is easier to accomplish on Vampires.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Melt Steel With a Thought (??? + ???) Matter 5/ Mind 3?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - What is Mind? Doesn\u2019t Matter. What is Matter? Never Mind.</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If I were challenged to incorporate Mind into a Matter effect that melted steel, I could do it, but outside of that challenge I would never even consider Mind for such a spell. So, while it is certainly possible, there\u2019s just no way I would classify Mind as a need. Nor Matter 5 for that matter. Matter 3 is certainly capable of reshaping steel, including in a way that we could call melting, and there\u2019s nothing Matter 5 has that adds to that. This really should be a Matter 3 spell.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If I had to rescue this\u2026 well I suppose <u>Matter 5 could give steel the quality of \u201cmelting when thought at\u201d and then Mind 3 provides the psychic blast.</u> I question how often the need for this would arise, though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any thoughts?</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-07-2025, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T08:19:56-07:00","id":1550739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550719#post1550719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing\u2019s been established because Matter 3 never even says it can transform matter into more complex forms than Matter 2. Only Matter 2 says that, and it gives no guidelines. That said, if Matter 3 can transform things directly into smartphones then there\u2019s not much that\u2019s too complex for it and Matter 4\u2019s sole improvement to the track is multiple parts.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other end of the scale Matter 2 could have just meant Matter 3 can conjure multiple states of matter at once. That would certainly be consistent with the rank, and it\u2019s likely closer to the intent.<br /> <br /> Of course, Matter 3\u2019s other abilities can make an integrated circuit board. A mage with that rank can definitely sculpt one from the appropriate materials, but that\u2019s a fundamentally different effect than conjuring them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The thing here is to balance things in a way that Matter 4 isn't useless and yet Matter 3 (which, unlike Matter 4 is accessible in char generation) is still useful to create things. I guess the best we can do is to try to separate complex from simple. Voidshaper suggestion is the way I see it. So, Matter 3 can create laptop parts one by one, but not a whole laptop.That would mean that you need a lot more time, successes and paradox to create a laptop with Matter 3 than Matter 4, but you still can use this rank to create technology.<br /> <br /> And on top of that, all the things you posted about Matter 4 being able to create things in a more efficient (impossible to assemble) way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T08:31:25-07:00","id":1550740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550738#post1550738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vampires to Lawn Furniture (??? + Perfect Metamorphosis - Matter 5 / Life 5?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Lawn Chairs Are Not Impossible Matter</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transforming a human to a chair was already established to be Life 5/Matter 4 in the Matter 4 section. The complexity of the chair has not changed, only the target. Life attacks on Vampires do require a Matter augment, but it is Matter 2, not 5. Even if we required Matter at 1 less rank than Life to affect Vampires (and that\u2019s not stated anywhere) that would still mean Matter 4.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Perhaps the goal is to change the target into a chair made of typical materials that nevertheless combusts in sunlight. That wasn\u2019t part of the brief, but it would take Life 5/Matter 5 to do that to a human.</u> Ironically, though, a mage shouldn\u2019t need Matter 5 to do the same to a vampire, since the indication is that the chair would automatically keep its vampiric nature regardless of what the mage does. In that one regard, the spell is easier to accomplish on Vampires.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire into a lawnchair is Life3+Matter 3, I believe. You need Life 3 to transform someone and vampires require Matter. Matter 3 is the rank that allows to change the shape of objects, unless you're changing shape with Life, then it would be Life 3+Matter 2?<br /> <br /> Anyway, M20 Life 5+Matter 5 is clearly a ridiculous attempt to nerf mage's powers and is just wrong. You would already need to bypass counterspell (if applied) and the required successes to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550738#post1550738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Melt Steel With a Thought (??? + ???) Matter 5/ Mind 3?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - What is Mind? Doesn\u2019t Matter. What is Matter? Never Mind.</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If I were challenged to incorporate Mind into a Matter effect that melted steel, I could do it, but outside of that challenge I would never even consider Mind for such a spell. So, while it is certainly possible, there\u2019s just no way I would classify Mind as a need. Nor Matter 5 for that matter. Matter 3 is certainly capable of reshaping steel, including in a way that we could call melting, and there\u2019s nothing Matter 5 has that adds to that. This really should be a Matter 3 spell.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If I had to rescue this\u2026 well I suppose <u>Matter 5 could give steel the quality of \u201cmelting when thought at\u201d and then Mind 3 provides the psychic blast.</u> I question how often the need for this would arise, though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any thoughts?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Another sphere bloat. Seems pretty common in spheres descriptions. This is a Matter 3 effect, you're only changing the steel shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T08:47:56-07:00","id":1550741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Contradiction Resolution - What is Mind? Doesn\u2019t Matter. What is Matter? Never Mind.</i></b><br /> <br /> If I were challenged to incorporate Mind into a Matter effect that melted steel, I could do it, but outside of that challenge I would never even consider Mind for such a spell. So, while it is certainly possible, there\u2019s just no way I would classify Mind as a need. Nor Matter 5 for that matter. Matter 3 is certainly capable of reshaping steel, including in a way that we could call melting, and there\u2019s nothing Matter 5 has that adds to that. This really should be a Matter 3 spell.<br /> <br /> If I had to rescue this\u2026 well I suppose <u>Matter 5 could give steel the quality of \u201cmelting when thought at\u201d and then Mind 3 provides the psychic blast.</u> I question how often the need for this would arise, though.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, it only makes sense of you want to create some sort of &quot;psychic metal&quot; that reacts to tought. The &quot;melting to tought&quot; needs to be a property of the material, and not the effect.<br /> <br /> Could be useful as <b><i>part </i></b>of the process to make &quot;T-1000 like&quot; beings. It's a &quot;brain of liquid metal&quot; that reshapes itself as it sees fit. Arguably could be made as an Artifact using Matter 3, but arguably you would need an activation roll for each time you need to alter the fluid body, it could be more &quot;fluid&quot; :P if it's a natural property of the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-06-2025, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T10:30:23-07:00","id":1550744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550739#post1550739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. The thing here is to balance things in a way that Matter 4 isn't useless and yet Matter 3 (which, unlike Matter 4 is accessible in char generation) is still useful to create things. I guess the best we can do is to try to separate complex from simple. Voidshaper suggestion is the way I see it. So, Matter 3 can create laptop parts one by one, but not a whole laptop.That would mean that you need a lot more time, successes and paradox to create a laptop with Matter 3 than Matter 4, but you still can use this rank to create technology.<br /> <br /> And on top of that, all the things you posted about Matter 4 being able to create things in a more efficient (impossible to assemble) way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a rough breakdown I was putting together. Something like a mid sized printer might have, lowball, 100 parts. It also might have 50 steps of assembly. If we are generous and say that each part takes only one spell and each step only takes one spell, that's a minimum of 150 spells to make a printer.<br /> <br /> Lets say a part or a step needs 2 successes, the same as a small fire. Taking into account failures an Arete 4 mage using his sanctum would need around 220 casts and rack up around 27 points of paradox through botches alone. If he tried doing the same thing in a factory with no witnesses it would take 285 casts and he would rack up an impressive 230 points of paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T12:23:25-07:00","id":1550751,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511787-the-promise-of-1528-the-giovanni-and-politics?p=1550742#post1550742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another sphere bloat. Seems pretty common in spheres descriptions. This is a Matter 3 effect, you're only changing the steel shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this spell locks the matter effect to the subjects mind so while the spell lasts the user can use it as a action (or even reflexive) and directing it with his mind without the need of casting the spell each time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T14:03:15-07:00","id":1550761,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Well, you don't need to create piece by piece, maybe by bundles. But still, probably 10+ effects just to create them...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550751#post1550751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe this spell locks the matter effect to the subjects mind so while the spell lasts the user can use it as a action (or even reflexive) and directing it with his mind without the need of casting the spell each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a possibility. Although I believe it was not the intention of the author (they just don't care about rules integrity), I think this could be done. I'm not very comfortable with locking with Mind sphere, since it's not a pattern sphere, but I think M20 has an example of that. Can't remember right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T14:49:21-07:00","id":1550764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550761#post1550761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Well, you don't need to create piece by piece, maybe by bundles. But still, probably 10+ effects just to create them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I was already lowballing the number of parts and lowballing the number of steps necessary to make the more complicated parts and assuming that very similar parts could be made with the same spell, and treating all screws as a single part. Possibly we are picturing different printers, though even a small receipt printer would be significantly over 10 successes.<br /> <br /> In fact, I just pulled up a video of someone assembling a small receipt printer. It started out partially assembled, but for parts I saw at the very least: the top casing (plastic), bottom casing (plastic), window, power switch, status indicator board, main board, I/O panel, a roller guide for the paper, a spindle for the paper, at least 3 harnesses, numerous screws and fasteners, and an already assembled print assembly which I assume had at least a metal casing, the printhead, a small motor, a small board, and a small harness. Now even assuming all the harnesses could be made at once, all the screws could be made at once, the plastic casings and windows could be made at once, and each board could be made in a single effect, and even ignoring how complicated printheads themselves can get, that's at least 12 parts different enough to require their own effect and at least 7 steps to assemble. And that's a simple receipt printer.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-07-2025, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T15:04:52-07:00","id":1550765,"title":"","content":"And, if I followed that correctly, that's no paper or ink/toner too. Which runs into the paper weight problem I cited with making a gun without ammo.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how well we can resolve this. Matter is not a well written Sphere, so there's a lot of personal interpretation. Matter is also more explicit about characters needing appropriate knowledge of how an item works than Life or Forces are with their Patterns, but doesn't really put any guidance on that, and if it varies by Sphere level. I would personally interpret that trying to use Matter 2/3 to create and assemble parts still requires as much knowledge and skill on the mundane side of things as buying the parts and tools and then building it, while Matter 4's more holistic methods allow a more &quot;platonic&quot; idea of how something works and thus takes less mundane knowledge of how to build something. This makes Matter 4 better than if you see the amount of skill necessary equal regardless of level, but I can't really argue that equal regardless of level is worse way to read the rules without getting into circular reasoning (I want Matter 4 to be better, so I'm advocating a position that makes it better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T15:47:37-07:00","id":1550768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550765#post1550765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, if I followed that correctly, that's no paper or ink/toner too. Which runs into the paper weight problem I cited with making a gun without ammo.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how well we can resolve this. Matter is not a well written Sphere, so there's a lot of personal interpretation. Matter is also more explicit about characters needing appropriate knowledge of how an item works than Life or Forces are with their Patterns, but doesn't really put any guidance on that, and if it varies by Sphere level. I would personally interpret that trying to use Matter 2/3 to create and assemble parts still requires as much knowledge and skill on the mundane side of things as buying the parts and tools and then building it, while Matter 4's more holistic methods allow a more &quot;platonic&quot; idea of how something works and thus takes less mundane knowledge of how to build something. This makes Matter 4 better than if you see the amount of skill necessary equal regardless of level, but I can't really argue that equal regardless of level is worse way to read the rules without getting into circular reasoning (I want Matter 4 to be better, so I'm advocating a position that makes it better).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats for sure but it still makes an underwhelming 4 dot sphere. There should be more like combining selected qualities of 2 materials or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T15:54:17-07:00","id":1550769,"title":"","content":"A big part of the problem with Matter is that you can make a gun with it, but you can't make a blaster with it; the latter is outside the scope of mundane science, and therefore requires Prime to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T16:26:58-07:00","id":1550772,"title":"","content":"Matter 5 doesn't specific you need Prime to make things outside of the scope of mundane science (it only uses Prime in one example). Using Matter 5 to make a blaster is probably more of a problem in terms of things like recharging/reloading it since that's also going to take magic on some level.<br /> <br /> If you took Star Wars (since it actually tried to explain how its blasters work in a manner that could pass as realistic) as inspiration, the blaster fires a bolt of highly charged plasma excited by an integral laser. Those blasters generally require the follow that's beyond mundane science: a chamber that can contain the rapid charge and expulsion of plasma bolts (no reason Matter 5 can't do this alone), a gas that is both compressible enough to be practical and capable of turning into a plasma state that can carry enough energy to be a lethal projectile (also something Matter 5 covers alone), a laser strong enough at that size (also Matter 5 as long as we're getting the energy from somewhere else), and then an energy cell to supply the weapon and specifically the laser (here you can argue Matter + Forces or Prime as we're finally getting beyond exotic materials and into harnessing some serious juice).<br /> <br /> That said, it's a lot more work than using Forces 3/Prime 2, and a blaster as an instrument instead. If a Matter 5 fictional gas is your ammo, then you have weapon that's a lot of effort to reload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T19:59:55-07:00","id":1550780,"title":"","content":"The catch is that a blaster is a Wonder; and unless you argue that it's a Trinket, that means that you use Prime to make it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T20:55:24-07:00","id":1550782,"title":"","content":"That presumes it's one thing and one thing only in the rules. Or that the M20 definitions of Trinket are as clear as they should be. Or that the definition of Trinket should override what the Spheres say they can do.<br /> <br /> If Matter 5 says I can make materials that don't exist under mundane scientific rules, and can do so without any other Spheres... then I can. If you need to add Prime to anything built out of magically produced materials/components, that should really be in the core rules of magic casting; since that impacts multiple Spheres. Hell, the whole point of &quot;Trinkets&quot; was to make Quick and Dirty Wonders from Revised more codified, and that was a category of magically enhanced items that didn't inherently need Prime to be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T06:31:25-07:00","id":1550788,"title":"","content":"I realized I left one important Matter 5 ability out. That's not so surprising because it is actually stated in Matter 3:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550738#post1550738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Added: From Matter 3:</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter 3 says Matter 5 is necessary to make permanent changes, which puts Matter alongside Life as the two spheres that directly lock permanent changes behind Rank 5. There is the same uncertainty of what this means as with Life (though Matter doesn\u2019t have to deal with Pattern Bleed), so I\u2019m not going to go through the possibilities again. Here is the permanent change possibility:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Here to Eternity (Alter Properties)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can change a target\u2019s pattern permanently. Unlike spells of permanent duration, there is no magic keeping the target\u2019s pattern this way, and this cannot be dispelled or unwoven because the magic is over and done with already. The new pattern is simply reality now.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T08:17:57-07:00","id":1550792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550780#post1550780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The catch is that a blaster is a Wonder; and unless you argue that it's a Trinket, that means that you use Prime to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can make a blaster as a Wonder or you can enchant an already made blaster (or gun, or toy gun whatever) with Forces and Prime to make it a Trinket that shoots plasma.<br /> <br /> You can also create a functioning blaster like people posted, but that would require Matter 5 and Prime (to fuel). <br /> <br /> All those are valid ways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T08:37:39-07:00","id":1550793,"title":"","content":"Wow, we are into Mind now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Mind</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview: </b>The Mind, the Astral, Consciousness, Illusion, Communication, Psychic powers</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Mind attacks are limited to bashing damage unless other spheres are involved.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 - Mind magic is coincidental unless other spheres are involved</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 - When Mind effects target an individual entity, Difficulty is based on the target\u2019s Willpower rather than the usual calculation. Drastic mind control and effects targeting mages or other supernaturals are at a +3 difficulty. The target can try to resist with Willpower.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T08:46:22-07:00","id":1550794,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Sense Thoughts &amp; Emotions/Mind Shield/Empower Self </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With basic mental magick, the mage learns to sense the emotions and surface impulses of other people. Although he cannot read specific thoughts, he\u2019s able to perceive psychic impressions about a person or (with Matter 1) a place or object. Through this perception, he can guess at the nature of weak Resonance signatures and read the stronger ones outright. Even without Resonance, that mage can scan auras, note mood shifts, discern truth from lies, or grasp someone\u2019s overall state of mind by way of a successful Arete roll.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meanwhile, the mage also learns to shield his own mind from the thoughts and emotions of other people, constructing mental barriers around his aura, emotions, and consciousness. Each success on a coincidental Arete roll removes one success from any other character\u2019s attempt to read those psychic elements.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On a related note, he also learns how to multitask and absorb data with startling acuity. Each success he rolls allows him to either consider an additional subject or speed the processing time that a normal person might require. For a scene or two, he can even raise one of his Mental Traits by one dot per success, thanks to a Mind Empowerment Effect that concentrates his mental faculties.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind is one of those spheres that gets a lot more than just senses at rank 1.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Emotion and Presence of Thoughts (Sense Thoughts &amp; Emotions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this power a mage can sense emotions and thoughts, or at least the presence of thoughts with maybe some information thrown in. It is possible that reading emotions is supposed to be similarly hazy, but that is not how it is worded here. Though limited in information, the mere ability to sense the presence of thoughts is quite powerful as it can alert the mage to who is around him.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also, while impressions of thoughts are limited, they is enough to determine intents and distinguish truth from lies, all of which are quite powerful in a social situation.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>The Life or Death of the Party</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The various emotions and intentions that Mind 1 can sense can easily help a mage control a social situation.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Identify Trigger</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Mind 1 cannot itself make attacks, it can help a mage to know vulnerable points for social attacks.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Psychic Impressions (Sense Thoughts &amp; Emotions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A subtly different power than sensing thoughts, this ability lets a mage sense the psychic impressions and resonances left by minds. He can read these automatically off of people, though needs Matter to read them off of things. Whether one person can leave these impressions on another is not stated, though it sounds plausible. From the text it sounds like this is subtly different from reading auras, though from the sphere writeups alone it is hard to tell. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That said, I\u2019m going to include reading auras as a part of this power as it is similar enough that it doesn\u2019t need its own section.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sense Arcanoi Remnants</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage should be able to, with difficulty, sense the remnants of Pathos and Angst used in various Arcanoi. Without help, I would limit this to Arcanoi that cross the Shroud.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Shield (Mind Shield)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also use Mind 1 to shield himself from attempts to read and influence his mind. Defense of this kind usually doesn\u2019t come until rank 2, but it makes a lot of sense here from a gameplay standpoint.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Cool as Ice </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oddly enough, while the one mechanical use is a defense against mind reading, the actual description is much broader. It reads like it includes incidental thoughts and emotions too. Practically this won\u2019t come up much with thoughts, but imprints and resonance can have an effect. If, say, an area has enough resonance or impression to cause fear and anxiety in a person, Mind 1 can let a mage shrug that off.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Boost Mind (Empower Self)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is such a notable power, at least in terms of day-to-day life, that I suspect most mages who have it abuse it. I certainly would. A mage can give himself the ability to multitask, speed his thought processes, and boost his mental stats. Honestly, there are a lot more mental processes that are likely enhanceable. In game terms it is a little bit less powerful as most changes would fall into the mechanics already stated.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Brute Force Pattern Recognition (AKA Accuracy Through Volume, Mind Edition)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By increasing multitasking a mage can run through more ideas and comparisons at a time. Even without boosting mental stats, this means he can go through more possibilities in the same amount of time, which increases his chances of discovering something.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Invalidate Your Fellow Players' Experiences </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On a technical level, Mind 1 is capable of \u2018curing\u2019 many neurodivergencies and other conditions. It is also capable of replicating them (arguably Brute Force Pattern Recognition replicates part of the ADHD experience. It\u2019s based on mine). Both of these need to be handled responsibly, especially if someone at the table has one of those neurodivergencies. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Despite the name there are reasons for actually using these effects. The name is just there to point out that context and communication matter a lot. </span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is one listed.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Psychic Impressions in Places and Things (Sense Thoughts &amp; Emotions + Matter Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I still find it interesting that reading impressions on objects requires Matter and reading impressions on people does not require Life. I don\u2019t see this as a contradiction, though. People have minds and they respond to the minds and actions of others. Psychic impressions on mindless creatures isn\u2019t covered, so it is ST call whether reading them off of, say, moss requires Life. The question is trivial if the mage has Matter, since there are always objects around, but it might matter if he only has Life.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T12:02:34-07:00","id":1550808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550794#post1550794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Identify Trigger</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Mind 1 cannot itself make attacks, it can help a mage to know vulnerable points for social attacks.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like a bit of a stretch at Mind 1, or at least is a lot more contextual than is practical. If you're actively watching someone via Mind 1 and they have a psychological trigger? Sure, they can't hide it without magic from you, and from context you should know what set them off. But sensing that someone is an arachnophobe when nothing sets off their fear doesn't really seem to mesh with the text. It's also just surface level stuff at Mind 1, so it's a lot less functional for aiding in social attacks than latter Mind powers that can delve much deeper into someone's thoughts. Esp. when it comes to more complex issues like PTSD, knowing what a trigger is, and what the actually trauma that you can manipulate is, takes a lot more knowing because they aren't usually as directly connected as a phobia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T12:40:44-07:00","id":1550810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550808#post1550808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This feels like a bit of a stretch at Mind 1, or at least is a lot more contextual than is practical. If you're actively watching someone via Mind 1 and they have a psychological trigger? Sure, they can't hide it without magic from you, and from context you should know what set them off. But sensing that someone is an arachnophobe when nothing sets off their fear doesn't really seem to mesh with the text. It's also just surface level stuff at Mind 1, so it's a lot less functional for aiding in social attacks than latter Mind powers that can delve much deeper into someone's thoughts. Esp. when it comes to more complex issues like PTSD, knowing what a trigger is, and what the actually trauma that you can manipulate is, takes a lot more knowing because they aren't usually as directly connected as a phobia.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I was having hard time coming up with any clever applications there. Mind 1 is definitely more an aide to observation than an actual probe in this context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T14:35:24-07:00","id":1550814,"title":"","content":"Going back to entropy for a second found this on page 562<br /> <br /> &quot;\u201cI\u2019m throwing out an intention,\u201d she says, \u201cthat someone will either take Jinx to lunch, or else give her enough money to buy a meal or two.\u201d As she shuffles and draws the cards, Jinx keeps glancing up at passersby, giving them the puppy-dog-eyes treatment.<br /> \u201cEntropy 2 to manipulate probability,\u201d Camille says, \u201cplus Life 2 to note hungry bystanders who\u2019d be likely to help a cute girl get a meal, and Spirit 1 to read auras so she can figure out who\u2019s most likely to feed her without expecting anything else in return.\u201d<br /> Using Entropy 2/ Life 2/ Spirit 1, Camille rolls two dice for Jinx\u2019s Arete. Jinx\u2019s battered cards count as a personalized instrument (-1 difficulty), and the Effect is coincidental because she\u2019s not doing anything that obviously defies reality or otherwise looks like magick. The roll\u2019s difficulty, therefore, is a base of 5 (highest Sphere + 3), -1 for the cards, for a total of 4. Camille rolls the dice and gets one success. In the story, Jinx spots a college girl not much older than Jinx herself. That girl\u2019s got store-bought distressed jeans, a Washington State sweatshirt, and a blue-green aura, suggesting trust and generosity, tinged with a bit of hunger. Jinx\u2019s spell tilts the odds in her favor, and the girl looks over to Jinx and smiles. \u201cHey,\u201d she says, holding out a hand. \u201cI\u2019m kinda hungry too. You wanna go catch some lunch? My treat\u2026\u201d&quot;<br /> <br /> This would asume Entropy can make things happen cause youre lucky even at low levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 05-08-2025, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T20:14:08-07:00","id":1550826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550814#post1550814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would asume Entropy can make things happen cause youre lucky even at low levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, that was a mess of a post...<br /> <br /> Of course Entropy can play with probability, that's in the reach of the sphere. But things need to be around and have a chance of happening. In the example, the ST judged ok to make someone willing to donate passing by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T21:05:11-07:00","id":1550828,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m still trying to figure out Life 2 \u2018to note hungry bystanders who\u2019d be likely to help a cute girl get a meal.\u2019 That\u2019s such a strange choice I don\u2019t know where to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T00:02:44-07:00","id":1550833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550828#post1550828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m still trying to figure out Life 2 \u2018to note hungry bystanders who\u2019d be likely to help a cute girl get a meal.\u2019 That\u2019s such a strange choice I don\u2019t know where to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it makes them hungry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T05:03:37-07:00","id":1550836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550828#post1550828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m still trying to figure out Life 2 \u2018to note hungry bystanders who\u2019d be likely to help a cute girl get a meal.\u2019 That\u2019s such a strange choice I don\u2019t know where to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be Life 1. Or as quelsec said, to make some good hearted person hungry too, but then it should be Life 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> PS: From char creation example, we can see that Jinx has the gollowing spheres:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With an Arete of 2, Jinx is limited to Sphere Rank 2. Camille gives her Entropy 2, Life 2, Forces 1, and Spirit 1 </div> </div> </div>So, I have the strong feeling that the author is simply very loose with the sphere rules and capabilities and as a ST would just go &quot;Oh, you have those spheres? Ok, let's see what you can do with them.&quot; And then just throws them in an effect relating each of them to an &quot;explanation&quot; of the spell, like the one posted, regsrdless of what the spheres ranks actually do. Each of the spheres alone should be enough to find someone hungry and/or willing to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 05-08-2025, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T08:33:39-07:00","id":1550843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550836#post1550836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I have the strong feeling that the author is simply very loose with the sphere rules and capabilities and as a ST would just go &quot;Oh, you have those spheres? Ok, let's see what you can do with them.&quot; And then just throws them in an effect relating each of them to an &quot;explanation&quot; of the spell, like the one posted, regsrdless of what the spheres ranks actually do. Each of the spheres alone should be enough to find someone hungry and/or willing to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>In play, characters will likely pad out spells with spheres and their own personal understanding of the spheres, so I'm very forgiving of fuzzy thinking of sphere use in this context. Then I remember that this example is still meant to show us how to play the game, and it is doing a terrible job of doing that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T08:40:29-07:00","id":1550844,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Read Surface Thoughts/ Empathic Bond/ Create Impressions/ Mental Impulse </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the mage begins to skim the contents of unshielded minds, discern emotional states, read memories that have been left behind on objects or places, and project single words or emotional impulses to other people. The simpler the emotional content, the easier it is to send or read; a flash of rage, for instance, is easy to project or receive, but the complex stew of reflective melancholy presents a challenge to inexperienced Mind-mages. (Game-wise, such complex feats demand more successes than a simple feat does.)</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Read Surface Thoughts (Read Surface Thoughts)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It seems obvious what this power does on the, well, surface, but there isn\u2019t much guidance for what constitutes a surface thought. Intuitively, though, it seems like this covers anything the target is actively thinking about, or can\u2019t avoid thinking about. It also seems that deeper motivations and anything the target is trying to hide will be harder to access or off limits.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While this is supposed to be less powerful than later ranks, it is worth pointing out that if the mage can read both surface thoughts and memories (and there is reason to think he can) there is an awful lot he can pull out of someone\u2019s head.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Detect Aphantasia</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In reading someone\u2019s surface thoughts, a mage will easily be able to tell if they form mental images or not, and if they have an inner voice or not. Since the presence or absence of either of these doesn\u2019t have a practical effect, especially in game, this is unlikely to have an impact in play. I just find it interesting that mind mages would have known about this phenomenon since the dawn of time.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Read Emotions (Empathic Bond)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Mind 1 or Mind 2</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Both rank 1 and 2 give the mage the ability to sense emotions. Mind 1 says \u2018sense emotions and surface impulses,\u2019 while Mind 2 is \u2018discern emotional states.\u2019 The best way of reconciling this I can see is that Mind 1 allows a mage to detect the presence of a strong emotion, with no real information about the reason. Meanwhile Mind 2 allows a mage to see the complex emotional state of a person, including some information on context. It is the difference between \u2018he is angry\u2019 and \u2018he is angry because he feels slighted by his brother.\u2019</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Given that this ability is in the same list as reading surface thoughts, it is quite likely that any context has similar limitations.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Detect Foreign Emotions</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Quite a few denizens of the WoD can manipulate the emotions of a target. An observant mage can likely use Mind 2 to tell the difference in context between a natural and an imparted emotion.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Read Memories (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Memories on Objects, Memories on People, Memories of People</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 2 says a mage can read memories left on objects or places. Objects and places is a term we saw in Mind 1 - a mage could use Mind 1/Matter 1 to read psychic impressions off objects and places. Two things of note:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First, there is no mention of Matter here. Read straight, that means it isn\u2019t necessary. That is an option. That said, the terminology is so close that we could also reasonably infer it. That\u2019s an ST call.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second, Mind 2 strangely leaves off reading the memories of a person, though it also doesn\u2019t explicitly exclude it either. Again based on the patterns of Mind 1, if a mage can read memories off an object he should be able to read them off a person. Indeed, it would be very strange for Mind 2 to bring up reading memories and not intend that meaning.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Memories Bound in Human Skin</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s not uncommon for someone to experience something profound or traumatic or overwhelming, then bury the experience so they can continue with their day. The memory was strong enough to read, but isn\u2019t any longer. However, the mage could potentially read the imprint it left on the person\u2019s clothes or even off the person's skin.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Send Thoughts (Mental Impulse)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Mind 2 a mage has the ability to send thoughts and emotions. I split the two apart because Thoughts needs special attention. The mage has a one word limit, but in practice, I think this is functionally capable of more than one word if only because of how language works. A concept that needs a single word in one language might need several in another, but as a thought there is little difference between them. I\u2019d go so far as to say that thoughts that have well known aphorisms, like \u2018don\u2019t make waves\u2019 should be possible, but that\u2019s an ST call. Indeed, some ST\u2019s might think things should work differently in different languages.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On another note, the text does not make it clear if the mental impulse is obviously foreign or not, so a mage can presumably have it work either way. </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That gives two major uses of this power:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>One Word Communication</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first is simple communication. Single words work very well as warnings and instructions, and can also be used to convey yes/no answers and simple ideas. Added: As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> points out, this would reasonably include talking with animals, though that might lean more towards the Send Emotion side.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Super Secret Handshake</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A variant of direct communication, here the mage imparts a code word that verifies his identity, whether he\u2019s been followed, etc. This would obviously need to be worked out in advance, but it is a great element of an espionage based game.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>And Always Let <s>Me</s> Your Conscience Be Your Guide</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The second main use of Send Thoughts is manipulation. The mage imparts a thought that is not obviously from elsewhere, and it is here especially where the one word count gets fuzzy. If the target is not aware the thought is from the outside, he probably isn\u2019t perceiving the word so much as its meaning. So here the limit is likely thoughts that can be easily summarized in a single word, like \u2018run,\u2019 or \u2018delicious,\u2019 or \u2018meh.\u2019</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Impart Emotion (Mental Impulse)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imparting emotions, like reading emotions, has more range and nuance. With more successes a mage can impart more complex emotions. Given the examples, there doesn\u2019t seem to be a limit to emotional complexity. Also, even if multi-word aphorisms aren\u2019t possible with Send Thought, the emotional meaning behind them is still possible here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is not stated whether the mage can set the subject of these thoughts and emotions, but the degree of control makes that unlikely. At least directly.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Memory Seed </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Actually implanting memories is a Mind 4 power, but Mind 2 has everything needed to \u2018help\u2019 a target develop their own false memories. By manipulating the emotional context of certain thoughts and memories, a mage can lay the groundwork for specific false memories to form. It takes multiple applications. First the mage uses this power to remind someone of a memory or thought or person or thing, then he uses it again to apply the emotion while the target is remembering. This is then repeated periodically over a period of time. This is a dark, dark power</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Not My Circus, Not My Monkeys (AKA Return of the SEP Field)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whether it comes as a thought or as an emotion a mage can project the sense that something is not worth getting involved with. Note that this version of this effect may not be able to set a specific target, but will instead apply to whatever the target is looking at or just in general.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternate title: \u2018He has a Clipboard, Don\u2019t Make Eye Contact\u2019</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The reverse of this gives the target or targets feelings that something is out of place and demands attention.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-09-2025, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T09:58:39-07:00","id":1550845,"title":"","content":"When Mind comes to play i decided to go like this:<br /> 1. Detect minds<br /> 2. Read emotions<br /> 3. Read minds<br /> Its definetly not RAW but makes more sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T14:45:54-07:00","id":1550859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550844#post1550844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Contradiction Resolution - Mind 1 or Mind 2</i></b><br /> <br /> Both rank 1 and 2 give the mage the ability to sense emotions. Mind 1 says \u2018sense emotions and surface impulses,\u2019 while Mind 2 is \u2018discern emotional states.\u2019 The best way of reconciling this I can see is that Mind 1 allows a mage to detect the presence of a strong emotion, with no real information about the reason. Meanwhile Mind 2 allows a mage to see the complex emotional state of a person, including some information on context. It is the difference between \u2018he is angry\u2019 and \u2018he is angry because he feels slighted by his brother.\u2019</div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to read Revised on this, because this is exactly what it's said as the limitations of Mind 1.<br /> <br /> I can't transcribe the paragraph because my Revised it's not on it's original language, but it does say that Mind 1 detects the emotion, but no specific information about it, such as at what it's directed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Memories on Objects, Memories on People, Memories of People</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 2 says a mage can read memories left on objects or places. Objects and places is a term we saw in Mind 1 - a mage could use Mind 1/Matter 1 to read psychic impressions off objects and places. Two things of note:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First, there is no mention of Matter here. Read straight, that means it isn\u2019t necessary. That is an option. That said, the terminology is so close that we could also reasonably infer it. That\u2019s an ST call.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second, Mind 2 strangely leaves off reading the memories of a person, though it also doesn\u2019t explicitly exclude it either. Again based on the patterns of Mind 1, if a mage can read memories off an object he should be able to read them off a person. Indeed, it would be very strange for Mind 2 to bring up reading memories and not intend that meaning.</span> </div> </div> </div>Something I've found on Revised Mind 2, but can be deducted from both this and the Impart Emotions, and could be interesting: The lvl 2 sample Effect &quot;psychic imprint&quot; (or something like that) allows to imprint an emotion on an object.<br /> <br /> This seems to have two uses.<br /> *An object with a strong emotion imprinted &quot;emanates&quot; that feeling, which allows to calm or otherwise manipulate people on it's area.<br /> *An object imbued of an emotion has greater &quot;mystical weight&quot;. What is this?, well, the text mentions that this as imposing a Resonance, so I would imagine that this is it (lowers/raises difficulties and such).<br /> <br /> Also could be used to send a &quot;message&quot; trough an object, since you know mages and people with Conscience can sense this stuff. A sort of &quot;invisible graffity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some considerations:<br /> <br /> *The idea that Mind 2 could imprint a Resonance. It's not incoherent, I think, since those are so often related to emotions on a place, but being a &quot;reserved word&quot; that refers to a rule that affects discretely many aspects of the system, I feel it would be better if it was more explicit how Mind relates to this on the Sphere itself rather than on a Rote, even if it's among the main samples of that level, and (at least in my opinion) &quot;makes sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> *I find it interesting that the Rote of Revised it's also purely Mind 2, in spite of it targeting an object (Revised Mind 1 doesn't mention Matter to read the &quot;vives&quot; on an object either).<br /> <br /> Maybe on M20 this would require Matter. But considering how the wording of Mind 2 here doesn't mention Matter when reading an object's emotional imprint either, it could be an indication that this sort of effects are something Mind 2 can do alone.<br /> <br /> If I had to justify this metaphysical, I would say this happens because on mage there are a few very real realities that aren't real (or, well, demonstrated) in our world. Such as objects carrying &quot;memory&quot; (something that it's also referenced on different gamelines, such as Vampire's Auspex). This is one of those, and so it's Resonance. You're affecting &quot;that&quot;, not an object nor people in contact with the object, but the Mind &quot;phenomenon&quot; that happens to be tied to a Matter pattern. Then again, that fails to explain why Mind 1 requires Matter, and - between Revised failing to mention this on either level, and Mind 1 not needing Life RAW to read the toughts left on moss , I'm starting to think <i>needing Matter </i>may be the outlier.<br /> <br /> Then again, that's just an interpretation and I reckon this requires further proof. But if the ambiguity on wheter the lvl 2 requires Matter or not on M20 it's an ST call, well, this could be argument to make that call.<br /> <br /> *If you can imprint an emotion, I would argue you can imprint the other stuff you can &quot;impart&quot;, such as a word. ST discretion if the &quot;memory of stuff&quot; can &quot;remember&quot; a word at all since this departs from Resonance (very often the &quot;memory of stuff&quot; on WoD includes more than just emotions, Revised Mind itself mentions intense memories and general vague ideas), also if this needs Matter even if the other use doesn't. <hr /><br /> In general, one (and also the books) would relate Mind to purely internal stuff. What we could call &quot;our psyche&quot; But sometimes Mind seems to depart from these to somewhat external phenomena that are also Mind related because they're related to emotions or concepts. Such as the so called memory of an object. I'm very interested on these &quot;stuff of mind&quot; that somehow exists or can exist outside what common sense would call &quot;the mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, because most Mind effects work on animals, stuff that would be indistinguishable from &quot;talking to animals&quot; can be done at levels 2-3. Emotions, impressions, memories, &quot;instincts&quot; - you can sense these things as part of your mystical awareness. And then project your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-08-2025, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T08:21:25-07:00","id":1550880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550859#post1550859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe on M20 this would require Matter. But considering how the wording of Mind 2 here doesn't mention Matter when reading an object's emotional imprint either, it could be an indication that this sort of effects are something Mind 2 can do alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Mind 1 and Mind 2 are written it appears that memories and emotions are naturally imparted on objects and places, which is fairly consistent with WoD and the stories it tries to tell. If emotions and memories can do that on their own, then the sphere of emotions and memories can do that on its own. That's the way I see it anyways.<br /> <br /> As for what is required to read those emotions, I could see that going either way. Mind should be able to read emotion or memory on its own, but... perhaps without Matter it can't tell where the emotion or memory is coming from. That would be a reasonable way of preserving the power of Mind, while explaining what Matter is doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, because most Mind effects work on animals, stuff that would be indistinguishable from &quot;talking to animals&quot; can be done at levels 2-3. Emotions, impressions, memories, &quot;instincts&quot; - you can sense these things as part of your mystical awareness. And then project your own. </div> </div> </div>Good point, I'm going to add that in.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T09:46:12-07:00","id":1550882,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 3</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Mental Link/ Project Illusions/ Dreamwalk/ Psychic Blast </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With increasing skill, the mage learns to link minds, forge telepathic communications, read or influence another person\u2019s thoughts, craft mental illusions, enter someone\u2019s dreams and explore dream Realms, and blast psychic assaults into an unwilling rival\u2019s consciousness. At this stage, Mind attacks can inflict painful \u2013 though rarely fatal \u2013 damage. Combined with Correspondence, Forces, Matter, or Life, he is able to employ telekinesis, pyrokinetics, and psychophysical assault, influencing objects, elements, or people with the power of his mind. Unlike most other Effects, this sort of thing is not coincidental, although such talents do have a place within popular culture.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here we come to one of the difficult lines and of course it comes from conjunctional Mind effects. Before that though, Mind 3 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link Minds (Mental Link)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Precious little information is given on what this means, so it is quite versatile. It seems to be the basis behind telepathic communication, reading minds, and influencing minds. That said, it is also listed alongside those, so it also must mean what it sounds like. A mage can link minds (his own doesn\u2019t have to be one of them), which presumably lets the linked mind share thoughts, senses, or memories depending on how the link is set. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m open to any arguments for limitations on this one, but I\u2019m not seeing any at the moment.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sympathy Pains</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Mind 3 a mage can curse someone to feel whatever he does to the mage, which is handy for making people think twice about hurting you. This could reasonably share wound penalties, too, so it would also ensure that the target is as incapacitated as the mage. </span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Telepathic Communication (Mental Link?)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the mage can fully communicate with others mentally. This expands the communication ability of impart thought to full on messages and ongoing dialogue. There's not much to be said about this as telepathy is common in fiction.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Forge Telepathic Communication - Faking a message</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m not really sure why the word \u2018forge\u2019 was added, and while I presume it was meant in the creative sense, it can also be in the deceptive sense. Indeed, there\u2019s no reason a mage with Mind 3 couldn\u2019t use telepathy to pretend to be someone or something else.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Read Thoughts (Mental Link)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now a person\u2019s mind is an open book. There is very little a mage can\u2019t pull out of it with enough successes</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Read Mortifying Moments</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hey, you know those stupid moments from your past that make you cringe? The ones you still find embarrassing even if, intellectually, you know they were no big deal? The ones your mind will occasionally dredge back up from the depths seemingly to torment you?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With Mind 3 a mage can find out about those. Pretty easily too, if they have that much staying power.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulate Thoughts (Mental Link)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Telepathic Communication was the continuation of the communicative side of Impart Thought, this is the continuation of the manipulative side. The mage can now actively alter the targets thoughts. He can twist the thoughts that are already there or implant new ones. At this point he can actively alter a target\u2019s current motivations and goals.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Ruthlessly Leave Someone\u2019s Mind Alone</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind is very powerful, but sometimes its subtlety accomplishes even more. A clever mage may decide to leave a target\u2019s mind entirely unchanged, except for the certainty that his head has been meddled with. This can cause the target to distrust his own memories and motivations. The mage doesn\u2019t have to spend any time or effort making sure the target\u2019s new memories match the old, because there are no new memories. He can just let the target\u2019s paranoia work for him.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Illusions (Project Illusions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also manipulate minds to see and sense things that aren\u2019t there. There is no restriction or limit given for how detailed these can be, so this can be anything from small tricks of the light to full on walking dreamscapes. Notably, these only affect the targets\u2019 minds, so nothing else will see them. That\u2019s what makes them mental illusions rather than all the other kinds.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>A Toddler in Motion</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A really simple but attention-grabbing illusion is a blur of motion in peripheral vision, either beside the head or near the feet. Since it is outside the range of clear vision the illusion doesn\u2019t have to have much detail, nor does it have to stick around long.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enter and Control Dreams (Dreamwalk)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can enter another person\u2019s dreams and live them or make alterations to them. Not much detail for the power is given here. Since projection is a Mind 4 power, I think this relies more on Link Minds to function. Where the limits between those two powers are, I'm not sure.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>\u201cProphetic\u201d Nightmares (AKA Manipulate the Chosen One)</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the bread and butter of many (well, at least two, Voldemort and Sideous) dark lords. By manipulating dreams to repeatedly predict \u2018future\u2019 outcomes a mage can disorient and torment a target. At the very least he can keep them anxious and sleepless, and possibly manipulate them to take dangerous actions to prevent the false future.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind Blast (Psychic Blast)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Raise Combat Skill by +2 each turn. Some creatures may be immune to Mindblast.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wait, wrong game.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the actual Mind 3 attack. It functions like any sphere attack except that without augmentation from other spheres it is always bashing damage.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Got Yer Nose</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can shape his Mind attack to look and feel like an attack of some other kind. In this case a disfiguring or mutilating attack that convinces the target that they are now missing part of themselves. </span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>From Forces 3:<br /> <br /> Transmute Thoughts</b></span><br /> <br /> As Forces 3 indicates, Mind 3 can transmute thoughts. It isn't unreasonable that shaping and manipulating thoughts and dreams would work this way, but it isn't obvious from Mind 3 that they could be shaped into other things. Forces 3 confirms that. <hr /><br /> <b>From Common Magical Effects (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a>)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Translate Languages</b><br /> <br /> At the level a mage can fully read someone's mind he can also fully understand relevant languages. This comes in two forms. The mage can use the target's thoughts to translate anything the target is saying or writing. He can also use the knowledge of nearby people to translate anything any one of them can understand or read. The former is very helpful when the mage finds himself in a strange land, the latter when he finds himself at an archaeological dig and he wants to read the artifacts without anyone knowing he can (assuming both the presence of ancient writing and someone who can read it)<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional effects:</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here we come to one of the difficult lines:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combined with Correspondence, Forces, Matter, or Life, he is able to employ telekinesis, pyrokinetics, and psychophysical assault, influencing objects, elements, or people with the power of his mind. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I really don\u2019t like this line and I traditionally view it as a wrongheaded attempt to incorporate Mind into psychic paradigms for no reason. However, the goal of this thread is to treat the language as intentional as much as possible, so\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From the placement of the comma I am going to interpret this as telekinesis, pyrokinetics, and psychophysical assault are the examples of influencing objects, elements, or people with the power of the mind. Unlike other Spheres, Mind has to be intentional here.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pyrokinetics (??? + Transmute Forces)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026pyrokinetics\u2026 </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here I am saved by Forces 3, which already indicated that instead of using Prime to manifest something out of seemingly nowhere, a mage can take a thought and transmute it into a pattern. <u>Here it converts thoughts to fire.</u> The more I think about it, the more this seems quite reasonable, and it is refreshing that the two spheres are actually corroborating each other.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That said, this only applies to actually creating fire. Just shaping and influencing it remains Forces only. Since most examples of pyrokinetics I can think of include creating fire, that works.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Telekinesis (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> he is able to employ telekinesis </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - What is Mind doing?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The \u201ctransmuting a thought\u201d explanation doesn\u2019t work here. I mean, it does if the mage <u>really wants to create the kinetic forces from seemingly nowhere</u>, but that\u2019s not necessary as there are always kinetic forces around to redirect and amplify. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>A Mind 3 attack paired with pattern spheres so that the blast affects material things works, but only for attacks</u>, which really doesn\u2019t fit the brief. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Outside of those two, I can\u2019t think of a situation where the same supplemental spheres couldn\u2019t accomplish the same effect without Mind. If anyone has an idea, I\u2019d love to know.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your Mind Makes It Real (Psychic Blast/Project Illusions + Life Attack)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and psychophysical assault </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This at least I already have an answer for. <u>Take a mental assault or a mental illusion and pair it with a life attack so that the wounds the target feels are made real</u>. Here at least there are reasons why a mage might want to use a spell like this.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-13-2025, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T05:03:41-07:00","id":1550899,"title":"","content":"I always interpreted the lines about <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">telekinesis, pyrokinetics</span> as an Effect that bestows those abilities upon the mage or someone else.<br /> <br /> For example, if you wanted to set somebody on fire then throw that fire as a fireball and finally heat yourself a cup of tea you would need 3 Forces Effects. If you'd give yoruself pyrokinesis with Mind 3, Forces 3 you could do all that under single Effect with prolonged duration. The Mind reads here the mind of a target and Forces moves the fire according to the given instructions. Similarly with telekinesis where Correspondence moves the something according to mind's instructions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24827-terhon","name":"Terhon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T05:49:06-07:00","id":1550901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terhon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550899#post1550899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always interpreted the lines about <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">telekinesis, pyrokinetics</span> as an Effect that bestows those abilities upon the mage or someone else.<br /> <br /> For example, if you wanted to set somebody on fire then throw that fire as a fireball and finally heat yourself a cup of tea you would need 3 Forces Effects. If you'd give yoruself pyrokinesis with Mind 3, Forces 3 you could do all that under single Effect with prolonged duration. The Mind reads here the mind of a target and Forces moves the fire according to the given instructions. Similarly with telekinesis where Correspondence moves the something according to mind's instructions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about that. What about the Arete roll? You make a ritual with 5 successes and then you can blast 12 levels of damage whenever you want?<br /> <br /> My reading is that Mind is there to transmute toughts into forces, not needing Prime 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T06:00:57-07:00","id":1550902,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> I think you are also missing the Mind 3 effect of language translation, see through other eyes. And the conjunctional effects to see Avatar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T06:43:30-07:00","id":1550903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550901#post1550901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure about that. What about the Arete roll? You make a ritual with 5 successes and then you can blast 12 levels of damage whenever you want?<br /> <br /> My reading is that Mind is there to transmute toughts into forces, not needing Prime 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>System-wise I was thinking more something like Successes on Arete roll equal Success you can &quot;spend&quot; on pyrokinetic attacks. You make a ritual with 5 successes and you can blast someone with 3 success and then someone with the remaining 2.<br /> Alternatively you could get the benefit of some Numina or something else that already describes that kind of psychic power in terms of Storyteller system. <br /> <br /> Of course such Effect would need some balancing, but I just think the idea seems valid and cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24827-terhon","name":"Terhon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T11:41:23-07:00","id":1550907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550901#post1550901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure about that. What about the Arete roll? You make a ritual with 5 successes and then you can blast 12 levels of damage whenever you want?<br /> <br /> My reading is that Mind is there to transmute toughts into forces, not needing Prime 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot to pay for the effect in question, i would say tying something to your mind is worth at least 2 succeses so its frying everyone for 8 damage. Or if youre not satisfied with that you could assume the damage is equal to the successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T11:49:28-07:00","id":1550908,"title":"","content":"Given how both Mind and Spirit deal with different sorts of ressonance and emotion and memory, I've always felt a weird edge between the two. Not as much in Mage, but in other splats where not really Spheres but other power kinda mesh the two arcana together. Specially with all the ways the paradigms of humanity, how they change the world and all, comes from the mind but alter the spiritual, the Umbra. <br /> But in many ways, Spirit Sphere always felt boring in how it is limited to play with only spirits and the spirit realm, while most other Spheres can do so much or at the very least be applicable in most scenarios one way or another. Mind is an example, it can affect yourself, obtain or put info in objects and places, affect others, go to other realms...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T22:57:15-07:00","id":1550983,"title":"","content":"I've had a problem with my computer, so were off-line a few days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550738#post1550738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If I had to rescue this\u2026 well I suppose <u>Matter 5 could give steel the quality of \u201cmelting when thought at\u201d and then Mind 3 provides the psychic blast.</u> I question how often the need for this would arise, though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any thoughts?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That could be an impossible material meant to be used by other people. <b>Mind</b> in that case would be added to give the material the ability to perceive the thought process that makes it melt (or whatever it does).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T08:04:31-07:00","id":1550994,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Control Conscious Mind/ Alter Consciousness/ Astral Projection </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The fearsome power of Black Suits and psychic assailants allows the mage to command another person\u2019s actions as well as her thoughts, alter her perceptions or mental state, and project his own mind from his physical form. At this Rank, a mage can change someone\u2019s memories, drive her crazy (or sane), overlay her aura with a desired impression, and set up posthypnotic suggestions and commands. (See Social Conditioning and Reprogramming, pp. 605-607.) And by using internal rather than external powers, he can also project his astral form, as detailed in Chapter Nine, pp. 476-478.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind Control (Control Conscious Mind)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Change Mind (Alter Consciousness)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Buried Commands (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These three powers overlap significantly. When a mage controls someone does he do it by manually controlling their actions or by changing their mind so they are the type of person who would take those actions. Both are possible. I would divide them up based on whether the mage is controlling actions or just influencing how the target chooses his own. Even then, there\u2019s a lot of overlap.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Post Hypnotic suggestions are likewise a particular presentation of Change Mind.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With these powers, the mage can alter perceptions, alter mental state, alter memories, or really any part of the mind. He can control a person\u2019s actions and control whether or not they realize he is doing that. He can make it impossible for a person to think certain thoughts, or impossible for them not to.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Don\u2019t Think of an Elephant</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the awesome power of Mind 4, a mage can say \u201cdon\u2019t think of an elephant\u201d and make sure that the target successfully obeys. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Alter Perceptions </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s not clear what the difference is between the illusions of Mind 3 and full altered perceptions. One possibility suggested by the Magical Reference Charts is that mental illusions can be overcome with a willpower roll, at which point they dissipate. Altered Perceptions don\u2019t go away. Even if the target knows exactly what\u2019s happening his senses are still limited by the spell.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>The Manchurian Postulate</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 4 is capable of implanting much more varied buried commands than any spy movie could conceive of. From full changes of personality to small but important motions that no one would notice. One subtle use of this power is altering regular people to do small tasks that they are otherwise unrelated to. These could be simple things like dead drops, or they could be complex assemblies put together piece by piece by random people.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The name comes from a likely tactic of the Technocracy: influencing prominent sleepers introduce key ideas at key moments to advance the great Timeline. I\u2019m not suggesting they prime someone with the complete idea, just one part of it slipped into reports and research papers and popular media as tangents and research opportunities. These ideas, inserted at the right time and place, building a foundation that the full idea can rest on.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Project Mind (Astral Projection)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notably, this is mentioned twice, and the wording of both is about projecting the mind or the astral form, not projecting it <i>into</i> the Astral. So, while this power includes the ability to project there, the mage is not limited to only projecting there.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In fact, Mind 4 does not restrict where the mage can project to, or how far into the astral he can travel, or any limits for duration other than the normal spell rules. These limitations are found elsewhere, but not in Mind.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Mental Possession</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a combination of projection and mind control. Instead of projecting into the Astral the mage instead projects into someone else\u2019s mind and takes control. With other spheres, the mage could also project into machines, etc.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter Other Aura (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not a lot of detail is given here.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thinking about it, this is a vital corollary to implanted memories and post hypnotic suggestions in any scenario that involves mages or other supernaturals. Seeing auras can often give away that someone has been tampered with or that their motivations are not what they appear to be.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Hide Diablerie</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One useful ability that could be a reason to bring a mage into a Vampire campaign is removing the obvious signs of diablerie from a vampire\u2019s aura.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>False Positive</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage knows he\u2019s up against aura senses, he can alter a number of people or other things to emit strange aura types (or specific ones, if that is relevant) as distractions.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Elsewhere:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perceive Through a Mental Illusions (from M20 Common Magical Effects Chart)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That is, if a mage creates a mental illusion of a dragon, he can see through its eyes. I suspect that this is an application of projection. The mage is projecting into the mental illusion and thus seeing from its point of view.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T09:28:01-07:00","id":1550998,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure this is also the level where you can shield the minds of others. It's a bit high compared to other Sphere's protective effects, but makes sense to me. On Mind 1 you can control your own mind, Mind 4 offers the same for the minds of others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T10:09:15-07:00","id":1551000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550998#post1550998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure this is also the level where you can shield the minds of others. It's a bit high compared to other Sphere's protective effects, but makes sense to me. On Mind 1 you can control your own mind, Mind 4 offers the same for the minds of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind itself doesn't say, but I think it is Mind 2 from the Common Magical Effects table. Of course that table is a bit unreliable when it comes to Mind, so I don't want to put it in until I'm sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T14:20:18-07:00","id":1551007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550994#post1550994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Alter Perceptions </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s not clear what the difference is between the illusions of Mind 3 and full altered perceptions. One possibility suggested by the Magical Reference Charts is that mental illusions can be overcome with a willpower roll, at which point they dissipate. Altered Perceptions don\u2019t go away. Even if the target knows exactly what\u2019s happening his senses are still limited by the spell.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is, effectively, the difference even if the implications are more profound than the mechanics would encapsulate. Someone suffering from synesthesia is not seeing an illusion, they are receiving the same exact sensory information as anyone else, but their brains/minds interpret this data using unusual pathways. While this can have negative impacts on interacting with other people and in a world designed for people that perceive differently from them, people with long term synesthesia have just as a coherent and sensible impression of the world around them as people with more average sensory perceptions.<br /> <br /> Not to delve back into the Life/Mind issues, but using Life to turn off someone's cone cells so they can only see in black &amp; white isn't an illusion. Using Mind to alter perceptions to the same effect shouldn't be considered an illusion either.<br /> <br /> We can also go deeper into the fact that humans don't perceive reality directly; that our minds construct a model of the world around us that is mostly accurate but has gaps due to a number of factors; including various mental shortcuts we take to expedite the process. Almost every person is walking around perceiving the world with some level of paraidolia and anthropomorphism (and the two frequently combine to skew our perceptions of objects in our environment). It's certainly within Mind 4's purview to ramp these mental shortcuts up drastically in an individual, and because it's already part of how people perceive the world, it only takes altering perceptions instead of altering consciousness.<br /> <br /> There's a near endless amount of existing gaps between human perception and reality that a mage with the right understanding could use to performing illusion-like effects that simply aren't illusions. If you consider that everything you visually see as &quot;now&quot; is in fact an interpolation of the short term past projected into the future (which helps make up for the giant blind spot in our eyes due to the optic nerve issue), what we see can be tricked without illusion if you can manipulate that interpolation process. You can do this to a small extent without magic: you can find the blind spot in your vision and put an object there which you will see a &quot;hole&quot; in because your mind is still using past data of what was behind the object to fill in the blind spot. Mind 4 doesn't need to create illusions if it can just change the parameters your mind uses to interpret data in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T15:52:47-07:00","id":1551010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terhon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1550903#post1550903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> System-wise I was thinking more something like Successes on Arete roll equal Success you can &quot;spend&quot; on pyrokinetic attacks. You make a ritual with 5 successes and you can blast someone with 3 success and then someone with the remaining 2.<br /> Alternatively you could get the benefit of some Numina or something else that already describes that kind of psychic power in terms of Storyteller system.<br /> <br /> Of course such Effect would need some balancing, but I just think the idea seems valid and cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh ok. Yeah that could work.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> , that's the optional dividing successes rule. Default rule just turns successes into damage directly, so 5 successes with Forces translates into 12 damage. But I can see that working as Terhon posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T12:07:13-07:00","id":1551018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551010#post1551010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh ok. Yeah that could work.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> , that's the optional dividing successes rule. Default rule just turns successes into damage directly, so 5 successes with Forces translates into 12 damage. But I can see that working as Terhon posted.</div> </div> </div> </div>If were not using that rule then it is impossible as spells either do damage or have a duration. Therefore the only way it would hapen is when using dividing successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T12:13:49-07:00","id":1551019,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Control Subconscious/ Forge Psyche/ Untether Consciousness </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A true Mind Master commands not only his own conscious mind but other minds as well. He may alter someone\u2019s mind forever, raising (or lowering) her Traits, rewriting her personality, changing her Nature Trait, or (with Life 4) switching her mind into another body. He can do the same things to his own mind as well, and he can untether that mind to explore the deeper reaches of astral space for hours or even days at a time. His greatest power, though, is the ability to fabricate entire consciousnesses, creating minds where no mind had been before.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have to say, I really don\u2019t like how Mind 5 is written. The very first line is probably meant for dramatic flair, but it could also be interpreted as saying earlier ranks of Mind were capable of more self-manipulation than shown, or that they were less capable of manipulating others than they said.<br /> <br /> In any case:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter Anything Mental (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is essentially the transmutation level for minds themselves. A Mind master can completely shape and mold a mind into whatever he wants. No part of the mind is off limits and nothing has to be done step by step. This, importantly, includes more mechanical elements like stats and Nature. Possibly Nature could have been sculpted the way personality was by Mind 4, but here it can be swapped out like a pair of shoes.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Uplift</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can take the mind of an animal, such as a cat, and raise it to sapience. He could even put it into a human or humanoid body (With Life of some rank, see later discussion), or use similar ranks of Life to just uplift the body too.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Fake Uplift</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can also just shape a human mind into the exact same kind of mind that he would create with the previous method, such that the target thought he was always an uplifted cat rather than whatever poor soul the mage targeted.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Forge Persona</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can give himself or others a different public face customized for a situation, complete with behaviors, mannerisms, and attitudes. This is not another identity like in DID (though presumably a Mind master could make one of those too), this is a role the target can slip into, the kind he might make for himself over time to deal with a situation. The advantage here is it can be made instantly and for situations the target has no familiarity with..</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Lower Willpower</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Mind 5 can raise and lower stats, then a smart mage will start off any major mind surgery by lowering the willpower of his target, thus reducing the difficulty of any future changes.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent Changes (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the third or fourth sphere that puts permanent changes behind rank 5. As always, it is unclear the meaning, and as in the previous cases I\u2019ll interpret this as the possibility of a permanent change rather than a permanent ongoing spell.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Mind (Forge Psyche)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition to being able to shape a mind into whatever he wants, a Mind master can also create one out of whole cloth. Unlike other creation spells, there is no indication that Prime is needed. Possibly this is an oversight, but it doesn\u2019t really matter. As we\u2019ve seen elsewhere, instead of fueling a pattern with quintessence a mage can instead use Mind 3 to transform a thought into a pattern. There\u2019s really no reason a Mind master would ever need to incorporate Prime since he already has access to Mind 3.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note: I don\u2019t see a limit that a mind has to have a body. I don\u2019t know where said mind would exist, but it may be possible.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a quite sad power if the mage doesn\u2019t make it permanent.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Boltzmann AI</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A rather mean power. The mage creates a temporary intelligence with a goal and a short amount of time to achieve that goal before dissolving. Other spheres will likely be needed if the goal is for the mind to do more than think.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Obliterate Mind</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage may also completely erase someone\u2019s mind, destroying their identity entirely. While there is reason to think the Avatar may complicate matters, it would seem to be possible with what is written here.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Untether Consciousness (Untether Consciousness)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Who is the target?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s a syntax oddity here. The second sentence lists off five things the mage can do to someone else. The third then says he can do those five things to his own mind as well, then \u2018untether <i>that</i> mind\u2026\u2019 which should refer to his own mind. Contextually, though, it has to be referring to whatever mind is the target. So, the first thing this power does is extend Project Mind to other targets.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apparently, it is also supposed to be a more powerful version of Project Mind, defined as being able to reach the deeper parts of astral space for hours or days. However, Project Mind was never given a limit on how far or long it can project unless we look to the Otherworlds section. Within the Mind section, the only actual improvement is who can be targeted.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the Otherworlds section is not part of this thread, but it does give some shaky insight. While the section is sometimes unreliable on spheres, it does indicate that Mind 5 is needed to pass the Horizon during Astral Travel. That gives a possible resolution: that Mind 5 isn\u2019t allowing further travel, it is piercing a specific barrier or shielding the mage so he can withstand more hostile areas.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Mind 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. Unless the ST specifically wants something locked behind archspheres, it should be possible here. Impossible minds might even be possible at this rank, though the only example I've been able to come up with is a mind which can fully contain/simulate itself. I'm not sure that's a good (or reasonable) example, though, so I'm not putting it forward as an application.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From elsewhere:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sever the Silver Cord</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is a Mind 5 attack to sever the silver cord that connects an astral traveler to their body. Presumably this is another aspect of Untether Consciousness otherwise it would make more sense as a Mind 3 attack.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Conjunctional Effects:</b><br /> \u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swap Minds (Untether Consciousness?)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is strangely written, and it gets stranger the more I think about it. Firstly, this has to be some application of Untether Consciousness. While an equivalent to this effect could also be done by transforming mind A to mind B and vice versa, that wouldn\u2019t need Life. However, even with an actual swap, this doesn\u2019t make a lot of sense as Life 4. Grafting techniques are usually some form of transmutation, and Transmute Other Complex Lifeform is Life 5. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We could say that minds want to be connected to bodies, so it just takes a nudge to get the process going but that\u2019s not clearly indicated in the text. This is part of a larger discussion of creation and resurrection, so I think I\u2019ll return here after Spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T12:32:02-07:00","id":1551022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551019#post1551019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Lower Willpower</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Mind 5 can raise and lower stats, then a smart mage will start off any major mind surgery by lowering the willpower of his target, thus reducing the difficulty of any future changes.</span> <hr /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Nowhere in the game does it say you can lower someones willpower. Its like saying you can lower someones arete rating.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1547490-am-i-missing-something-about-the-sluagh?p=1551020#post1551020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent Changes (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the third or fourth sphere that puts permanent changes behind rank 5. As always, it is unclear the meaning, and as in the previous cases I\u2019ll interpret this as the possibility of a permanent change rather than a permanent ongoing spell.</span><br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> Maybe permament effects are ment to be behind 5 paywall or it means you no longer need the double successes.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T12:52:10-07:00","id":1551023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551022#post1551022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in the game does it say you can lower someones willpower. Its like saying you can lower someones arete rating.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Willpower is at least arguably a property of the mind, while Arete is something much more metaphysical. Also mages can alter someone's Arete rating, though only through the brute force method of Gilgul. <br /> <br /> I'm not set on the idea that a mage can lower someone's Willpower, but it would take a compelling argument to say it is out of the reach of Mind 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T13:33:09-07:00","id":1551024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551023#post1551023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that Willpower is at least arguably a property of the mind, while Arete is something much more metaphysical. Also mages can alter someone's Arete rating, though only through the brute force method of Gilgul.<br /> <br /> I'm not set on the idea that a mage can lower someone's Willpower, but it would take a compelling argument to say it is out of the reach of Mind 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that willpower is tied to magic in game (minimum is 5 for a mage). If magic is willworking then willpower is tied to Arete and the Avatar. Also no the burden of proof is on you to show that willpower can be modified (by Mind 5 or anything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T14:19:32-07:00","id":1551025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551024#post1551024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would argue that willpower is tied to magic in game (minimum is 5 for a mage). If magic is willworking then willpower is tied to Arete and the Avatar. Also no the burden of proof is on you to show that willpower can be modified (by Mind 5 or anything).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't play burden of proof games. We can discuss why it should or should not be modifiable, but there is no &quot;I'm right unless you can prove otherwise.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's certainly a connection with magic, but does that connection mean that Willpower is a metaphysical aspect of the game linked to the Avatar? Or is it just that Willpower is a more natural function of the mind that happens to be important in magic? Given that everyone has willpower, including things that don't have avatars, and given that willpower has applications outside of magic, I'm inclined to think the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T14:21:30-07:00","id":1551026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551025#post1551025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't play burden of proof games. We can discuss why it should or should not be modifiable, but there is no &quot;I'm right unless you can prove otherwise.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's certainly a connection with magic, but does that connection mean that Willpower is a metaphysical aspect of the game linked to the Avatar? Or is it just that Willpower is a more natural function of the mind that happens to be important in magic? Given that everyone has willpower, including things that don't have avatars, and given that willpower has applications outside of magic, I'm inclined to think the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no power in the whole WOD that can lower someones willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T14:43:04-07:00","id":1551027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551026#post1551026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no power in the whole WOD that can lower someones willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Losing a familiar costs permanent willpower. Botching a willpower roll to resist Mind magic can lower permanent willpower. Intense shock, prolonged physical or emotional agony, and &quot;Horror Beyond Madness&quot; can destroy permanent Willpower. Disastrous seekings can take away permanent willpower. Quiets can take away permanent willpower. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T15:00:47-07:00","id":1551028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551027#post1551027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Losing a familiar costs permanent willpower. Botching a willpower roll to resist Mind magic can lower permanent willpower. Intense shock, prolonged physical or emotional agony, and &quot;Horror Beyond Madness&quot; can destroy permanent Willpower. Disastrous seekings can take away permanent willpower. Quiets can take away permanent willpower. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again there is no described power in the entire WOD: Wraith, Vampire, Changeling, Mage, Werewolf, Hunter, Mumy, Demon that alows you to lower someone elses willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T17:22:11-07:00","id":1551030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551018#post1551018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If were not using that rule then it is impossible as spells either do damage or have a duration. Therefore the only way it would hapen is when using dividing successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, I always thought it weird that the rule on dividing successes is optional. How do you even build most magical effects without dividing successes in some way?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551026#post1551026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no power in the whole WOD that can lower someones willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>That hardly means it should be beyond Sphere Magic. In fact, it doesn't even means such powers are impossible, just that they haven't been thought out yet.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely convinced yet either, but the rationale is solid. If <i>Willpower</i> isn't <b>Mind</b>, what else would it be? And why should it be protected from tampering when nothing else is?<br /> <br /> Specially Attributes, which are far more important and expensive character traits than <i>Willpower</i>, yet a <b>Mind</b> mage can change then from the get go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T18:54:20-07:00","id":1551032,"title":"","content":"Most effects don't deal damage, and have binary effects, so they just fall under the Feats of Magic success requirements. After that, most of the remaining effects are going to benefit from extra duration and not actually deal damage... and most of the time when you'd want both damage and duration... there's a sensible reason not to allow you to boost both at the same time.<br /> <br /> As for Willpower... the problem is that the games are very circumspect about what Willpower actually is. It's not actually true that there's no way to reduce Willpower in the games - though the vast majority of times you can force people to lose points instead of dots, and even more ways to mess with Willpower rolls with bonus/penalty dice/difficulties - but their tends to be a treatment of Willpower as something that isn't just a function of having a strong mind. Now, the level of changes in Mind include lots of other things like Nature too, so that would certainly lean on the side of Mind being able to adjust Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T19:01:20-07:00","id":1551033,"title":"","content":"The Mind 5 write-up itself either operates on some significant assumptions or its supposed to describe a naturalistic account of the environment, kind of like how Spirit 5 went with Gilgul. Some paradigms wouldn't work with it. In regards to destroying minds, it seem like the write-up indicates that it is personality, memory, and behavioral patterns that are annihilated rather than self-awareness. There is no indication that a being with a destroyed mind goes into vegetative state. Honestly that itself feels like it would require Life to mess with the central nervous system such that the organic processes of cognition cease, or else a consciousness would just appear in the system even if the previous one was annihilated. And that's not even counting the additional ontological questions raised by the body still having the same Avatar and all of that. RAW, it seems like there are two options; either the being has their personality wiped but they retain the same stream of awareness, or their consciousness is annihilated entirely and any new minds that come into the vacant body are ontologically distinct persons from the original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T05:24:51-07:00","id":1551036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551018#post1551018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If were not using that rule then it is impossible as spells either do damage or have a duration. Therefore the only way it would hapen is when using dividing successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. However, the optional rule is kinda loose. There are examples of it not needing to meet base successes with DoT spells and simply Divides the successes into damage and time. I believe that's also how revised worked and that M20 optional dividing successes rule was just written wrong and never corrected. You don't need to neet the base *and* spend successes into damage and time\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> About the Willpower reduce thing, I kinda agree with Quelsec. From a mechanical pov, reducing willpower shouldn't be easy at all and I bet that if there was a rote out there that did it, it wouldn't be Mind 5 alone. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I really dislike the idea that mages can't do something. With the right spheres and enough successes, there should be no limits.<br /> <br /> So, maybe reducing willpower from a mortal (sleeper) eould be just Mind 5, while reducing from a Night folk would require a combination of Mind and Prime to reflect their supernatural nature and how their willpower is directly tied to their powers? As Quelsec said, mages need 5 WP, other night folks also have an initial WP set and use it for a lot of their powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T07:16:51-07:00","id":1551040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551028#post1551028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And again there is no described power in the entire WOD: Wraith, Vampire, Changeling, Mage, Werewolf, Hunter, Mumy, Demon that alows you to lower someone elses willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll continue then. From Wraith:<br /> <br /> I'll set aside the numerous Arcanoi that wraiths can spend permanent Willpower on and focus on two outside influences that can definitely lower permanent willpower.<br /> <br /> Spectres in the grip of Rapacity may attack a target's permanent willpower in a contested willpower roll. Each extra success reduces permanent willpower by 1. A mortal who drops to 0 permanent willpower literally dies of fright. <br /> <br /> The drug Pigment temporarily halves the user's permanent willpower.<br /> <br /> Given the nature of both, there's a case to be made that Willpower has more to do with Spirit than Mind (although the counterpoint is that Wraith is much more likely to describe things in terms of the spiritual than the mental). Whatever the case, there are two more things that can lower someone else's permanent willpower.<br /> <br /> Someone else can check the other books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T09:25:47-07:00","id":1551043,"title":"","content":"If there is something that is unprecedented in Storyteller rules then there is no better place for it to be than a level 5 Sphere.<br /> <br /> Specially since a hard-coded game that tries to be systematical as possible already exist in Pathfinder and Chronicles of Darkness in many ways. Mage Ascencion is more gun-ho, for good and bad, so limiting effects and possibilites of the top-most powerful magic available in the game goes agains the ethos of the game.<br /> <br /> Rules are supposed to give base and arbitration to the setting and the game itself. They got to give players a way to take part and also become the setting, incorporating its meaning, simulating its themes and tones. If Mage was supposed to be a very limiting, tricks only, tight-packed McGiver procure on site style game, than the rules are doing a bad job of it. The ruleset gotta respect the principles behind the setting as much as the design in an rpg like WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T10:48:07-07:00","id":1551044,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's of much use to look at other powers to determine whether Mind can alter Permanent Willpower or not; it's also more interesting to figure out whether Willpower is a function of mind or soul.<br /> <br /> It might help to split the question into Permanent Willpower and Temporary Willpower, because the former is often used as a type of 'spiritual fortitude' while the latter is used for concrete feats of will. I think I tend towards classifying Permanent Willpower as something closer tied to the identity of a person (like Arete) that isn't alterable with Mind alone - maybe as a combination effect, the kind that will change the inherent Nature of something.<br /> <br /> Temporary Willpower on the other hand? Sure. You could say Temp WP is the active expression of the potential (Perm WP) realized through a function of Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T11:11:08-07:00","id":1551045,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Prime</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview: </b>Quintessence and the Essence of all Things</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Those who use a lot of Prime tend to leave strong imprints on their resonances. This may not even be a rule so much as a roleplaying suggestion.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T11:28:22-07:00","id":1551046,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Etheric Senses/ Consecration/ Infuse Personal Quintessence </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A beginning study of Prime allows the mage to perceive and channel Quintessence from Nodes, Tass, Wonders, and magickal Effects. She may spot energetic ebbs and flows, can sense and at least try to read Resonance and Synergy signatures, and could also absorb Quintessence into her personal Pattern. Mages without at least one dot in Prime cannot absorb Quintessence beyond their Avatar Background rating. A Prime-skilled mage, however, may do so.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When infusing her Quintessence into an object, that mage may also consecrate the object with her personal energy. When she shapeshifts, steps sideways, or otherwise alters her Pattern\u2019s metaphysical nature, that consecrated object will then change with her. In the process, it also picks up her personal Resonance\u2026 which, because it both identifies her and becomes essentially connected to her, is not always a good thing.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime is another of the spheres that gets a lot of non sensory abilities at rank 1. Indeed, some of them aren't even spell abilities.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perceive Quintessence (Etheric Senses)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can sense quintessence in nodes, as well as particularly notable (energetic) flows of it in other areas. The greatest use of this is sensing Tass, Wonders, and magical spells. He can also sense the presence of resonance and synergy and with more successes actually read it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sense Vampires and Disciplines</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vampire blood is, if I recall correctly, sometimes described as a form of Tass. Between that and the ability to sense resonance and synergy, Prime 1 should be able to sense vampires and even the use of Disciplines.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>The Stink of Consecration</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since Consecration imparts resonance to the consecrated thing, Prime 1 can both determine that an item is consecrated and (if he\u2019s familiar with the resonance) who it is consecrated to.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>See Magic</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can see the threads of quintessence that go into weaving a spell. This won\u2019t let him identify the spell, but he can tell it is being cast and likely some information on where.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is worth noting that in Revised, this wasn\u2019t even a spell, it was an ability inherent to learning Prime 1, much like holding more than your Avatar rating in quintessence. That is not present here, though.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beginning Quintessence Channeling (Infuse Personal Quintessence)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Prime 1 a mage can channel the essence from a Node and Tass into his own pattern.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution \u2013 Channeling Spells?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For reasons I am not quite sure of, perception and channeling were combined into one list, which as written means that a mage can channel any quintessence he can sense. For instance he could channel the quintessence from wonders and spells into his own pattern. That\u2019s probably not intentional, at least not directly, as spells don\u2019t have a set pool of quintessence points associated with them</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Possibly channeling the quintessence in spells is the basis for the optional unweaving rules.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anyways, I really can\u2019t come up with an application that doesn\u2019t just restate channeling quintessence from a node or tass Any thoughts?.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Expand Quintessence Pool (Infuse Personal Quintessence)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is less an ability and more an augment that comes with knowing Prime 1. A mage is no longer limited to his Avatar rating for his quintessence pool.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Consecration (Consecration)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can infuse his quintessence into an object connecting it to himself in a metaphysical way. The object picks up his resonance and will change with him when he changes and stay with him when he . Shapeshifting and stepping sideways are specifically called out as uses for Consecration, but they are not exclusive. No special rules for duration, cost, or other spheres are given so standard rules apply.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As written, this doesn\u2019t take additional spheres, even if the Prime 2 version to Consecrate Life does.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Yoink</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is not stated that consecrated items have to be on a mage\u2019s person when he changes in order to change with him. There are a few clever applications for giving an item over to a person then changing it on them when they aren\u2019t expecting it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Consecrate Energy</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Much like in Entropy the place of energy in this power is uncertain. Likely a mage can consecrate an energy pattern, it just has to be one that would stick around like an everburning fire or a ball of light or some other magical effect.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T13:08:52-07:00","id":1551048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551046#post1551046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution \u2013 Channeling Spells?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For reasons I am not quite sure of, perception and channeling were combined into one list, which as written means that a mage can channel any quintessence he can sense. For instance he could channel the quintessence from wonders and spells into his own pattern. That\u2019s probably not intentional, at least not directly, as spells don\u2019t have a set pool of quintessence points associated with them</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Possibly channeling the quintessence in spells is the basis for the optional unweaving rules.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anyways, I really can\u2019t come up with an application that doesn\u2019t just restate channeling quintessence from a node or tass Any thoughts?.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought would be exactly what you said, just not only unweaving but countermagick as well as it doea require Prime, iirc. <br /> <br /> Although, it would be cool if Prime had more of a &quot;metamagick&quot; feeling as many players seem to grant this title to the sphere. Maybe channeling quintessence in spells means changing things about them like duration, damage or even taking control of the spell. Certainly, that would require more than rank 1.<br /> <br /> About the consecration, it's inportaimportant to note that the mage is infusing his own personal Resonance into the object, making it as it was a very part of the mage himself. This could potentially grant some advantages, like affecting the object when using spells on yourself, locking them with Life and also granting the bonus of a personal instrument, if it is used that way. <br /> <br /> The downside is that this object is a direct link to your pattern, which means that anyone in possession of it could use Correspondence at the lowest difficulty to affect you. So it *is* very risky.<br /> <br /> One last note, it seems you can consecrate and de-consecrate as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T21:47:39-07:00","id":1551058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551044#post1551044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's of much use to look at other powers to determine whether Mind can alter Permanent Willpower or not; it's also more interesting to figure out whether Willpower is a function of mind or soul.<br /> <br /> It might help to split the question into Permanent Willpower and Temporary Willpower, because the former is often used as a type of 'spiritual fortitude' while the latter is used for concrete feats of will. I think I tend towards classifying Permanent Willpower as something closer tied to the identity of a person (like Arete) that isn't alterable with Mind alone - maybe as a combination effect, the kind that will change the inherent Nature of something.<br /> <br /> Temporary Willpower on the other hand? Sure. You could say Temp WP is the active expression of the potential (Perm WP) realized through a function of Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the case for altering Willpower being a combination of <b>Mind</b> and <b>Spirit</b> is a stronger one than not being affected at all.<br /> <br /> On <b>Prime 1</b>, I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a>, including about it being interesting to use it as a &quot;metamagic&quot; Sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T08:14:43-07:00","id":1551065,"title":"","content":"Prime 1, in particular, has quite the metamagic vibe. If you count how Revised describes it, it has potentially three non spell abilities: quintessence absorption beyond Avatar rating, advanced countermagic, and sensing the casting of spells. So I would be quite interested in other metamagic abilities at other levels.<br /> <br /> I go back and forth on Willpower. On the one hand, many of the classic ways of losing Willpower are quite psychological, and in particular the possibility of losing Permanent Willpower when botching while resisting Mind magic is a strong indicator. On the other hand Wraith has very spiritual ways of damaging permanent Willpower.<br /> <br /> My initial thought of how I would handle this as an ST is that temporarily lowering Permanent Willpower requires a combined Mind/Spirit attack, both at rank 3. To make that permanent, either Mind or Prime has to be at 5 (since Rank 5 seems to be the permanency rank). That might seem low, but against a mage that's normally a mimimum difficulty of 8, and if it is anything like the Spectre ability it is a contested roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T08:27:50-07:00","id":1551066,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Fuel Pattern/ Construct Patterns/ Enchant Patterns/ Body of Light </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attaining a degree of control over Prime energies, the mage may divert Quintessence into new or existing forms. Combined with other Spheres, this allows that mage to create new Forces, Life, or Matter Patterns (conjuring them from thin air), and to infuse existing items with Primal Force to strengthen them or enhance their protective or destructive power.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weapons or attacks infused with Quintessence through Prime 2 Effects may hurt spirits or inflict aggravated damage, and substances infused the same way may protect against such harm. (See Chapter Nine\u2019s Combat section for details.) On a related note, she may also \u2013 with Life 2 for simple organisms, or Life 3 for complex ones \u2013 consecrate a living thing at this Rank, as if that life-form were an object described above.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Through similar applications of energy, the mage can also conjure a simple Body of Light: an idealized self projected from ephemeral energy. Although this Body of Light has no substance or special properties (unlike the astral form described in Chapter Nine, p. 477), it presents a glowing holograph of the mage herself.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It begins. Prime takes this odd stance that working on living things should be harder than working on other patterns. So much harder that it takes both an additional rank and the Life sphere. This is a break from Revised, but it is what is stated in 20th. Unfortunately, Prime is very bad about what ranks of Life are needed.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fuel Pattern (Fuel Pattern)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The bread and butter of Prime 2. This is the power that pairs with Transmutation effects to create patterns from nothing.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enchant Objects (Enchant Patterns) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can also channel quintessence into objects to improve them in some metaphysical way. Improved weapons can hurt spirits and inflict aggravated damage. Other things improved in this way can instead soak aggravated damage and spirit attacks.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Nerf Brand Spirit Herder</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The normal way enchanting works is upgrading bashing or lethal damage to aggravated, but another possible use is upgrading a seemingly harmless weapon like, say, a Nerf gun, into something that does small amounts of damage to spirits and ghosts. </span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Body of Light (Body of Light)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can use Prime 2 to project a hologram like replica of his body. M20 is not as clear as previous editions about what this is supposed to be used for. There are, however, a few places in M20 that use this as the base for other effects, most prominently as a basis for a more robust astral form than normal projection. Note that as written this only lets a mage make a projection of themeselves, which is a break from previous editions. Given that this is seemingly the basis for some illusion spells, though, this likely isn't an intended restriction.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Alibi</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depending on what the Body of Light looks like, a mage could use one to appear to be in a different place than he actually is.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Remote Avatar</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m pulling this from Revised, but there\u2019s nothing in M20 that indicates it doesn\u2019t work here. The Body of Light can be the foundation for a material form made with appropriate Pattern Spheres. He can then project into this form (with Mind) which lets him physically act in a different place than he is.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Effects?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Consecrate Living Thing (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Where Are These Life Rules Coming From</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is perhaps the strangest requirement in these Sphere descriptions. With Prime 2 a mage can now consecrate living things much like he could consecrate objects, except\u2026 Prime 2 can\u2019t do this on its own, it needs Life as well. Now, that\u2019s a clunky, clunky way of handling this, but it isn\u2019t a contradiction.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The contradiction is the requirement of Life 2 for simple creatures and Life 3 for complex, which is not the usual progression for Life. The usual would be 2/4 for Alter Simple/Complex, and that\u2019s likely what is supposed to be here. The only Life ability that has a 2/3 progression is healing, and consecration would be a rather sketchy use of healing.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Widen Spell Targets</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Consecration allows metaphysical alterations like shapechanging, stepping sideways, and arguably teleportation and time travel, to work on people at ranks they would ordinarily not be available on. This bypasses restrictions on how many people can be brought across the gauntlet and allows shape changing at lower ranks of life.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It may be that this was the consideration that led to Prime 2 needing Life 2+ to consecrate living things.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Elsewhere in M20</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animate Corpse (from Common Magical Effects)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Somehow Prime 2 has the ability to animate the remains of living things. It takes Life 2 or Matter 2 depending on the nature of the remains. It\u2019s not clear what Prime is doing here or what the supplemental spheres are doing for that matter. My best guess is that this is a Body of Light locked to the parts, though that would mean that a Body of Light can be programmed to act in certain ways. It would also mean that Prime 2 can animate just about anything with Life 2, Matter 2, or Forces 2. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T08:29:12-07:00","id":1551067,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I just realized, enchanting energy to hurt spirits would be quite effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T10:15:17-07:00","id":1551072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551065#post1551065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial thought of how I would handle this as an ST is that temporarily lowering Permanent Willpower requires a combined Mind/Spirit attack, both at rank 3. To make that permanent, either Mind or Prime has to be at 5 (since Rank 5 seems to be the permanency rank). That might seem low, but against a mage that's normally a mimimum difficulty of 8, and if it is anything like the Spectre ability it is a contested roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll personally steal and apply this ruling. And it would be hard against Mages and Nightfolk in general, as it would be resisted, high-difficulty and prone to countermagic. I usually give Nightfolk some sort of countermagic, and I'm yet to see a PC in my groups with Willpower below 5. For NPCs, being weak against such an attack isn't particularly a problem.<br /> <br /> On <b>Prime 2...</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>Body of Light</b></i> is quite a handful. It's a very strange power for <b>Prime</b> without added assumptions, but seems quite interesting when we do add such assumptions.<br /> <br /> As an illusion I would liken it to the Shadow illusions of D&amp;D: something imbued with semi-real properties. Without that it seems out of place in <b>Prime</b>, something better handled by <b>Forces</b>.<br /> <br /> My guess is that a <i><b>Body of Light</b></i> has at least the properties you stated, being an avatar of sorts and being programmable. Also, you can cast spells from it, even if this is a bit awkward if you don't have <b>Mind </b>or <b>Correspondence</b> to perceive what you're doing.<br /> <br /> What about programming it to use Magic? Would that be possible?<br /> <br /> Finally, I'm unsure if <b><i>Consecrate Living Thing</i></b> should require <b>Life</b>, but if it does I'd accept at face value the ruling of 2/3 instead of the usual 2/4. The consecration comes primarily from <b>Prime</b>, it makes some sense that <b>Life</b> <b>3</b> would be enough. My impression is that they put <b>Life</b> in it because consecrating characters and companions sounds too useful. I can't playtest it, though, because in my current Mage game the PC with <b>Prime</b> is also the one with <b>Life</b> anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T10:46:14-07:00","id":1551074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551040#post1551040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the nature of both, there's a case to be made that Willpower has more to do with Spirit than Mind (although the counterpoint is that Wraith is much more likely to describe things in terms of the spiritual than the mental). Whatever the case, there are two more things that can lower someone else's permanent willpower.<br /> <br /> Someone else can check the other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be of interest that in MotA restoring temporary Willpower it's one of the functions of ArchMind. This is described as &quot;refresh Willpower <b>fortifying his mental Pattern</b>&quot;. This requires expenditure of Quintessence, but I don't think this is a call-out to other Spheres, it could also be as how Life requires Quint to heal Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> On the opposite end, a counter-argument for Willpower being ruled by Spirit it's that beings with the Souless Defect can have Willpower ... Now, agreed that Mage it's iffy with the whole spiritual side of humans, calling the Avatar <i>soul </i>albeit one would think there should be more to it ... but Hit Marks are robots, created w/o Spirit AFAIK, and they have Willpower. Now, one could say this is just for the purpose of mechanics, but (unless they changed something in the new Guide to the Technocracy) there aren't any rules about such construct players not having Willpower. And I couldn't find any on Gods &amp; Monsters, if anything they're even more vague on the subject of how willfull are intelligent constructs.<br /> <br /> Overall, it does seem to me that Willpower it's more Mind than Spirit.<br /> <br /> Of course, this whole subject is quite unexplored, but I haven't found proof of it being the other way. <hr /><br /> Interestingly, on the subject that combines Spirit and Mind 5, ArchMind does some stuff that should absolutely be coupled with Spirit for the rules to make any sense - but that should arguably be possible at these levels with both spheres: <i>Interacting with the &quot;mind&quot; of an Avatar</i>. In concrete, this allows to access the Backgrounds of Past Lives and Dream, that are, if I understand correctly, function of what information your Avatar reveals to you trough different means (Past Lives it's accessing memories of previous holders of the Avatar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-16-2025, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T12:30:41-07:00","id":1551077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551074#post1551074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may be of interest that in MotA restoring temporary Willpower it's one of the functions of ArchMind. This is described as &quot;refresh Willpower <b>fortifying his mental Pattern</b>&quot;. This requires expenditure of Quintessence, but I don't think this is a call-out to other Spheres, it could also be as how Life requires Quint to heal Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> On the opposite end, a counter-argument for Willpower being ruled by Spirit it's that beings with the Souless Defect can have Willpower ... Now, agreed that Mage it's iffy with the whole spiritual side of humans, calling the Avatar <i>soul </i>albeit one would think there should be more to it ... but Hit Marks are robots, created w/o Spirit AFAIK, and they have Willpower. Now, one could say this is just for the purpose of mechanics, but (unless they changed something in the new Guide to the Technocracy) there aren't any rules about such construct players not having Willpower. And I couldn't find any on Gods &amp; Monsters, if anything they're even more vague on the subject of how willfull are intelligent constructs.<br /> <br /> Overall, it does seem to me that Willpower it's more Mind than Spirit.<br /> <br /> Of course, this whole subject is quite unexplored, but I haven't found proof of it being the other way. <hr /><br /> Interestingly, on the subject that combines Spirit and Mind 5, ArchMind does some stuff that should absolutely be coupled with Spirit for the rules to make any sense - but that should arguably be possible at these levels with both spheres: <i>Interacting with the &quot;mind&quot; of an Avatar</i>. In concrete, this allows to access the Backgrounds of Past Lives and Dream, that are, if I understand correctly, function of what information your Avatar reveals to you trough different means (Past Lives it's accessing memories of previous holders of the Avatar).</div> </div> </div> </div>As written I don't think that Past Lives is necessarily coupled with the Avatar. The description made it sound like it was intended to be an all purpose &quot;memories of another life&quot; background, for which you could slot in things like reincarnation memories, gifted memories of other people's lifetimes, Avatar memories, etc. By RAW I don't think it has to be connected to the Avatar at all. Same thing goes for Dream, it sounded like it was supposed to represent general universal communions of all sorts and not just specifically Avatar-mediated ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T12:37:38-07:00","id":1551079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551066#post1551066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enchant Objects (Enchant Patterns) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can also channel quintessence into objects to improve them in some metaphysical way. Improved weapons can hurt spirits and inflict aggravated damage. Other things improved in this way can instead soak aggravated damage and spirit attacks.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, there is a text in M20 with an example of Prime reinforcing a device that isn't about soaking/damaging. Like, making a machine just run better. I don't know exactly how this would translate into game mechanics, though, but it seems very useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Body of Light (Body of Light)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can use Prime 2 to project a hologram like replica of his body. M20 is not as clear as previous editions about what this is supposed to be used for. There are, however, a few places in M20 that use this as the base for other effects, most prominently as a basis for a more robust astral form than normal projection. Note that as written this only lets a mage make a projection of themeselves, which is a break from previous editions. Given that this is seemingly the basis for some illusion spells, though, this likely isn't an intended restriction.</span>[/quote]<br /> <br /> I never understood exactly what this power is for, and being just a body to use when in the Umbra seems very lame to me. Your examples of using as an &quot;avatar&quot; (a body being controlled) doesn't make much sense if Correspondence is required..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551066#post1551066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Widen Spell Targets</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Consecration allows metaphysical alterations like shapechanging, stepping sideways, and arguably teleportation and time travel, to work on people at ranks they would ordinarily not be available on. This bypasses restrictions on how many people can be brought across the gauntlet and allows shape changing at lower ranks of life.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It may be that this was the consideration that led to Prime 2 needing Life 2+ to consecrate living things.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That is very interesting. I wonder if the cons of consecration would also apply with living beings, like using them as a link for the mage. But then, they could probably be used already, since the mage can't consecrate someone that he didn't ever meet. Consecrating would just make it a bit easier for Correspondence attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551066#post1551066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Elsewhere in M20</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animate Corpse (from Common Magical Effects)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Somehow Prime 2 has the ability to animate the remains of living things. It takes Life 2 or Matter 2 depending on the nature of the remains. It\u2019s not clear what Prime is doing here or what the supplemental spheres are doing for that matter. My best guess is that this is a Body of Light locked to the parts, though that would mean that a Body of Light can be programmed to act in certain ways. It would also mean that Prime 2 can animate just about anything with Life 2, Matter 2, or Forces 2. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Prime is the animating force. This also appears in hdydt. Matter2/Prime2 can animate bones while Life2/Prime 2 can animate tissue (limbs,heads, bodies, etc.). Animation does not includes consciousness, so what *is* animation?<br /> <br /> Maybe something like a computer program? A hive mind that works in instinct and can only follow orders? If that is the case, an if body of light can be animated, the mage could create an useful assistant with this power. I wonder what would be the capabilities of the body of light? Would it be a clone of the mage char sheet?<br /> <br /> <br /> PS: Note that this rank had no &quot;metamagick&quot; power at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T15:18:50-07:00","id":1551088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551079#post1551079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, Prime is the animating force. This also appears in hdydt. Matter2/Prime2 can animate bones while Life2/Prime 2 can animate tissue (limbs,heads, bodies, etc.). Animation does not includes consciousness, so what *is* animation?<br /> <br /> Maybe something like a computer program? A hive mind that works in instinct and can only follow orders? If that is the case, an if body of light can be animated, the mage could create an useful assistant with this power. I wonder what would be the capabilities of the body of light? Would it be a clone of the mage char sheet?<br /> <br /> <br /> PS: Note that this rank had no &quot;metamagick&quot; power at all...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit contradictory, if i can make a steak with matter why should i need life to animate a corpse? I understand it could be a possibility (fungi zombie for example) but it explicitly excludes matter for zombies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T21:02:07-07:00","id":1551092,"title":"","content":"Note that <b>A Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b> adds a massive capability to Prime 1: the ability to access Primal Ventures, in very much the same way that Primal Utility can. And <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> generalizes the concept beyond financial Ventures to practically any collective human endeavor, with its Stable Wellsprings (which are basically Primal Ventures stripped of the economic terminology). I'm going to use &quot;Stable Wellspring&quot; to refer to both concepts, as it's the most general and arguably subsumed the notion of Primal Ventures. And you should arguably be able to target <i>temporary </i>Wellsprings as well; consider a Cultist using the Practice of Bardism on the audience of her rock concert to treat the enthusiastic participants as a temporary Wellspring\u2026<br /> <br /> This addition has <i>major </i>ramifications, not the least of which being that it arguably becomes possible to <i>target</i> a Stable Wellspring with <i>other Magick. </i>Once you've done the due diligence to be able to access a Stable Wellspring (which generally involves contributing to it in some way), why <i>shouldn't </i>you be able to target the entire Stable Wellspring with other Effects as if it was a single thing? <i><b>Go Big or Go Home</b>.</i> <br /> <br /> This potentially steps on the toes of Correspondence, in a big way. Because targeting a Wellspring is very similar to targeting everyone who meets a particular criterion, regardless of where they are or how many of them there are. The good news is that it includes something roughly analogous to needing to find a Sympathetic connection to your target(s) \u2014 namely, the aforementioned need to contribute to it. But once you've done that? Boy howdy, can you do a lot. You could, for instance, arguably use Forces to set fire to every participant in the Wellspring \u2014 something which arguably would only be prevented by the fact that you'd end up targeting yourself as well. But what about using Life to heal every participant? Or any other beneficial Effect. <br /> <br /> Even with the rules a written, you can tank the Wellspring by overdrawing from it. This is analogous to something that normally requires the highest level of Entropy: futzing with the efficiency of an abstract system, in a way that causes it to break down. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking that much of this functionality should be relocated to Correspondence, with &quot;access Stable Wellspring&quot; being a conjunctional Correspondence/Prime Effect, rather than simply a Prime Effect. Arguably, the ability to target everyone associated with the Stable Wellspring should require Correspondence 5, being analogous to Co-Location; and the &quot;contribute to the Wellspring&quot; part of it is simply the bog standard &quot;establish a Sympathetic connection to it&quot;. Though maybe it should only be Correspondence 4, since you're not actually stacking locations? <br /> <br /> But then there's the matter of Entropy, which <i>also</i> has the ability to target distributed systems\u2026 Should <i>it</i> maybe be involved in Effects such as this? Maybe Entropy, rather than Prime, is what's needed to treat an organization as a single thing\u2026 But should that be in addition to, or instead of, requiring Correspondence? <br /> <br /> That said, I could be persuaded that Prime is always needed to target a Wellspring on the basis that it largely amounts to a far more effective counterpart to &quot;affecting multiple targets&quot; in much the same way that Correspondence is a far more effective counterpart to &quot;affecting targets at range&quot;. The usual rules for hitting multiple targets doesn't increase nearly as rapidly as the number of participants in a Wellspring does, as five ranks in a Wellspring has the potential to affect people all over the world, with a population comparable to a nation. I don't object to that being <i>possible</i>; but I don't think five dots in a single Sphere should be enough to do it, especially when that Sphere is already being used to overcome range. Tying it to Prime would also let you argue that most such Effects should arguably cost Quintessence; and the larger the Wellspring, the more Quintessence it should cost to affect it. So maybe Correspondence 5/Prime 2, a Sympathetic connection, and a Quintessence cost equal to the dot rating of the Wellspring to affect all of its participants as of they were a single thing. <br /> <br /> Or maybe not; I don't know. There's a lot of interesting possibilities to consider, but also a lot of room for abuse. <br /> <br /> Thoughts? <br /> <br /> (PS: there's also the matter of how this plays into the optional Management and Human Resources rule in M20 on page 595.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T07:30:55-07:00","id":1551097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551092#post1551092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that <b>A Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b> adds a massive capability to Prime 1: the ability to access Primal Ventures, in very much the same way that Primal Utility can.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this means that <b>Prime </b>can do everything that <b>Primal Utility</b> can?<br /> <br /> Possibly more, if memory serves there are some effects that Prime could do and Primal Utility couldnt (I am having a hard time remembering right now), and the difference was justififed by Primal Utility offereing access to Primal Ventures.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-17-2025, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T14:46:24-07:00","id":1551104,"title":"","content":"As far as I understood by rereading <b>Primal Utility</b>, it can't use common Nodes for <i>some</i> effects. But it can for others, and that includes the effect of <i>creating </i>a Node, which is a bit strange.<br /> <br /> Overall <b>Primal Utility</b> seems to be a bit overpowered, because access to Primal Ventures is a <u><b>BIG</b></u> thing, and the only counterbalance is a couple levels where it don't affect Nodes and the need for technocratic Instruments. Which is also weird, because Instruments shouldn't have anything to do with a Sphere's powers, but that's a staple of the &quot;Technocratic Spheres&quot;.<br /> <br /> By the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, will you go through those extra Spheres, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T21:43:05-07:00","id":1551108,"title":"","content":"Primal Utility is better at creating Wonders: it only needs three dots to create a Device, as opposed to the four dots that Prime needs to make a Talisman.<br /> <br /> As well, while it's never explicitly said that you need Primal Utility for this, the Technocracy knows of a way to set up a facility which lets you create Devices or Grimoires without having to expend personal Utility to make the rolls, or to expend a point of Willpower to complete the process; though you still need a source of Utility to integrate into the Device or Grimoire. My guess is that this &quot;Enlightened Science assembly line&quot; requires Primal Utility 5 to set up; though I'm open to arguments that it only requires 4 dots. Either way, it <i>is</i> something that the Technocracy still has a monopoly on.<br /> <br /> And M20 Sorcerer leverages this a step further by saying that mages can create Hedge Paths using the rules for creating Talismans. A logical extrapolation of this is that Technocrats get to create Paths the same way they create Devices, which means that they need only three dots in Primal Utility to do so, and can also set up &quot;factories&quot; for doing so. By all rights, Technocrats ought to dominate Sorcery as a result of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-18-2025, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T21:56:41-07:00","id":1551109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551104#post1551104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understood by rereading <b>Primal Utility</b>, it can't use common Nodes for <i>some</i> effects. But it can for others, and that includes the effect of <i>creating </i>a Node, which is a bit strange.<br /> <br /> Overall <b>Primal Utility</b> seems to be a bit overpowered, because access to Primal Ventures is a <u><b>BIG</b></u> thing, and the only counterbalance is a couple levels where it don't affect Nodes and the need for technocratic Instruments. <u>Which is also weird, because Instruments shouldn't have anything to do with a Sphere's powers, but that's a staple of the &quot;Technocratic Spheres&quot;.</u><br /> <br /> By the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, will you go through those extra Spheres, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. For instance, Data shouldn't require you to connect to the Internet in order to use it; that's &quot;merely&quot; a case of the Technocratic Focus utilizing the Internet as an Instrument. If I were remaking Data as a Correspondence variant, I'd probably just treat it like normal Correspondence but with more information-based examples of the various levels of Correspondence Range. <br /> <br /> Well, I might tweak it to remove much of the teleportation and space manipulation stuff, at least in ordinary space, but giving it more of an edge when accessing and manipulating the Digital Web; but that's just me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T22:08:58-07:00","id":1551110,"title":"","content":"And a reminder: Primal Utility no longer has a monopoly on Primal Ventures. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick p.54</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bank Run (\u2022 Prime)</b><br /> This spell originated among the Syndicate. While it's still used in the Convention, it's also made its way into other Awakened factions\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Prime 1 reveals the energy flow in financial and industrial institutions. If they have a connection to the institutions, the mage may use them as Nodes.<br /> <br /> One success makes the primal force in these institutions visible. Using them asNodes requires a connection to your institution as determined by the Primal Ventures chart (<b>Mage 20</b>, p. 527).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T01:43:08-07:00","id":1551114,"title":"","content":"At this point i see no reason to make a distinction. Either make it a unique sphere in its own right or dont make it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T02:10:00-07:00","id":1551115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551110#post1551110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a reminder: Primal Utility no longer has a monopoly on Primal Ventures.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure of how much this book can be taken as official ruling.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm against it. Quite the opposite, I'm starting to read it and I stated how OP <b>Primal Utility</b> is precisely because I agree that <b>Prime</b> should have this ability, too.<br /> <br /> But the thread is about what the official book actually says, regardless of what is a better ruling or not.<br /> <br /> For targeting a <b>Stable Wellspring</b> as a single entity, I think that's a neat trick for <b>Prime</b>, and I'm not so sure it needs other Spheres, much less at too high levels.<br /> <br /> You already needs the Sphere of whatever effect you want to target the <b>Wellspring</b> with, and targeting the whole thing carries its own risks, as <i><b>you don't control who's a part of it</b></i>. Healing thousands of people at the same time is cool, but how many <i>Sleeper witnesses</i> that is?<br /> <br /> My opinion is that we can balance it perfectly well with <b>Quintessence</b> cost and <b>Paradox</b>. 1 Quint for each level of the <b>Wellspring</b> seems good enough for me, and <i>maybe</i> extra Paradox due to the sheer amount of witnesses. For Sphere level, you already have the level of <b>Primal Utility</b> needed, or how much you're in with the <b>Wellspring</b>.<br /> <br /> On top of that, I would rule that if you tap into a <b>Wellspring</b>, you got quite a strong connection that can be used against you. I'd use the chart on your commitment to the <b>Wellspring</b> as a basis to rule this connection. Any participant becomes a means to get you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T03:11:49-07:00","id":1551116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551115#post1551115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unsure of how much this book can be taken as official ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an official M20 book, <i>not </i>Storyteller's Vault. Why <i>wouldn't </i>it be an official ruling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T04:05:28-07:00","id":1551117,"title":"","content":"For this thread at least? M20 core trumps supplements if there's a contradiction. So if M20 core says normal Prime can't do X, but Primal Utility can, but a M20 supplement contradicts that, the default assumption of the OP for this thread is that normal Prime can't do that thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T07:38:39-07:00","id":1551121,"title":"","content":"M20 doesn't say that Prime \u2022 can't do it; it also doesn't say that it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T09:03:11-07:00","id":1551123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551114#post1551114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point i see no reason to make a distinction. Either make it a unique sphere in its own right or dont make it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly my thought. Both mages and crats are doing the exact same thing afterall, so why make new different spheres for technocrats? I don't like that at all, and I'd day that what one can do, the other can as well, as long as it fits paradigm. <br /> <br /> Also, I really don't like how Primal Utility is vague and needs a LOT of mental gym to work. Like, how exactly does it create something from scrath with rank 2 and a pattern sphere? M20 explanation is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T09:11:38-07:00","id":1551124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551104#post1551104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understood by rereading <b>Primal Utility</b>, it can't use common Nodes for <i>some</i> effects. But it can for others, and that includes the effect of <i>creating </i>a Node, which is a bit strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have examples of which effect it can not use? I don't have access to my books for the next couple of days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551117#post1551117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this thread at least? M20 core trumps supplements if there's a contradiction. So if M20 core says normal Prime can't do X, but Primal Utility can, but a M20 supplement contradicts that, the default assumption of the OP for this thread is that normal Prime can't do that thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was always under the impression that specific supercedes general. So Core books are the general rule, unless a specific supplement expands or contradicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-18-2025, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T09:16:24-07:00","id":1551125,"title":"","content":"Hence the OP set out a specific heuristic for prioritization in the first post of the thread; it's not what most people would consider the normal method, but it's somewhat necessitated by how Mage has been written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T09:17:08-07:00","id":1551126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551115#post1551115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I'm against it. Quite the opposite, I'm starting to read it and I stated how OP <b>Primal Utility</b> is precisely because I agree that <b>Prime</b> should have this ability, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think gwtting access to Primal Ventures is OP? Easy Quintessence? Because Prime has a lot of other ways of getting easy Quintessence. And Quintessence is not that big deal of a resource. It's not that useful.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T14:17:21-07:00","id":1551130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551124#post1551124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have examples of which effect it can not use? I don't have access to my books for the next couple of days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Level 4 effect <b><i>Create Tass</i></b> can't be made with <b>Quintessence</b> of a Node, only <b>Primal Ventures</b> and <b>Wellsprings</b>.<br /> <br /> And that's it. By the Core this is the whole price you pay for the benefits of <b>Primal Utility</b>. Although I <i><b>did not</b></i> compare every level to verify if there's something else, this effect is the only <i><b>expressly </b></i>said to have this limitation, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T14:26:10-07:00","id":1551131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551126#post1551126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do you think gwtting access to Primal Ventures is OP? Easy Quintessence? Because Prime has a lot of other ways of getting easy Quintessence. And Quintessence is not that big deal of a resource. It's not that useful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because it lets you have an abstract Node you can access from anywhere, anytime.<br /> <br /> This isn't game breaking, but is big nonetheless because access to a Node is a meaningful thing, and by the Core this is the only stable form of abstract Node that exists.<br /> <br /> Also, it's big in context: big as a difference between two Spheres where one gets this nice benefit and the other gets almost nothing.<br /> <br /> Overall I agree that while they're interesting concepts, in practice the Technocratic Spheres are a very awkward execution. <b>Primal Utility</b> specially so for gatekeeping access to <b>Primal Ventures</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T08:04:10-07:00","id":1551137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551121#post1551121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 doesn't say that Prime \u2022 can't do it; it also doesn't say that it can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, Primal Utility does say that a mage has to have Primal Utility to access the Quintessence in Ventures. Specifically &quot;Only a character with at least one dot in Primal Utility can access the Quintessence from that Venture; another mage might sense the energies but remain unable to access their power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, one of the rules of this analysis is that if a Sphere and Rank claims to be able to do something, no other entry can contradict it, so if Prime 1 claimed to be able to access Ventures it really wouldn't matter what Primal Utility said. Prime doesn't, though, so the Primal Venture restriction carries a lot more weight.<br /> <br /> The only thing that muddies the waters is that Prime 1 merges the list of Quintessence it can perceive and Quintessence it can channel. That said it never actually says that <i>any energy</i> a mage can see with Prime 1 he can also channel with Prime 1. So even though Primal Utility gives Prime the ability to sense the quintessence in a Venture, that doesn't mean Prime also gets the ability to use them.<br /> <br /> None of this invalidates RBGtM, by the way. That book is carving out an exception to the rules of M20, or rewriting them in one specific aspect and it can stand as an official source. It just doesn't mean much for the purposes of what M20 says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T10:14:57-07:00","id":1551141,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[quote]\u2022\u2022\u2022 Channel Quintessence/ Enchant Life/ Energy Weapon/ Craft Periapts &amp;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Temporary Wonders</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By tapping into the flow of Quintessence around her, the Prime-skilled mage can draw both free and raw Quintessence from Nodes, Junctures (special times), and Tass (solidified Quintessence)\u2026 and she may also channel that energy into new and existing Patterns as well. With such powers, she could (with Life 3) enchant a living thing so that it could inflict or endure aggravated damage; inflict aggravated damage by shaking up that organism\u2019s life force; pull small amounts of life force from a living sacrifice or (with Matter 2) from inert objects; instill Quintessence into a vessel called a Periapt; or \u2013 with other Spheres \u2013 craft temporary Talismans or Devices by infusing them with Primal Force. (Permanent enchantments require Prime 4 \u2013 see Crafting Wonders on p. 508, and Quintessence Amounts on p. 507.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In desperate circumstances, a Prime-schooled mage can also create temporary weapons out of pure concentrated energy \u2013 blasts of Quintessence or swords of light. Such weapons inflict aggravated damage (as per the Base Damage or Duration chart) and cost one point of Quintessence per use\u2026 or, for weapons that last for a length of time, one point per turn. When the mage runs of out Quintessence, the weapon disappears. Unless channeled through energy-guns or conjured as miracles among the faithful, such attacks are inevitably vulgar.[quote]</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the record, it really doesn\u2019t help that Prime keeps introducing terms that are never used anywhere else in M20. This rank it is \u2018Juncture,\u2019 but future ranks will introduce \u2018Soulgem\u2019 and \u2018Soulflower.\u2019</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Channel Available Quintessence (Channel Quintessence)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I want to start out by mentioning that channeling quintessence from Nodes and Tass was already something mentioned in Prime 1, so that's a problem. Now looking at the actual Quintessence rules, channeling quintessence is described not as a spell but as a meditation action, with Prime 1 allowing a mage to absorb more Quintessence than his Avatar rating. <u>So one good possibility is Prime 1 essentially enhances the mage\u2019s natural ability while the Prime 3 version magically handles the Quintessence directly.</u> This makes sense as Prime 3 lets a mage move Quintessence to places other than his own pool. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tass discrepancy is harder as there isn\u2019t an direct statement of how a mage would naturally use Tass. That said, the examples of refilling Quintessence from Tass in the Quintessence section seem to indicate that a mage can absorb appropriate forms of Tass (eating edible Tass, for instance). If so then <u>Prime 1 would let him handle more than his Avatar rating. Meanwhile Prime 3 would let the mage absorb the Quintessence from any form of Tass or channel it anywhere he wants.</u> </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition Prime 3 mentions both available and raw quintessence, <u>it may be able to pull more quintessence than a Node has as available quintessence.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One new thing mentioned in Prime 3 is Junctures. Mages can now draw from auspicious moments of particular potency. Prime 3 is the only place in M20 that even mentions Junctures so we never get a good description of what they are and what separates them from Wellsprings. Presumably they are things like alignments of the stars and other auspicious or metaphysically significant moments, but your guess is as good as mine.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I\u2019ll Gladly Pay You Tuesday for a Quintessence Burger Today</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can channel Quintessence where he wants and that includes other mage\u2019s pools. That is a mage can give another mage some of his own Quintessence, or channel the Quintessence from somewhere else into another mage. He may also be able to take from another mage, willingly or unwillingly, although he would not be able to forcibly drain a mage lower than their Avatar rating, it seems.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enchant Creature (Enchant Life)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Wut?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once again, channeling quintessence into a pattern takes a higher rank for living things than objects, and once again it takes Life supplementation. This time it takes Life 3 for all Life patterns, which doesn\u2019t match up to Alteration, Transmutation, or Healing. I can\u2019t say for certain the reasoning here, but when Matter is mentioned in another effect it uses the level for Transmute Simple, and that\u2019s what Life 3 handles as well. But since this is a completely different ruling than in Prime 2, I can\u2019t really tell what Life is doing so I can\u2019t come up with a real resolution.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts?</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime Attack (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - The Life of Prime</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with most spheres, Prime can be used for attacks, and this damage is automatically aggravated. Based on the placement in the sentence it is tempting to think this requires Life 3, but none of the other elements of the list seem to need Life. Also, Prime naturally does aggravated damage on its own. And even though that is not mentioned in the sphere writeups, we\u2019ve already seen Prime used to augment other attacks into aggravated so we know that\u2019s one of its natural capabilities.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We also can\u2019t assume this is a Life attack augmented to do aggravated damage, even though that\u2019s exactly what \u2018shaking up the target\u2019s life pattern\u2019 sounds like. Life naturally does aggravated damage, so it certainly wouldn\u2019t need help from Prime. So it really looks like this wasn\u2019t meant to be a conjunctional effect.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Quintessence Vampire</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The aformentioned unwilling draining of Quintessence, if it is a thing, would likely be handled as a Prime attack that targets the Quintessence pool rather than the Health pool.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pull Quintessence From Pattern (Channel Quintessence)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now Prime 3 can pull life force from living targets, <i>or with Matter 2</i> from inert objects. Now if we were just talking about pulling quintessence out of a pattern, this would not make sense. After two ranks of effects that require Life for living things but not Matter for objects, this would be a strange turn. There is an important word, though: sacrifices. That indicates that this is meant to be a destructive act, not just a little drain. The reason, then, that creatures don\u2019t require Life is that the mage is ending them in a non-magical way. Now I still don\u2019t quite understand why breaking or melting or in some other way destroying an object doesn\u2019t also work, but I can at least see the thought process.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Snuffing Out the Candle</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once again, the third pattern sphere is forgotten, but Prime should be just as capable as drawing from energies in the right circumstances. The hard part is engineering the \u2018destruction\u2019 of significant enough sources of energy. Despite the name I chose, a single candle isn\u2019t likely enough.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Temporary Wonders (Create Temporary Wonders)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Prime 3 a mage can craft a temporary talisman, which is different from a regular talisman because\u2026 because\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution? - Temporary Talismans</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The problem? M20 never defines what a temporary talisman is. It could be a Charm that is expended when used. It could be a talisman with a non-refuelable quintessence pool. It could be a talisman that only lasts for a set duration. All three would seem to fit the description.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>I Prepared Explosive Runes Today</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perhaps the simplest example of a temporary talisman is one that destroys itself in the process of working its wonders.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft Periapt or Use Periapt (Craft Periapt)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Making or Using</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Prime 3 a mage can channel quintessence into a periapt. The language gets confused here. From the text it sounds like this is meant to fill an existing periapt with quintessence. From the headers, though, Prime 3 can <i>Craft Periapts</i>. From Prime 4 and 5 it appears that was supposed to be a higher rank power (though Prime 4 is muddled on this), but it is explicit here.<br /> <br /> Added: The sticking point is <i>Soulgems </i>and <i>Soulflowers</i> from Prime 4 and 5 respectively. I'll cover this more when we get to them, but Soulgems are written as if they are something different from periapts, but Soulflowers are written as if they (and by extention, Soulgems) are the same. If they are something different, there is no conflict, <u>Prime 3 is the rank for periapts and Prime 4 and 5 are talking about something else</u>. </span>That is consistent with what is written here as it appears that Prime 3 is all that is required to create Periapts and that this does not in any way require supplemental spheres.<br /> <br /> If we do want to split that power between Prime 3 and later ranks, the best resolution I can think of <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">for this is that <u>in the same way that Prime 3 can create Temporary Wonders (whatever they are) it can create Temporary Periapts</u>. These would function like periapts but with the same time (or other) restrictions as temporary wonders.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>And the Frame is Probably Worth Something Too</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the periapt is already a one-time use item then drawing a little bit extra out of it by sacrificing it might be a good move.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manifest Weapon (Energy Weapon)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a quite expensive power. A mage can expend his personal quintessence to briefly manifest attacks or weapons. These cost 1 quint per turn manifested, or per point of ammunition, whichever is more applicable. It is worth noting that the Common Magical Effects table says 1 quint per point of damage done, but even if that is an option it is by far the worst unless the mage wants to limit the damage he does.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Lightsabers</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Given how overt this spell is, most applications of it are likely vulgar. Ironically, there are enough prop lightsabers around that generating a lightsaber is one of the few applications with a chance of being coincidental. The mage would still have to justify pulling it from seemingly nowhere, but the weapon itself looks more reasonable than a longbow made of light.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-20-2025, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T11:26:42-07:00","id":1551142,"title":"","content":"Missing line from the Create Periapt section that I will add once the edit timer passes:<br /> <br /> As written it appears that Prime 3 is all that is required to create Periapts and that this does not in any way require supplemental spheres. If we do want to split that power between Prime 3 and later ranks, the best resolution I can think of is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T13:12:44-07:00","id":1551143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551142#post1551142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime Attack (???)</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>The damage with prime is realted to using quintesence weppoons or missails (you can shoot energy bolts with prime 3). At this lvl you also should be able to &quot;rub the bones&quot; but that deals bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T18:02:45-07:00","id":1551145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551131#post1551131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it lets you have an abstract Node you can access from anywhere, anytime.<br /> <br /> This isn't game breaking, but is big nonetheless because access to a Node is a meaningful thing, and by the Core this is the only stable form of abstract Node that exists.<br /> <br /> Also, it's big in context: big as a difference between two Spheres where one gets this nice benefit and the other gets almost nothing.<br /> <br /> Overall I agree that while they're interesting concepts, in practice the Technocratic Spheres are a very awkward execution. <b>Primal Utility</b> specially so for gatekeeping access to <b>Primal Ventures</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly does that works? The mage still needs Node background, right? He can't just tap into Quintessence from any abstract source, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T18:48:51-07:00","id":1551146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551141#post1551141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B][FONT=Arial]Presumably they are things like alignments of the stars and other auspicious or metaphysically significant moments, but your guess is as good as mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this seems to be the intention, yes. First because it would otherwise be the same as tapping a <b>Wellspring</b>, second because this is a very thematic thing to do, but missing anywhere else in the book, third because this is cool. I'd use this ruling even if it wasn't the intention, but I do think it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551141#post1551141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B][FONT=Arial]Once again, channeling quintessence into a pattern takes a higher rank for living things than objects, and once again it takes Life supplementation. This time it takes Life 3 for all Life patterns</div> </div> </div> </div>My two cents: <b>Life</b><b> 3</b> is both <i>Transmuting</i> and <i>affecting others</i> (with Healing). I don't really believe it and I think they were just eyeballing those things, but that can justify the ruling.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I think it certainly should be <b>Life2/4</b>, <i>Transmuting</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551141#post1551141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B][FONT=Arial]So it really looks like this wasn\u2019t meant to be a conjunctional effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it isn't a conjunctional effect, just more eyeballing to somehow not making <b>Prime</b> too powerful (which I don't think it is regardless).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551141#post1551141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B][FONT=Arial]M20 never defines what a temporary talisman is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make sense for it to be a bit of everything here: Unless you add successes to <i>Duration</i>, it's single use. If you do add successes to <i>Duration</i>, it still can't refuel without another <b>Prime 3</b> effect.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551141#post1551141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B][FONT=Arial]The best resolution I can think of for this is that <u>in the same way that Prime 3 can create Temporary Wonders (whatever they are) it can create Temporary Periapts</u>. These would function like periapts but with the same time (or other) restrictions as temporary wonders.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is correct. Comparing a <i>Periapt</i> with a <i>Talisman</i> seems a safe assumption in this regard.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551141#post1551141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B][FONT=Arial]It is worth noting that the Common Magical Effects table says 1 quint per point of damage done</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was just lack of attention on what they were doing.<br /> <br /> Possibly it was written with the rules for <i>Spirits</i> still fresh in the mind, as there are charms that do this 1 point per damage thing (and I already think they're off, a prohibitive cost).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T03:26:39-07:00","id":1551151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551145#post1551145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How exactly does that works? The mage still needs Node background, right? He can't just tap into Quintessence from any abstract source, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Node Background is for controlling a Node, not the ability to tap into one. If a PC belongs to a Chantry with a Node, but doesn't take any dots in Node, the PC can still use the Node when the NPCs allow it; it's just at their discretion.<br /> <br /> Primaly Ventures are significantly different from other Nodes and Node-like things in that it's truly abstract. There isn't a place, or a thing, or a person, or a unique set of circumstances, it is reliably connected to that requires you to be present to access. You just need to be associated with the Venture in some fashion (variable based on your investments in the Venture and your Primal Utility dots). A Master of Primal Utility can literally walk into any nation wide restaurant chain, buy a meal, and then be able to access the equivalent of a Rank 4 Node; no Node background required. That said, some Syndicate member is likely not going to be happy about this; but the same could be said about any other case of using Prime to take Quintessence someone else has worked to cultivate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T04:35:32-07:00","id":1551152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551145#post1551145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How exactly does that works? The mage still needs Node background, right? He can't just tap into Quintessence from any abstract source, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Heavy Arms said.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds aren't locked behind dots, and <b>Primal Ventures</b> have clear and <u><i>easy</i></u> means for you to tap into them. In fact, they're relatively easy to make in the first place, even if not every business is one of them.<br /> <br /> Sure the ST can decide to never make anything into a <b>Primal Venture</b> unless it's under the Node Background, but that's contrived and outside the intent of the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T05:54:37-07:00","id":1551154,"title":"","content":"So taking into account M20 and the rote in Rich Bastard's Guide.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime </b>can now do everything that <b>Primal Utility</b>, but not viceversa?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> I would love your input.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I am aware that for this thread M20 has precedence, but reading both books?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T08:48:30-07:00","id":1551157,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Expel or Infuse Energy/ Tap Wellspring/ Craft Tass &amp; Permanent Wonders </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The terrible power of draining Quintessence from objects or forces (though not yet from living things) can disintegrate those targets, consume them in Primal flames, or decay them almost instantly. Reversing that flow, the mage can craft objects that cannot be broken, or bond organic and inorganic materials together to create cybernetic implants, nanotech, and other Wonders. At this stage, she is able to enchant items permanently and draw Quintessence from the energetic Wellsprings of exciting events. By infusing her personal Quintessence into a Periapt, the mage might use Matter 4 to craft a Soulgem: a portable vessel that\u2019s filled with her own Resonance and energy.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drain Quintessence (Expel Energy)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Prime 4 a mage can rip the quintessence out of Forces and Matter patterns. It appears that the mage (or at least player) can choose the form this takes. There is no mention of supplemental spheres.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is not stated what the mage can do with this quintessence, but the operative term is \u2018draining\u2019 so presumably it can go directly into his personal pool, a reservoir like tass or a periapt, or even fuel spells directly.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>External Sublimation Engine</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One application of this is burning some kind of fuel for quintessence to reduce the difficulty of other spells. I could just about see an Etherite with a back mounted furnace that he keeps shoveling fuel into to power his gear (instruments).</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infuse Quintessence (Infuse Energy)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can likewise channel extra quintessence into an object or force. It isn\u2019t clear what this does for a force, but it makes objects unbreakable. This is an ability we could use more explanation but it appears that this refines, reinforces, or perfects patterns. Beyond just making things unbreakable, this could likely improve them in other ways.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>The Eternal Flame</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One possible way this could affect forces is make them continue forever, or at least until the quintessence and spell run out. Given there is no indication of this spell burning through the infused quintessence and that Permanent Enchantments are possible at this rank, that really could be forever, though. This would make flames that burn forever (temporarily), areas that always shove whatever passes through them, eternal voltage sources, etc.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent Enchantment (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most spheres don\u2019t mention permanency until rank 5, but it is rank 4 for enchantments on items. That said, I think the standard questions apply. Are we talking about permanent spells or permanent results? That\u2019s going to be an ST call. </span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft Wonders (Craft Wonders)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage with Prime 4 has the full ability to create wonders. The wonder rules are not in the sphere description,</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Interestingly, no supplemental spheres are required to bond organic and inorganic materials together, or create cybernetics or nano bots. I don\u2019t take this to mean no spheres are required to set up the Wonder\u2019s effects, but it does sound like none beyond those and Prime are required to make the wonder and, more notably, to install it where it is supposed to go.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Cybernetics</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When I think of cybernetics I usually think of Matter and Life grafting, which would be in the Life 5/Matter 3+ range for a human target. It really appears that Prime 4 is an alternate method. Given we\u2019ve seen Prime be used as an animating force before, this is not unreasonable.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft Tass (Craft Tass)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We have this solely from the headers, it isn\u2019t mentioned in the text itself. Still, it appears that a mage with Prime 4 can turn quintessence into Tass. With no guidance I would think this applies to creating Tass from his personal Quintessence Pool, or directly from any source that he draws from.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Custom Flavor Bomb</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tass is often flavored with resonance. With control over where and how the Tass is made, the mage can potentially create Tass for specific purposes.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Draw Quintessence from Events (Tap Wellspring)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this rank a mage doesn\u2019t need to have a full fledged Node but can, at the appropriate moments, tap into temporary moments of power. These would seem to include both places that periodically bring forth quintessence, and moments, events, or situations that combine to temporarily bring forth that essence.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Pink Slime</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The slime from Ghostbusters 2 is essentially congealed Tass created not by a Node but by the permanent Wellspring that is NYC in the 80\u2019s, or rather by the temporary but frequent Wellsprings of pleasant social encounters, easy traffic, and polite window washers of NYC in the 80s.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft Soulgem (Infuse Energy + Transmute Complex Matter?) </span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - What is a Soulgem?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I want to stress this wording because it is the biggest impediment to figuring out Prime\u2019s periapt progression:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By infusing her personal Quintessence into a Periapt, the mage might use Matter 4 to craft a Soulgem: a portable vessel that\u2019s filled with her own Resonance </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This clearly sounds like the mage takes an existing periapt and turns it into a Soulgem, and that this Soulgem contains his resonance. That this starts with an existing periapt reinforces that Prime 3 is the rank to create periapts. The description of a soulgem as a container for resonance does the same. On the other hand there is no information on why a mage would want a container of his own resonance and what such a thing could do. Soulgems are not mentioned anywhere else in M20. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cLegends tell that the Hollow Ones used to leave burning bags of their \u2018resonance\u2019 on the Chantry doorstep, ring the bell, then run away\u2026\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The main possibility based on M20 alone is that Soulgem is the term for a material periapt, and this is just a convoluted name for Craft Periapt.</u> This is consistent with Prime 5\u2019s description of a Soulflower as a living periapt and also makes it clear why a mage would want to do this. This interpretation, though less consistent with the text as written, actually has a meaning. This contradicts Prime 3\u2019s stated ability to Craft Periapts, though, unless we assume that rank can only make temporary ones. It also doesn\u2019t explain why this needs Matter when crafting a temporary periapt does not and crafting a permanent wonder does not.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now if we consult other sources we can get a few ideas. Revised does mention Soulgems as <u>a type of periapt that can only be used by the mage who made it</u>. That makes sense as a step up from a normal periapt, so Prime 4 makes sense, but would in no way need Matter 4.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">HDYDT depicts them as <u>a periapt that travels with the mage as if it were consecrated.</u> That is a terrible effect for Prime 4 alone, let alone Prime 4/Matter 4. IIf we make some key wording do <i>a lot</i> of heavy lifting we can infer that this <u>is only usable by the mage.</u> This also in no way needs Matter 4, but at least with that effect Prime 4 makes sense.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those are both consistent with what is written in Prime 4, though I\u2019d probably never think of either one on my own.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts?</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T08:56:14-07:00","id":1551158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551104#post1551104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, will you go through those extra Spheres, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, though I haven't done any prep work on them. Before starting this thread I did a pass through of the main nine to at least divide up the basic effects, ambiguities, and contradictions. I don't have that for the Technocratic variants, and I haven't done much with them in previous threads.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T09:27:51-07:00","id":1551159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551154#post1551154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So taking into account M20 and the rote in Rich Bastard's Guide.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime </b>can now do everything that <b>Primal Utility</b>, but not viceversa?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier, I wasn't comparing them level by level to see if anything changed level. It did.<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Utility</b> has access to Creating Devices 1 level earlier (which is also 1 dif lower), 3 instead of 4. In my opinion this is already quite strong, more than the power to turn Quint from a Node into Tass, but YMMV.<br /> <br /> I remain in the opinion that the better handle for this, for now, is to simply treat it as <b>Prime</b> by another name. But if we talk RAW, they're kind of balanced once <b>Primal Ventures</b> become accessible.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551157#post1551157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think of cybernetics I usually think of Matter and Life grafting,</div> </div> </div> </div>While it isn't stated in the Sphere (no surprise), here they're talking the Cybernetics covered by the Technomantic Background. They're basically Wonders, that's why they're covered by <b>Prime</b>.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't even say that &quot;normal&quot; cybernetics need <b>Life + Matter</b>, they're pure <b>Life</b>. While you can use <b>Matter</b> to create the implants, they're not necessarily magical, and <b>Life</b> alone should be able to take care of rejection and whatnot.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551157#post1551157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revised does mention Soulgems as <u>a type of periapt that can only be used by the mage who made it</u>.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think <i>Revised</i> is right here, and being <i>also</i> kind of consecrated fits it. I don't think this is just a name for a permanent <i>periapt</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T17:44:58-07:00","id":1551165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551154#post1551154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So taking into account M20 and the rote in Rich Bastard's Guide.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime </b>can now do everything that <b>Primal Utility</b>, but not viceversa?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> I would love your input.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I am aware that for this thread M20 has precedence, but reading both books?)</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is that the remaining difference after the inclusion of the Rich Bastard's Rote is that regular Prime doesn't have the function of reducing the level of investment you need to tap into a Venture.<br /> <br /> So if you're just using normal Prime, you can tap into Ventures, but you're still stuck at whatever level of Resources you can toss around for it (hence it's in the Rich Bastard's guide, it's only useful to mages of significant mundane wealth). Primal Utility's requirements to tap into a Venture are reduced as you gain dots in Primal Utility.<br /> <br /> So Prime 5 and Primal Utility 5 can in theory do all the same things, but Primal Utility is still better at using Ventures in practical application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T18:40:09-07:00","id":1551166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551165#post1551165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My reading is that the remaining difference after the inclusion of the Rich Bastard's Rote is that regular Prime doesn't have the function of reducing the level of investment you need to tap into a Venture.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that, it's true. A Master of <b>Primal Utility</b> can tap into any <b>Venture</b> with very little investment, while with <b>Prime</b> alone you'd need to be a founder or something like it to tap into a Level 5 <b>Venture</b>.<br /> <br /> With that I change my view: <b>Primal Utility</b> is still patently stronger than <b>Prime</b>. Not as absurdly as before, but definitely stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T19:08:50-07:00","id":1551167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551151#post1551151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Node Background is for controlling a Node, not the ability to tap into one. If a PC belongs to a Chantry with a Node, but doesn't take any dots in Node, the PC can still use the Node when the NPCs allow it; it's just at their discretion.<br /> <br /> Primaly Ventures are significantly different from other Nodes and Node-like things in that it's truly abstract. There isn't a place, or a thing, or a person, or a unique set of circumstances, it is reliably connected to that requires you to be present to access. You just need to be associated with the Venture in some fashion (variable based on your investments in the Venture and your Primal Utility dots). A Master of Primal Utility can literally walk into any nation wide restaurant chain, buy a meal, and then be able to access the equivalent of a Rank 4 Node; no Node background required. That said, some Syndicate member is likely not going to be happy about this; but the same could be said about any other case of using Prime to take Quintessence someone else has worked to cultivate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but any mage can meditate at a Node and restore Quintessence. Does that mean that anyone with Primal Unity can tap into the Primal Venture anywhere and juat restore Quintessence? How does this works mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T19:34:44-07:00","id":1551168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551154#post1551154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So taking into account M20 and the rote in Rich Bastard's Guide.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime </b>can now do everything that <b>Primal Utility</b>, but not viceversa?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> I would love your input.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I am aware that for this thread M20 has precedence, but reading both books?)</div> </div> </div> </div>When I have to choose if a rule from another book should be used, I analyse two things: If the rule contradicts any other rule in M20 and if the rule makes sense inside the Mage setting.<br /> <br /> Personally, Technocratics Spheres i just unnecessary and wrong, contradicting even several Mages editions, which all says that &quot;all of them (Trads and crats) are doing the same thing: magick&quot;. So, instead of having new spheres, why not just bring them together and let paradigm say what one can and cannot do, <b>just like with all the other 6 speheres?!?</b><br /> <br /> Now, if we're talking raw, and to answer your question, yes, I think Prime can do anything Primal Unity can do *and* vice-versa. I'm not sure if Prime can do anything that Primal Unity can't...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T22:24:41-07:00","id":1551173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551167#post1551167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, but any mage can meditate at a Node and restore Quintessence. Does that mean that anyone with Primal Unity can tap into the Primal Venture anywhere and juat restore Quintessence? How does this works mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that you need to be connected in some way to the Primal Venture in order to draw Quintessence from it. Any of the activities that are suggested for accessing a Primal Venture ought to work for the purpose of recharging, in place of &quot;meditating at a Node&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T22:40:15-07:00","id":1551174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551168#post1551168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I have to choose if a rule from another book should be used, I analyse two things: If the rule contradicts any other rule in M20 and if the rule makes sense inside the Mage setting.<br /> <br /> Personally, Technocratics Spheres i just unnecessary and wrong, contradicting even several Mages editions, which all says that &quot;all of them (Trads and crats) are doing the same thing: magick&quot;. So, instead of having new spheres, why not just bring them together and let paradigm say what one can and cannot do, <b>just like with all the other 6 speheres?!?</b><br /> <br /> Now, if we're talking raw, and to answer your question, yes, I think Prime can do anything Primal Unity can do *and* vice-versa. I'm not sure if Prime can do anything that Primal Unity can't...</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree about the Technocratic variants being wrong, in that the differences should never have been as extensive as they ended up being. Originally, Dimensional Science was just Spirit with an exception to the Gauntlet Strength chart; and if the Technocratic Variants had merely been &quot;swap out this Magickal Chart that's obviously got an anti-tech bias built into it for an alternate chart that's more friendly to technology&quot;, that would have been fine. <br /> <br /> In particular, I'm not at all happy with Data having &quot;access to the Internet&quot; built in to its mechanics: that <i>should</i> be a result of using the Internet as an Instrument. <br /> <br /> With that said: yes, there are things that Prime can do that Primal Utility cannot. The most blatant example is Body of Light; but there are others, such as Primal Utility sometimes being restricted to where Quintessence can come from: as others have pointed out, they sometimes can't draw Quintessence from anywhere <i>other than</i> Primal Ventures. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T07:47:23-07:00","id":1551191,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime 5</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Infuse or Withdraw Life Force/ Create Node &amp; Soulflower/ Nullify Paradox </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Prime Master can draw Quintessence from anywhere, at any time, and channel it into other vessels as well. A dark, vulgar aspect of that power allows her to obliterate a living being by consuming all of his life force, whereas the reverse of that power infuses him with life force so strong that he\u2019s essentially blessed. Combining that ability with Life 5, she may turn complex organisms into Soulflowers: living Periapts who become walking batteries of boosted Quintessence. Such Mastery also allows the mage to create Nodes in significant places, and to nullify Paradox as described under Nullifying Paradox, p. 549.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Zero Point Quintessence (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can now draw quintessence from anywhere and at any time and likewise channel it to just about any means. There\u2019s not much more to say about this.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Energy Vampire (Withdraw Life Force)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This extends the energy draining powers of Prime 4 to life patterns. The text specifically mentions obliterating the being, though at such a high rank lesser scourgings should also be possible. Note that this does not require Life.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because a mage can draw quintessence from anywhere, drawing it from a creature is a deliberate choice. Notably the text focuses more on the destruction than on the energy gained but this does work by consuming the life force so the energy must be gained.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ST\u2019s are going to need to decide how much quintessence this gives. There is not guidance here.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>You Can\u2019t Eat Just One</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The resonance of quintessence derived this way likely lends itself to destruction and consumption, so it will lend itself to helping in similar spells in the future. A mage who gains enough resonance this way will likely also have an easier time-consuming creatures and a harder time using tamer forms of quintessence. In the right story this could even become an important element. I suppose this is less an example and more a potential consequence.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bless (Infuse Life Force)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While actual effects are thin, this appears to be the living upgrade of the Prime 4 power. Prime 4 could make objects nigh unbreakable, so this power would make people nigh unbreakable. It is reasonable that immortality is another possible option. Like Energy Vampire, there\u2019s no indication this requires Life. As with Prime 4 there is no indication that the quintessence runs out... or that it doesn't.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Plot Immunity</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power turns someone into a cinematic hero (or villain) who can shrug off things mere mortals would be incapacitated or killed by. This is both a good way of thinking about what Bless is capable of and a possible mark to shoot for with Bless.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Node (Create Node)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Prime 5 a mage can create nodes. The reference to significant areas indicates they can\u2019t be created just anywhere. I suspect the lack of guidance isn\u2019t an oversight as the decision of what counts as significant matters more to the table than to the game systems. The limitation turns what could be a broken power into a story seed instead.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Create Wellspring or Juncture</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a Prime Master can create a Node, he should also be able to engineer a wellspring or even a Juncture. The mage could take a moment not quite significant enough to be a wellspring and open it up as one. This could be either a one time event or a recurring one.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">He could also take a moment of seeming importance, like a longstanding tradition or a recently discovered astronomical phenomenon, and tip it over the edge into a Juncture. With time and patience he could even create a tradition to build this event around.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Nodes would seem to be superior, Junctures would have two advantages. The first is creating them is easier, the second is you don\u2019t have to defend them when they are not active.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nullify Paradox (Nullify Paradox)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rules for this are given elsewhere and basically let a mage eliminate paradox in his own pattern, though at rank 5 Prime can probably eliminate paradox in someone else\u2019s pattern as well.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Prime 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. Unless the ST specifically wants something locked behind archspheres, it should be possible here.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Soulflower (Create Soulflower)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Prime 5 a mage can extend the Soulgem creation powers to living creatures and create Soulflowers. All the same possibilities from Create Soulgem are present here. This time, at least, there is a direct statement that Soulflowers are periapts, though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The three possibilities from before are:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>1 \u2013 Soulflowers are permanent periapts made from living creatures.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>2 \u2013 Soulflowers are living periapts only the mage can use</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>3 \u2013 Soulflowers are living periapts consecrated to the mage (and possibly only he can use them)</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 and 2 still have no indication of why this would require Life 5 when the Prime 3 version does not. Consecration of living things requires Life, so at least possibility 3 has a reason for including it, though Life 5 is not consistent with what Prime 2 uses.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T08:56:53-07:00","id":1551194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551174#post1551174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that said: yes, there are things that Prime can do that Primal Utility cannot. The most blatant example is Body of Light; but there are others, such as Primal Utility sometimes being restricted to where Quintessence can come from: as others have pointed out, they sometimes can't draw Quintessence from anywhere <i>other than</i> Primal Ventures.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is that explicitly said in M20 or somewhere else? If Primal Utility can create things from scratch, why not a body of light?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T09:43:40-07:00","id":1551195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551167#post1551167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, but any mage can meditate at a Node and restore Quintessence. Does that mean that anyone with Primal Unity can tap into the Primal Venture anywhere and juat restore Quintessence? How does this works mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahn... yes, that's exactly how <b>Primal Ventures</b> work, it's their entire point. You can do as little as buy something from them or revise your shares portfolio to draw from them. The requisite is to form a connection, but this isn't necessarily hard to do.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms example was literal. A Master of <b>Primal Utility</b> can form a connection with a Level 4 <b>Venture</b> simply by buying a meal at a restaurant of a chain, and immediately start to channel <b>Primal Energy</b>.<br /> <br /> In fact the book doesn't say how you do meditate over a <b>Primal Venture</b>, and it's probably simpler than forming the connection to begin with. But it's ludicrous to think it should be <i>harder</i>, as the connection is the whole point.<br /> <br /> <i>Some</i> effects suggest what you have to do in order to enact them, but that's ultimately a suggestion of <b>Instrument</b> for the effect, but for meditation nothing is said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551194#post1551194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that explicitly said in M20 or somewhere else? If Primal Utility can create things from scratch, why not a body of light?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Body of Light</b> isn't cited directly. In fact, even for Nodes, only <b>Create Tass</b> says it can't be done with normal ones. In all other effects, it seems that you can use a normal Node no problem.<br /> <br /> And as far as it goes, <b>Body of Light</b> could be out because the whole way <b>Primal Utility</b> sees Quintessence is too abstract for that.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551191#post1551191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ST\u2019s are going to need to decide how much quintessence this gives. There is not guidance here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I distinctly remembers somewhere being rotes for creating a human from scratch/resurrecting people, and it costs 10 Quint. Also, Vitae = Quint in most regards, and a human has 10 Blood Points. I'd say 10 points total for a human body is a good rule of thumb, with each point causing 1 Agg to the person.<br /> <br /> Other life forms could either follow the same tables as Vampire (assuming the Quint comes from a &quot;metaphysical weight&quot;), or follow weight. Both are equally interesting to me, as they say different things about the metaphysics of the setting, I would use one or the other depending on the chronicle, or even depending on Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T10:18:48-07:00","id":1551197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551174#post1551174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With that said: yes, there are things that Prime can do that Primal Utility cannot. The most blatant example is Body of Light; but there are others, such as Primal Utility sometimes being restricted to where Quintessence can come from: as others have pointed out, they sometimes can't draw Quintessence from anywhere <i>other than</i> Primal Ventures.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of things Prime can do that Primal Utility cannot, but that's not one of them. At least not as written in M20. Primal Utility 2 makes the specific claim that it can do all the normal Prime 2 effects, and Body of Light is one of the normal Prime 2 effects.<br /> <br /> At a quick glance the differences in M20 are:<br /> <br /> At rank 1 Primal Utility can do what Prime 1 can do plus access ventures. Primal Utility is purely better at this level.<br /> <br /> At rank 2 there is no difference.<br /> <br /> At rank 3 Primal Utility gets a specific method of creating permanent devices, while Prime 3 is limited to temporary devices (whatever they are). On the other hand, Prime 3 can directly pull from Nodes and Junctures as well as from sacrifices. Primal Utility gets none of those. Prime can also manifest energy weapons and attacks and Primal Utility cannot. Prime gets a lot more at this level, though Primal Utility gets one powerful trick.<br /> <br /> At rank 4, Prime now gets the complete ability to create Permanent Wonders, Primal Utility is still restricted to the specialized method from PU3. Primal Utility also gets downgraded versions of tass creation and Drain Quintessence. Prime doesn't specifically say it can make use of the quintessence pulled from objects but Primal Utility is explicit that it cannot. Prime can also infuse objects while Primal Utility makes no mention of that. Prime also can make soulgems and there is nothing equivalent in Primal Utility (although to be fair, we'd need to know what a soulgem is to be sure). For this rank Prime is purely better.<br /> <br /> At rank 5 Primal Utility finally gets full access to permanent wonders. It can also make Nodes and Ventures, while Prime is restricted to just Nodes. On the other hand Prime can pull Quintessence from anywhere, while Primal Utility cannot. Prime can also pull quintessence from living things and use it, while if Primal Utility doesn't say. If it follows the pattern of rank 4, though, it can only destroy and not use the released energy. Prime can also infuse living things with quintessence, and Primal Utility cannot. Finally, Prime can create soulflowers, while it looks like Primal Utility cannot. Possibly that's what Living Assets are, but more likely those are Ventures. Like Rank 3, it looks like Prime gets a lot more but Primal Utility gets a significant trick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T11:48:39-07:00","id":1551212,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Spirit</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview: </b>Otherworlds and things of the Otherworlds, The Gauntlet, Ephemera, Souls</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Spirit typically uses the local Gauntlet rating for difficulty rather than calculating based on sphere rating. The Base Spirit section doesn\u2019t indicate what would be the exceptions. The most intuitive ruling is that any spell that goes across a Gauntlet or interacts with the Gauntlet uses the Gauntlet rating, while other spells use the usual rules. </span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T11:58:10-07:00","id":1551213,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Spirit Sight/ Spirit Sense </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To most of humanity, the spirit world remains invisible. Not to a mage who knows the Spirit Sphere. Although he\u2019ll be most attuned to spirits with Resonance similar to his own, that mage can read the local Gauntlet\u2019s thickness, discern auras, sense spirits of all types, peek into the Penumbra through the Vidare (see Chapters Three and Four), and determine whether or not a material object has a spiritual component (as mystic Fetishes do).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combined with other Spheres, that mage can spot forces, places, or items with unusual ties to the spirit world, such as Awakened objects, elemental spirits, possessed organisms, Shallowings, Nodes, and so forth.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Gauntlet and See Through Gauntlet (Spirit Sight)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can both sense the Gauntlet and sense across the Gauntlet. Sensing the Gauntlet gives it\u2019s local thickness and likely any meddling done with it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seeing across the Gauntlet allows to see the Penumbra of the Otherworlds using one of the Vidare as a lens. If the mage is in the Penumbra they should also be able look into the physical. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note that seeing the strength of the gauntlet should include seeing an actual hole in the gauntlet (aka a Shallowing), which for some reason is stated to require conjunctional effects. Perhaps there are things about a shallowing that can\u2019t be determined without help, but actually seeing one should be purely in the domain of Spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>See Gauntlet Realms</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is not really my specialty, but as I recall Werewolf has certain realms hidden in the layers of the Gauntlet itself. If there are any that apply to Mage, a mage would be able to see them with enough successes.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See Spirits (Spirit Sight)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the header says Spirit Sight, the text says sense. This is not a contradiction or limitation but an invitation to tailor each mage\u2019s spirit senses to their paradigm. This presumably applies both to spirits on the other side of the Gauntlet and spirits that are on the same side but in some way hidden.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I was under the impression that elemental spirits were still spirits and so this power should work on them with no need for another sphere, though if they are possessing an element that might be a different story.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See Auras (Spirit Sense)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also see the aura of people and other creatures, with all of the information that aurasight brings.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>See Aura of Unseen</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is not stated that a mage needs to be able to see the creature to see its aura. In situations where the creature is hiding or invisible it may not have concealed its aura and aura sight could give it away.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Spiritual Component (Spirit Sense)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this power a mage can determine if an object has a spiritual component. Fetishes are given as an example of something that does. However, so would awakened objects and possessed creatures, which are for some reason locked behind conjunctional effects. It is possible that Spirit Sense is restricted to objects, so maybe it can\u2019t see possession without Life, but awakened objects should still count.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The other possibility is that <u>detecting the spiritual component requires close examination of the target, whereas the conjunctional effects make it obvious for all relevant objects/creatures in the area</u>.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T12:48:43-07:00","id":1551214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551213#post1551213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that seeing the strength of the gauntlet should include seeing an actual hole in the gauntlet (aka a Shallowing), which for some reason is stated to require conjunctional effects. Perhaps there are things about a shallowing that can\u2019t be determined without help, but actually seeing one should be purely in the domain of Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view on this is that the Shallowing itself (whatever form it takes) and the effect of it's existence (the Gauntlet being zero) aren't the same thing. A Shallowing generally refers to a persistent if not permanent Gauntlet zero area, not something like a Garou or Mage using a power to open a hole in the Gauntlet that lets others pass through without rolling for a few minutes. Given most durable Shallowings are &quot;attached&quot; to something like a Node, I think this would be much like your Sense Spiritual Component underlined interpretation (something I find the most reasonable given the rest of the text): Spirit alone can detect the reduced Gauntlet and with time and study could deduce the form of the Shallowing. Conjunctional Spheres let you detect the full nature of the Shallowing direct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not really my specialty, but as I recall Werewolf has certain realms hidden in the layers of the Gauntlet itself. If there are any that apply to Mage, a mage would be able to see them with enough successes. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Realms&quot; in the Gauntlet itself are a fairly rare thing to exist. Usually it's either something like the Bastets' Den Realms - which exist in the Penumbra but can't normally be found or accessed from that side and can normally only be found by figuring out their physical entrance on the material plane - or any patterns that have been caught in the Gauntlet during transit and are stuck in the web until something else can free them (which can, in theory, apply to &quot;pocket realms&quot; created by various effects, not just supernatural entities crossing the Gauntlet). I think being able to notice a &quot;flaw&quot; in the Gaunlet where something is stuck is definitely within Spirit 1's purview, but I'm not sure Spirit 1 alone should be able to find specific things caught in the Gauntlet, or know what an encapsulation contains, by itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See Aura of Unseen </div> </div> </div>This feels like a bit of a stretch. &quot;Sight&quot; is of course a misnomer in the sense that mages are not just limited to their eyes, but the default rule is that you need to be able to sense something to apply magic to it. If you can't see it (though of course Spirit 1 lets you see a lot of things you can't normally see already), you can't scan it's aura. Having the aura extend beyond the subject enough to give the target away isn't really in-keeping with anything stated in the text IMO, and being able to override stealth powers (esp, since aura-senses aren't part of many WoD games, so those games don't have any discussions of hiding auras or powers that specifically do so) feels unintended at best to what Spirit 1 describes. Given that other Spheres are very explicit when they can find things that cannot normally be sensed, I'm not sure this reading holds up well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Spiritual Component (Spirit Sense)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this power a mage can determine if an object has a spiritual component. Fetishes are given as an example of something that does. However, so would awakened objects and possessed creatures, which are for some reason locked behind conjunctional effects. It is possible that Spirit Sense is restricted to objects, so maybe it can\u2019t see possession without Life, but awakened objects should still count.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The other possibility is that <u>detecting the spiritual component requires close examination of the target, whereas the conjunctional effects make it obvious for all relevant objects/creatures in the area</u>.</span> </div> </div> </div>I side with the underlined version. Given that - while not quite as stressed as it is in Werewolf - the WoD is an animist world, the vast majority of things have a &quot;spiritual component.&quot; Unawakened objects have spiritual components that are dormant too after all. This would also in many ways override aura-sense otherwise, because you could sense the Beast/P'o/chimerical nature/spirit-half/etc. that is inherent in most other WoD supernaturals directly instead of having to infer from your aura roll. <br /> <br /> A Fetish is something with an extra spirit shoved into it (maybe even more than one) that is only bound by magical means and that binding can be broken and the spirit freed/left without its comfy home. Full spiritual possession fuses the spirit and subject into one new entity, and awakened objects don't have any new &quot;components&quot; they didn't have before. I think there's definitely room for a range of necessary Spheres to instantly recognize something for what it truly is, instead of having to rely on impressions and existing knowledge to puzzle it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T20:56:36-07:00","id":1551218,"title":"","content":"There's actually a splat that works with auras: Vampire.<br /> <br /> And while <b>Auspex</b> gives benefits to uncover hidden things, at no point does it establish that you can notice hidden people by noticing the &quot;uncovered aura&quot;.<br /> <br /> In fact this isn't stated even when talking about powers geared towards concealment, and while <b>Obfuscate</b> works as a Mind effect, <b>Chimerstry</b> and other, rarer effects, don't. None whatsoever let you pinpoint hidden people through auras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T06:55:11-07:00","id":1551230,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more along the lines of Orpheus where Kirlian cameras were able to detect ghosts. Given the associations between Kirlian photography and auras, it seemed reasonable that Spirit 1 could replicate the abilities the Orpheus cameras. Note that Orpheus is not an example of seeing across the Gauntlet because ghosts in Orpheus are stuck on the living side of the Shroud (Stormwall).<br /> <br /> The idea is not that an aura automatically gives someone away, it is that in situations where they can't be physically seen but their aura can be a mage with this power will be able to see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T10:05:10-07:00","id":1551235,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Touch Spirit/ Manipulate Gauntlet </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perception moves to contact. The Spirit-savvy mage can now reach through the Gauntlet for a turn or two; call across the Gauntlet; speak to spirit entities, or touch them for a brief moment; and thin or thicken the local Gauntlet. In the latter case, each success lowers or raises the Gauntlet rating by +1 for each success rolled. (Four successes would raise or lower it by four levels, for example.) That said, a human mage cannot lower the Gauntlet to less than 4 within the mortal world.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By adding other Spheres, that mage could project thoughts across the barrier (Mind 4 or 5); stir up elemental disturbances within the Otherworlds (Forces 2 or higher); imbue material objects with ephemeral power (Matter 2); drain Essence from a spirit (Prime 3); or help other living creatures sense or contact the spirit realms (Life 2).</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reach Across Gauntlet (Manipulate Gauntlet)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While a mage can\u2019t pass through the gauntlet at this rank, he can reach across, cast across it, and call across it. Indeed, this seems very much like the Spirit equivalent of Correspondence 2. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Call across the gauntlet is an odd word choice, but would seem to include speaking and making connections. It is definitely different from speaking to spirits as that is a different power in this list.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 Reach</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Correspondence, Reach Through Space includes being able to move small objects across that distance. Since the same terminology is used here there is at least the plausible reading <u>that a mage can move small objects or creatures (housecat or smaller) across the Gauntlet.</u> Whether or not this would convert them to ephemera depends on if moving into the umbra automatically does this (which is apparently a matter of debate in universe according to Stepping Sideways on pg 88 for whatever that is worth)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Will a Mr. Umbral Entity Please Come to the Courtesy Desk </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Call Across Gauntlet could include putting out a request or invitation for an entity to come. Actually forcing it to come would be Spirit 4, but the request could reasonably happen at Spirit 2. For what it is worth HDYDT seems to think this is the purpose of this ability, though take that with a grain of salt.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Hide Contraband</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One use for moving things across the gauntlet is quickly stashing problematic items. That said there\u2019s nothing keeping a local spirit from taking the item so a wise mage will use this power carefully.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speak With Spirits (Touch Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a deceptively important power. The section on spirits themselves makes it clear that they communicate in an entirely different way than people and that unless they themselves can translate, Spirit 2 is necessary to communicate with them. That\u2019s not directly stated in Spirit, but the wording here is consistent.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dig beneath the surface, though, and this isn\u2019t just a translation of spirit speech, though, it is a translation of spiritual impressions and meanings. So this power isn\u2019t just limited to translating what a spirit says, it also can translate information about what the spirit is or even translate what it is thinking, provided the mage has ways of finding that out.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Change Spirit Appearance</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a bit of a stretch, but spirits often appear in different forms that fit the spirit\u2019s nature and the expectations of the viewer. In some ways, how it appears is another form of communication and so can be translated accordingly. Provided the new image fits the spirit\u2019s nature and doesn\u2019t mechanically change the scene, a mage may be able change the spirit\u2019s appearance for himself and anyone he shares this with.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Speak Without Spirits </i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In theory at least, two mages with Spirit 2 can communicate in spiritual impressions in a way that no one without Spirit 2 could understand.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Act on Spirit (Touch Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power lets a mage touch and affect spirits regardless of their state. This is also the ability to enable spells to affect spirits (if the spell couldn\u2019t already).</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Quit Hitting Yourself</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m struggling to find a use for Touch Spirit that isn\u2019t obvious, but bullying a spirit by smacking it around with its own limbs, tentacles, or other appendages has a certain stupid charm. If Cobra Kai was an actual Akashic faction I could see this being a rote they would use.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gauntlet Thickness (Manipulate Gauntlet)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also alter the thickness of the gauntlet up or down. The two biggest impacts of this are that spirits will have a harder or easier time crossing, and most Spirit effects are based on the thickness of the gauntlet.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is technically self-referential. The difficulty should be the current gauntlet rating, and the spell is directly affecting that. That said there\u2019s not really a need to get into that unless the table really wanted to. What does matter is that if a mage thickens the gauntlet it is harder for another mage to undo that change, while if a mage thins the gauntlet it is easier for another mage to thicken it again.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Breach Gauntlet Pocket</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since the base power is technically called Manipulate Gauntlet, not Thicken Gauntlet, there's the potential for affecting more than just gauntlet rating. If a mage managed to find a Bastet Den Realm (thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> for the reminder of them) or other like pockets in the Gauntlet, this power may let him alter or manipulate the way into them and thus break in. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><b><i>Open Existing Portal</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> A mage can't open a path to the Umbra by himself yet, but he should be able to open one that already exists, or close it for that matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Selective Gauntlet Protection</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It may be possible to use this power like Correspondence 2\u2019s Minor Ward to selectively change the gauntlet difficulty for certain creatures. As with wards, setting those conditions may take other spheres.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue Object (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution or Lack Thereof</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m not really sure why a mage would want to do this. It\u2019s not wrong, per se, I just don\u2019t know what the practical outcome of the effect is. <u>One possible result is that the object can touch spirits</u>, but that\u2019s speculation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This idea doesn\u2019t come up again within Spirit, so this is not a power that is one rank higher when done to life forms. Either it is only possible with objects, or it is possible with any pattern sphere at this level.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drain Essence From Spirit (Touch Spirit + Pull Quintessence From Pattern)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage can\u2019t mundanely kill the target of a Prime 3 sacrifice he needs an appropriate sphere to apply the effect to something. At least, that\u2019s why I think the Prime 3 power needs Matter for objects but not Life for living things. So here it needs Spirit 2 to touch spirits.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extend Spirit Senses and/or Contact to Others (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution</i></span></span></b>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There's a lot opened up in a very few words.<br /> <br /> There are two powers extended here: senses and contact. Senses clearly means taking the sensory powers of Spirit 1 and giving them to another creature. This appears to say that Life 2 is enough to extend these senses to any living creature including people. At the very least most who read the text would be thinking of giving people the ability to see spirits, though I am sure there are some niche applications for crabs that can see across the gauntlet.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Contact has to mean either speaking or touching, both of which are Spirit 2 powers. Again, the clear text seems to say sharing this ability is Life 2, regardless of what kind of creature it is shared with. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I am not at all sure why the Spirit 1 power needs an extra rank to be shared but the Spirit 2 power does not.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s no indication this Life ability is restricted to Spirit, by the way. And while perhaps only Correspondence and Time have contact powers that could be shared, all the spheres have sensory powers.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T10:12:32-07:00","id":1551237,"title":"","content":"For the variable gauntlet thickness, the idea came from three places:<br /> <br /> Dimensional Science mentions that Technocrat labs have a high gauntlet rating, except for technocrats with appropriate paradigm/practices.<br /> <br /> The Shroud has different places that it is weak or strong than the Gauntlet. <br /> <br /> If I recall correctly, Anansi have an easier time crossing a thick Gauntlet than a thin one.<br /> <br /> So there's at least some indication that the Gauntlet can treat some entities differently from others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T13:23:26-07:00","id":1551241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551235#post1551235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue Object (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Give a spirit a weapon that works in both worlds, profit<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T14:00:15-07:00","id":1551243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551230#post1551230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more along the lines of Orpheus where Kirlian cameras were able to detect ghosts. Given the associations between Kirlian photography and auras, it seemed reasonable that Spirit 1 could replicate the abilities the Orpheus cameras. Note that Orpheus is not an example of seeing across the Gauntlet because ghosts in Orpheus are stuck on the living side of the Shroud (Stormwall).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wouldn't this just be Spirit 1 sense spirits with the Mortem Vidare? Auras don't seem necessary to mix in with this as far as what the Sphere does. &quot;Kirlian&quot; photography &quot;auras&quot; are more of a paradigm thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551235#post1551235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, this seems very much like the Spirit equivalent of Correspondence 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the books really support quite the level of inference drawing from Correspondence you're doing in this post. It's not necessarily a bad way to look at how to handle some of Spirit's effects, but it's not what the text directly states.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Call Across Gauntlet could include putting out a request or invitation for an entity to come. Actually forcing it to come would be Spirit 4, but the request could reasonably happen at Spirit 2. For what it is worth HDYDT seems to think this is the purpose of this ability, though take that with a grain of salt. </div> </div> </div>Older books also make this distinction, not just HDYDT? so I'd consider it less needing of some salt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Change Spirit Appearance</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a bit of a stretch, but spirits often appear in different forms that fit the spirit\u2019s nature and the expectations of the viewer. In some ways, how it appears is another form of communication and so can be translated accordingly. Provided the new image fits the spirit\u2019s nature and doesn\u2019t mechanically change the scene, a mage may be able change the spirit\u2019s appearance for himself and anyone he shares this with.</span> </div> </div> </div>I don't know... this feels like more than a stretch. Nothing in Spirit 2 implies it can shape or manipulate ephemera like this. This is like saying if you can magically translate someone, you inherently have the power to magically adjust their presentation... I don't see the support for this concept in Mage (not to say the line of thinking is never explored... Changeling has some moments like this).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Selective Gauntlet Protection</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It may be possible to use this power like Correspondence 2\u2019s Minor Ward to selectively change the gauntlet difficulty for certain creatures. As with wards, setting those conditions may take other spheres.</span> </div> </div> </div>This feels like it should be in the conjunctional effects. This sort of selective application isn't in Spirit and is very much in other Spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue Object (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution or Lack Thereof</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m not really sure why a mage would want to do this. It\u2019s not wrong, per se, I just don\u2019t know what the practical outcome of the effect is. <u>One possible result is that the object can touch spirits</u>, but that\u2019s speculation.</span> </div> </div> </div>In older books, this is how you made weapons that could attack spirits. Even if they're on the material side of the Gauntlet, spirits and other entities are frequently intangible and thus immune to blades or bullets. Imbue object is a way to address that (Prime can as well by most interpretations).<br /> <br /> In theory this can play into negotiating with spirits as well, as spirits might want something from the physical world that they can't get themselves, and imbuing the object ensures it can be moved into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551237#post1551237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's at least some indication that the Gauntlet can treat some entities differently from others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is a backwards conclusion. Different entities interact with the Gauntlet differently. The Gauntlet itself is broadly treated as a passive obstacle in all of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T14:24:41-07:00","id":1551246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551243#post1551243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wouldn't this just be Spirit 1 sense spirits with the Mortem Vidare? Auras don't seem necessary to mix in with this as far as what the Sphere does. &quot;Kirlian&quot; photography &quot;auras&quot; are more of a paradigm thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Though it works the other way too, that Kirlian photography is a technological approach to seeing auras. The Vidare, though, doesn't come into play because ghosts in Orpheus are not on the other side of the gauntlet/shroud/stormwall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure the books really support quite the level of inference drawing from Correspondence you're doing in this post. It's not necessarily a bad way to look at how to handle some of Spirit's effects, but it's not what the text directly states. </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't use it one for one, but there are some broad similarities, especially in the sense that they are both effects that can tack on to other spells to extend range and capabilities.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth I don't think the intention was to be able to move small objects across the gauntlet, but given the wording it's not an interpretation we can disregard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Older books also make this distinction, not just HDYDT? so I'd consider it less needing of some salt.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Good to know. I was worried I was out on a limb on that one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know... this feels like more than a stretch. Nothing in Spirit 2 implies it can shape or manipulate ephemera like this. This is like saying if you can magically translate someone, you inherently have the power to magically adjust their presentation... I don't see the support for this concept in Mage (not to say the line of thinking is never explored... Changeling has some moments like this). </div> </div> </div>The restrictions that the appearance must still match the spirit and there can't be a mechanical effect are important to the effect. This really doesn't affect the spirit in any substantive way, it just changes between reasonable perceptions of it. This one is playing off of the way spirits can present differently to different people at the same time that is brought up elsewhere in M20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This feels like it should be in the conjunctional effects. This sort of selective application isn't in Spirit and is very much in other Spheres. </div> </div> </div>I considered it, and it often would require other spheres much like wards, but some of the selective effects would be purely within the Spirit sphere, such as thickening against spirits or choirs of spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In older books, this is how you made weapons that could attack spirits. Even if they're on the material side of the Gauntlet, spirits and other entities are frequently intangible and thus immune to blades or bullets. Imbue object is a way to address that (Prime can as well by most interpretations).<br /> <br /> In theory this can play into negotiating with spirits as well, as spirits might want something from the physical world that they can't get themselves, and imbuing the object ensures it can be moved into the Umbra. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that, my copy of Revised is back in storage and I didn't have the chance to check.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-27T08:48:01-07:00","id":1551313,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 3</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Pierce Gauntlet/ Step Sideways/ Rouse &amp; Lull Spirit </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the mage can cross over, transmuting his living tissue to ephemera. He may carry a few material possessions, although transmuting them as well raises both the difficulty of the roll and the number of successes required for the trip. (Normal clothing and items raise both factors by +1; bulky clothing and items raise them by +2.) That traveler must step sideways on his own; bringing large items or other people across demands a higher Spirit Rank. Meanwhile, a combined Spirit 3/ Mind 2 Effect allows the mage to read Resonance, Synergy, and other spiritual energies (Essence, a spirit\u2019s place within a hierarchy, etc.).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this Rank, a mortal mage can also harm an Umbral entity as if he was using Life 3 against that entity. While Spirit 2 allows the mage to touch that entity, Spirit 3 lets him actually damage its ephemeral Pattern\u2019s integrity the way that Life 3 damages a physical creature\u2019s form.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By combining this Rank with Matter 3 and Prime 2, the mage can also create short-lived objects from ephemera; such creations must be constructed as if they were material things, and they fade away at the end of the Effect\u2019s duration. Finally, this Rank helps the mage rouse the slumbering spirits within objects or places, or else put active spirits to sleep. (See Awakening Substances in Chapter Nine, p. 443).</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Step Sideways (Step Sideways) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power is as iconic to Spirit as casting from a distance is to Correspondence or casting ex nihilo is for Prime.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notably, there is some contention between Prime and Spirit on this. Spirit says that clothing and carried items automatically make the journey with the mage (though at increased difficulty) while Prime lets a mage consecrate items so they pass with him automatically. <u>Presumably Consecration bypasses both the size restrictions and the difficulty increases, as well as letting the mage bring a creature across the umbra at Spirit 3</u>.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transmute Ephemera (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While it is only described as a part of stepping sideways, Spirit 3 can transmute physical patterns into ephemera or vice versa. However, this does not work the same as other transmutation effects.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike other transmutation effects, this does not require the pattern sphere appropriate to the thing being changed. A mage does not need Life 4 to convert himself in the stepping sideways process, in either direction. It is possible this rule only applies when Stepping Sideways and other conversions would require Pattern Spheres.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I am putting this in as a separate effect from Stepping Sideways because one of the conjunctional effects (create short lived ephemeral objects) appears to use it that way. I\u2019ll get into this when I cover that effect, but one way or another it is using Spirit 3 for transmuting in some capacity.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Said conjunctional effect also implies that there is a limit on transmutation that other spheres don\u2019t have, but I\u2019ll cover that when we get to the effect.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Force Materialization</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If indeed a mage can transmute ephemera to physical matter then he can force a kind of materialization on spirits at this level. Since it takes Spirit 4 to move something else across the gauntlet, this would only work on spirits on the same side as the mage.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harm Spirit (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is one of the simpler powers of this rank. At this level a mage can directly attack a spirit\u2019s pattern. This is explicitly equivalent to a Life 3 attack on a living pattern.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Rouse or Lull Spirit</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As per usual, attacks don\u2019t have to be direct damage attacks. The example given of rousing or lulling a spirit is a good example of a non damaging spirit attack spell.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Effects</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Resonance, Synergy, and Other (??? + Read Surface Thoughts?)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m a little unclear on this one. Prime 1 can explicitly read Resonance and Synergy, so it is possible that most of this is just a much more expensive alternative method to accomplish the same thing. However, this also lets a mage divine things about a spirit such as its place in a spiritual hierarchy, which is a completely different thing. </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Overall, it seems like two different effects mashed together.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Conflict Resolution - Two different effects</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Resonance and Synergy</i> </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit ? to sense resonance and synergy.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is largely a sensory ability so it is probably Spirit 1. That rank seems to have most of the relevant abilities. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit Data - Spirit 2 Mind 2 (Read Surface Thoughts + Speak to Spirit)</span></b></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pull identity information from a spirit and translate it. This also includes reading the inherent resonance and synergy of the spirit. It\u2019s arguably that identity and place in the hierarchy are deeper ideas than Mind 2 can access so Mind 3 might be necessary, though that\u2019s not the way I picture spirit minds working.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The odd thing is that neither of these makes sense as Spirit 3. In other words, while I\u2019m sure Spirit 3 Mind 2(3) can be used, I don\u2019t see the ability of Spirit 3 that is being used and it looks like the same effect would be possible at Spirit 2 Mind 2(3).</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short Lived Ghost Things</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ex Nihilo creation of a thing composed of ephemera with Spirit 3/Matter 3/Prime 2. For that small effect this is going to be a big section.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Ex Nihilo</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a really strange spell and its existence has ramifications on how we interpret Spirit 3. I\u2019ll say at the outset, it is <u>possible that Matter was just an error</u>. If it wasn\u2019t though\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requiring both Matter and Prime is a very strange choice. If the idea is to create ephemera out of nothing, surely Prime alone is all that\u2019s required. That\u2019s all any other \u2018something from nothing\u2019 effect needs. There are basically two possibilities I see:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 \u2013 <u>Spirit 3 can\u2019t be used to directly create something ex nihilo</u>. This spell is a workaround that creates physical matter ex nihilo and <i>converts</i> it to spirit matter.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 \u2013 <u>Spirit can only create generic ephemera ex nihilo, defining it down to an object requires Matter as well.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note that both of these are using Spirit 3 in a transmutational capacity. The former as a matter to ephemera transmutation and the latter as a quintessence flow to ephemera transmutation. Since there is no indication this spell is a gauntlet crossing one, that implies that Spirit 3 can transmute even when the gauntlet isn't involved.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As for why either of these would be the case, my best guess is that if Spirit 3/Prime 2 could create ephemera and Spirit 3 could convert ephemera to matter, forces, and life patterns without the use of Pattern Spheres, then Spirit 3/Prime 2 could be used to create almost anything without pattern spheres. One of those two needed some kind of restriction.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Or maybe I\u2019m completely off base. This is a strange effect, both in what it appears to do and the method it appears to use. If anyone has another idea of what this spell is doing and why Matter is involved I\u2019d love to add it here.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-27T09:54:02-07:00","id":1551314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, there is some contention between Prime and Spirit on this. Spirit says that clothing and carried items automatically make the journey with the mage (though at increased difficulty) while Prime lets a mage consecrate items so they pass with him automatically. <u>Presumably Consecration bypasses both the size restrictions and the difficulty increases, as well as letting the mage bring a creature across the umbra at Spirit 3</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, older editions do specify that you can't bring anything your mage can't carry<br /> <br /> Doylist speaking, it's so you don't need to be nacked, and can bring your &quot;inventory&quot; (to borrow gaming lingo) with you. Prime Consecration, as with other effect, serves to increase it's range of options at relatively low Sphere levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ex Nihilo creation of a thing composed of ephemera with Spirit 3/Matter 3/Prime 2. For that small effect this is going to be a big section.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Contradiction Resolution - Ex Nihilo</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> This is a really strange spell and its existence has ramifications on how we interpret Spirit 3. I\u2019ll say at the outset, it is <u>possible that Matter was just an error</u>. If it wasn\u2019t though\u2026 </div> </div> </div>If it's an error, it's a very old one because even as far as Second Edition that required Prime and Matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1 \u2013 <u>Spirit 3 can\u2019t be used to directly create something ex nihilo</u>. This spell is a workaround that creates physical matter ex nihilo and <i>converts</i> it to spirit matter.<br /> <br /> 2 \u2013 <u>Spirit can only create generic ephemera ex nihilo, defining it down to an object requires Matter as well.</u><br /> <br /> Note that both of these are using Spirit 3 in a transmutational capacity. The former as a matter to ephemera transmutation and the latter as a quintessence flow to ephemera transmutation. Since there is no indication this spell is a gauntlet crossing one, that implies that Spirit 3 can transmute even when the gauntlet isn't involved. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what the authors had in mind with this limitation, but I'm tempted to say it may be <i>both?</i>.<br /> <br /> If I'm not wrong, both to create a spirit and to directly transmute ephemera are mentioned as Spirit 5.<br /> <br /> Spirit 3 transmutative powers don't change the object in any way other than &quot;Matter to Ephemera&quot; and viceversa. It doesn't alter the object as much as it alters it's relation to the Cosmology, so to speak.<br /> <br /> So, you're able to &quot;create physical matter ex nihilo and <i>convert</i> it to spirit matter&quot;. Arguably you could also use Prime 3/Spirit 3 to channel Quintessence and &quot;translate&quot;\u200b it to spirit Essence or a &quot;raw ephemera&quot; of sorts - and viceversa. But you can't create actual spirit matter nor shape it, atleast not with Spirit 3 alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-27-2025, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-29T09:28:09-07:00","id":1551334,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Rend Gauntlet/ Seal Breach/ Bind Spirit </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the mage approaches Mastery, he can tear Gateways in the Gauntlet, allowing groups or large objects to pass through\u2026 or close such breaches, too. Both applications, of course, are deeply vulgar.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this Rank, the mage may also compel spirits to appear, bind them into Fetish objects, or tie them to certain spots or prisons. For obvious reasons, such bondage is risky, especially if the spirit is powerful. A brave or foolish Spirit mage can even turn himself into a temporary Fetish, channeling a spirit entity into his mortal body; in such cases, he loses his ability to use true magick, but he may employ the capabilities of the spirit inside him. On the flipside, he can also exorcise a spirit that has possessed a mortal host. In all cases, the mage enters a series of resisted rolls against the spirit, pitting his Willpower against that spirit\u2019s own.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gauntlet Gateway (Rend Gauntlet)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The escalation for crossing the gauntlet for Spirit is much like the escalation for teleportation for Correspondence. Rank 3 allows personal instantaneous portals or travel, while Rank 4 allows lasting gateways.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power does not specifically say that these gates convert the people and things that pass into ephemera so that is technically up to ST discretion. It is probably intended that this gauntlet crossing functions mostly like the crossing of Spirit 3.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Create Shallowing</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One application that could be possible is creating a shallowing, or at least creating a place where the gauntlet is gone. Even if a shallowing doesn\u2019t count as a gateway, this should fall under rending the gauntlet. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The other more narrative, mystical, and associative elements of a shallowing may have to wait for Spirit 5, though.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Close Shallowing</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whether or not a mage with Spirit 4 can create a shallowing, he should be able to close one. A shallowing may be more than just a place with a gauntlet of zero, but that is one of its necessary components.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Compel Spirits (Bind Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level a mage can compel behavior out of spirits. I think there\u2019s some rule that at this point I\u2019m supposed to say that this is likely to anger spirits, especially powerful ones. I\u2019m not going to say that, though, because 1) spirits are alien and what they consider respectful and appropriate is similarly alien and 2) because it is possible to command without being demeaning.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One particularly important application of this is summoning which works on spirits not in the current location. It is possible this requires Correspondence, but given the behavior of Spirit 2, probably not.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m also going to include binding and trapping spirits to specific spots or prisons part of this power. That doesn\u2019t really need its own section. Same for banning.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Humiliate Spirit</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While I did just stress that commanding spirits does not inherently anger spirits it is definitely possible to anger them with this power either unintentionally (if the mage doesn\u2019t know enough) or intentionally (if he does and chooses to).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">He could also just compel the spirit to feel humiliated regardless of circumstances. This would of course wear off when the spell does. Whether the spirit continues to consider the spell a humiliation after that will depend on the spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Fetish (Bind Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages can bind spirits into objects, and in doing so create a wonder. While how a fetish works is (to a limited degree) found elsewhere, the text here indicates that the binding process functions much like any other attempt to compel a spirit with Spirit 4.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Unorthodox Fetish</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s a lot of gray area in the word \u2018object\u2019 and given the capacities of Spirit 4, it is likely a mage could bind a spirit into counterintuitive things like air or a location. The fire of an eternal flame (either the kind in cemeteries or the kind in burning mines and natural leaks) could function as a pattern to bind a spirit to. I suspect the reason this is not talked about is less because it is not possible and more because it is inadvisable, but YMMV.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exorcise Spirit</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In many ways this is the opposite power of creating a fetish, it is separating the spirit from a mortal host (or presumably item). This should apply both to spirits that have possessed a host under their own power, spirits that have possessed a host with the help of another mage, and spirits that have been bound into a host with Compel Spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Exorcise Awakened Item</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll admit, this one probably doesn\u2019t make sense but I don\u2019t have another unusual idea for Exorcism, and I\u2019m curious. Say a mage awakens the spirit of an item, then exorcises that item, separating the spirit from the item it shared. What does that do to the spirit and what does that do to the item?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T09:15:54-07:00","id":1551344,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Forge Ephemera/ Gilgul/ Break the Dreamshell </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Spirit Master is now able to command ephemera itself, creating, challenging, and destroying spirit matter as he Wills. With such power, he may craft Realms, imbue or drain a spirit of Essence, instill a soul within an empty shell of Life or Matter, and bestow the awful sentence of Gilgul \u2013 the destruction of a mage\u2019s Avatar. Such powers are always vulgar and feature devastating consequences even when the mage succeeds.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power also allows the mage to break the Dreamshell and venture beyond the Horizons, wandering into the Deepest of Umbrae. Such tasks demand at least 10 successes, but a courageous Master can travel as far as his soul wants to go.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We have a problem here in that supplemental spheres are completely unmentioned, even for effects we already know are conjunctional, like putting a soul in a body. On a strict reading that means Spirit 5 is capable of everything mentioned without help.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If we do take the more reasonable stance that some of these are conjunctional we are left to guess which ones.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create or Destroy Spirit Matter (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Spirit 5 a mage has full transmutational control of spirit matter allowing him to create and destroy ephemera, spirits, and souls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On straight reading this is Spirit 5 alone, but contextually this may require Prime for creation effects.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Create Spirit</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits are creatures of ephemera, so they should fall under this ability. Further, if a mage can create a soul at Spirit 5, he should also be able to create a spirit. </span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Challenge Spirit Matter</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Challenge?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have no idea what this means, but I suspect the word should have been \u2018changing.\u2019 Changing and sculpting is a power that usually goes along with creation and destruction in other spheres.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If \u2018challenge\u2019 is intentional, possible meanings could include:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5 lets a mage claim status in spirit courts, enabling them to take formal actions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5 lets a mage make formal challenges that spirits must respond to.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5 may let a mage set spirit related bans and wards.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Remake Spirits</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Spirit 5 a mage can completely reshape spirits not just in their appearance or form, but in their identity and purpose, even into diametrically opposed ones. Pain spirits can be remade into healing spirits, mountain spirits into ocean spirits, etc.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Realm (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We get two words for a power with so much scope. With no boundaries given, this would seem to allow a mage to create Horizon realms, regular Umbral realms, small zones of influence, and really anything.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whether this can create the entire realm or just carves out the space for other spheres to define is left unsaid. I\u2019m fairly certain any time this is brought up in previous editions it does involve other spheres, so that\u2019s the safe bet. As written, though, no other spheres are mentioned</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Create Shard Realm</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m not saying that the Shard realms were actually created by mages, but it does seem to be within the hypothetical capabilities of Spirit 5 as written here. The number of successes required would be absurd, though.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue/Drain Essence (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can now pull or impart essence from or to a spirit directly rather than by damaging or (presumably) healing said spirit. Essence is not quintessence, but it can probably be turned into quintessence with the help of Prime.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sacred Hunt</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Between Compel Spirit and Drain Essence, a mage can probably simulate the hunting rites of werewolves where the spirit agrees to be drained in a specific way with the condition that it will not be destroyed. Careful negotiation of agreements and treaties to allow the mage this right are likely better long term options than Compel Spirit, though some spirits may relish certain competitions enough that they would welcome the opportunity.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Werewolves tend to use actual hunts, but the spirits mages work with might prefer other competitions like chess matches, improv theater, interpretive dance, Greek wrestling, etc.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Soul (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level a mage can create souls. On a technical level, \u2018instill\u2019 has connotations that could limit this. It could be read to mean that souls are slowly grown in the shell, for instance. Nevertheless, it appears mages can create and impart souls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with the rest of this rank, no supplemental spheres are listed. Contextually, though, Prime or Mind may be.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Convert Spirit to Soul</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage can create a soul and change ephemera, he can probably convert a spirit into a soul, or at least into something that functions like a soul rather than a spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gilgul (Gilgul)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because Mage is a little cagey on what the Avatar is, it is unclear if this is destruction of a separate entity or soul surgery that amputates part of a person\u2019s soul or something inbetween. Technically all of those would be possible at Spirit 5.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Avatar Inversion</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We know this is possible because the Cauls do it. We know it manipulates a mage\u2019s Avatar, which puts it in the same rank (or higher) than Gilgul. I\u2019m not saying that Spirit 5 should give easy access to this, because as a storyline element it is next to impossible and should be the stuff of legends, at least on a level with curing vampires. What I am saying is that, barring Archspheres, the Spirit component of this freakishly difficult effect should be rank 5.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Journey Beyond Horizons (Break the Dreamshell)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exactly what it says. When using Spirit to break through the Horizon it takes Rank 5. This would presumably apply to any Horizon like barrier found out in the reaches.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Spirit 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. Unless the ST specifically wants something locked behind archspheres, it should be possible here.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Move Soul</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage can create and impart a soul, he should also be able to take and move one. Possibly even destroy one, though that may be a bridge too far as a game element for some tables.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T16:10:47-07:00","id":1551368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551344#post1551344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We have a problem here in that supplemental spheres are completely unmentioned, even for effects we already know are conjunctional, like putting a soul in a body. On a strict reading that means Spirit 5 is capable of everything mentioned without help.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If we do take the more reasonable stance that some of these are conjunctional we are left to guess which ones.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create or Destroy Spirit Matter (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Spirit 5 a mage has full transmutational control of spirit matter allowing him to create and destroy ephemera, spirits, and souls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On straight reading this is Spirit 5 alone, but contextually this may require Prime for creation effects.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Create Spirit</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits are creatures of ephemera, so they should fall under this ability. Further, if a mage can create a soul at Spirit 5, he should also be able to create a spirit. </span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Challenge Spirit Matter</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution - Challenge?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have no idea what this means, but I suspect the word should have been \u2018changing.\u2019 Changing and sculpting is a power that usually goes along with creation and destruction in other spheres.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If \u2018challenge\u2019 is intentional, possible meanings could include:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5 lets a mage claim status in spirit courts, enabling them to take formal actions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5 lets a mage make formal challenges that spirits must respond to.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 5 may let a mage set spirit related bans and wards.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Remake Spirits</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Spirit 5 a mage can completely reshape spirits not just in their appearance or form, but in their identity and purpose, even into diametrically opposed ones. Pain spirits can be remade into healing spirits, mountain spirits into ocean spirits, etc.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Realm (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We get two words for a power with so much scope. With no boundaries given, this would seem to allow a mage to create Horizon realms, regular Umbral realms, small zones of influence, and really anything.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whether this can create the entire realm or just carves out the space for other spheres to define is left unsaid. I\u2019m fairly certain any time this is brought up in previous editions it does involve other spheres, so that\u2019s the safe bet. As written, though, no other spheres are mentioned</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Create Shard Realm</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m not saying that the Shard realms were actually created by mages, but it does seem to be within the hypothetical capabilities of Spirit 5 as written here. The number of successes required would be absurd, though.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue/Drain Essence (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can now pull or impart essence from or to a spirit directly rather than by damaging or (presumably) healing said spirit. Essence is not quintessence, but it can probably be turned into quintessence with the help of Prime.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sacred Hunt</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Between Compel Spirit and Drain Essence, a mage can probably simulate the hunting rites of werewolves where the spirit agrees to be drained in a specific way with the condition that it will not be destroyed. Careful negotiation of agreements and treaties to allow the mage this right are likely better long term options than Compel Spirit, though some spirits may relish certain competitions enough that they would welcome the opportunity.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Werewolves tend to use actual hunts, but the spirits mages work with might prefer other competitions like chess matches, improv theater, interpretive dance, Greek wrestling, etc.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Soul (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level a mage can create souls. On a technical level, \u2018instill\u2019 has connotations that could limit this. It could be read to mean that souls are slowly grown in the shell, for instance. Nevertheless, it appears mages can create and impart souls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with the rest of this rank, no supplemental spheres are listed. Contextually, though, Prime or Mind may be.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Convert Spirit to Soul</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage can create a soul and change ephemera, he can probably convert a spirit into a soul, or at least into something that functions like a soul rather than a spirit.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gilgul (Gilgul)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because Mage is a little cagey on what the Avatar is, it is unclear if this is destruction of a separate entity or soul surgery that amputates part of a person\u2019s soul or something inbetween. Technically all of those would be possible at Spirit 5.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Avatar Inversion</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We know this is possible because the Cauls do it. We know it manipulates a mage\u2019s Avatar, which puts it in the same rank (or higher) than Gilgul. I\u2019m not saying that Spirit 5 should give easy access to this, because as a storyline element it is next to impossible and should be the stuff of legends, at least on a level with curing vampires. What I am saying is that, barring Archspheres, the Spirit component of this freakishly difficult effect should be rank 5.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Journey Beyond Horizons (Break the Dreamshell)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exactly what it says. When using Spirit to break through the Horizon it takes Rank 5. This would presumably apply to any Horizon like barrier found out in the reaches.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Spirit 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. Unless the ST specifically wants something locked behind archspheres, it should be possible here.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Move Soul</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage can create and impart a soul, he should also be able to take and move one. Possibly even destroy one, though that may be a bridge too far as a game element for some tables.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see how the destruction of souls would be too much for some tables if the creation of souls is already possible at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T06:44:34-07:00","id":1551415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551368#post1551368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really see how the destruction of souls would be too much for some tables if the creation of souls is already possible at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I still think its worth checking if it is a red card issue for any of the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T06:54:45-07:00","id":1551416,"title":"","content":"Can we even define what is a soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T07:45:36-07:00","id":1551420,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Time</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview: </b>Time, Timing, Triggers, Duration. For some reason the writeup uses \u2018Tricking the Flow.\u2019</span> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Rules and Limitations</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 - Like Correspondence, Time has its own range chart to deal with attempts to look through, reach through, or move through time.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 \u2013 Time can extend duration at rank\u2026 the base writeup doesn\u2019t say.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 Duration Enhancement</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Time\u2019s writeup says it can extend duration, the actual rules just point to spending successes via the Optional Dividing Successes rule, or adding Entropy 3. <u>Possibly this means that if Time is included to extend duration the Optional rules are no longer Optional, and adding Entropy 3 as well just extends the duration indefinitely until some trigger is met.</u> If the Optional rules are used already, it seems Time would only be involved for the Entropy condition.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 - Travelling back in time has difficulty and paradox penalties. If this applies even on a botch it explodes very rapidly. The 50 year time jump in the book would garner 8 points of paradox if successful and 56 points on a botch. It is possible to read the paradox penalty as only applying when the mage actually time travels, but it isn\u2019t the most obvious or direct read.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I personally think these rules are unjustified and quite badly thought out, but they are the rules.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T07:48:13-07:00","id":1551421,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Time Sense </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Temporal understanding begins with the mage\u2019s own perceptions of time. At this stage, she develops a precise internal clock and can spot the temporal ripples left behind by (or, in many cases, developing ahead of) Time Effects. Other phenomena, too, leave disturbances in the time-stream, and the mage can notice them as well. Combined with additional Spheres, this Rank allows the mage to detect the influence of the Time Sphere on other spells or patterns too.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Internal Clock (Time Sense)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can know basic facts about Time like the current time. There is nothing indicating that this is limited to a specific convention, it should work with just about any way of measuring time. A mage should be able to get time of day, time of year, year, years in AUC (from the founding of Rome), daylight savings time, and possibly even the current time zone.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Time Effects (Time Sense)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can sense nearby manipulations of times. From the wording this includes time effects in nearby times, for instance time effects that are about to happen. This does not put any restriction on what Time effects can be detected.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Sense Stable Temporal Loop</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whether stable time loops are possible in your game is up to you. If they do exist, though, a mage with this power should be able to sense if he is in one and sense what he has to do to break free or stay in the loop.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I bring that up because IF stable loops are a thing in a game then it is arguably that they don\u2019t suffer from the increased difficulty and paradox of time travel. The spell isn\u2019t violating causality but reinforcing it. That\u2019s at least a plausible game element and this power would be important to using it.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Effects</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Detect Time Effects on Patterns</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are no coherent examples. From the text it sounds like time effects on some things require conjunctional spheres, but either this means any time effect on any pattern or spell is invisible to Time senses without other spheres, or there are specific things that ordinarily don\u2019t show up without help. The former would be ridiculously constrained, the latter needs more definition.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The best I have is that <u>this lets a mage detect when objects or things have been or will be manipulated by time effects but are not currently, recently, or about to be</u>. A mage can detect if an object was moved through time or aged, for instance. Now I would have thought that this would need Time 2 to look into the target\u2019s past or future, but maybe there is temporal residue.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T08:15:54-07:00","id":1551424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551416#post1551416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we even define what is a soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think we can. Not because of a lack of capability, but because Mage has chosen to be deliberately ambiguous about what it means. Still, rules mention them directly as things you should work with. Very often. So, such thing as a &quot;soul&quot; exists, falls under the purview of Spirit rather explicilty, and the precise definition it's left as a chore for the ST. And in classic ancient RPG style, Mage offers 0 guidelines to &quot;make your own soul&quot; <hr /><br /> Historically on Mage &quot;soul&quot; its often used in a way that can be exchanged for the word &quot;Avatar&quot;. Such as with the &quot;souless&quot; defect, that basically means you don't have an Avatar. So, one possible take it's that when Mage talks about the soul, it means the Avatar (let's leave aside for the moment how massively problematic this is with the way other gamelines use the word)<br /> <br /> However, Spirit doesn't specify that. There's nothing in the Spheres that will allow to make you such an interpretation. M20 sometimes mentions Avatar and soul as the same (or at least a very related) thing - such as the description for Gilgul. It also talks about the soul as the fuel behind passions and emotions - which contradicts the former because many beings w/o Avatar can have those. Having a soul it's also equaled to having a spirit. M20 seems to make a point in saying &quot;mind and soul&quot;, as if they weren't sinonimous - but never really explains what could be the difference.<br /> <br /> Personally I like Mummy's take on the nature of the soul as a multi-partitioned self. One can posit the Avatar as one of these parts w/o rejecting the idea that it could also be the energy behind passions and emotions, and the spirit-self that leaves the body to go to the afterlife. It's a possible way to conciliate Mage with other gamelines, that also allows to conciliate Mage's own vague use of the word.<br /> <br /> But the Spheres themselves don't have a take on this other than souls being under the purview of Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T17:43:24-07:00","id":1551433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551415#post1551415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps, but I still think its worth checking if it is a red card issue for any of the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is fair, it is a controversial topic, just think that creating souls should also fall under the red card area if spiritual annihilation covered by it. Things get a bit murkier when it comes to Avatars and Gilgul, but given how some visions of them include having them as souls, I think that they can also be a touchy topic. Unfortunately it is a bit difficult to remove the possibility of Gilgul wholesale when the requirement of the Avatar for Awakened magic is baked into the mechanics, along with social matters related to both in Awakened society, like with Gilgul being employed as a punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T08:20:05-07:00","id":1551442,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Past &amp; Future Sight/Thicken the Walls of Time </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the mage can look forward or backward through time. Although those impressions are fleeting, hazy, not entirely accurate, and bound by the limitations of that time and place (that is, what a bystander in that specific time and location could sense under the circumstances), they allow the Time-seer to catch glimpses of the past or future.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By itself, this Effect allows the mage to see in her present location only. By combining Past/ Future Sight with other Spheres, however, she could read the probable past or future impressions of objects or places (Matter), living things (Life), and alternate locations (Correspondence). Entropy 2 even allows her to glimpse multiple futures and pick out the one</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">most likely to occur.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reversing her powers of perception, that same mage can thicken the walls of time, which makes other Time Effects more difficult. Each success she rolls deducts one success from the attempts of other Time-savvy characters.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Look Forward to the Future, or Past to the Back (Past &amp; Future Sight)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bonus points if you recognized the reference without looking it up. A mage can look into the past or future. This power is limited to the current location, though Correspondence allows the spell to follow other locations and Pattern Spheres let the spell follow a pattern rather than a location. No guidance is given on how to determine the appropriate rank of pattern sphere but the spell is essentially locking to the pattern so that\u2019s how I would determine it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While this does look through time, it doesn\u2019t involve moving in time so as written it shouldn\u2019t invoke the +3 difficulty and Paradox multiplication. That said, mages can sense this, which means a mage in the past could be affected by this spell, so a mean ST could treat this as a risky endeavor.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 Entropy</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note that the Entropy addition likely only lets the mage know which timeline is the most likely, Time is probably the sphere that is looking into multiple futures.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Alternate Past</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One potential use of Entropy here is, when scrying into the past, taking a brief peek into offshoot timelines. This is a bit strange so I\u2019ll give an example. Say a mage needed to see the face of someone who usually wears a mask. He looks into the past several times but doesn\u2019t find a time where the target removes their mask. He does find one where the target almost does, but is distracted by a phone call. So the mage uses entropy to try to peek into a timeline where the phone call doesn\u2019t happen. That timeline isn\u2019t what happened but it is close (maybe it even could lead to the present anyways) so Entropy allows him to briefly see it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Temporal Semaphore</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It may seem cheap to say a mage risks Temporal Paradox if someone in the past detects his scrying, but a clever mage could use scrying itself as a form of communication. At certain times that only he knows he turns on his senses to check for temporal scrying. These moments would be keyed to certain plans he has for the future. In the future if he decides that plan was a bad idea he can scry on his past self in that moment, his past self will detect the scrying and change plans accordingly.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time Thickening (Thicken the Walls of Time)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can also make it more difficult to cast Time effects into a specific time and place. Though this is written mostly in the context of blocking scrying and travel, it should work on other effects like speeding and slowing time.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This doesn\u2019t involve moving in time so it doesn\u2019t invoke the +3 difficulty and Paradox multiplication.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Time Ward</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence 2\u2019s Thickening effect appears to be the basis for minor wards, so Time 2\u2019s may also be the basis for Time based wards. Presumably these would be wards that make it more difficult to act in the range of the spell during a specific time period. Since spells, by default, are cast on places, this wouldn\u2019t be much different from the Correspondence based ward.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Setting conditions on the ward would likely involve the same kind of supplemental spheres that Correspondence does.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T07:33:44-07:00","id":1551459,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time 3</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Time Contraction or Dilation/\u201cBullet Time\u201d/ Rewind Time </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speeding or slowing her relationship with time, the mage can now gain multiple actions, slow other characters or phenomena, or rewind small snatches of time. In game terms, every two successes allow the character to take one additional action that does not involve casting magick (only one Arete roll may be made per turn); or else slow another character, object, or even herself down by one increment per success. (Four successes, for example, would slow a person down to a quarter of his normal speed.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By rewinding time, the mage can also move her immediate surroundings back one turn for every two successes \u2013 an Effect that pulls her out of the normal flow of time and allows her to retcon an action or two. (See above.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combining this Rank with other Spheres, the mage can affect other Patterns (Forces, Life, or Matter 2), cast Effects across distance and time (Correspondence 3), move back in time while recalling events from the future she just left (Life 3/Mind 1), or even invoke multiple probabilities (Entropy 3). Again, such attempts are Paradox magnets with awful long term consequences.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed or Slow Time (Time Contraction and Dilation)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exactly what it says on the tin. I want to note that as written it doesn\u2019t take supplemental spheres to slow time for a person or thing. Locking spheres would still be necessary if the target moves out of range, though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This doesn\u2019t involve moving backwards in time so it doesn\u2019t invoke the +3 difficulty and Paradox multiplication.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Temporal Singularity</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When I picture this effect, I normally think of two different flows of time, the normal one and the sped up or slowed down one. A mage could reasonably have a gradient of time, say designate a location where time is running its slowest and the closer someone or something is to it the slower time passes for that thing. It\u2019s a bit like pop culture depictions of how time functions in the near proximity to a black hole.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reload Quicksave (Rewind Time)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can also briefly rewind time a matter of turns. He is not included in the rewind process. Despite the name I gave this, the mage is not restored to the state he was in at the point of return unless he adds extra spheres.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is directly stated in the Base Prime section to use the enhanced difficulty and paradox rules for time travel and is automatically vulgar (though quite possibly without witnesses), so barring any helpful modifiers this has a difficulty of 10 and multiplies paradox by the number of turns.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Fast Forward</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage should also be able to fast forward several turns, which is functionally equivalent to disappearing for several turns. Since this is forward movement, there is no difficulty or paradox penalty.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Effects</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is one of the bad entries for conjunctional effects, the given examples are quite vague.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Affect Other Patterns (Time 3 + Pattern Sphere 2)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Affect other patterns\u2026 with Time 3? In general? <u>I can only assume this is meant to refer to locking effects.</u> The lack of any specifics is jarring.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cast Across Distance and Time</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution \u2013 Cast Across Time</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I would have thought, based on the way Correspondence and Spirit scale, that Time 2 was the rank to cast across time. Time 2 doesn\u2019t claim the ability, though, and <u>we can read \u201ccast Effects across distance and time\u201d as giving the power of casting across time to Time 3</u>. Correspondence 3 is still wrong as casting across space is Corr 2. That said, a mage would have to have Corr 3 to use Time 3 across space, so this line is not wrong about the requirements, it just doesn\u2019t match how M20 states sphere costs</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Casting back in time is not one of the events directly stated to cause Temporal Ultra-Megadox, but it does involve manipulating the past in a significant way so STs may easily and reasonably say that it counts.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Move Back in Time While Remembering</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In other threads I considered this a contradiction because just a paragraph before a mage could rewind time without having to add spheres to remember. <u>However, if a mage is rewinding himself as well as everything else (which he might undo recent wounds), he would naturally lose memories unless he does something to stop that.</u> I don\u2019t see why the mage needs both Mind and Life, though. Either should suffice.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another possibility is this effect <u>lets the mage duplicate himself. He appears in a past where his previous self still exists. That self continues the way he did before (within reason) until such time as he casts the spell to rewind time. The later self gets to act however he wants</u>. It\u2019s a time based co-location effect where one of the selves knows what is going to happen, which might explain the particular use of Life 3/Mind 1.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ST\u2019s who use this the second way should decide whether the future self can cast on the same turn as the past self. That\u2019s normally not possible even with self duplication, but the future self also isn\u2019t on the same turn <i>in his timeline</i> as the past self.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Both versions count as rewinding time for the purposes of difficulty and paradox.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Invoke Multiple Probabilities</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 There is no Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Invoke multiple probabilities to do what? I can\u2019t resolve this because there\u2019s too little substance to even be wrong. If the book had said \u2018At Time 3, a mage can cast Time 3/Entropy 3 spells\u2019 it would have said just as much. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If anyone has any ideas, let me know.<br /> <br /> Added: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> suggests that this could be invoking alternate pasts. Pasts that did not happen but were likely to happen. Two applications of this would be pulling an item from an alternate timeline that came from that alternate past, and a microrewind that causes that alternate past to happen.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-05-2025, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T12:59:48-07:00","id":1551463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other threads I considered this a contradiction because just a paragraph before a mage could rewind time without having to add spheres to remember. <u>However, if a mage is rewinding himself as well as everything else (which he might undo recent wounds), he would naturally lose memories unless he does something to stop that.</u> I don\u2019t see why the mage needs both Mind and Life, though. Either should suffice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading Revised this seems to be the explanation. But there's no information about why those Spheres, and much less why those levels.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 it's sometimes used to dissociate mind and body, and it can probably be used to &quot;save&quot; memories trough time, so I can see it. Life 3, however, seems like a tax on healing :P<br /> <br /> Otherwise I think your other idea it's a good one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Invoke Multiple Probabilities</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 There is no Resolution</i></b><br /> <br /> Invoke multiple probabilities to do what? I can\u2019t resolve this because there\u2019s too little substance to even be wrong. If the book had said \u2018At Time 3, a mage can cast Time 3/Entropy 3 spells\u2019 it would have said just as much.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any ideas, let me know. </div> </div> </div>Super weird. Nothing like this in Revised nor 2e<br /> <br /> Closest I can think of it's Everett Volumes:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VE revised convention book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Correspondence 3/Entropy 4/Time 3 transports one person to an alternate present...These methods allow an Enlightened scientist to change physical location as well \u2014 an essential trait, given that alternate universes possess different buildings and geographical features.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> The second part tells us Correspondence isn't necessary, it's just convenient to change location to be safe. So, that leaves Entropy 4/Time 3 to disappear from this timeline into an alternate present...The only thing that doesn't match it's the level of Entropy. I guess that level it's needed because the one traveling it's a living being. Maybe you cold send stuff to (or from) Everett Volumes with Time 3/Entropy 3.<br /> <br /> So, maybe you can summon something that isn't there, but could be. Like the fabled &quot;there could possibly be a gun into this trash can&quot; - but for real this time rather than being a misinterpretation of what Entropy can do.<br /> <br /> Another idea that occurs to me that sounds like &quot;Invoke multiple probabilities&quot;:<br /> <br /> Say, one of your goons shoots somebody but fails and you act next. Knowing Everett Volumes, it's theoretically sound to say that in another branch of time the bullet did hit the target. You could Entropy 3/Time 3 to rewind time but in a way that it &quot;edges&quot; out to the other present (Actually has nothing to do with Everett stuff, just got inspired by it: The effect uses Time 3 to rewind time including yourself, no need to remember anything so it bypasses Mind/Life requirements, and uses Entropy so this time the bullet hits - no need to narrate the action again, just roll damage and go)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-04-2025, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T07:35:10-07:00","id":1551476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551463#post1551463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second part tells us Correspondence isn't necessary, it's just convenient to change location to be safe. So, that leaves Entropy 4/Time 3 to disappear from this timeline into an alternate present...The only thing that doesn't match it's the level of Entropy. I guess that level it's needed because the one traveling it's a living being. Maybe you cold send stuff to (or from) Everett Volumes with Time 3/Entropy 3.<br /> <br /> So, maybe you can summon something that isn't there, but could be. Like the fabled &quot;there could possibly be a gun into this trash can&quot; - but for real this time rather than being a misinterpretation of what Entropy can do.<br /> <br /> Another idea that occurs to me that sounds like &quot;Invoke multiple probabilities&quot;:<br /> <br /> Say, one of your goons shoots somebody but fails and you act next. Knowing Everett Volumes, it's theoretically sound to say that in another branch of time the bullet did hit the target. You could Entropy 3/Time 3 to rewind time but in a way that it &quot;edges&quot; out to the other present (Actually has nothing to do with Everett stuff, just got inspired by it: The effect uses Time 3 to rewind time including yourself, no need to remember anything so it bypasses Mind/Life requirements, and uses Entropy so this time the bullet hits - no need to narrate the action again, just roll damage and go)</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoy both of those as Time/Entropy effects, especially the second one. A sort of 'Invoke Alternate Past.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T07:53:25-07:00","id":1551477,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Time Determinism/ Trigger Effect/Time Bubble/ Anchor Point </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the mage learns to withdraw herself from the normal flow of time, hold Effects until they get triggered by events, or \u2013 by adding in Correspondence, Forces, Life, Matter, and/or Spirit \u2013 capture other beings or phenomena in bubbles of time. Thus, a mighty (vulgar) Time/ Forces/ Entropy Effect could capture a tornado and shunt it off into no-time space until some trigger sets it free. At this level of expertise, the mage can also set a temporal anchor point for herself for when she dares to travel through time at Rank 5.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stop Time (Time Bubble?)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is one of two things that I can count as withdrawing from the normal flow of time and the one that makes sense in Time 4. The mage can essentially freeze time while still moving around.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Despite dramatically playing with the flow of time, the mage is not changing his location in the time stream so this doesn\u2019t invoke the +3 difficulty and Paradox multiplication.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Nap Time</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A tired mage can stop time and take a nap. This is nothing special, but it is definitely what I would use this power for.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger Effect (Trigger Effect)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The signature ability of Time 4. The mage can essentially pause a spell until a given time or condition is met. This doesn\u2019t specifically say that the spell can determine or detect those events with Time alone and I suspect that it needs supplemental spheres similar to how wards and geases do. Strictly speaking, though, that isn\u2019t stated here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This does not involve travelling back in time so there is no increased difficulty or paradox\u2026 or is there.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Propagation Through Time Takes\u2026 Time?</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the movie Looper changes in the past seem to take time to reach the present. Someone loses a body part in the past but their future self continues to have it until a specific point then gets to see it disappear. If this is how time travel works in your game, there\u2019s another purpose of Time Trigger. Setting a countdown on a destructive spell sent to the past gives a mage time to leave the area before the aftereffects of the spell reach the present. If he sends something radioactive to the past, he can leave the scene before the radiation \u2018appears\u2019 in the present.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the trigger itself wouldn\u2019t cause an increase in difficulty or paradox, casting into the past probably would.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Temporal Anchor Point (Anchor Point)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This would be such a powerful and interesting effect\u2026 if M20 gave the slightest indication of what it was talking about. Yes, this is setting a point that is allegedly useful when time travelling, but with no system I don\u2019t even know how or why a mage would need to do that. <u>Perhaps it is meant to be a point that doesn\u2019t take extra successes to travel to, regardless of how much time is covered.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>It might also be a point that bypasses the normal difficulty and Paradox penalties for travelling to.</u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I set a temporal anchor point before looking into HDYDT to figure out what was going on. As often happens when I look into that book, I found myself back here with no memory, a bad headache, and a nasty note from myself.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m kidding. The bad headache is because I do remember what HDYDT says. It nerfs Time 5 time travel to make this anchor point necessary and <u>then says Temporal Anchor points let a mage return to that Anchor point with Time 4 instead of Time 5</u>. Apparently Time 5 time travel is supposed to be substantively worst than Time 4.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This may be the setup for time travel, but by itself the anchor doesn\u2019t involve moving in time so it doesn\u2019t invoke the +3 difficulty and Paradox multiplication. </span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjunctional Effects</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trap Things Outside Time</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Mage can isolate things in a pocket of no-time removed from the rest of reality. Whether this pulls the targets out of reality or just makes a location inaccessible because no time is passing within is unclear and this effect could probably work either way.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i>Contradiction Resolution - Pattern Spheres</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is unclear why a mage would need to include supplemental spheres when targeting spheres aren\u2019t really a thing and the subjects aren\u2019t going to move outside the spell. That said, this spell could easily involve separating buildings from foundations and other pattern splits and if that happened pattern spheres would be needed for the separation.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T08:51:02-07:00","id":1551480,"title":"","content":"Apparently my posts on this thread need approval now... no idea why.<br /> <br /> Anyways, Time 4 is up and awaiting approval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-05-2025, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T07:08:03-07:00","id":1551535,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Temporal Travel/ Time Immunity </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The \u201cDr. Who Effect\u201d allows the mage to exist outside of time; immunize people, places or things from time\u2019s passage; or travel forward or backward through time. Such godlike feats\u2026 feats that often cause a mage to become forever lost to history\u2026 are often best left to the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. Even for Masters, Time travel is a mysterious and maddeningly imprecise art. For extensive details about such things, see the sourcebook How Do You DO That?</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Dr. Who Effect (Time Immunity) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terry Pratchett</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u201cTime was something that largely happened to other people; he viewed it in the same way that people on the shore viewed the sea. It was big and it was out there, and sometimes it was an invigorating thing to dip a toe into, but you couldn't live in it all the time. Besides, it always made his skin wrinkle.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is arguably two effects, exist outside of time and immunize people against time. There\u2019s a lot of overlap between the two, and they both fall under \u201cThe Doctor Who Effect.\u201d For that matter so does Time Travel, but that still needs its own section.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can make himself or other people exist outside the flow of time and/or immunize them against its passage. This has several possible meanings, but every one I\u2019ve come up with makes sense for Time 5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This does not involve movement in time (almost the opposite) so it doesn\u2019t invoke the +3 difficulty and Paradox multiplication.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>A Fixed Point in Time</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can make himself or someone else immune to changes in the timeline. Even if written out of existence the target will continue to exist.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This would also make a lot of sense as a metamagic ability for Time Masters, though by default it is an effect.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Temporal Robustness</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can make a target is immune to damaging or complicating time effects such as being split across multiple times or time speeds. The target also can\u2019t be hindered by slowed or stopped time.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Functional Immortality</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The target is immune to the passing of time and does not age.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time Travel </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Travel in Time. It\u2019s time travel, it functions like time travel however that happens to work in your stories.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The management would like you to know how very, very much they hate this effect, they think it is a bad effect and that you should feel bad if you want to use it in your campaign. How dare you want to use the Time sphere to actually travel in time.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a mage actually uses this to go backwards, it is specifically stated to be a godlike effect, so 20+ successes at difficulty 10 plus two or three extra successes for going over the difficulty cap. In fact, the section on how to handle spell difficulties above 10 takes the time to specifically call out time travel as dangerous and rare, because the management really, really wants to make this point clear.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Alternate Pasts</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One idea I\u2019ve had for a time travel centric game is that each Tradition and Convention has its own past. All the pasts lead to the current moment but they are otherwise mutually exclusive. If such a scenario existed, a mage could go into multiple different pasts or jump between them.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Time 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. Unless the ST specifically wants something locked behind archspheres, it should be possible here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In particular, there are several abilities that Correspondence 5 has, which Time 5 reasonably has as well, such as superimposing time periods, distorting time so that events lead to unexpected places in the timeline, and allowing patterns to exist across multiple different times at once. How these work is heavily dependent on how time works at your table, though, so I\u2019m not going to call them out as missing powers for Time.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T10:35:01-07:00","id":1551565,"title":"","content":"That's all the main spheres. I am working on the Technocratic variants, but I'll state now that I am not as familiar with them. I'm mainly going to compare them to their regular counterparts and I'm not planning on putting in examples. If I miss something, be sure to let me know.<br /> <hr />There is one issue I've been putting off, though, which is the whole issue of life and mind and soul. I didn't tackle this in any of the spheres because it isn't clear which sphere writeup we should listen to, none of them ever give a metaphysical explanation of how a soul or mind attach to a body and they don't say the same thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> According to Life:<br /> <br /> Giving a body consciousness is Life 5/Mind 5. The body in question was specifically a complex body, so it may only be Life 3/Mind 5 to give a crab consciousness.<br /> <br /> Instilling a spirit into a body is Life 5/Spirit 3 or Life 5/Spirit 5. What the difference between the two of them is not stated, though the most reasonable option I see is <u>Spirit 3 instills an actual spirit while 5 instills a soul.</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> According to Mind:<br /> <br /> Creating a mind is Mind 5. It is unstated if this is a freefloating mind or one in a body.<br /> <br /> Swapping someone's mind into another body is Mind 5/Life 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> According to Spirit:<br /> <br /> Binding a spirit, which presumably includes binding it into a body, is Spirit 4. There is not a stated need for other spheres.<br /> <br /> Instilling a soul is Spirit 5, with no stated need for Life.<br /> <br /> <br /> So instilling soul is either Spirit 5/Life 5 or Spirit 5, depending on if we listen to Life or Spirit. Binding a spirit into a body is either Life 5/Spirit 3 or Spirit 4, depending on if we listen to Life or Spirit. And instilling a mind is either Mind 5/Life 5 or Mind 5/Life 4, or Mind 5 depending on if we listen to Life or Mind or Mind. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now the simplest solution I see is that for situations where a person is created complete with mind and soul, it doesn't matter. All three are used at Rank 5 anyways. For situations where things are done step by step, Spirit is the deciding factor on issues of soul, Mind on minds, and Life doesn't get to insert itself unless the other two agree. Simple, but it assumes a specific metaphysic about how minds, bodies, and souls work that may not be true.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T14:22:21-07:00","id":1551570,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that creating a mind with Mind 5 only makes a &quot;freefloating&quot; mind, something like an AI. It makes sense that you need other Pattern Spheres to either lock this new mind into a pattern or make it an inherent part of it.<br /> <br /> I also think those contradictions should be solved by giving each Sphere preference when stating its own main effects, so:<br /> <br /> 1. With Mind 5, Life 3/5 imparts consciousness to a body, while Life 4 swaps the mind of a body that already has one;<br /> <br /> 2. Mind 5 is enough to create a freestanding Mind, while adding a Pattern Sphere lets you impart consciousness as in Life 3/5;<br /> <br /> 3. Binding a spirit is Spirit 4. It doesn't necessarily imparts the spirit actual control over the &quot;body&quot;, that just occurred me;<br /> <br /> 4. As per above, binding a spirit into a body in a way that imparts the spirit with control over the body is Life3/5/Spirit 4;<br /> <br /> 5. Instilling a soul is Spirit 5. It imparts the target with all the features of a soul, whatever they may be, but not with a mind, not by itself.<br /> <br /> While this assumes a certain metaphysics, or at least a few metaphysical assumptions, I think at this point this is unavoidable: we have to accept some assumptions for the game to work at all, and it is easy enough for an ST to change things around if they want, easier than trying to extirpate such assumptions from the rules.<br /> <br /> STs have to decide what a soul entails anyways. Our only confirmation is that they're tied somehow to the Avatar, including the un-awakened avatar every human has.<br /> <br /> One curious thought I had: maybe a crab instilled with both mind and soul through a Life 3/Mind 5/Spirit 5 effect would be able to pass on those traits to offspring, initiating a lineage of intelligent souled crabs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T20:25:09-07:00","id":1551577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551565#post1551565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's all the main spheres. I am working on the Technocratic variants, but I'll state now that I am not as familiar with them. I'm mainly going to compare them to their regular counterparts and I'm not planning on putting in examples. If I miss something, be sure to let me know.<br /> <hr />There is one issue I've been putting off, though, which is the whole issue of life and mind and soul. I didn't tackle this in any of the spheres because it isn't clear which sphere writeup we should listen to, none of them ever give a metaphysical explanation of how a soul or mind attach to a body and they don't say the same thing.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your service! Now we just gotta solve the litte contradictions where we can. But I think the bigger problem are the omission.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T09:27:48-07:00","id":1551591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551577#post1551577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for your service! Now we just gotta solve the litte contradictions where we can. But I think the bigger problem are the omission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. And that's always the hardest, because we don't always know the omissions. Sometimes there are indications, such as the varying rules for otherworlds travel covered only in that section, or the resurrection spell on the magical effects chart. Other times we only realize there's something missing when we think of trying to do something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T11:41:26-07:00","id":1551627,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data Base</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purview: Data covers connections, with the implication that it also covers space as a byproduct.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Rules and Limitations</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 \u2013 Data largely functions like Correspondence but with different ranks of connection. So unless Data states that it does not have a power, or puts an effect at a different rank than Correspondence, it can be assumed to have the same broad capabilities as Correspondence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 \u2013 To target something with Data it needs to be \u201con the grid\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 \u2013 Base Data does not say that when extending spell range a specialist needs to have a rank in Data as high as the highest Sphere being used. However, Data 2 does say this and Data 2 is the rank for extending range so the rule still exists.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4 \u2013 Data does not say that it can move patterns without additional spheres the way Correspondence does. This can be inferred from rule 1, but strictly speaking it is not stated.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T11:47:37-07:00","id":1551628,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 On the Ones and Zeros </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Through a haze of code, the Data initiate begins to see the interconnectedness of all things. Bringing that esoteric level of comprehension to the world beyond his keyboard, the specialist can determine the exact distance between points or the connections between visible objects. His understanding allows him to work on base-level projects without instruments, thanks to a growing familiarity with relationship information. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data 1 explicitly lets a mage:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know Distance Between Objects (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike with Correspondence, Data specifically limits this power to visible objects. It does not, as written, apply to other senses. Whether that omission is intentional or not, I don\u2019t know, but spells default to sensory distance, so without specifically denying Data the use of other senses, I have to assume it can.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Detect Connection (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike Correspondence, Data is not missing this power. A Data initiate may determine the connections between visible objects. The word \u201cobjects\u201d may mean this power is limited to Matter patterns.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Level Projects (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is my unfamiliarity with the Data showing. I suspect this simply means that for most effects at this level the specialist doesn\u2019t need special instruments on site the way he does for later ranks. The later ranks are very clear about needing equipment on both ends of the effect.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the following powers are not given to Data, they may still be in its purview as it is supposed to function like Correspondence in regards to powers.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Things in Vicinity (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Hidden Objects (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is strange that the first of these two is not specifically called out as an ability of Data. Mapping out the surrounding area seems right up its alley.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sensing hidden objects may actually be an intentional omission, given that Data functions by already having information on targets. That said, the base rules of Data mean this should be possible too.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know Directions (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While unstated, it would be almost laughable if Data couldn\u2019t be used to pull up directional data. In fact, it could reasonably be an application of Detect Connection.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Detect Spatial Anomalies (Imm. Spatial Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a very interesting one. Because Data has the abilities of Correspondence, it can do this. On the other hand, it makes sense it shouldn\u2019t do this as well as Correspondence, and that Data and Correspondence should have increased difficulties in detecting each other, so it is plausible this is a deliberate omission.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even if it is, though, that doesn\u2019t override Base Data.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T09:23:13-07:00","id":1551656,"title":"","content":"While going through Data, I realized that Data 5 has the same oddity of duplicating Co-Locate senses as Correspondence does. They both put a version in rank 3 and rank 5 with no apparent difference other than number of different locations. That said, the wording of Data, though it still talks in terms of number of locations, does also hint at the idea of covering entire regions. That may be the difference between the Rank 3 and Rank 5 powers for both spheres, that the rank 5 version extends a mage's senses to everywhere in a chosen area.<br /> <br /> Does that sound right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T14:42:51-07:00","id":1551662,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 The Reach and the View </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With a few quick calculations, the specialist can assess theoretical and practical space \u2013 assessments that allow him to perceive what\u2019s happening elsewhere. Expanding the metaphysical elements of this discipline, this understanding allows the agent to see and touch places in other areas of the world, so long as he has instruments that allow him access to distant locations.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combining Data with other Spheres, the specialist can extend the practical range of Technocratic Effects. Matter allows him to modify Union tech from a distance; Mind lets him communicate with agents or targets worldwide; Forces lets him attack distant targets; and Entropy allows him to predict and alter probability patterns and spot flaws in objects that he can perceive. As with regular Correspondence, the operator\u2019s Data Rank must be equal to, or higher than, the highest Rank in a connected Effect..</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another thing Data doesn\u2019t suffer from: Unlike Correspondence, its ability to extend the range of actions, senses, and spells is not left to other sections.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extend Senses (Sense Through Space)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exactly what it says on the tin. Definitely not called scrying. Report to Room 101 if you called it that. As with Data 1, only vision is called out though the power wouldn\u2019t make sense if at least hearing wasn\u2019t also possible.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extend Range (Reach Through Space) </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data separates out extending the range of actions and extending the range of spells, but they are both in the writeup. It is worth noting that a specialist has to have instruments that allow access to the locations.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We could interpret this section to mean that a specialist already has to have equipment in the area that can do what he wants to do, and if he doesn\u2019t he needs a remote Matter spell to modify any nearby Union equipment to set that up. I bring that up as a possible fun game element.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Missing from Data but, as written, still possible:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Block Scrying </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A mage can use Thicken space data manipulation to keep other people from using Correspondence or Data to spy on him. He can also use this to cover his tracks when spying on others. These seem like the same thing but the latter implies a mage can do a bit more.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pull Things Through Tiny Holes (Reach Through Space)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pull small items through space. This extends the ability of touching distant things to grabbing them. As written there is no reason Data can\u2019t do this, though likely the equipment needed for it is more specialized.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#e36c0a\">Minor Ward? (Thicken Space) from Common Magical Effects</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data 2 never mentions thickening space, though since that was the basis behind blocking spying we can at least infer that it can do so in some applications. If it can use that for minor wards is less certain. One of the specific changes Data makes is moving Wards from Correspondence 4 to Data 3. Whether this also includes moving minor wards from Correspondence 2 to Data 3 is uncertain, as Correspondence 2 never specifically mentioned them so they would reasonably be omitted from Data 2 either way.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T08:57:53-07:00","id":1551737,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Data 3</span> </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Quantum Teleportation / Firewalling / Surveillance Hub </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Advanced Data transfer techniques allow the specialist to more or less sidestep conventional physics of spatial dimensions. In practical terms, this allows him to download himself into quantum teleportation mode; erect firewalls of particle physics that effectively ward objects, places, or people; and divide his perceptions across a multilocational surveillance hub. Combined with other Spheres, this expertise helps the agent move things, forces, and living beings through intervening space.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Again, however, these Procedures demand the appropriate gear on either side of the Effect. Such violations of conventional physics demand the proper technology.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data 3 gives:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Quantum Teleportation </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Allows a specialist to teleport himself (or others) along with any small items. Much like Correspondence 3, the text applies to the specialist himself, but later text implies other people or objects are possible</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulate Position (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also like Correspondence 2, there is a section about moving objects through space and pattern spheres are involved. Data doesn\u2019t say the key line about moving things without touching them, but it does specifically call out moving them through intervening space while teleportation usually bypasses that space, so if anything Data is more direct about what is happening here.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data likewise doesn\u2019t make the distinction that Pattern Spheres aren\u2019t needed to manipulate full patterns but without a word to the contrary it is assumed. The extra spheres listed here, then, are most likely locking spheres.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Co-locality Perceptions (Co-locality Perceptions)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perceive multiple places at once. It is not mentioned in this section, but handling multiple points of view at once is difficult without the addition of Mind.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now we come to a big break from Correspondence.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ward (Ward)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data puts Wards\u2026 ahem, firewalls of particle physics\u2026 in Data 3. Whether this covers both Minor and Greater Wards or just Greater Wards is uncertain. This is explicitly different from Correspondence, one of the very few places that is.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These next two were missing powers from Correspondence 3. That is, they were implied by the bolded abilities but never described in the text. Data doesn't do either so it is unclear if it has them. I still default to yes, the case is just harder.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#e36c0a\">Collapse Gates (Close Gates)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#e36c0a\">Open or Close Existing Gate (Open and Close Gates)</span></span></b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T12:40:29-07:00","id":1551743,"title":"","content":"Data and Correspondence may have an easier or harder time opening, collapsing or closing certain gates, depending on which of the two was used to create the gate.<br /> <br /> Not my preferred method of differentiating them, but it's always an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T12:43:44-07:00","id":1551827,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Between Space/Dimensional Cohabitation/Multilocation Access </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With such technology in place, the expert specialist can open quantum gateways between locations, create pocket dimensions between conventional space-time continuums, and disperse holographic manifestations of himself into several concurrent locations. With the appropriate Life, Mind, and Primal Force Procedures, those manifestations can even become as solid as the agent himself and perform different tasks in the finest Agent Smith tradition. </span> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lasting Quantum Gates (Rend Space)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Data 4 specialists can now create gates with duration which can be used by more than one person and can accommodate larger things</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pocket Dimension (Rend Space or Ward)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A specialist can create pocket dimensions, which presumably does the same thing as in Correspondence: isolate things in spaces removed from the rest of reality.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Co-Locate Self (Co-locate Self)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A specialist can project holographic manifestations multiple places at once, which is quite useful. Well it\u2019s actually of limited use on its own since he is still limited to the same mind <s>and can only make the same motion in each location</s>. Actually, for Data this works differently. Life is needed to make these manifestations solid, not to have them act differently from each other. Since Primal Force is listed as well, this version apparently creates new bodies.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I would think just using Forces would be easier in context.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not directly stated:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Teleport Anything (Rend Space) (from Corr 3)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like Correspondence 4, Data 4 should remove all the limitations from Data 3\u2019s quantum teleportation. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T14:39:05-07:00","id":1551845,"title":"","content":"I'm at work and don't have my copy handy; but I recall seeing somewhere something about getting a reduced difficulty when using Data instead of Correspondence when computer systems are involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-26T06:32:14-07:00","id":1551871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551845#post1551845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm at work and don't have my copy handy; but I recall seeing somewhere something about getting a reduced difficulty when using Data instead of Correspondence when computer systems are involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's in M20, but it might be in RBGtM. Many of the example pieces of connection given, though, are computer based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-26T06:34:39-07:00","id":1551872,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Redistribute Physical PropertiesFold Space/ Hyperdispersed Perceptions </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data Mastery merges conventional physics with sophisticated hypermath. The few specialists at this level can stack physical locations into the same space, alter the spatial dimensions and properties of a target, or disperse their perceptions into so many concurrent locations that a specialist may truthfully be said to have eyes and ears everywhere. </span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data specifically gets:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Superimpose Places (Co-Location)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A specialist can stack physical locations into the same space. This is likely as vulgar as the Correspondence version, hypermath or no hypermath.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Distort Spatial Dimensions and Properties (Spatial Mutation)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A quick line that pretty much covers much of the spatial warping of Correspondence 5. This can reasonably apply to warping space and directions, altering size, stretching or compressing things, and connecting patterns that are not touching.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Super-Mega-Hyper-Co-Locate Senses (Co-Location)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like Correspondence, Data 5 acts as if there is some sort of upgraded Co-locate Senses at this rank. This time the wording depicts the upgrade as a dramatic increase in number, which is strange, but also a dramatic increase in coverage, which makes more sense. Essentially it appears that Data 5 means the operative can have blanket coverage of an area rather than a discrete number of sense locations. It doesn\u2019t limit Data 3, per se, but it does mean Data 5 is carrying out a fundamentally different effect.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data doesn\u2019t mention these, but it should be able to do what Correspondence can here.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Co-Locate Anything (Co-Location)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In a sense this is the inversion of superimposing different things. Data should also be able to co-locate anything to multiple places.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, Data 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. The existence of <s>Arch</s> Multidimensional Hyperspheres could change this, but they aren\u2019t listed in M20.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T11:13:50-07:00","id":1551951,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Base Dimensional Science</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purview: </b>Otherworlds and things of the Otherworlds</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Rules and Limitations</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 \u2013 Dimensional Science is stated to be largely the same as Spirit. Unless specifically stated, we will assume it has the same capabilities. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T11:16:10-07:00","id":1551952,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 EDE Scan/ Evaluate Gauntlet/Map Dimensional Region </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Through applied principles and technologies, the specialist learns to perceive EDE presence and potential incursions, evaluate the characteristics of alternate dimensions and thickness of the barrier that keeps them outside the Consensus, and perceive the essential terrain in the pocket dimensions on the other side of that Gauntlet. </span> </div> </div> </div>Dimensional Science 1 can explicitly:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Barrier and past Barrier (Evaluate Gauntlet and Map Dimensional Region)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A specialist can both sense the Gauntlet and sense across the Gauntlet. Sensing the Gauntlet gives it\u2019s local thickness and likely any meddling done with it.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See EDE (EDE Scan)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Much like Spirit\u2019s Spirit Sight, a specialist can see spirits of all types and states.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">DimSci does not mention, but presumably can:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See Auras (Spirit Sense)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A specialist can also see the aura of people and other creatures, with all of the information that aurasight brings.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense ED Component (Spirit Sense)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this power a mage can determine if an object has contamination from across the dimensional barrier.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T11:51:54-07:00","id":1551953,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure about Seeing Auras, if for no other reason, because it's the hardest of the effects to parse through their stated understanding of Dimensional Sciences. Of course, we always have the problem that we never know if an omission is intended or not, but in this particular case I see a good chance that it was intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T13:16:52-07:00","id":1551956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1551953#post1551953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure about Seeing Auras, if for no other reason, because it's the hardest of the effects to parse through their stated understanding of Dimensional Sciences. Of course, we always have the problem that we never know if an omission is intended or not, but in this particular case I see a good chance that it was intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly seems outside their normal presentation. At the very least, if it does manifest as actual aurasight, it will have a paranormal element that sits on the edge of normal for the Technocracy. Kind of like psychic abilities. That's not actually out of type for Void Engineers.<br /> <br /> That said, the important element is the information that aurasight gives, not the actual appearance of Auras. It should still be able give all of the information that aurasight gives without actually showing an aura. It's not hard to imagine a Void Engineer having a few bits of tech (or even one integrated one) that can pick up emotional state and the telltale signs of a handful of common non-humans and reality deviants. That should let DimSci function like Spirit while still letting it integrate into a wide array of Technocratic methods. That's probably the best method.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Now, because I find it funny, I would actually have a particular Void Engineer NPC programming his HUD to give this information in a series of color overlays on whatever he's looking. Coincidentally, it happens to look a bit like an aura. It's purely a stylistic choice, of course, and not at all because it annoys his handler. Same with the way he has it give health scans in terms of hit points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T15:21:12-07:00","id":1551961,"title":"","content":"Kirlean Photography.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T15:35:20-07:00","id":1551963,"title":"","content":"Thoroughly agree, and it would be interesting to have some examples of &quot;Aura Sight&quot; as picking signs from tangential dimensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T03:00:04-07:00","id":1552070,"title":"","content":"Remember: despite the Ghostbusters being Etherites rather than proper Technocrats, they're still a good reference for Dimensional Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-11-2025, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T08:16:02-07:00","id":1552282,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science 2</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Dimensional Vibration/Modify Dimensional Gauntlet/Transdimensional Field </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level of expertise, the specialist can use radiation pulses, hypermath, and samples of transdimensional matter to grant access to those alternate dimensions. With the correct instruments, that specialist can send out artificial ripples into nearby subdimensions in order to attract EDEs and leave signals for other Dimensional Specialists.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thanks to the hypermathematical models and recordings involved in Dimensional Science, a specialist can also manipulate the Gauntlet, raising or lowering it, even as low as 0 \u2013 a feat mystic mages cannot duplicate. The Gauntlet 0 Effect lasts for only one scene, but it counters the punishment of the Dimensional Anomaly (that is, the Avatar Storm) if that phenomenon is still in play. However, the specialist herself still suffers feedback damage as she works the Effect. (In game terms, she takes the usual Avatar Storm damage, though she prevents other characters from taking it during that scene.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On a related note, the specialist learns to also surround herself (or, with the appropriate Spheres, other people or objects) with a transdimensional field; this, in turn, allows her to interact with subdimensions on a limited level (brief touch) without suffering harm from the Dimensional Anomaly </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The stated abilities of Dimensional Science 2 are:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reach Across Gauntlet (Manipulate Gauntlet)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When it comes to acting across the gauntlet, has the same main capabilities as Spirit in that a specialist can speak to or touch things on the other side. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science is also explicit that it is capable of calling or luring spirits that are not immediately present on the other side of the gauntlet.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Added Benefit</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the <s>Avatar Storm</s> Dimensional Anomaly is involved, Dimensional Science specialists can block damage from it when reaching across the gauntlet.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gauntlet Thickness (Manipulate Gauntlet)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#9900ff\"><i>Added Benefit</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not only can Dimensional Science lower the gauntlet, it is explicitly better at it than Spirit. Dimensional Science can lower it all the way down to 0. This can be used to bypass the Dimensional Anomaly, though the one who actually lowers it still takes the damage in the teeth. <br /> <br /> If there are any limits, such as that a person cannot leave the affected area on the Extra Dimensional side, it is not stated here. This means that taking people across the gauntlet is possible at a much earlier rank for Dim Sci than for Spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science does not mention these abilities, but given Base Dimensional Science it likely has them:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Communicate With EDEs (Touch Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those specialists who actually consider trying to communicate with EDEs will be able to work out at least some method of translation with this rank.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I mentioned in Spirit that since the way a spirit appears is at least partially a form of communication Spirit 2 might be able to change a spirit\u2019s appearance to other thematically appropriate ones. I suspect Technocrats would be more likely to use this.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Act on Spirit (Touch Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It would be quite strange if Dimensional Science didn\u2019t follow Spirit on this one. A specialist should be able to use this rank to touch and affect EDEs regardless of their state. This is also the ability to enable procedures to affect EDEs.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Conjunctional Effects:</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">None of the conjunctional effects of Spirit are mentioned in Dimensional Science, though we have to presume Dimensional Science is capable of its part in these, even if the other sphere is not.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue Object (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In previous discussions it looks like this creates an object that can affect spirits. Dimensional Scientists would definitely see the utility of this. I'm sure they would describe it differently such as using special energies or forms of radiation rather than actual spirit energies, but the effect would be the same.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#980000\"><i><b>Drain Essence From Spirit (Touch Spirit + Pull Quintessence From Pattern)</b></i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is not at all clear that a Technocrat can do this <i>but</i> if there is a deficiency it is in Primal Ventures, not Dimensional Science. Using Dimensional Science to allow spells to affect EDEs should carry over from Spirit.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extend EDE Senses to Others (??? + ???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While there would definitely need to be appropriate gear, Technocrats tend to think of sharing their effects more than Traditionalists do, so there's no reason DimSci wouldn't be able to do this.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T10:07:48-07:00","id":1552747,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science 3</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Dimensional Shift/Manipulate Paraphysical Phenomena/Phase Disruption Field </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Increased understanding allows the specialist to step sideways into alternate dimensions, manipulate the paraphysical matter (that is, ephemera) of those dimensions, and \u2013 with the correct weaponry \u2013 send out destructive phase disruption fields of vibrations that disorient, injure, or disintegrate EDEs. (In short, her attacks can harm spirit entities.) Thanks to the Stun/Kill/ Disintegrate settings on those weapons, she can choose whether to inflict bashing, lethal, or aggravated damage on Umbral targets\u2026 and although EDE\u2019s experience all forms of damage the same way, dimension-hopping humans and Deviant werebeasts do not. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s not much change at this rank, except that Dimensional Science spends no time on example conjunctional effects, and it clarifies something about direct damage spells that most spheres don\u2019t mention.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Step Sideways (Step Sideways) </span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oddly enough, the name doesn\u2019t change even with the Technocratic focus. Although, I suppose that\u2019s not really surprising as they are viewed as subdimensions that exist alongside the physical.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harm Paraphysical Things (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science is a little more informative than Spirit on this. First, it establishes that the ability can cause damage types other than Aggravated. Second, it establishes that it is not limited to targeting spirits.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now this does raise the question of when it can target things other than spirits and the wording leaves open a reasonable interpretation that it is essentially targeting things made of ephemera. That is, it can target anyone who has stepped sideways and been converted into ephemera.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulate Ephemera (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not a lot is given on what this means, but specialists can manipulate the substance of alternate dimensions. In this case it almost certainly has whatever ability Spirit has, with little to no variation.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most of the conjunctional effects from Spirit 3 needed resolution and there\u2019s nothing in Dimensional Science 3 that indicates it works differently than Spirit 3 in this regard, so I\u2019m not going to copy them.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science 4</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Alter Dimensional Topography/Dimensional Gateway/Stabilize Dimensional Field </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Increased understanding and appropriate technologies help the specialist make lasting changes to alternate dimensions. Reworking the paraphysical constraints of a given space, she may craft pocket domains and dimensional walls in order to block or catch EDEs. A skilled specialist can do this even from the Earthly side of the Gauntlet, thus avoiding the effects of the Dimensional Anomaly. Using similar techniques, the specialist can also carve out rapid-transit paths; in game terms, this Effect cuts down the specialist\u2019s travel time within the Otherworlds by (normal travel time divided by successes +1).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The specialist can also open large gateways into the subdimensions, although the people passing through those gates suffer the effects of the Anomaly unless the Gauntlet has already been lowered to 0 by a Dimension Science 2 Procedure.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Channeling Primal Energy (Quintessence) through appropriate technology, the specialist can also strengthen the Enlightened Anthropic Principle enough to prevent Void Adaptation (that is, disconnection and disembodiment; see Disembodiment in Chapter Four, pp. 88-89; and Disconnection and Disembodiment in Chapter Nine, p. 483.) Each point of Quintessence allows one character to resist Void Adaptation for one week. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Things get really interesting here. Dimensional Science 4 puts its focus in different places than Spirit 4. The one ability they both mention is:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gauntlet Gateway (Rend Gauntlet)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This pretty much functions exactly like the Spirit 4 variety. Most of the different word count focuses on the Dimensional Anomaly.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science 4 also lists a few abilities that Spirit 4 does not. These are not listed as unique to DimSci so presumably Spirit 4 can do them as well.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulate Extra Dimensional Topography (Alter Dimensional Topography)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While this is described in terms of how it affects spirits, it clearly focuses less on manipulating EDEs and more on manipulating the way other dimensions work. Indeed, one application is simply reducing the travel time of otherworld travel.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Pocket Dimensions or Dimensional Walls (Alter Dimensional Topography)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These may or may not be separate powers. They primarily deal with blocking spirits, so this may just be DimSci\u2019s method of binding. Nevertheless the wording implies more. A specialist may even be able to create small ED realms, though where these would be is never stated.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prevent Void Adaptation </span></b>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another Dimensional Anomaly specific power, specialists can put off Void Adaptation at the cost of Primal Energy. There's nothing here specifying this as unique to Dimensional Science.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meanwhile Dimensional Science mentions nothing about manipulating EDEs themselves, though we can presume it is still capable of it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Compel Spirits (Bind Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A specialist should be just as capable of summoning, compelling, and binding EDEs as Spirit is. If it is not directly mentioned, it may just be because few Technocrats would do this in any traditional way. Combined with the previous abilities of creating dimensions to trap EDEs there is a very Ghostbuster quality to DimSci at this point.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Fetish (Bind Spirit)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It should be at least within the abilities of Dimensional Science 4 to create fetishes, even if isn\u2019t a particularly technocratic approach.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exorcise Spirit</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This goes unmentioned but it would be unthinkable if Dimensional Science couldn\u2019t separate and banish EDEs</span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-01-2025, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T13:51:53-07:00","id":1552752,"title":"","content":"Void Adaptation isn't unique to the Dimensional Anomaly; it's always been the case that spending too much time in the Umbra presents an escalating risk of becoming a spirit. MRev leaned into it; but it didn't create the phenomenon. If I recall correctly, it didn't even <i>change </i>how it works; it just pointed out the logical consequences of the existing mechanics. <br /> <br /> &quot;We can presume that these DimSci things can also be done using Spirit&quot;/&quot;we can presume that these Spirit things can also be done using DimSci&quot;: I'm not going to rule it out; but that's not what the book says. It's silent on the matter, meaning that you can run it either way and still be fully compatible with what the book says. On the one hand, disallowing such overlap limits what both Spirit and DimSci can do, which I find problematic; but in the other hand, it helps make the two feel distinct from each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-30-2025, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T22:34:34-07:00","id":1552759,"title":"","content":"The Dimensional Anomaly didn't create or even change the rules on Void Adaptation, but it did have an impact: in practical terms it increased in orders of magnitude the documented occurrences of the phenomenon, as the isolated Realms and Constructs ended up unprotected against its effects.<br /> <br /> Anyway, is it just me or we jumped from <b>Dimensional Science</b> 2 to 4? Or did 3 got temporarily swallowed by the forum in an edit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T07:42:11-07:00","id":1552772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1552759#post1552759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dimensional Anomaly didn't create or even change the rules on Void Adaptation, but it did have an impact: in practical terms it increased in orders of magnitude the documented occurrences of the phenomenon, as the isolated Realms and Constructs ended up unprotected against its effects.<br /> <br /> Anyway, is it just me or we jumped from <b>Dimensional Science</b> 2 to 4? Or did 3 got temporarily swallowed by the forum in an edit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really thought I had posted it a week or two ago and I didn't check. I'll add it to the DimSci 4 post soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1552752#post1552752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;We can presume that these DimSci things can also be done using Spirit&quot;/&quot;we can presume that these Spirit things can also be done using DimSci&quot;: I'm not going to rule it out; but that's not what the book says. It's silent on the matter, meaning that you can run it either way and still be fully compatible with what the book says. On the one hand, disallowing such overlap limits what both Spirit and DimSci can do, which I find problematic; but in the other hand, it helps make the two feel distinct from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>All three of the Technocratic spheres have lines in their Base description that indicates they operate similarly to their regular counterparts. The one for DimSci is &quot;In game terms, Dimensional Science is largely the same as the Spirit Sphere.&quot; So unless they are clearly given different capabilties at different ranks (like how Data uses different ranks for warding) or a power is clearly stated to only belong to one (Like DimSci's greater ability to drop the gauntlet), then wording indicates they have the same abilities.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T18:45:34-07:00","id":1552787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1552772#post1552772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All three of the Technocratic spheres have lines in their Base description that indicates they operate similarly to their regular counterparts. The one for DimSci is &quot;In game terms, Dimensional Science is largely the same as the Spirit Sphere.&quot; So unless they are clearly given different capabilties at different ranks (like how Data uses different ranks for warding) or a power is clearly stated to only belong to one (Like DimSci's greater ability to drop the gauntlet), then wording indicates they have the same abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree. While it seems off here and there, assuming they're capable of the same things is both how it's said in their presentation, logical most of the time, and the most useful take.<br /> <br /> Sure, there <b>are</b> some cases where it's really hard to say for sure, but that's mostly because of the take on making those Spheres too tied to a specific Paradigm, both in Instruments and theories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T06:52:07-07:00","id":1552799,"title":"","content":"I put Dimensional Science 3 in the same post as 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T17:10:02-07:00","id":1552935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do?p=1552747#post1552747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It should be at least within the abilities of Dimensional Science 4 to create fetishes, even if isn\u2019t a particularly technocratic approach.</span> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily see a Ghostbusters-style trap being used as a battery to enable some other device to draw spirit energy out of it for a variety of effects. I don't imagine it would sit well with most imprisoned spirits, however, so they're probably a lot more glitchy and prone to catastrophic failure than the Traditions' more tried-and-true analogs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T09:06:14-07:00","id":1553171,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science 5</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Anthropic Field/ Breach Spatial Horizon/ Cosmogenesis </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Utilizing the ultimate applications of Anthropic Principle Fields, the specialist can generate her own Anthropic Field (with the right instruments, of course) that allows her to venture beyond both Horizons and venture into the Deep Universe. By crafting a reality bubble around herself, that specialist can keep other Earthly beings alive with her as well (two passengers per additional success beyond the second) and can engineer and pilot vehicles for Deep Universe travel. For design and construction systems, see Inventing, Modifying, and Improving Technology in Chapter Nine, (pp. 463-464).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Employing the arcane technologies of Cosmogenesis, that Master Specialist may also engineer and create Horizon Constructs and custom-designed and constructed EDE organisms. She must employ Primal Utility energies as well (often including Life and Matter if the EDE construct is to survive outside the subdimensions\u2026 that is, if it\u2019s going to be more than simple ephemera), but these cosmic computations allow Void Engineers to harness powers not unlike those of legendary gods.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science 5 can:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breach Horizon (Breach Spatial Horizon and Anthropic Field)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science dedicates an entire paragraph to this power, and includes some details that Spirit left out, like what it takes to bring other people along and that vehicles can be made for this purpose. Considering that non-technocrats make ships for the Deep Umbra as well (most notably, but not exclusively, the SoE Etherjammers) these are definitely not rules exclusive to DimSci.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Construct (Cosmogenesis)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Much like with Spirit, there is a lot of possibility hidden in the words Horizon construct. The scope here could be anything from small zones of influence to full realms. Similarly, no mention of other sphere requirements (for realms) is given but is likely intended if other editions are considered. As written, though, it is unstated.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create or Destroy Spirit Matter (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In DimSci the creation of Ephemera is lumped in with the creation of realms. DimSci is even more clear than Spirit that this includes making spirits. It does contain an interesting line that if the creation is intended to survive outside of the \u2018subdimensions\u2019 it often requires Life or Matter.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#b45f06\"><i>Ambiguity Resolution \u2013 Spirit or Other</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s a little unclear what this is referring to. It could mean that <b>unless spirits are created with Matter or Life, they don\u2019t function the same way when crossing the gauntlet that regular spirits do</b>. That\u2019s a strange interpretation, though it is within the given wording. I suspect this means that <b>if the Operative wants the creation to be more than a Spirit he needs to include other spheres</b>.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dimensional Science does not mention the following powers, but because it operates like Spirit we can presume it has them.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imbue/Drain Essence (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A specialist can now pull or impart essence from or to an EDE directly rather than by damaging or (presumably) healing said spirit. Essence is not quintessence, but it can probably be turned into quintessence with the help of Prime.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Soul (Forge Ephemera)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is possible that the ambiguous wording for creating EDEs was intended to include creating the transdimensional elements of living creatures that the overly poetic Traditions insist on calling souls. Whether or not this was intended, Dimensional Science should be able to accomplish it if the specialist even considers the need to do so.</span> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gilgul (Gilgul)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s no reason I can think of that Technocrats wouldn\u2019t be able to do this, even if they\u2019d have completely different terminology for how it works.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything Else (???)</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with all Rank 5s, DimSci 5 should be able to do just about everything possible within the Sphere\u2019s purview. Unless the ST specifically wants something locked behind archspheres, it should be possible here.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T20:05:29-07:00","id":1553192,"title":"","content":"If anything, we can say that the Technocratic Spheres actually help to better define some of the rules for the regular Spheres. Dimensional Science was particularly full of that.<br /> <br /> By the way, I have to keep this in mind, because my current chronicle does include an Etherite that specializes in Spirit with a full DmSc-like paradigm (his focused on Aliens and studying Alien tech).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}